[1393]={nameES="Artistic Direction",objectivesES={"Return to Borlach with his ingredients","Obtained clay","Obtained charcoal","Obtain clay from a potter","Artistic Direction","Obtained flowers","Obtain charcoal from the chef Ciriel","Obtain flowers from the gardener Lebadar","Borlach waits for you on the Second Circle, near the entrance to the First Circle.\
\
You have gathered his ingredients and should let him create his paints.","On the Third Circle, Ciriel works at the ovens, and the potter next to the House of Craft. Lebadar may be on the Second Circle, at the base of the entryway to the Third Circle.\
\
Borlach has requested that you ask them for the following ingredients: charcoal, clay, and flowers, respectively.","Thanks to the festival, a painter has suddenly been struck by inspiration, but his poor sense of direction keeps him from acquiring paint ingredients.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>"}},
[1394]={nameES="Arvaethor's Patrol",objectivesES={"Complete The Orkish Path","Talk to Arvaethor to dismiss him","Complete In Ethring's Defence","Arvaethor's Patrol","Complete White Mountain Plague","Complete Vale of Shadow","Arvaethor is near the pillaged lumber camp in Ringló Vale.\
\
You should speak with Arvaethor.","Use the whistle to summon your new friend if you become separated","Arvaethor has asked you to join him on his task of protecting the Vale","Arvaethor asks for assistance as he patrols the Vale and secures its safety.","This noble Arvaethor wishes to help you deal with the invasive White Mountain Orcs that descended upon Ringló Vale.\
\
You should complete a number of tasks in Ringló Vale, using the whistle to call your friend for help if you become separated.","Speak with Arvaethor","Complete Under the White Mountain"}},
[1395]={nameES="As Dead as Stone",objectivesES={}},
[1396]={nameES="As The River Runs",objectivesES={"Talk to Mellien","DNT -- will not be seen","Concerned by the emergence of the Dead in Blackroot Vale, Sarnir has asked you to investigate how far their influence has grown.","Mellien can be found in Sardol, to the south-west of Alagrant in Blackroot Vale.\
\
Sarnir is concerned that the Dead's influence might extend to the south and has asked you to aid the people of Sardol.","As The River Runs"}},
[1397]={nameES="Ashes and Stars, Chapter 1",objectivesES={"Forced into the tunnels under Osgiliath after a daring ploy by Faramir, the Rangers of Ithilien, led by Mablung, now hope to reunite with their lost captain.","Talk to Mablung","Mablung can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath.\
\
You have spoken to Damrod about Faramir's gambit, and should now speak to Mablung about searching for Faramir in the tunnels under Osgiliath.","Damrod can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath.\
\
Mablung has asked you to speak to Damrod about Faramir's daring attack that allowed many of their number to escape the city.","Ashes and Stars, Chapter 1"}},
[1398]={nameES="Ashes and Stars, Chapter 2",objectivesES={"The letter can be found at the make-shift camp-site in the sunken labyrinth beneath Osgiliath.\
\
You have discovered a small, empty camp-site in the tunnels beneath Osgiliath. You should take the note and examine it before pressing onward.","The Ranger suddenly dashes away into the dark of the tunnels!","Ashes and Stars, Chapter 2","Mablung can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath.\
\
You have recovered a troubling letter and encountered a strange hooded Ranger in the sunken tunnels of Osgiliath. You should now return to Mablung.","Search further in the depths of Osgiliath","A mysterious Ranger stands near the gates...","Desperate to learn of their lost captain's fate, Mablung and Damrod begin their search for Faramir in the winding tunnels beneath Osgiliath.","You have found an emptied camp-site with only a note left behind...","The Ranger is standing near the gate to Muzgásh's chamber in the sunken labyrinth.\
\
You have defeated Muzgásh, but now a strange Ranger stands near the gate to his chambers. You should approach the Ranger and attempt to speak to him.","The note is hastily-written and swiftly descends into madness and incoherence...","Faramir might be found somewhere within the sunken labyrinth beneath Osgiliath.\
\
Mablung has asked you to search the depths of Osgiliath for Faramir, who may have fled into the tunnels in the wake of his attack on the fell-beast.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>You must complete the \\qSunken Labyrinth\\q instance to complete this quest.</rgb>","Examine the note at the abandoned camp-site","Search for Faramir in the depths of Osgiliath","Deliver the note to Mablung and tell him of the mysterious Ranger","Approach the mysterious Ranger","Faramir might be found somewhere within the sunken labyrinth beneath Osgiliath.\
\
You have not yet found Faramir in the tunnels beneath Osgiliath, but you should continue your search deeper in the labyrinth."}},
[1399]={nameES="Ashes and Stars, Chapter 3",objectivesES={"As you examine the shield, the Ranger darts out beneath the broken bridge and flees!","As you examine the horn, the Ranger appears and dashes across the nearby bridge-rafts","Return to Mablung and tell him of the Ranger's elusiveness","Signs of the Ranger's passing can likely be found in southern Osgiliath, especially around the wharfs and nearby ruins.\
\
Mablung has asked you to pursue the mysterious Ranger you encountered in the sunken tunnels of Osgiliath. By the way he took to escape, Mablung suggest searching the wharfs and the nearby ruins.","As you examine the necklace, the Ranger dashes up a nearby staircase!","Disturbed by the note you recovered and your sighting of a mysterious Ranger in the depths of Osgiliath, Mablung sends you to the streets above to track this elusive stranger.","Search Osgiliath for signs of the mysterious Ranger's passing","Mablung can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath.\
\
You have lost the trail of the mysterious Ranger, and should now report his elusiveness to Mablung.","Ashes and Stars, Chapter 3"}},
[1400]={nameES="Ashes and Stars, Chapter 4",objectivesES={"Deliver the remains of Faramir's cloak to Mablung","Garbed in the tattered remains of Faramir's cloak, the corrupted Ranger falls defeated!","Ashes and Stars, Chapter 4","After losing the trail of the mysterious Ranger, Mablung asks you and your fellows to search the ruined city and uncover his identity at any cost.","Mablung can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath.\
\
You have defeated the corrupted Ranger that bore Faramir's cloak. You should now return the cloak to Mablung.","The fallen Ranger can be found inside the Palace of Eldacar.\
\
You have defeated the corrupted Ranger bearing the cloak of Faramir and should now reclaim it for the Rangers of Ithilien.","You have recovered Faramir's cloak, but his whereabouts still remain unknown...","Reclaim Faramir's cloak from the fallen Ranger","Pursue and confront the mysterious Ranger","The mysterious Ranger can be found somewhere within the ruined city of Osgiliath.\
\
Mablung has asked you to search the ruined city for any sign of the mysterious Ranger you encountered in the sunken tunnels.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Note: You must complete \\qThe Ruined City\\q instance to complete this quest.</rgb>"}},
[1401]={nameES="Ashes and Stars, Chapter 5",objectivesES={"The site where Faramir speared the great fell-beast can be found to the north-east of the Dome of Stars.\
\
In desperation, Mablung has asked you to search the site where Faramir speared a fell-beast in hopes of uncovering where he may have gone.","The broken spear can be found near the ruined bridge to the north-east of the Dome of Stars.\
\
You have found the site as well as the broken spear that Faramir once wielded. You should examine the spear.","After pursuing and defeating the Ranger corrupted by a Morgul-blade, Faramir's trail is all but lost. As his hope begins to wane, Mablung sends you to the location where Faramir struck down a mighty fell-beast of Mordor.","You are filled with dread as a dark shadow passes over you!","Search the site where Faramir slew the fell-beast","Ashes and Stars, Chapter 5","The splintered remains of the spear that Faramir used to slay the fell-beast lay nearby...","Mablung can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath.\
\
You have encountered one of the Nazgûl, the Black Blade of Lebennin, who claims to hold Faramir captive atop the Dome of Stars. You should tell Mablung of this at once.","Examine Faramir's broken spear","Talk to Mablung of the Nazgûl's captive"}},
[1402]={nameES="Ashes and Stars, Chapter 6",objectivesES={"Mablung can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath.\
\
You have triumphed over the Black Blade of Lebennin if only for a moment, and learned of Faramir's fate. You should return to Mablung with this news.","Free Faramir from the Dome of Stars","Confront and defeat the Black Blade of Lebennin","The Black Blade of Lebennin and his captive can be found atop the Dome of Stars.\
\
Mablung has asked you to free Fararmir from the Black Blade of Lebennin and attempt to banish his spirit before the coming battle.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Note: You must complete \\qThe Dome of Stars\\q instance to complete this quest.</rgb>","One of the Nazgûl, the Black Blade of Lebennin, has revealed himself as Faramir's captor and now holds the captain of the South-rangers atop the Dome of Stars.","The Nazgûl's lies are revealed, for Norhún's noble sacrifice allowed Faramir to escape Osgiliath alive!","Ashes and Stars, Chapter 6","Talk to Mablung and tell him of Faramir's fate"}},
[1403]={nameES="Ashes and Stars, Chapter 7",objectivesES={"Talk to Mablung","Damrod can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath.\
\
Mablung has asked you to tell Damrod of Faramir's escape from Osgiliath.","Ashes and Stars, Chapter 7","Through Norhún's steadfast loyalty and sacrifice, Faramir was able to escape the western gates of Osgiliath. Their hope restored, Mablung and his men make ready for the journey ahead.","Talk to Damrod","Mablung can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath.\
\
You have told Damrod of your successes in Osgiliath and should now speak to Mablung once more."}},
[1404]={nameES="Ashes of Knowledge",objectivesES={}},
[1405]={nameES="Ashunûg, the Fane of the Accursed -- Solo/Duo",objectivesES={"A fierce brute is guarding the way deeper into the mines of Ashunûg.\
\
Defeat Eshêgur the Reaper.","Defeat Nâkhugir","Defeated Nâkhugir","A monstrous scorpion dwells deep within the mine of Ashunûg. This must be the Anâkhi's idol, and it must be destroyed before it can bring terror to the nearby lands in Ambarûl.\
\
Defeat Nâkhugir.","Defeat Anâkhi Ensemble","Ashunûg, the Fane of the Accursed -- Solo/Duo","We have discovered a dangerous cult of usan-kûni worshippers hiding in our own back-yard. They call themselves Anâkhi, and have made their home inside Ashunûg, a salt mine in northern Ambarûl that has long been abandoned. We are only recently freed of Sauron, the All-seeing, and must not allow this new cult to take hold. The Anâkhi scorpion worshippers must be driven from our lands.","Defeated Anâkhi Ensemble","Defeat Eshêgur the Reaper","A group of Anâkhi cultists stand at the passage even deeper to the mine, guarding something important. Their rituals must be stopped.\
\
Defeat the Anâkhi Ensemble.","Defeated Eshêgur the Reaper"}},
[1406]={nameES="Ashunûg, the Fane of the Accursed -- Tier 1",objectivesES={"A fierce brute is guarding the way deeper into the mines of Ashunûg.\
\
Defeat Eshêgur the Reaper.","Defeat Nâkhugir","Defeated Nâkhugir","Defeat Anâkhi Ensemble","Ashunûg, the Fane of the Accursed -- Tier 1","We have discovered a dangerous cult of usan-kûni worshippers hiding in our own back-yard. They call themselves Anâkhi, and have made their home inside Ashunûg, a salt mine in northern Ambarûl that has long been abandoned. We are only recently freed of Sauron, the All-seeing, and must not allow this new cult to take hold. The Anâkhi scorpion worshippers must be driven from our lands.","Defeated Anâkhi Ensemble","Defeated Eshêgur the Reaper","Defeat Eshêgur the Reaper","A group of Anâkhi cultists stand at the passage even deeper to the mine, guarding something important. Their rituals must be stopped.\
\
Defeat the Anâkhi Ensemble.","A monstrous scorpion dwells deep within the mine of Ashunûg. This must be the Anâkhi's idol, and it must be destroyed before it can bring terror to the nearby lands in Ambarûl.\
\
Defeat Nâkhugir."}},
