[2812]={nameES="Campeón de Maethad",objectivesES={"Campeón de Maethad","Has reclamado una de las mazas de Ronkûrz","Lleva la maza de Ronkûrz a Hwati","Reclama una de las mazas de Ronkûrz","Ronkûrz, el campeón de Maethad, puede encontrarse entrenando Uruks en el campamento orco de Mor Maudhúl, al norte de Gabilshathûr, al otro lado del lago en Duvuinen.\
\
Una vez que hayas reclamado una de las mazas de Ronkûrz, llévala de regreso a Hwati en Gabilshathûr."}},
[2813]={nameES="Campeón: Camino del Campeón Marcial",objectivesES={"Campeón: Camino del Campeón Marcial","Valthor está acampado en las Fundaciones de Piedra, en Moria.\
\
Se te ha ordenado buscar la guía del campeón Valthor.","Habla con Valthor en las Fundaciones de Piedra","Valthor te ha convocado."}},
[2814]={nameES="Campeón: El camino más audaz es la disciplina",objectivesES={"Reúnete con Gwesgylliel para recibir más entrenamiento de campeón","Como campeón, has alcanzado tal renombre que has recibido una convocatoria de Gwesgylliel en Lin Giliath, en Meluinen.\
\
Debes buscar a Gwesgylliel para recibir más entrenamiento en tu clase.","Gwesgylliel está en Lin Giliath en Meluinen en las Quebradas del Norte.\
\
Te han dicho que la doncella elfa Gwesgylliel, ella misma una poderosa campeona, desea hablar contigo.","Campeón: El camino más audaz es la disciplina"}},
[2815]={nameES="Champions of the Falcon",objectivesES={}},
[2816]={nameES="Change for the Worst",objectivesES={"Find Gadda at the abandoned farm","Gadda and a small handful of men loyal to Stanric have escaped Stangard and set up camp at the little farmstead where you planted some hopeful seeds.\
\
You should find Gadda at the abandoned farm in the east of Eorlsmead.","Change for the Worst","You have returned to Stangard to hear some dire news from your friend Sabert at the gate."}},
[2817]={nameES="Changing of the Guard",objectivesES={"Talk to Thurferth, Captain of the Guard","Thurferth suggested other guards posted around the city may be able to help.","Thurferth is near the centre of Woodhurst.\
\
You should tell Thurferth of what you learned from the guards around town.","Changing of the Guard","Thurferth is near the centre of Woodhurst.\
\
Herubrand told you to speak with Thurferth, Captain of the Guard, about the two men posted at the Mead Hall and whether they have seen anything unusual.","The Mead Hall was attacked by men from Woodhurst for an unknown cause. The Reeve's advisors have worked to keep the attack a secret to help maintain peace."}},
[2818]={nameES="Chaos on the Sea",objectivesES={}},
[2819]={nameES="Chapter 1 - The Books of Balance",objectivesES={}},
[2820]={nameES="Chapter 1 - The Eyes and Ears of the City",objectivesES={"The sea-hawk swoops down and enjoys the dinner. Now is your chance!","The Watcher on the Wing waits dutifully for you to give it a message to bring back to Achardis. Bring the note and tie it to her leg so she may return it to the Order of the Eagle's leader in Umbar Baharbêl.","Speak with Harthabor","Retrieve the message from the sea-hawk","Pick up a scrap of meat from the plaza near the sea-hawk","The flat stone on the rampart to the north-east may prove a suitable place to lure the sea-hawk from its perch.","Deliver the message to Harthabor at Jax Phanâl","You gently remove the paper tied to its leg. The sea-hawk does not seem to mind, and in fact appears to be very comfortable exchanging the information for the delicious dinner you set before it.","The sea-hawk flies away over the ramparts, bearing the message","Chapter 1 - The Eyes and Ears of the City","The sea-hawk sits atop a roof through the archway and east of Harthabor in Jax Phanâl. Find a method to draw the bird down, collect its message, and return it to the agent.","Concern over the new powers in control of Umbar and their potential relationship to the Haradrim or the Church of the All-Seeing cause the Order of the Eagle to maintain watch over threats from Umbar Baharbêl.","Attach the message to the sea-hawk courier","Harthabor is need of assistance to contact his leader in Umbar Baharbêl. Speak with him to learn more.","Perhaps this scrap of meat will entice the sea-hawk from its perch?","The bird is away. Harthabor awaits your return in Jax Phanâl. Go to the agent and inform him that all went well.","Harthabor is waiting to see the message you retrieved.","Place the scrap of meat on the flat stone to the north-east","The sea-hawk looks up expectantly, and you fasten the return message to its leg.","You drew the bird down from its perch and should now remove the message from its leg."}},
[2821]={nameES="Chapter 1.10: Inside Every Shadow",objectivesES={"King Elessar's most trusted bodyguard greets you with a warm smile.","Chapter 1.10: Inside Every Shadow","Talk to King Elessar's most trusted bodyguard","Legolas and Gimli have come with King Elessar's travelling party to Imloth Melui.","King Elessar told you to find his trusted bodyguard somewhere outside the Hall of Lady Vanyalos, in Imloth Melui, King's Gondor.","King Elessar is inside the tower guard-house in the centre of Imloth Melui, in King's Gondor.","According to Pethanar, the gossipmonger of Linhir, King Elessar's travelling party will have reached Imloth Melui by now.","Talk to King Elessar inside the tower guard-house in the centre of Imloth Melui","Find King Elessar's trusted bodyguard somewhere outside the Hall of Lady Vanyalos","You have found Elessar's most trusted bodyguard","The gossipmonger spoke true: King Elessar's travelling party has come to Imloth Melui","Travel to the entrance of Imloth Melui in King's Gondor","You learned from a gossipmonger in Linhir that King Elessar has begun to tour his kingdom, and indeed has already departed Minas Tirith!","Talk to Legolas at the entrance to Imloth Melui","Talk to Líniel outside the tower guard-house in the centre of Imloth Melui","Líniel is outside the tower guard-house in the centre of Imloth Melui.","Talk to Gimli at the entrance to Imloth Melui"}},
[2822]={nameES="Chapter 1.1: A King Should See His Kingdom",objectivesES={"Talk to Gimli north-east of the Harlond, in King's Gondor","Talk to Legolas north-east of the Harlond, in King's Gondor","Talk to Glindor in Minas Tirith (Midsummer) and go with him to see King Elessar","Chapter 1.1: A King Should See His Kingdom","Glindor, King Elessar's herald, is outside the stables in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).","Legolas is north-east of the Harlond, in King's Gondor.","King Elessar, recently crowned and newly wedded, is eager to heal the hurts of his kingdom and to move Gondor into an age of prosperity.","Gimli is north-east of the Harlond, in King's Gondor."}},
[2823]={nameES="Chapter 1.1: Beyond the Black Gate",objectivesES={"Talk to Mithrandir just inside the ruin of the Black Gate","Talk to Rhogrin at Mornaur, in western Udûn","Talk to Rhogrin in Cirith Gorgor","Rhogrin is at Mornaur, in western Udûn.","The forges of Mornaur are on the western side of the vale of Udûn.","Rhogrin asked you to push over some of the anvils at Mornaur, rendering them difficult for the Orcs to use.","Sauron has been defeated, but the shroud over Gorgoroth must be pierced if the Free Peoples of Middle-earth are to be made safe of the evils the Dark Lord set in motion before his fall.","A number of dead Orcs and trolls lie here. What was the cause of the infighting?","Mithrandir asked to meet you just inside the ruin of the Black Gate, there to take the measure of the adventurers that desire to press forward into the land of Mordor.","Talk to Covadil in Cirith Gorgor","Adventurers have passed through the ruins of the Black Gate into Cirith Gorgor, and intend to seek treasure and glory in Mordor. Mithrandir asked you to speak to them and warn them against taking brash action.","You have found the Forges of Mornaur, where Sauron equipped his armies","Search the basin where the group of Orcs travelled, north-east of Durthang","Dangerous foes stalk the vale of Udûn, and Mithrandir asked you to venture forth with caution and defeat them.","Search Udûn for the forges of Mornaur","Rhogrin has come to Mornaur, in western Udûn.","Talk to Annoth in Cirith Gorgor","Talk to Harthalín in Cirith Gorgor","Chapter 1.1: Beyond the Black Gate","From the cliff's edge below Mornaur, Rhogrin saw a large group of Orcs and trolls in the basin of the vale north-east of Durthang, and asked you to investigate in order to make the area safe for other soldiers of Gondor."}},
[2824]={nameES="Chapter 1.1: The Legacy of Durin and the Trials of the Dwarves",objectivesES={"Chapter 1.1: The Legacy of Durin and the Trials of the Dwarves","Talk to Durin by the stable-master in Skarháld","Durin asked you to climb the stairs at Skarháld in search of Longbeards, Zhélruka, and Stout-axes who might share their opinions on what he should do for them.","Durin is pleased you have returned to Skarháld, for he has had some difficulty forging a workable alliance between the dwarves who have come to the Grey Mountains and could use your help.","Talk to King Thorin Stonehelm in the Hall Under the Mountain, in Erebor","Durin is on the lowest level of Skarháld, near the stable-master, waiting for your report from the three dwarf-clans who inhabit the mountain fortress.","Talk to Kóvo of the Stout-axes in Skarháld","Talk to Glóin of the Longbeards in Skarháld","Durin's father, King Thorin Stonehelm, is at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain in Erebor.","Talk to Bórnek of the Zhélruka in Skarháld"}},
[2825]={nameES="Chapter 1.2: The Cruel History of Durthang",objectivesES={"Talk to Annoth outside Durthang","Annoth went to the fortress of Durthand, in Udûn, and has not returned.","Annoth is consumed by his desire to avenge his ancestors, the Thandrim, and Rhogrin worries that his friend has fallen into trouble on account of it.","Talk to Annoth outside Durthang and listen to his tale of the Thandrim","Talk to Annoth outside Durthand, once the fortress of the Thandrim","Find Annoth outside Durthand, once the fortress of the Thandrim","Annoth is outside the fortress that once belonged to the Thandrim, and was called Durthand.","Chapter 1.2: The Cruel History of Durthang","Annoth is outside the fortress of Durthang, in southern Udûn.","You have found Annoth. He lives still"}},
[2826]={nameES="Chapter 1.2: The Land Remembers It All",objectivesES={"Legolas is working along the docks south-east of Othanar in the Harlond.","A small crowd of Gondorians speaks in hushed tones to the east of Legolas and Gimli. You should get closer to them and <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> to their conversation.","The crowd glares at you with distrust","Approach the small crowd and <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> to their conversation","Berthon glares at you with suspicion and dislike writ on his face","Othanar oversees the rebuilding of the Harlond by the north-eastern entrance.","Gimli is in the Harlond, helping Legolas with the rebuilding effort.","Othanar asked you to clean up rubble piles, collect wooden planks, and defeat the rats that now infest the Harlond.","Bring the wooden planks to Othanar in the Harlond","Legolas stands to the west of the whispering Gondorians by the docks of the Harlond.","Talk to Berthon in the Harlond","Chapter 1.2: The Land Remembers It All","The War of the Ring left much of Gondor in ruin, and now its people work to restore their lands.","Talk to Legolas in the Harlond","Talk to Gimli in the Harlond","Berthon speaks to a small crowd of Gondorians by the docks of the Harlond.","Talk to Othanar inside the Harlond","Legolas suggested that someone to the south-west must be overseeing the repairs of the Harlond."}},
[2827]={nameES="Chapter 1.2: Treachery Remembered",objectivesES={"Stáli the Hewer has been restoring a mosaic depicting the death of Mótsog and the end of the Greymaul Rebellion, and he has invited you to admire it. The mosaic is currently in his workshop of Nabgûn-mazaru, but it will be returned to the hall where it came from once his work is finished.","This is the home of Stáli the Hewer, Longbeard artist and sculptor of some renown","The mosaic depicting the death of Mótsog still needs repair, but its subject is clear","Talk to Stáli the Hewer in Nabgûn-mazaru","Examine the mosaic depicting the death of Mótsog","King Thorin Stonehelm has tasked you with going to Nabgûn-mazaru, the home of Stáli the Hewer, south-west of the entrance to the Dwelling-halls of Erebor, and asking him about 'the Greymauls.'","Stáli the Hewer, a Longbeard artist and sculptor of some renown, lives at Nabgûn-mazaru, south-west of the entrance to the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.","Stáli the Hewer, a Longbeard artist and sculptor of some renown, lives south-west of the entrance to the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.","Chapter 1.2: Treachery Remembered","Find Nabgûn-mazaru, the home of Stáli the Hewer, south-west of the entrance to the Dwelling-halls of Erebor","King Thorin Stonehelm is displeased to hear of the situation in the Grey Mountains and worries for his son Durin."}},
[2828]={nameES="Chapter 1.3: Father of the Dwarves",objectivesES={"King Thorin Stonehelm sent you to consult with Stáli the Hewer, a Longbeard artist of some renown who might tell you of the treacherous Greymaul dwarves and their rebellion against Durin the Deathless in the First Age.","Stáli the Hewer is in Nabgûn-mazaru, his workshop and home in the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.","Examine the statue of Durin the Deathless carved by Stáli the Hewer","Talk to Stáli the Hewer in Nabgûn-mazaru","King Thorin is in the Hall Under the Mountain, in Erebor.","Talk to King Thorin in the Hall Under the Mountain, in Erebor","The statue of Durin is quite impressive. Stáli is more skilled than he is modest","Stáli the Hewer has invited you to look at the statue he carved of Durin the Deathless, located in his home and workshop of Nabgûn-mazaru.","Chapter 1.3: Father of the Dwarves"}},
[2829]={nameES="Chapter 1.3: Sighting of the Scourge",objectivesES={"Search for some sign of Balakhôr by the shore south of Arnach, in King's Gondor","Gimli has joined you by the camp-fire south of Arnach, in King's Gondor.","According to Baranor, some folk of Arnach believe Balakhôr survived the fighting at Pelargir and came ashore south of Arnach.","Examine the bag of dirty clothes","Some folk of Gondor whisper that Balakhôr the Scourge survived the war and will yet trouble Elessar's kingdom.","You found the remnants of an old camp... but how old is it, and who made it?","Examine the boat among the reeds not far from the camp-fire","The ash of the burnt timbers has cooled, and no embers remain","The clothes inside this bag are of the style favoured by Corsairs","Talk to Baranor in the centre of Arnach","Legolas stands deep in thought near the abandoned camp-fire south of Arnach, in King's Gondor.","Wild beasts and other dangers to Arnach can be found throughout Lossarnach.","Examine the abandoned camp-fire","Baranor, Captain of the Guardsmen of Arnach, nods in welcome","Baranor stands in the centre of Arnach, in King's Gondor.","Travel to the village of Arnach, south-west of the Harlond, in King's Gondor","Talk to Gimli by the abandoned camp-fire south of Arnach","You found the burnt timbers of an old camp-fire near the shoreline","Legolas believes the three of you should investigate these rumours in the village of Arnach, to the south-west.","Talk to Legolas by the abandoned camp-fire south of Arnach","No longer sea-worthy, this boat served its former occupant well enough","Chapter 1.3: Sighting of the Scourge"}},
[2830]={nameES="Chapter 1.3: Unintentions",objectivesES={"The guard of the vault has been recently attacked","Talk to Annoth in the dungeon of Durthang","The prisoner in this cell is already dead, and beyond rescue","The guard of the vault of Durthang was attacked by Ayorzén when the Easterling escaped.","Talk to the Vault-guard","Ayorzén fled from the dungeon, but he headed deeper into the fortress of Durthang. Where is he going?\
\
Annoth volunteered to search the western side of the fortress, which leaves the north-eastern corner for you.","You have freed a number of prisoners from their cells in the dungeon of Durthang.","The fortress of Durthang is in southern Udûn.","Open cell doors in the dungeon of Durthang (2/3)","Talk to Annoth outside Durthang","Find Ayorzén in the north-eastern section of Durthang","Annoth believes that the downfall of Sauron is a sign that the time for the vengeance of the Thandrim has come at last, and he wants to recapture the fortress of Durthang.","Chapter 1.3: Unintentions","The dungeon of Durthang is in the south-eastern corner of the fortress.","Annoth is outside the fortress of Durthang, in southern Udûn."}},
[2831]={nameES="Chapter 1.4: Ayorzén, Twice-Imprisoned",objectivesES={"Annoth has come to the Isenmouthe in search of Ayorzén.","Bring the corrupted heirloom to Mithrandir, just inside the ruined Black Gate","Annoth believes Ayorzén will try to pass through the Isenmouthe, the gate in Carach Angren that bars passage between Udûn and Dor Amarth.","Many foes occupy the Isenmouthe. Did Ayorzén come this way?","Show the message you recovered to Annoth near the Isenmouthe <rgb=#00FF00>(The message can be read from your inventory)</rgb>","Mithrandir is just inside the ruined Black Gate, in Cirith Gorgor.","Chapter 1.4: Ayorzén, Twice-Imprisoned","There is no sign of Ayorzén. If he came here, he is gone now","Talk to Annoth by the road south of the Easterling encampment in Udûn","You should search the Easterling camp of Rhûd Vorn for any sign of Ayorzén.","Talk to Ayorzén the Wily by the side of the road in Udûn","Defeat Easterlings at Rhûd Vorn, in Udûn (5/6)","Find the Isenmouthe, the gate between Udûn and Dor Amarth","Many foes hold the Isenmouthe.","Ayorzén may have gone to Rhûd Vorn, an Easterling camp in Udûn. You should defeat its warriors while you search for him.","Wait, is that...? Have you found Ayorzén?","You have found Ayorzén. He is sitting with his back against a rock by the side of the road, south of the Easterling encampment in Udûn.","Annoth was going to follow you to the Easterling camp. Walk down the slope south of the Easterling camp and tell him there was no sign of Ayorzén.","Many foes hold the gate of Isenmouthe.","Annoth is south of the Easterling encampment in Udûn, where Ayorzén waited for you.","You find a crumpled paper covered in a crude scrawl","Ayorzén the Wily fled from Durthang, but not before he stole an artifact of some kind from the fortress vault.","Ayorzén gives you the heirloom he stole from Durthang; it has an unpleasant aura about it","Find Annoth along the road south of Rhûd Vorn","Defeat enemies near the Isenmouthe (4/5)"}},
[2832]={nameES="Chapter 1.4: Survivors of the Orc Wars",objectivesES={"Chapter 1.4: Survivors of the Orc Wars","Reithvald Red-ember still burns for battle!","Talk to Lági Helmbiter and measure his combat prowess","Talk to Reithvald Red-ember and measure his combat prowess","Talk to Agnar Brokentooth and measure his combat prowess","Agnar Brokentooth proved too much for you!","Lági Helmbiter proved too much for you!","The passage of years has not slowed Lági Helmbiter one bit!","King Thorin Stonehelm is at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain, in Erebor.","King Thorin Stonehelm has ordered a great force of Longbeard warriors to go with you to reinforce Durin in the Grey Mountains, but first he wants you to test the mettle of some of the eldest.","Reithvald Red-ember proved too much for you!","Agnar Brokentooth remains as eager for battle as ever!","King Thorin Stonehelm asked you to test the combat readiness of three survivors of the Sixth War of Dwarves and Orcs, which occurred more than two hundred and twenty years ago. These three heroes can be found in the passages leading to the Dwelling-halls and the New-lodes, in Erebor.","Talk to King Thorin in the Hall Under the Mountain, in Erebor"}},
[2833]={nameES="Chapter 1.4: The Legacy Lives On",objectivesES={"Listen to Glassiel speak of the Five Sisters","Travel to the town of Halach in King's Gondor","Legolas sits on a bench by the entrance to Glaniath, in King's Gondor.","Breglang, a sailor at Halach, has called for your attention.","Glassiel stands inside the entrance to Halach.","It is time for you to meet up with Legolas and Gimli in the town of Glaniath, to the north-west.","Glassiel speaks to you of the Five Sisters of Lebennin.","Glassiel has arrived safely at her home of Halach","Legolas stands at the Crossings of Erui, in King's Gondor.","Legolas is concerned that the legacy of Balakhôr the Scourge may still threaten King's Gondor.","Return to Breglang in the town of Halach, in King's Gondor","Legolas and Gimli greet you warmly as you arrive in Glaniath","Talk to Legolas by the entrance to Glaniath, in King's Gondor","Travel to the Crossings of Erui, south-west of Arnach, in King's Gondor","Talk to Legolas at the Crossings of Erui, in King's Gondor","The Crossings of Erui are located to the south-west of the village of Arnach, in King's Gondor.","Glassiel is at the Crossings of Erui, in King's Gondor.","Talk to Baranor in the centre of Arnach","Baranor is the Captain of the Guardsmen of Arnach, north of the abandoned camp-site in King's Gondor.","Breglang is in the town of Halach, waiting for you to return from your errands.","Talk to Glassiel at the Crossings of Erui, in King's Gondor","Talk to Gimli at the Crossings of Erui, in King's Gondor","Talk to Glassiel in her home-town of Halach","You agreed to aid the folk of Lebennin by defeating foes between the Crossings of Erui and Halach.","Legolas and Gimli planned to meet up with you in the town of Glaniath","The woman Glassiel floats offerings on the river Erui","At the Crossings of Erui you encountered the woman Glassiel, floating baskets on the river.","A sailor standing nearby calls for your attention","Travel to the town of Glaniath, north-west of Halach in King's Gondor","Fishing nets can be drawn in along the docks of Halach.","Gimli stands at the Crossings of Erui, in King's Gondor.","Chapter 1.4: The Legacy Lives On","Talk to Breglang in Halach","You agreed to make safe the lands between the Crossings of Erui and Glassiel's home of Halach, in King's Gondor. Now you should ensure she arrived safely."}},
[2834]={nameES="Chapter 1.5: An Echo in the Mountains",objectivesES={"Glóin stands near the stable-master at Skarháld, pleased to see the Longbeard reinforcements from the Lonely Mountain.","<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel to Skarháld with a large force of Longbeards when you accept this quest.</rgb>\
\
'Go now to the mountain-fortress where waits my son! Bring him this mighty force, and tell him his father knows he will bring glory for the Longbeards for so long as there is glory there to be had!'","Return to Skarháld with the Longbeard force","Mírkuz eyes the Longbeard force with great suspicion.","Talk to Glóin and go with him to search for Durin","Glóin's brow creases in thought and with worry","A warrior of the Zhélruka eyes the large Longbeard force with suspicion","Durin has returned to Skarháld with renewed purpose, his eyes alight with hopeful flame.","King Thorin has asked you to return to Skarháld with the great force of Longbeards he commanded to reinforce his son Durin.","Talk to Durin by the stable-master in Skarháld","Talk to Glóin by the stable-master in Skarháld","Glóin stands near the stable-master at Skarháld. He is worried that Durin left the fortress some time ago and has not returned.","Talk to Mírkuz at Skarháld","King Thorin Stonehelm has commanded a large force of Longbeards to travel with you to reinforce his son Durin in the Grey Mountains.","Chapter 1.5: An Echo in the Mountains"}},
[2835]={nameES="Chapter 1.5: The Air of That Place",objectivesES={"Find the foundries of Anglach","Mithrandir has asked you to aid soldiers who might have run afoul of the choking fumes that belch from the mines and foundries of Anglach, in Udûn.","Mithrandir is outside the Black Gate.","Talk to Belaith at Anglach","Chapter 1.5: The Air of That Place","Bring the treasure you collected to Belaith, at Anglach","Ayorzén sits near Mithrandir outside the Black Gate.","Belaith leads a group of adventurers seeking treasure in at Anglach, in Udûn.","Talk to Ayorzén outside the Black Gate","The foundries of Anglach have filled the air with choking fumes","The foundries and mines of Anglach are in north-eastern Udûn.","Talk to Mithrandir outside the Black Gate","Belaith asked you to delve into the mines below Anglach in search of treasure and refused to return to the Black Gate with his men until you have brought him some.","Ayorzén, sitting nearby, laughs coldly","Adventurers affected by the choking fumes can be found at the foundries of Anglach, in north-eastern Udûn."}},
[2836]={nameES="Chapter 1.5: The Lord of Lebennin",objectivesES={"Sirgon has come to a decision, and is ready to speak with you.","Meet Sirgon in his room of keepsakes, to the north","Talk to Gimli by the entrance to Glaniath, in King's Gondor","The port city of Pelargir is to the south-west of Glaniath, in King's Gondor.","Sirgon's son Faltharan has joined you in the room of keepsakes","Enter Sirgon's Manor in Pelargir and find its lord","Talk to Faltharan inside Sirgon's room of keepsakes","Chapter 1.5: The Lord of Lebennin","Travel to the eastern entrance of Pelargir, south-west of Glaniath, in King's Gondor","Arvellon is in the centre of Glaniath, and Legolas believes you should speak with him.","Captain Thandor is in the square by the eastern entrance to Pelargir, in King's Gondor.","Gimli is by the entrance to Glaniath.","Faltharan stands within his father's room of keepsakes.","Talk to Captain Thandor by the eastern entrance to Pelargir","Sirgon's Manor is located down the street to the west of the north-east entrance of Pelargir, in King's Gondor.","Wait for Sirgon to speak","Talk to Sirgon in his manor","Talk to Sirgon inside his room of keepsakes","Captain Thandor hails you in greeting","Sirgon rests on a bench inside his manor, thinking about the tidings you brought to him.","Talk to Sirgon inside his manor","Arvellon is in the centre of Glaniath, waiting for you to return with the tokens cast in support of his proposal.","Sirgon has asked to meet you in his room of keepsakes, to the north, where he will speak with you further.","Sirgon stands in his room of keepsakes, appraising his treasured memories.","Talk to Arvellon in the centre of Glaniath, in King's Gondor","Sirgon has suggested that you examine the keepsakes he acquired over a long life at sea.","Sirgon appears to have come to a decision","Sirgon rests on a bench inside the entrance to his manor.","Sirgon considers the treasured memories in his room of keepsakes.","Examine Sirgon's keepsakes and listen to what he has to say about them","Talk to Sirgon in his room of keepsakes","Legolas and Gimli wish to return soon to Minas Tirith with word of what you discovered, but first they wish to consult with Sirgon, Lord of Lebennin.","Collection boxes can be found beside stone buildings on the outskirts of Glaniath.\
\
Arvellon asked you to gather the tokens cast by townspeople of Glaniath in support of his proposal.","Sirgon nods at you as you approach"}},
[2837]={nameES="Chapter 1.6: A Proud, But Dangerous, Tradition",objectivesES={"You hear a horn blowing in the distance east of Skarháld, but it ends abruptly","One of the Zhélruka hunting parties went to the east of Skarháld.","Collect weapons from the eastern armoury inside the Skarháld keep","This armoury has also been emptied of weapons. Tomókh calls you to him","The armoury has been picked clean of weapons by persons unknown","You found the second Zhélruka hunting-party, but they are already slain","Find the second Zhélruka hunting-party somewhere to the north-east","Talk to Tomókh in the eastern armoury inside the Skarháld keep","One of the Zhélruka hunting parties went east of Skarháld.","Return the \\qborrowed\\q weapons to Durin at the stable-master in Skarháld","Talk to the Zhélruka drake-hunter east of Skarháld","Durin is waiting by the stable-master in Skarháld for you to return with the weapons the Zhélruka \\qborrowed.\\q","Durin is waiting by the Skarháld stable-master for you to return with weapons from the armouries.","The Zhélruka cheer the victory","Reinvigourated by the arrival of the Longbeard reinforcements from the Lonely Mountain, Durin wishes to prepare for an assault upon Gundabad, the Mountain-home of Durin's Folk.","Talk to Durin by the stable-master in Skarháld","The first armoury was empty of weapons. Perhaps some implements of war remain in the other armoury on the eastern side of the Skarháld keep.","Find the Zhélruka hunting party east of Skarháld and help them slay a drake of the Frost-horde","The western armoury is up the stairs inside the Skarháld keep.","Chapter 1.6: A Proud, But Dangerous, Tradition","The second Zhélruka hunting-party continued their hunt to the north-east of the first.","Collect weapons from the western armoury up the stairs inside the Skarháld keep","Tomókh has called for your attention inside the eastern armoury inside the Skarháld keep.","The second Zhélruka hunting-party ran afoul of the drakes they sought, and now you should collect the weapons they took from Skarháld."}},
[2838]={nameES="Chapter 1.6: True Hearts and Proven Loyalties",objectivesES={"The Armour of the Usurper remains where it was left","Faltharan agrees that the Heirs of Castamir might try to steal the Armour of the Usurper, but believes the relic is safe.","Convince Legolas that you are truly <rgb=#00FF00>angry</rgb>","The suspicious onlooker is to the south-east of the Pelargir Armoury, in King's Gondor.","Talk to Legolas outside the Pelargir Armoury","Legolas stands outside the Pelargir Armoury, pretending to be angry with you.","Legolas stares at you with his eyes aflame and his fists clenched. He needs your help to show that you are truly <rgb=#00FF00>angry</rgb>.\
\
You will be most convincing if you target the Elf and use the <rgb=#00FF00>Angry</rgb> emote.","Chapter 1.6: True Hearts and Proven Loyalties","Legolas has had an idea.","Cuguril invited you to check on the Armour of the Usurper inside the Pelargir Armoury, as long as you also deal with any of the pests you might find inside.","Cuguril stands watch outside the Pelargir Armoury.","The Pelargir Armoury is to the south of Sirgon's Manor.","Walk by the suspicious onlooker to the south-east and see if she speaks to you","Find the Pelargir Armoury south of Sirgon's Manor, in King's Gondor","Check that the Armour of the Usurper remains inside the Pelargir Armoury","Talk to Aithil south-east of the Pelargir Armoury, in King's Gondor","The armoury is watched day and night by a rotating shift of guards","Legolas has begun a dramatic argument for the benefit of the nearby onlooker, and he needs your help to show that you are truly <rgb=#00FF00>angry</rgb>.\
\
You will be most convincing if you target the Elf and use the <rgb=#00FF00>Angry</rgb> emote.","Talk to Cuguril outside the Pelargir Armoury","The guardswoman Cuguril stands watch outside the Pelargir Armoury.","The woman eyes you curiously","The woman Aithil is south-east of the Pelargir Armoury, in King's Gondor."}},
[2839]={nameES="Chapter 1.6: Whispers from the Other Side",objectivesES={"Talk to Arâm at the Black Gate","You should tell Ayorzén that he will have a place in Gondor","Mithrandir is outside the Black Gate.","Ayorzén has given you the names of especial terrors in Mordor, and wants you to speak those names to some of the freed Nurnhoth at the Black Gate.","Itli shudders when you ask him about Dulgabêth and clenches his fists.\
\
'I can tell you nothing of him that a dozen others could not. He was the Mouth of Sauron, and his knights rode at his command. They plucked me from my village by the Sea and marched me long leagues to Udûn, where I was put to work at the forges. I only saw the Mouth once, from afar, for he was too busy with Sauron's errands to spend time tormenting the Nurnhoth.\
\
'But Sauron is gone, and if the Mouth had a leash, it is now off him. We should not... we should not be speaking of him here, so close to Mordor. It will bring ill fortune. Speak no more to me of him!'","Aragorn is outside the Black Gate.","Talk to Hujâ at the Black Gate","Chapter 1.6: Whispers from the Other Side","The waggon-driver Rathnor can be found near the Black Gate.","Talk to Ayorzén outside the Black Gate","Talk to Rathnor the waggon-driver","Talk to Itli at the Black Gate","Talk to Aragorn outside the Black Gate","Arâm stares at you coldly.\
\
'You should not speak of Urudanî. They say if you speak her name, she hears it and will come. Her kiss is death, her embrace torment. Have we not suffered enough? Let the Stonemaiden slumber, and awaken her not!'","Ayorzén is outside the Black Gate.","Talk to Mithrandir outside the Black Gate","Mithrandir believes that Ayorzén's knowledge of Mordor might be made useful by those who adventure within its bounds.","Hujâ stares at you with wide eyes, and when he speaks it is no more than a whisper.\
\
'Ugrukhôr... he is the Captain of the Pit. He knows no mercy. He delights in death.'\
\
Tears well in his eyes as he speaks.\
\
'His face... terribly scarred... but not always! They say Sauron punished him... punished him for something. Held him... held him to the Fire!'\
\
Hujâ falls silent and will speak no more, but his trembling persists for some time."}},
[2840]={nameES="Chapter 1.7: Castamir's Shadow",objectivesES={"<rgb=#00FF00>Agree</rgb> with Aithil to preserve your deception","Travel to Amon Anglebed, the beacon outside Ost Anglebed, in King's Gondor","The man raises an eyebrow and stares at you appraisingly","Faltharan told you that Amon Anglebed has been kept burning, and may be the beacon about which the skulking woman spoke.","Aithil nods, smiling discreetly","The beacon remains lit, as Faltharan suspected","Chapter 1.7: Castamir's Shadow","Faltharan is inside his father's manor.","Talk to Maethon by the lit beacon, in King's Gondor","A man stands by the beacon. Perhaps he is the contact about whom you were told, and if you <rgb=#00FF00>agree</rgb> with him he will reveal himself.","Convinced by your argument with Legolas, the woman Aithil has welcomed you as a supporter of the Heirs of Castamir.","Sirgon's Manor is located to the north of the Pelargir Armoury, in King's Gondor.","Return to Sirgon's Manor with what you have learned","Legolas and Gimli have come to Sirgon's Manor to await your tidings.","Talk to Legolas inside Sirgon's Manor","<rgb=#00FF00>Agree</rgb> with the man and determine his loyalties","Maethon stands by the burning beacon of Amon Anglebed, in King's Gondor.","Talk to Gimli inside Sirgon's Manor","Talk to Faltharan in his father's manor","The woman Aithil, south-east of the Pelargir Armoury, is convinced that you <rgb=#00FF00>agree</rgb> with the Heirs of Castamir. You should ensure she continues to believe it."}},
[2841]={nameES="Chapter 1.7: Close Quarters",objectivesES={"The ale-keg ran dry after filling two of the mugs, and now you need to find another keg or risk making the dwarves' quarrel worse instead of better!","A keg of ale stands south of the quarrelling dwarves in Skarháld. You have gathered four (mostly) clean mugs and should now fill them from an ale-keg.","Find Imák and calm him down","Chapter 1.7: Close Quarters","Fill mugs of ale from another ale-keg (2/4)","You remember seeing a keg of ale and clean mugs on this level of Skarháld","Fill mugs of ale from the ale-keg south of the quarrelling dwarves (1/4)","After filling the second mug, the ale-keg runs dry!","Heilar dusts himself off and scowls at Imák","Talk to Imák","Imák the Stout-axe still glowers at Heilar the Longbeard. Durin asked you to ease the tensions among these dwarves, if such a thing is possible.","Bring the mugs of ale to the quarrelling dwarves in the north-west corner","Help Heilar to his feet and find out what happened","Tensions run high as Stout-axes, Zhélruka, and Longbeards quarrel at Skarháld. Durin tasked you with easing these tensions, if such a thing is possible.","Talk to Heilar","You fill one of the mugs with ale","You pass out the mugs of ale, and the dwarves set aside their differences (for now)","Find Gílpi and calm him down","Talk to Durin by the stable-master in Skarháld","Fill mugs of ale from another ale-keg (3/4)","You found another ale-keg in Skarháld and can now fill the last of the mugs you collected.","The quarrelling dwarves are two levels up from the stable-master at Skarháld, in the north-west corner, waiting for you to return with the mugs of ale you promised.","Tensions run high as Stout-axes, Zhélruka, and Longbeards quarrel at Skarháld.","Talk to Venko","In order to help ease the tensions among the quarrelling dwarves, you have decided to fetch four clean mugs and fill them with ale from one of the kegs at Skarháld.","The brawling dwarves can be found to the north-west and up two levels from the stable-master in Skarháld.","Happily, this ale-keg is nearly full and you are able to pour a third mug","Fill mugs of ale from the ale-keg south of the quarrelling dwarves (0/4)","A keg of ale stands south of the quarrelling dwarves in Skarháld. You have gathered four (mostly) clean mugs and should now fill them from the ale-keg.","You fill the last of your mugs from the ale-keg","Durin is waiting by the stable-master in Skarháld for you to return.","The arrival of the large Longbeard force has escalated the tensions between the dwarf-clans at Skarháld, and Durin has asked you to try and resolve the brewing conflict."}},
[2842]={nameES="Chapter 1.8: A Watchful Eye",objectivesES={"Imák and Venko can be found two levels up from the stable-master in Skarháld, in the north-west corner.","Bring the supplies to Glóin by the stable-master at Skarháld","Talk to Glóin by the path leading into Misthallow","Talk to Imák of the Stout-axes in Skarháld","Durin's scouts have reported the presence of a raiding-party from Gundabad near the Wells of Langflood, and he thinks he may have found a solution to more than one of the problems that troubles him.","Chapter 1.8: A Watchful Eye","You have met up with your travelling companions near the pass to the Wells of Langflood","Glóin is by the stable-master in Skarháld.","A bag of foodstuffs can be found two levels above the Skarháld stable-master.\
Climbing gear can be found three levels above the Skarháld stable-master\
Flint and camping supplies can be found two levels above the Skarháld stable-master.","Glóin has made it known he wishes to speak with you and Durin at the stable-master in Skarháld.","Talk to Durin by the stable-master in Skarháld","The way to the Wells of Langflood from the Grey Mountains is west of Skarháld, accessible by a narrow pass in the southern cliffs east of the broken Rushgate.","Collected the bag of climbing gear","Imák of the Stout-axes is in the north-west corner, two levels up from the stable-master in Skarháld.","Talk to Glóin by the stable-master in Skarháld","Imák and Venko stop drinking as you approach","Venko of the Zhélruka is in the north-west corner, two levels up from the stable-master in Skarháld.","Glóin is at the entrance to the pass that leads to the Wells of Langflood from the Grey Mountains, east and south of the broken Rushgate.","Return to Imák and Venko in the north-west corner, two levels up from the Skarháld stable-master","Find your travelling companions to the west of Skarháld, at the pass to the Wells of Langflood east and south of the broken Rushgate","Talk to Venko of the Zhélruka in Skarháld","Collect the bag of camping gear in Skarháld, two levels up","Durin is by the stable-master in Skarháld.","Collected the bag of camping gear","Collect the bag of climbing gear in Skarháld, three levels up","Collect the bag of foodstuffs in Skarháld, two levels up","Durin is waiting by the Skarháld stable-master to hear that Imák and Venko will go in search of the raiding-party in the Wells of Langflood.","Collected the bag of foodstuffs"}},
[2843]={nameES="Chapter 1.8: The Imposter",objectivesES={"Residents of Ost Anglebed can be found throughout the city if you wish to hand out the parchments, <rgb=#00FF00>or</rgb> you can burn Maethon's parchments in the nearby brazier.","Pick up <rgb=#00FF00>either</rgb> of the barrels north of the fountain and carry it to Maethon, below the cliffs south of the eastern entrance to the city","Wait for Maethon to leave before you begin his errand","Chapter 1.8: The Imposter","Ladben asked you to bring the container of beacon oil to Halwen for safekeeping. Halwen keeps watch over the supplies near the north-east fountain in Ost Anglebed.","Pick up the beacon oil at Amon Anglebed","Talk to Halwen by the supplies near the north-east fountain in Ost Anglebed","Collect Maethon's parchments from the crate outside the Hall of Ost Anglebed","After you deliver the beacon oil, you hear someone whispering your name","Return to Maethon at the lit beacon of Amon Anglebed","A guardsman of Ost Anglebed, Ladben, stands by the lit beacon.","Maethon is missing. In his place stands a guard of Ost Anglebed","Maethon admires the high quality weapons you have brought for the Heirs of Castamir","Talk to Maethon below the cliff south of the eastern entrance of Ost Anglebed","Maethon sees the rusty implements and shrugs. 'Better than nothing!' he says","Halwen believed your story that Ladben needs a barrel of weapons, and she told you to take one from the other side of the fountain. She warned you that there is a barrel of rusty weapons there as well, so be careful not to bring Ladben weapons of poor quality.","Eager to make use of the help you have offered, Maethon has a number of tasks for you to complete on behalf of the Heirs of Castamir.","Maethon stashed a number of parchments to distribute on behalf of the Heirs of Castamir in a crate outside the Hall of Ost Anglebed, to the north-east.","Distribute Maethon's parchments in support of the Heirs of Castamir to residents of Ost Anglebed, or burn the parchments in the nearby brazier","Talk to Maethon by the stairs","Maethon stands below the cliff south of the eastern entrance to Ost Anglebed.","Maethon stands beside the stairs to the Hall of Ost Anglebed, calling for you in hushed tones.","Talk to Ladben at the lit beacon of Amon Anglebed","Maethon makes himself scarce so you can accomplish his goal.","Residents of Ost Anglebed can be found throughout the city if you wish to hand out the parchments, or you can burn Maethon's parchments in the nearby brazier.","Halwen stands by the supplies near the north-east fountain in Ost Anglebed.","Maethon's parchments quickly turn to ash in the heat of the brazier","Maethon will want to hear about your efforts on behalf of the Heirs of Castamir. He should still be at the lit beacon of Amon Anglebed.","Distribute Maethon's parchments in support of the Heirs of Castamir to residents of Ost Anglebed, <rgb=#00FF00>or</rgb> burn the parchments in the nearby brazier"}},
[2844]={nameES="Chapter 1.9: Kindred Spirits",objectivesES={"Enter the building by the fountain in the northern half of Linhir and attend the meeting","You should find a gossipmonger in Linhir and learn if Elessar has left Minas Tirith","This is the building Maethon described","You should enter the building by the fountain in the northern half of Linhir and attend the meeting.","Talk to the gossipmonger inside the eastern entrance to Linhir","Maethon described the location where the supporters of the Heirs of Castamir intend to meet. It is a dwelling in the northern half of the city of Linhir, opposite a fountain and with a bronze door.","Talk to Nakási outside Linhir","Find the entrance to the dwelling in the northern half of Linhir where supporters of the Heirs of Castamir intend to meet","The Linhir gossipmonger has news, and can be found just inside the eastern entrance to Linhir, in King's Gondor.","Chapter 1.9: Kindred Spirits","Maethon told you supporters of the Heirs of Castamir are to meet soon in a secret place in Linhir, and he invited you to attend. This may be a chance to learn more of their plans!","Nakási is outside Linhir, south of the eastern entrance."}},
[2845]={nameES="Chapter 10.10: The Moon Over Ambarûl",objectivesES={}},
[2846]={nameES="Chapter 10.11: The Lessons of Memory",objectivesES={"Bring the scorpion stingers to Girhâzi in Iridír","Join Khôltekh outside the brigand camp of Bidrokh-nûn","Talk to Sigileth in Iridír","Only at this bridge may the Ikorbân River be safely crossed, lending it much importance","Girhâzi's trust is not easily gained, for she and her people have long memories.","Girhâzi gave a number of tasks to your travelling companions for them to complete in order to earn the trust of her people, and to learn valuable information that will benefit your own mission in Ambarûl.","Scout the road from Ambarûl to Urash Dâr, south-east of Iridír","Your companions have been given a number of places to scout and enemies to defeat there: at the eastern side of the Wrackwade in the camp of Sûru, an Ordâkhai camp at Eshadur across the river, a brigand camp to the south-east, and the road to Urash Dâr.","Eshadur has been occupied by the Ordâkhai, and they prepare for war","Chapter 10.11: The Lessons of Memory","Recent quakes have blocked the road to Urash Dâr","Brigands established camps along the path that climbs the rocky slope","Talk to Rothog in Iridír","Talk to Khôltekh in Iridír","Girhâzi waits for your successful return in Iridír.","Join Rothog outside the Ordâkhai camp at Eshadur","Talk to Belondor in Iridír","Talk to Corudan in Iridír","Scout the eastern side of the Wrackwade in the camp of Sûru to the south"}},
[2847]={nameES="Chapter 10.12: The Short Road and the Long",objectivesES={"Sigileth refuses the gift","Offer a pillow to Khôltekh","Chapter 10.12: The Short Road and the Long","Your task complete, you can now rest for the night in the village of Iridír. Sleeping mats for this purpose can be found on the western side of the lodge.","Prepare your sleeping mat on the western side of the lodge in the village of Iridír","Your own sleep disturbed by troubled dreams, you hope that your companions are feeling more rested than you. They can be found at the entrance of Iridír to the north of the lodge.","Offer a pillow to Rothog","Offer a pillow to Corudan","Rothog refuses the gift","Rahâzi gives you a number of pillows to distribute among your companions","You awaken from disturbing dreams, the memory of them fading into nothingness","Rahâzi is on the eastern side of her mother's lodge in Iridír.","Your sleeping mat awaits on the western side of the lodge in the village of Iridír.","Talk to Sigileth at the entrance of Iridír","You set down the excess pillows and prepare your sleeping mat for the night, making it as comfortable as you can.","Corudan accepts the gift","Your own sleep disturbed by troubling dreams, you hope that your companions are feeling more rested than you. They can be found at the entrance of Iridír to the north of the lodge.","Talk to Rahâzi on the eastern side of the lodge in Iridír","Offer a pillow to Sigileth","Your companions throughout the village of Iridír may welcome the gift of pillows, or they may not.","Rest for the night on your sleeping mat in the lodge within Iridír","Offer a pillow to Belondor","Khôltekh refuses the gift","Girhâzi has agreed to provide you with supplies and assistance as you prepare to take the necessary longer road in pursuit of Azagath.","Talk to Sirgon at the entrance of Iridír","Talk to Corudan at the entrance of Iridír to the north of the lodge","Belondor accepts the gift","You lie down on the sleeping mat and prepare to rest, giving your journey south into Khûd Zagin a good beginning."}},
[2848]={nameES="Chapter 10.1: A New Journey",objectivesES={"Make your way through Eryn Lasgalen to the Forest Gate in the west","Gandalf stands at the Forest Gate on the western edge of Eryn Lasgalen, waiting to speak with you.","Make your way to the entrance of the Beorninghús south-west of the Forest Gate","Talk to Grimbeorn at the Beorninghús","Talk to Gandalf at the Forest Gate in Eryn Lasgalen","The Beorninghús is located in the Beorning-lands, south-west of the Forest Gate.","The Forest Gate stands open, as King Thranduil commanded","King Thranduil is in the throne room of Felegoth, in Eryn Lasgalen.","Gandalf believes that Karazgar will remain a threat to the dwarves at Skarháld for as long as the Black Book remains there, and he wants to bring it on a journey away from the Ered Mithrin.","Durin is on the upper level of Skarháld, waiting to speak with you following Karazgar's defeat.","Grimbeorn stands at the Beorninghús.","Talk to Durin on the upper level of Skarháld","The Forest Gate is located on the western edge of Eryn Lasgalen, along the forest road.","The sound of buzzing bees and sweet smell of clover welcome you to the Beorninghús","Chapter 10.1: A New Journey","Talk to King Thranduil at his throne in Felegoth"}},
[2849]={nameES="Chapter 10.1: Different Roads",objectivesES={"Talk to Nimrodel in the Sail-haven","You send them off with a proud salute","Many of your friends, including the crew of the Wave-hunter, prepare to depart Umbar Baharbêl from the Sail-haven. Jaith told you to find them not far from the Beacon-gate on the west side of the city.","Talk to Legolas in the Sail-haven","The child Thorongil stands by his mother in the Sail-haven in Umbar Baharbêl, east of the Beacon-gate.","Talk to Thorongil in the Sail-haven","Talk to Sirgon in the Sail-haven","With solemn reverence, Nimrodel's chosen bodyguards salute you","The crew of the Wave-hunter, and others of your friends, make ready to leave the city","Talk to Lady Nauriel in the Sail-haven","Find your friends and crew in the Sail-haven, not far from the Beacon-gate on the west side of Umbar Baharbêl","Talk to Gimli in the Sail-haven","Sirgon is not yet prepared to leave Umbar Baharbêl, and wishes to speak with you about the days to come.","Chapter 10.1: Different Roads","You send them off with an understanding wave","Nimrodel's guardians are preparing to depart, and you should acknowledge them with a <rgb=#00FF00>salute</rgb> or a <rgb=#00FF00>wave</rgb>.","Nimrodel stands among your friends in the Sail-haven in Umbar Baharbêl, east of the Beacon-gate.","<rgb=#00FF00>Salute</rgb> or <rgb=#00FF00>Wave</rgb> at your assembled friends","Nauriel shakes her head disapprovingly","The guard outside the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja has received word that some of your friends have made preparations to depart Umbar Baharbêl.","Legolas stands ready to depart for Gondor on a merchant vessel leaving Umbar Baharbêl.","You send them off with a particularly flashy salute","Gimli stands ready to depart for Gondor on a merchant vessel leaving Umbar Baharbêl.","Lady Nauriel of Pinnath Gelin stands in the Sail-haven in Umbar Baharbêl, east of the Beacon-gate."}},
[2850]={nameES="Chapter 10.1: Fitting the Pieces",objectivesES={"A number of Longbeards stand in Zul-mazal, studying the broken mosaic and the curious stone block in the centre of the chamber.","Talk to Durin in Zul-mazal","Return to Zul-mazal by the upper crypts on the western side of the Pit of Stonejaws","Zul-mazal is by the upper crypts on the western side of the Pit of Stonejaws.","Talk to Bróin in Zul-mazal","Chapter 10.1: Fitting the Pieces","With the mithril hammer in his possession, Prince Durin is interested to learn from where it came, and what significance it might hold for his conquest of the Mountain-home.","Talk to Stáli the Hewer in Zul-mazal","Durin stands in Zul-mazal, deep in thought.","Talk to Fastrith in Zul-mazal"}},
[2851]={nameES="Chapter 10.2: The Mystery of Zul-mazal",objectivesES={"Durin stands beside a secret stair deep beneath Gundabad, marvelling at the long-hidden passage.","Durin believes that Zul-mazal holds some secret, and he is determined to learn what it may be.","Durin is in Zul-mazal, determined to unravel whatever mystery lies within the curious chamber's walls.","Talk to Durin deep beneath Gundabad","Chapter 10.2: The Mystery of Zul-mazal","Talk to Durin and help him uncover the secret of Zul-mazal"}},
[2852]={nameES="Chapter 10.2: The Next Move",objectivesES={"Talk to Sigileth in the Sail-haven","Sirgon is waiting in the Sail-haven east of the Beacon-gate to go with you to meet with the Kindred of the Coins.","Talk to Sirgon in the Sail-haven and go with him to meet the Kindred","Corudan and Sigileth are in the Sail-haven, east of the Beacon-gate in Umbar Baharbêl.","Talk to Corudan in the Sail-haven","Belondor has requested that you and Sirgon meet with him and the rest of the Kindred of the Coins in the Citadel of the Winds to discuss your next course of action.","Talk to Sirgon outside the Lords' Gate in the Fleetfast","Sirgon stands in the Fleetfast outside the Lords' Gate, waiting to discuss your meeting with the Kindred of the Coins.","Chapter 10.2: The Next Move"}},
[2853]={nameES="Chapter 10.2: The Price of Lodging",objectivesES={"Bring the useful pieces of flint to Grimbeorn at the Beorninghús","Gandalf wishes to speak with you. The Wizard stands near the entrance to the Beorninghús.","Chapter 10.2: The Price of Lodging","Grimbeorn is at the Beorninghús, in the Beorning-lands.","Grimbeorn has tasked you with a number of errands to undertake in the Beorning-lands, and Gandalf has helpfully doubled the required quantities of each.","Grimbeorn has demanded that if you and Gandalf are to stay at the Beorninghús, you must work for your keep.","Talk to Gandalf at the Beorninghús"}},
[2854]={nameES="Chapter 10.3: Buried Secrets",objectivesES={"Durin believes that none have travelled these secret stairs for an age, but he will not allow that to dissuade him from seeking whatever may lie at the bottom.","You enter a long-forgotten chamber deep below Gundabad","Chapter 10.3: Buried Secrets","The statue of Mótsog has changed. Where once it was worked in grey stone, now the statue is given the colour he might have had in life. So too is there another change: the statue is now shorn of any beard.\
\
Despite its lifelike colour, the statue remains unmoving and bereft of life.","The secret stairs have not been travelled for an age, descending far below Gundabad.\
\
What lies beyond their lowest step?","Durin has asked you to meet him on the stairs outside the long-forgotten chamber.","A statue of Mótsog stands in the long-forgotten chamber.","Descend the secret stairs far below Gundabad and explore the deepest caverns","Wait for Durin to catch up with you","Something about the air feels different. But what?","Return to Durin and learn what has disturbed him","Durin looks around the chamber with wide eyes","Durin runs into the long-forgotten chamber.","Talk to Durin in the long-forgotten chamber","Meet up with Durin at the bottom of the stairs outside","Durin stands in the long-forgotten chamber deep below Gundabad.","Examine the statue of Mótsog","A cool breeze blows past you, and Durin cries out in surprise","This statue of Mótsog is very detailed; someone crafted it with care","Durin stands in the long-forgotten chamber beneath Gundabad."}},
[2855]={nameES="Chapter 10.3: Good Fences",objectivesES={"Talk to Gandalf inside the Beorninghús","Gultheg is at Vegbár, the watch-fort west of the Old Ford in the Wolf-denes.","You have arrived at the village of Hultvís. Adalfon nods in greeting","Grimbeorn is at the Beorninghús, waiting for you to return with the collected tolls from Vegbár.","Talk to Gultheg at Vegbár","You should return to the Beorninghús with the delivery Grimbeorn requested","He hands you a small pouch. Now you should continue to Hultvís","Townsfolk throughout Hultvís will speak to you of the legends that have been passed down among the Woodmen.","Talk to Gelfrida in Hultvís","Talk to Veremund by the cooking fires in Hultvís","Chapter 10.3: Good Fences","Adalfon asked you to help the village of Hultvís recover and rebuild following the recent battle.","You hunted wild harts for the Woodmen of Hultvís, and now Veremund waits by the fires in the village for the meat you obtained.","Gandalf is inside the Beorninghús, studying the Black Book of Mordor within Grimbeorn's lodge.","Veremund is by the cooking fires of Hultvís, waiting for you to return from speaking with the people of the village.","Bring the flanks to Veremund by the cooking fires in Hultvís","Bring the collected tolls to Grimbeorn at the Beorninghús","Adalfon has greeted you at the entrance to the village of Hultvís.","Grimbeorn has another task for you. He wants you to check on the Woodmen, his neighbours to the south, and aid them with their difficulties.","Talk to Mavi in Hultvís","Talk to Adalfon at the entrance to Hultvís","Hultvís is on the eastern side of Woodsedge, in the Vales of Anduin.","Talk to Eurik in Hultvís","Find the entrance to the village of Hultvís, on the eastern side of Woodsedge"}},
[2856]={nameES="Chapter 10.3: Leave The City Behind, Part One",objectivesES={"Chapter 10.3: Leave The City Behind, Part One","Sirgon is by the east gate of Umbar Baharbêl, preparing to depart the city.","Talk to Sirgon by the east gate of Umbar Baharbêl","The leaders of the Kindred await your assistance with their preparations in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja.","Talk to Rothog in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja","Deliver Khôltekh's orders to Ilbidûn at Stonecliff Market in the Lower Ward","Rothog gives you a set of orders to deliver to the arena armourer","Talk to Belondor in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja","Deliver Hármelak's orders to Jakbir at Bith Gabâr, the Forum in the Upper Ward","Talk to Khôltekh in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja","Mêshka is already on the way to see her husband","The leaders of the Kindred of the Coins have a number of preparations to make before your combined pursuit of Azagath Sea-shadow can begin.","The leaders of the Kindred await your assistance in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja.","Deliver Rothog's orders to Mekhamun on the steps of Dahâl Huliz in the Tor-gardens","Talk to Mêshka somewhere within the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja","Khôltekh gives you a set of orders to deliver to the warehouse keeper","Talk to Hármelak in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja","You assure Mekhamun that you do not have the answer to that question","Hármelak gives you a set of orders to deliver to the caravan master","The Kindred of the Coins have given you orders to deliver to a number of people at various locations within the city: Bith Gabâr, the forum in the Upper Ward, at Stonecliff Market in the Lower Ward, and on the steps of Dahâl Huliz, the arena in the Tor-gardens."}},
[2857]={nameES="Chapter 10.4: Scholarly Pursuits",objectivesES={"Bring 'Kanash-tubu-hârra' to Ghâlim at Kên Taghlim in Umbar-môkh","Ghâlim is on a terrace in the Tor-gardens of Umbar Baharbêl.","Caebar is on a terrace west of the Arena in the Tor-gardens of Umbar Baharbêl.","Talk to Ghâlim at Kên Taghlim in Umbar-môkh","Retrieve the book 'Kanash-tubu-hârra' from Harkhaphâr in Kamrabezûr, in Umbar-môkh","Chapter 10.4: Scholarly Pursuits","Find Caebar's teacher Ghâlim at Kên Taghlim in Kamrabezûr, in Umbar-môkh","Ghâlim shakes his head in disapproval","Given that the preparations for your departure will still take some time, Sirgon believes you should learn what you can about the lands of Near Harad into which you must travel.","Ghâlim tucks the book under one arm and leaves by the door to the surface","Caebar will teach you what he knows, but first he needs your help to finish the chores given to him by his instructor: picking berries from bushes down the steps to the east to be used for the making of inks and pigments.","Talk to Ghâlim on the terrace in the Tor-gardens","Talk to Caebar on a terrace west of the Arena in the Tor-gardens of Umbar Baharbêl","Talk to Caebar on the terrace west of the Arena in the Tor-gardens","Caebar is on a terrace west of the Arena in the Tor-gardens of Umbar Baharbêl, waiting for you to return with the pigment berries you picked.","Ghâlim is at Kên Taghlim in Umbar-môkh.","Caebar's teacher, a man named Ghâlim, is at Kên Taghlim in Kamrabezûr, in Umbar-môkh.","Ghâlim has asked you to retrieve the book 'Kanash-tubu-hârra' from Harkhaphâr, far to the south of Kamrabezûr, in Umbar-môkh.","Caebar is on the terrace west of the Arena in the Tor-gardens of Umbar Baharbêl.","You pick up the book 'Kanash-tubu-hârra,' taking care not to damage it","You have found Caebar's teacher Ghâlim","Bring the pigment berries to Caebar on the terrace in the Tor-gardens"}},
[2858]={nameES="Chapter 10.4: The Disaster of the Gladden Fields",objectivesES={"Chapter 10.4: The Disaster of the Gladden Fields","Meet up with Gandalf further north along the road by the Gladden Fields","Despite the warmth of springtime, you feel a chill in the air","Talk to Gandalf on the road north of Duskenvale, near the Gladden Fields","As you survey the terrain, you can almost hear the harsh war-cries of the Orcs","Meet up with Gandalf further east along the road, in Laerlad","Gandalf has called a halt alongside the river-bank. He asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> around you as Isildur must have done when he knew the end was near.","Gandalf has called a halt beside the road by the Gladden Fields.","Gandalf asked to meet you on the road north of Duskenvale, near the Gladden Fields.","Gandalf has called a halt along the wooded road in Laerlad. He asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at the surrounding countryside and consider the landscape Isildur would have seen as he rode north.","Gandalf has called a halt beside the road alongside the Gladden Fields.","Gandalf desires to walk east along the road into Laerlad, where he will speak further on the subject of Isildur's journey north from Gondor.","Gandalf has called a halt along the river-bank in the Gladden Fields.","Gandalf has called a halt alongside the river-bank.","Gandalf indicates that he wishes to stop here beside the road","Talk to Gandalf beside the road","Talk to Gandalf by the wooded road in Laerlad","Gandalf motions for you to stop","Gandalf wants to meet you on the road north of Duskenvale, but first he has asked you to defeat Orcs and half-orcs in the Gladden Fields.","Gandalf desires to walk north along the road beside the Gladden Fields, where he will speak further on the subject of Isildur's journey north from Gondor.","Gandalf has called a halt beside the road by the Gladden Fields. He asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at the surrounding countryside and consider the terrain within which the Orcs attacked Isildur's company.","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> at the surrounding terrain as Gandalf suggested","Gandalf has called a halt along the wooded road in Laerlad.","Gandalf desires to meet you down the slope along the river-bank, further to the north-west.","Talk to Gandalf alongside the river-bank","Meet up with Gandalf by the river-bank, down the slope and to the north-west","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> around you as Gandalf suggested","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> at the countryside nearby as Gandalf suggested","What did Isildur feel as the battle turned against him?","Gandalf looks around at the countryside with satisfaction","Gandalf has run into some difficulty deciphering the mysteries of the Black Book of Mordor, and has decided to walk with you in the Gladden Fields to clear his head."}},
[2859]={nameES="Chapter 10.4: The Dreaming Dwarf",objectivesES={"There is something strange about this chamber and the statue of Mótsog it contains, but Durin has vowed not to rest until he unravels their mysteries.","Talk to Durin in Mótsog's Tomb","Durin contemplates the lifelike statue and the strange chamber in which it stands.","Talk to Durin and unravel the mystery of the long-forgotten chamber","Something about the lifelike visage compels your eye, but the strange enchantment that encircles the statue of Mótsog resists your study. The feeling that you are being watched by an invisible presence grows stronger and more unwelcome.","Durin stands in Mótsog's Tomb, shaken by what he has seen and experienced.","Chapter 10.4: The Dreaming Dwarf"}},
[2860]={nameES="Chapter 10.5: The Greymaul Rebellion",objectivesES={"Mótsog stands in a long-forgotten chamber deep below Gundabad.","Talk to Durin in Mótsog's Tomb","Durin wears an impassive expression as he considers Mótsog.\
\
'These crimes are unforgiveable, and they match my understanding of the Greymaul Rebellion. You deserved the death given to you by my ancestor Durin, to whom you owed fealty.\
\
'You claim you were his friend? You say you speak the truth about the Greymaul Rebellion, but I deem you speak falsely on this: you were no friend of Durin. Nor are you a friend of mine.'","Durin has demanded that Mótsog account for himself, and deny his treachery if he can.","Chapter 10.5: The Greymaul Rebellion","Durin stands in Mótsog's Tomb deep beneath Gundabad.","Talk to Mótsog","Talk to Mótsog and hear his account"}},
[2861]={nameES="Chapter 10.5: The Isle of the Flowers",objectivesES={"Gandalf desires to conclude his tale of the Disaster of the Gladden Fields, where Isildur fell and the Ruling Ring was lost.","Gandalf waits on the island of Tol Send, ready to conclude the story of Isildur and his loss of the Ring.","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> around you on the isle of Tol Send, as Isildur must have done","Chapter 10.5: The Isle of the Flowers","The island is covered in small white flowers","Meet Gandalf on Tol Send, a small island in the Anduin to the west","Gandalf has pointed out an island in the Anduin to the west, declaring that the end of Isildur's story can there be told.","The sound of the water rushing by fills your ears, but all else is quiet","Gandalf asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> around you while standing on the isle of Tol Send, as Isildur must have done after swimming across the river.","Talk to Gandalf on Tol Send"}},
[2862]={nameES="Chapter 10.5: The Lands of Shagâna",objectivesES={"Keeping his eyes upon you, Ghâlim slowly upends the jar. Water spills out onto the ground until the jar is empty.","Caebar wishes to do what he can to help you learn about the lands into which you must travel.","Retrieve a jar of clean water for Ghâlim from the fountain down the stairs to the east of the terrace in the Tor-gardens","Ghâlim stands on the terrace in the Tor-gardens, waiting for you to return with the jar of water he requested.","A jar of clean water can be found down the stairs to the east of the terrace in the Tor-gardens.","Chapter 10.5: The Lands of Shagâna","Ghâlim upends the jar you brought him and spills the water onto the ground","Caebar is on the terrace in the Tor-gardens.","Ghâlim has wasted the clean water you brought to him in service of making a point.","Ghâlim is in the Tor-gardens, instructing you about the lands of Shagâna.","Return to Ghâlim with the jar of clean water","Talk to Caebar on the terrace in the Tor-gardens","Wait for Ghâlim to speak","Talk to Ghâlim on the terrace in the Tor-gardens","You pick up the jar of clean fountain-water","Suitably chastened by the words of his instructor, Caebar wishes to do what he can to help you learn about the lands into which you must travel.","Ghâlim is on the terrace in the Tor-gardens.","Ghâlim has determined that you need some instruction in the geography and history of the land men of Gondor call \\qNear Harad\\q but which the folk who live there call \\qShagâna.\\q"}},
[2863]={nameES="Chapter 10.6: A Request",objectivesES={"Eurik, a hunter from Hultvís, was frightened away from his prey by a terrible apparition at the Old Ford, located in the Wolf-denes north-west of the village.","Adalfon at the village of Hultvís may have a request for you.","Talk to Adalfon at the village of Hultvís","Karazgar stands by the Old Ford. He has declared that he means you no harm, but wishes only to speak with you.","Veremund is by the cooking fires in the village of Hultvís.","Eurik is in the village of Hultvís.","Adalfon asked you to slay forest-harts in Woodsedge for their flanks, in order to help fill the hole left in the town's food-stores.","Chapter 10.6: A Request","Gandalf stands with Elrond outside the Beorninghús.","Talk to Karazgar, but remain alert for treachery","Karazgar stares at you, his eyes filled with malice.","Investigate the terrible apparition Eurik saw at the Old Ford","Talk to Karazgar and learn of his request","Bring the flanks to Veremund by the cooking fires in Hultvís","Gandalf has asked you to return Hultvís, the village of the Woodmen, and lend them whatever assistance they might require.","You have found the apparition Eurik encountered: Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior!","Talk to Eurik in Hultvís","Talk to Gandalf outside the Beorninghús"}},
[2864]={nameES="Chapter 10.6: Leave The City Behind, Part Two",objectivesES={"Talk to Sirgon by the east gate of Umbar Baharbêl","Talk to Rothog in Dâr Laja","Belondor is by the east gate of the city.","Talk to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja","Talk to Belondor in Dâr Laja","With preparations for the journey delayed or otherwise obstructed, the Kindred has suggested that you gather at the east gate of the city and form an advance travelling party.","Talk to Belondor by the east gate of Umbar Baharbêl","You should speak with Hármelak about the status of the preparations. The Golden Queen is inside the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja.","Sirgon is by the east gate of the city.","Once the preparations for your departure have been made, you will be ready to leave the city of Umbar Baharbêl behind and set forth into the lands of Shagâna.","Meet with your companions at the east gate of the city","Chapter 10.6: Leave The City Behind, Part Two","Talk to Hármelak in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja","Hármelak has asked you to speak with the other members of the Kindred of the Coins in Dâr Laja.","The advance travelling party has assembled at the east gate"}},
[2865]={nameES="Chapter 10.6: The Sunder-battle",objectivesES={}},
[2866]={nameES="Chapter 10.7: Beyond Telperiën's Wall",objectivesES={"Bring the fallen stones to Hûta at his guard-post by Telperiën's Wall","Talk to Hûta at his guard-post beside Telperiën's Wall","Journey east to the guard-post beside Telperiën's Wall","Journey to the guard-post east of Umbar Baharbêl","Belondor is at the guard-post beside Telperiën's Wall.","The first step of your journey lies to the east of the city, along the Road of Riches, at the guard-post Belondor suggested.","Talk to Hûta at the guard-post beside Telperiën's Wall","Khashig acknowledges the arrival of your travelling party with a raised eyebrow","Talk to Corudan at the guard-post east of the city","Patrol northward along Telperiën's Wall","You have arrived beside Telperiën's Wall, where Hûta keeps watch","Khashig is at his guard-post east of the city.","Talk to Khashig at the guard-post east of the city","You followed Hûta's suggestion but found nothing out of the ordinary","Chapter 10.7: Beyond Telperiën's Wall","Talk to Rahâzi at the entrance of Iridír","Corudan is at the guard-post east of the city.","The next step of your journey lies further to the east, by the ruins of Telperiën's Wall.","A young woman leaving the village stops in her tracks at the sight of you","Find the west entrance to the village of Iridír, in Ambarûl","Belondor suggests you help Khashig with the sand-flies that trouble him","Sand-flies can be found in the vicinity of Khashig's guard-post, east of Umbar Baharbêl.","Hûta asked you to patrol northward and retrieve stones that have fallen from the wall.","Hûta gave you directions to the village of Iridír in Ambarûl, east of Telperiën's Wall.","Rahâzi stops in her tracks as you seek to enter the village of Iridír.","While Khôltekh and Rothog remain behind to see to the final preparations, your advance company sets forth toward the Valley of Ikorbân in the lands of Shagâna.","Hûta is at his guard-post beside Telperiën's Wall.","Talk to Belondor at the guard-post beside Telperiën's Wall","Talk to Khashig at the guard-post east of Umbar Baharbêl"}},
[2867]={nameES="Chapter 10.7: The Arrival of the Wise",objectivesES={"Grimbeorn is waiting to speak with you about the many new arrivals at his home.","Talk to Gandalf inside the Beorninghús","Talk to Elrond at the Beorninghús","Elrond, Arwen, and Glorfindel have come to the Beorninghús on their journey to Gondor.","Chapter 10.7: The Arrival of the Wise","Elrond and some of his household have made the journey across the Misty Mountains in preparation for his daughter's wedding.","Talk to Glorfindel at the Beorninghús","Gandalf has gone back inside the Beorninghús to study the Black Book of Mordor.","Habla con Grimbeorn","Talk to Arwen at the Beorninghús"}},
[2868]={nameES="Chapter 10.7: The Legacy of Durin",objectivesES={"Talk to Durin in Mótsog's Tomb","Talk to Durin and hear his remembrance","Chapter 10.7: The Legacy of Durin","Mótsog stands in a long-forgotten chamber deep beneath Gundabad.","Talk to Mótsog","Mótsog has finished his account, and he has told you that the conclusion is for someone else to tell.","Durin stands in a long-forgotten chamber beneath Gundabad, clearly confused by the words of Mótsog.","Durin looks at you with realization dawning in his eyes."}},
[2869]={nameES="Chapter 10.8: The Daughters of Iridír",objectivesES={"Rahâzi was sent to the insect den of Gurakhu, north-west of Iridír, and now her mother Girhâzi wants you to help with her assigned task.","Talk to Surdûsha at Gurakhu","Rahâzi has asked you to collect the bristles she was sent to retrieve from the insects at Gurakhu, west of Iridír. In the interest of continued collaboration, you should do what you can to help Girhâzi's daughter.","The distraction writ upon Rahâzi's face is clear to you as you report finishing the task.\
\
'Good enough,' she answers you.\
\
'Surdûsha has brought wondrous tidings to me! Speak to her and hear them!'","A young woman named Rahâzi has directed you to speak with her mother Girhâzi, leader of the village of Iridír in Ambarûl.","Girhâzi watches you carefully as you approach","Rahâzi is at Gurakhu, north-west of Iridír, waiting for you to return to her with her task complete.","Talk to Girhâzi inside her lodge within Iridír","Girhâzi is inside her lodge within the village of Iridír, in Ambarûl.","Talk to Rahâzi at the insect den of Gurakhu, north-west of Iridír","Girhâzi is inside her lodge in the village of Iridír, in Ambarûl.","Talk to Rahâzi at Gurakhu","Rahâzi is at Gurakhu in Ambarûl.","Rahâzi runs into the wild, leaving you to speak to her mother Girhâzi.","Belondor is in Girhâzi's lodge within the village of Iridír.","Wait for Rahâzi to depart the village","Talk to Belondor inside Girhâzi's lodge within Iridír","Find Girhâzi within the lodge inside the village of Iridír","According to Rahâzi, her mother Girhâzi will be interested in speaking with you within her lodge to the south.","Rahâzi's fellow Dumûri warrior, Surdûsha, is at Gurakhu, north-west of Iridír.","Chapter 10.8: The Daughters of Iridír","Bring the zizanu bristles to Rahâzi at Gurakhu"}},
[2870]={nameES="Chapter 10.9: Hunting the Remnants",objectivesES={"Talk to Surdûsha outside Omboha","Surdûsha told you that Rahâzi pursued fleeing Ordâkhai warriors to the north.","Pick up the weapon of the slain Ordâkhai","Chapter 10.9: Hunting the Remnants","The Elf-warden Shanthar stands within the grove of Arwáth.","An Elf-warden stands watch within the grove of Arwáth","On the body of the slain warrior you find a token of the Church of the All-seeing","Shanthar suggested that you <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> for the faded Kintai in the grove of Arwáth.","Rahâzi is on the outskirts of the grove of Arwáth.","Talk to Shanthar at Arwáth","Rahâzi is eager to hunt down and defeat the Ordâkhai who remain in Ambarûl to threaten her people.","As you approach, you see that Rahâzi defeated the warriors she pursued","You hear the rustling of leaves and feel a light breeze on your skin, but that is all","The weapon bears sign of use in many battles, but the blood on the blade is dry","Find Rahâzi to the north of Omboha","Talk to Rahâzi outside the grove of Arwáth","Outside the grove of Arwáth, Rahâzi asked you to search her foes for signs of their purpose in Ambarûl.","Rahâzi believes you should venture within the grove of Arwáth and ensure that no Ordâkhai hide within.","Ordâkhai remnants gather at a war-camp to the north-east of Iridír, in Ambarûl.","Find the camp of the Ordâkhai to the north-east of Iridír","Rahâzi is interested to examine the items you collected from the body of her foe.","<rgb=#00FF00>Listen</rgb> for the faded Kintai in the grove of Arwáth","Surdûsha keeps a watchful eye on Omboha.","Rahâzi pursued the Ordâkhai to the outskirts of the grove of Arwáth.","Venture within the grove of Arwáth to the north","Search the body of the slain Ordâkhai warrior outside Arwáth","Stand in the grove of Arwáth beside one of the trees with red leaves","Ordâkhai remnants gather at Omboha, north-east of Iridír","Present the items you found to Rahâzi outside the grove of Arwáth"}},
[2871]={nameES="Chapter 10: Blood-marks",objectivesES={"Wadu is at Echad Dagoras, the camp of the Grey Company in Fordirith, Enedwaith.\
\
You have collected blood-marks and weapons from fallen Uch-lûth and should bring them to Wadu as he requested.","Wadu has expressed his displeasure at the slaying of his kin by other Dunlending clans and wants you to fight on his behalf.","Talk to Lothrandir at Echad Dagoras","Bring blood-marks and Dunlending weapons to Wadu at Echad Dagoras","Chapter 10: Blood-marks","Lothrandir is at Echad Dagoras, in Fordirith, northern Enedwaith.\
\
You have pleased Wadu with your heroics on his behalf among the Dunlending deserters and should tell Lothrandir of your successes.","Deserters can be found north of Echad Dagoras, in Fordirith.\
\
Wadu has asked you to recover blood-marks from the Dunlending deserters in Fordirith and to recover the weapons of his fallen kinsmen."}},
[2872]={nameES="Chapter 10: Echoes of the Dead",objectivesES={}},
[2873]={nameES="Chapter 10: Feast of the Zhélruka",objectivesES={}},
[2874]={nameES="Capítulo 10: Linaje olvidado",objectivesES={"Wafi está en la Sala de Forja de la Mansión de Thorin, en Ered Luin.\
\
Rósar, el Maestro de la Forja, ha identificado tu arma, y ahora deberías mostrársela a Wafi.","Habla con Wafi","Rósar, el Maestro de la Forja, está en la Sala de Forja de la Mansión de Thorin, en Ered Luin. Tiene la habilidad necesaria para identificar el arma misteriosa que has adquirido.\
\
Wafi te ha indicado que Rósar, el Maestro de la Forja, identifique tu arma para que puedas comprender su fuerza y su potencial.","Wafi está en la Sala de Forja de la Mansión de Thorin, en Ered Luin.\
\
Wafi te ha pedido que encajes una de las reliquias en tu arma para personalizar aún más sus capacidades.","El Maestro de la Forja ha identificado el arma, revelando sus fortalezas ocultas.","Encaja una reliquia de montura en tu arma","Capítulo 10: Linaje olvidado","Wafi está en la Sala de Forja de la Mansión de Thorin, en Ered Luin.\
\
Wafi te ha pedido que encajes en tu arma una de las reliquias que tienes para personalizar aún más sus capacidades, y ahora está esperando para hablar contigo.","Has encajado una reliquia de montura en tu arma","Equipa tu nueva arma","Lleva el arma al Maestro de la Forja para que la identifique","Wafi está en la Sala de Forja de la Mansión de Thorin, en Ered Luin.\
\
Hundi te ha dicho que le muestres tu nueva arma a Wafi en la Mansión de Thorin. Wafi podrá ayudarte a determinar las características intrínsecas del arma.","Ahora que tu arma ha sido identificada, debes equiparla si quieres aumentar su valor.","Has recibido un arma de los Días Antiguos, descubierta por los enanos en un escondrijo oculto, y ahora debes desentrañar sus secretos."}},
[2875]={nameES="Capítulo 10: Linaje olvidado",objectivesES={"Dithalion está junto a las forjas de Rivendel.\
\
Hundi te pidió que le muestres tu nueva arma a Dithalion, un elfo de Rivendel que podrá ayudarte a sacar partido de tu arma.","Has recibido un arma de los Días Antiguos que los enanos descubrieron en un escondrijo oculto, y ahora debes desentrañar sus secretos.","Habla con Dithalion junto a las forjas de Rivendel","Dithalion está en las Forjas de Rivendel.","Dithalion está en las Forjas de Rivendel.\
\
Has inscrito una tracería en tu arma y ahora deberías hablar con Dithalion.","Capítulo 10: Linaje olvidado"}},
[2876]={nameES="Capítulo 10: El Intercambio",objectivesES={"Capítulo 10: El Intercambio","Laeglang, Lamwen y Súlthel están en algún lugar de Gathbúrz, al este de Ost Galadh y fuera de los muros de Dol Guldur.\
\
Gruingalas te ha pedido que llames de vuelta a los exploradores que vigilan la fortaleza de Dol Guldur en Gathbúrz.","Habla con Súlthel en Gathbúrz","Habla con Gruingalas en Ost Galadh","Gruingalas está fuera de la entrada de Gadorgar, en Ost Galadh.\
\
Has llamado de vuelta a los exploradores de Gathbúrz y deberías regresar con Gruingalas con las noticias que reunieron en el territorio salvaje.","Habla con Lamwen en Gathbúrz","Habla con Gruingalas y reúne con la Guardia Oculta","Gruingalas está en Ost Galadh, esperando para hablar contigo.\
\
La misión de la Guardia Oculta está llegando a su fin: ha llegado el momento de intercambiar a Mazog por los prisioneros enanos.","Habla con Laeglang en Gathbúrz","La misión de la Guardia Oculta continúa: es hora de llamar de vuelta a los exploradores de la Hueste Dorada y llevar a Mazog a las puertas de Dol Guldur a cambio de los prisioneros.","Gruingalas está fuera de la entrada de Gadorgar, en Ost Galadh.\
\
El intercambio no salió según lo planeado, y la misión de la Guardia Oculta ha terminado en fracaso: Achardor está muerto, Mazog ha sido capturado y Bori sigue en cautiverio"}},
[2877]={nameES="Chapter 11.10: A Dead Man In The Desert",objectivesES={"This man is not dead! His breathing is shallow, but he lives... for now","Chapter 11.10: A Dead Man In The Desert","Some of the water passes parched lips, but more of it spills onto the sand","Tharashil is on the leader's rise in south-western Shonith.","Talk to Silirtas by the dying man","Sigileth is in southern Khûd Zagin.","Tharashil nods as you approach, but her expression is guarded","Silirtas hurries away.","Sigileth hands you her water bladder","Talk to Tharashil in south-western Shonith","Balakhâd eyes you warily","Find Balakhâd behind the pavilions north of the water in Shonith","You have done what you can for the dying man, and should give Sigileth's water bladder back to her.","Sigileth believes the dying man can be saved, but if he is to recover at Shonith you will need Tharashil's permission.","Talk to Sigileth in southern Khûd Zagin","Sigileth and Silirtas have found something in the dry reaches of Khûd Zagin.","Return her water bladder to Sigileth","Balakhâd is behind the pavilions north of the water in Shonith.","Balakhâd is behind the pavilions to the north of the water in Shonith.","Examine the dead man by Sigileth and Silirtis in Khûd Zagin","Silirtas stands in southern Khûd Zagin by the dying man.","Sigileth stands by the dying man in southern Khûd Zagin.","Talk to Balakhâd in Shonith","Wait for Silirtas to depart","Return to Tharashil in south-western Shonith","Offer water to the dying man in southern Khûd Zagin","Sigileth has asked you to examine the dead man to discover what spelled his end.","The man is barely alive, but a gift of water may help bring him back from death's brink."}},
[2878]={nameES="Chapter 11.11: Among Enemies",objectivesES={}},
[2879]={nameES="Chapter 11.1: A Window On the Past",objectivesES={"Gandalf, Elrond, and Glorfindel have come to Tol Send, where they await an audience with the shade of Isildur.","A chill breeze disturbs the petals on the Isle of the Flowers","Talk to the shade of Isildur on Tol Send","The shade of Isildur is on Tol Send, in the Gladden Fields.","Talk to Elrond outside the Beorninghús","Gandalf, Elrond, and Glorfindel wish to meet you on Tol Send, the Isle of the Flowers in the Gladden Fields.","Meet up with Gandalf, Elrond, and Glorfindel on Tol Send in the Gladden Fields","Talk to Glorfindel outside the Beorninghús","Chapter 11.1: A Window On the Past","Glorfindel is outside the Beorninghús.\
\
Gandalf and Elrond wish for you to ask Glorfindel to go with you to Tol Send, there to speak with the shade of Isildur about several matters of import.","Talk to Gandalf on Tol Send","The shade of Isildur may be able to tell you much about events long shrouded in mystery, but only if he can cast off the remaining vestiges of the Maiden's enchanted slumber.","Elrond is outside the Beorninghús.\
\
Gandalf asked you to bring Elrond word of his intent to speak with the shade of Isildur, and his desire that Elrond and Glorfindel accompany the two of you to Tol Send."}},
[2880]={nameES="Chapter 11.1: Girhâzi's Price",objectivesES={"Belondor stands beside the road that runs from Ambarûl into Khûd Zagin.","The time has come for your travelling party to take the road south into Khûd Zagin.","The food and water Girhâzi has provided for your travelling party can be found at the entrance of the village.","Belondor also has something to say to you.","Chapter 11.1: Girhâzi's Price","Talk to Belondor by the road that runs from Ambarûl into Khûd Zagin","Wait for the new arrival","Talk to Khôltekh at the village entrance of Iridír","Either Rothog or Húrshauk rumbles appreciatively. It is difficult to say which it was","Girhâzi has given you assistance and supplies to help you on the road into and through Khûd Zagin... but not without a price.","You supply yourself with the food Girhâzi provided, and suggest your companions do the same","Rahâzi has arrived at the entrance of her village.","Corudan stands beside the road leading south into Khûd Zagin.","Rahâzi arrives on the run","Take the road south into Khûd Zagin from Ambarûl","Rothog has something to say.","Talk to Corudan along the road into Khûd Zagin","Corudan calls a halt to your southward travel","Talk to Rahâzi at the village entrance of Iridír","You supply yourself with the water Girhâzi provided, and suggest your companions do the same","Khôltekh is at the village entrance of Iridír.","Restock your supplies using Girhâzi's provided water","Restock your supplies using Girhâzi's provided foodstuffs","Someone approaches at a run.","Talk to Belondor at the village entrance of Iridír","Talk to Rothog at the village entrance of Iridír","Corudan has suggested that you defeat the birds, jackals or servals, and lizards or snakes that threaten your southward journey into Khûd Zagin."}},
[2881]={nameES="Chapter 11.1: Soon To Wake",objectivesES={"Wait for Durin to come to a decision","Talk to Durin in Mótsog's Tomb","Mótsog nods solemnly at Durin.\
\
'I swear to fight for you, my friend of old, my king, for as long as I am able. I will deliver to you control of the kingdom I once stole, and if the last rays of the sun vanish behind the mountain before I seize your victory, I will perish with sorrow in my heart, and none before or since will know such grief as I know in my failure.'","Mótsog stands silently, and says nothing more.","Mótsog addresses you once again.\
\
'I deem you are his close advisor. Advise him then of this: I will walk in the world for only one more day before my long life is spent. When the sun sets on this day, my breath will be stilled and I will disappear from this place, never to return. In that time I have but one desire. I wish to do whatever my friend commands, for the vigil of so many years has given me this knowledge: Durin is the rightful king of the dwarves.\
\
'He was my first friend, my dear companion, and having made him an enemy I mourned the brother I lost. Now in the span of the single day I have remaining to me I will do what I can to deliver him his kingdom.'","Mótsog waits quietly for Durin's decision, and says nothing.","Talk to Mótsog and learn if he will accept Durin's decision","Durin waits for Mótsog's answer.","Durin stands in Mótsog's Tomb far below Gundabad.","Durin stands in Mótsog's Tomb far below Gundabad, trying to decide what is to be done.","Durin stands in Mótsog's Tomb.","Mótsog has told you that he will walk in the world for only one more day before his long life is spent, and he wants to do what he can for the friend he once betrayed.","Chapter 11.1: Soon To Wake"}},
[2882]={nameES="Chapter 11.2: An Incident On The Road",objectivesES={"Rahâzi is by the water in Ghalbûru.","Talk to Rothog in Ghalbûru","Khôltekh is in the caves of Ghalbûru.","Find Khôltekh inside the caves of Ghalbûru","Ghalbûru's apothecary Babarín is located outside in the village, beneath her canopy on the island in the middle of the pool.","It will take some time for Babarín to prepare the soothing poultice. You can wait for it to be ready, or you can speak to your companions throughout Ghalbûru.","Rothog is by the water in Ghalbûru.","Babarín is beneath her canopy on the island in the middle of the pool.","Bring the healing poultice to Sadûkh in the caves of Ghalbûru","Babarín's healing poultice must surely now be ready","Chapter 11.2: An Incident On The Road","The hideout of Ghalbûru is among the rocks south-east of the road through Khûd Zagin.","Your travelling party encountered some difficulty with highwaymen on the road into Khûd Zagin and followed them back to their hideout.","Ingredients needed by Babarín can be found throughout Ghalbûru: hardy plant leaves and riverside reeds.","Khôltekh has found an injured man resting in the caves of Ghalbûru.","Talk to Sirgon in Ghalbûru","Babarín gives you the healing poultice she prepared","Talk to Babarín, the apothecary in Ghalbûru","Talk to Babarín in Ghalbûru","Find the entrance to Ghalbûru in Khûd Zagin","Examine the injured man lying on the bed in the caves of Ghalbûru","Bring the ingredients you collected to Babarín in Ghalbûru","Sadûkh is resting in the caves of Ghalbûru. The entrance to the caves is located in the heights on the eastern side of Ghalbûru.","Khôltekh nods in the direction of the injured man lying on the bed","The man is seriously injured. He is dressed in the Umbari style","Sirgon is at the north-western entrance of Ghalbûru.","Khôltekh is inside the caves of Ghalbûru. The entrance to the caves is in the heights on the eastern side of Ghalbûru.","Talk to Rahâzi in Ghalbûru","The rest of your travelling companions have come to Ghalbûru","Talk to Khôltekh in the caves of Ghalbûru","Wait for the poultice to be prepared or speak to your travelling companions throughout Ghalbûru"}},
[2883]={nameES="Chapter 11.2: Dwarrowmoot",objectivesES={"Chapter 11.2: Dwarrowmoot","Durin fears that the foes prowling the Welkin-lofts may have hindered the arrival of his dwarves, and wants you to make the high passes as safe as possible.","Talk to Bósi, Bróin, or Bori in Zul-mazal","Climb the secret stair out of the depths and return to Zul-mazal","Talk to Imák on the western shore of the lake in Gloomingtarn","Meet up with the dwarves on the south-eastern side of the Thing-fold for Dwarrowmoot","Durin is at the Thing-fold in the Welkin-lofts for Dwarrowmoot, but is disappointed that more dwarves have not already arrived.","Talk to Durin at the Thing-fold in the Welkin-lofts","Talk to Prince Ingór at Maergrind in Máttugard","Talk to Glóin at the Steepset in Máttugard","Many dwarves have arrived for Dwarrowmoot... but not enough","Your friends greet you with enthusiasm and with worry","Durin has decided to call for Dwarrowmoot, a meeting of all the dwarves, where it will be decided what should be done to secure Gundabad.","Your efforts have enabled more dwarves to arrive for the Dwarrowmoot. Durin is eager to begin.","Durin has asked you to climb from the depths and return to Zul-mazal, where you can begin gathering the dwarves for Dwarrowmoot.","Talk to Durin at the Thing-fold","Durin has called for Dwarrowmoot on the south-eastern side of the Thing-fold, in the Welkin-lofts.","Durin asked you to bring word to a number of dwarves about the upcoming Dwarrowmoot:\
\
Bósi, Bróin, or Bori at Zul-mazal.\
Prince Ingór at Maergrind in Máttugard.\
Glóin at the Steepset in Máttugard.\
Imák on the western shore of the lake in Gloomingtarn.\
\
These dwarves will select others of their kind to attend the Dwarrowmoot. Time is short!"}},
[2884]={nameES="Chapter 11.2: The Same As You",objectivesES={"Retrieve weather-stained coffer from Sharkey's Slough","You set the weather-stained coffer down among the flowers","Ontamo is in Díngarth, chief fortification of the Great Alliance in Mordor Besieged.","Elrond is on Tol Send, the Isle of the Flowers in the Gladden Fields.\
\
Elrond examines the weather-stained coffer with some interest.","Talk to Ontamo in Díngarth, Mordor Besieged","Talk to the shade of Isildur","Chapter 11.2: The Same As You","The Memories of the Great Alliance will allow you to experience the Siege of Barad-dûr at the end of the Second Age, as relayed to you by the shade of Isildur.","The shade of Isildur has agreed to tell you what he remembers of the Elf named Magoldir and the Siege of Barad-dûr that concluded the Second Age.","The dented coffer is caked in mud, ravaged by the passage of years","The shade of Isildur is waiting for you to bring the weather-stained coffer to Tol Send.","Talk to Elrond on Tol Send","Bring the weather-stained coffer to Tol Send","The shade of Isildur is pleased that you found the weather-stained coffer and brought it to Tol Send, and now wishes to tell you the tale he promised.","Use the Memories of the Great Alliance and be transported to Mordor Besieged (Second Age)","The shade of Isildur asked you to retrieve a weather-stained coffer from the encampment of Sharkey's Slough, south-west of Tol Send."}},
[2885]={nameES="Chapter 11.3: A Day at Díngarth",objectivesES={"Talk to Magoldir among the bodies of the slain Orcs","Ontamo asked you to collect wood and stone for patching up the fortifications at Díngarth and to keep resting soldiers from giving Isildur the impression of laziness when he comes to inspect the defences.","Ontamo awaits your return in Díngarth.","Ontamo is at Díngarth, awaiting word of your success against the Orcs.","An Elf stands among the bodies of a slain Orc raiding party","Talk to Ontamo at Díngarth","You have stumbled upon an Elf surrounded by the bodies of a slain Orc raiding party.","The guttural voices of Orcs can be heard among the rocks far to the south of Díngarth.","Ontamo has asked you to improve the fortifications at spots in need of repair in and around Díngarth.","Chapter 11.3: A Day at Díngarth","Ontamo is worried about the imminent inspection of the fortifications of Díngarth by Isildur, King of Gondor, and has requested your aid in their improvement.","Investigate the sound of Orc voices far to the south of Díngarth","An Orc raiding party was seen patrolling south of the encampment of Díngarth, and Ontamo asked you to take care of it before King Isildur arrived for his inspection of the defences. Orcs can be found leaving their encampment of Mokh Shapat, far to the south of Díngarth."}},
[2886]={nameES="Chapter 11.3: Knives Everywhere",objectivesES={"Rahâzi is by the water in Ghalbûru.","Corudan asked you to go to the south-western entrance to Ghalbûru and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> for some sign of Sadûkh.","Sadûkh is no longer here. Where did he go?","Khôltekh is in the caves of Ghalbûru.","Talk to Corudan outside the entrance to the caves of Ghalbûru","Talk to Urugal at the south-western entrance to Ghalbûru","Rahâzi suggested that you return to Sadûkh to tell him what you learned of Balakhad's location before you help her infiltrate the fortress above Jirush. Sadûkh is recovering from his injuries in the caves of Ghalbûru.","Corudan is outside the entrance to the caves of Ghalbûru, located in the heights on the eastern side of the village.","There is no sign of Sadûkh at the north-eastern entrance to Ghalbûru","In the caves of Ghalbûru, Sadûkh seeks assurances that you will protect him from his enemies.","Sadûkh sees enemies all around him, believing there to be knives everywhere... even within Ghalbûru.","Go to the south-western entrance to Ghalbûru and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> for some sign of Sadûkh","Silence hangs over the town of Jirush, as if the entire town holds its breath","Rahâzi has suggested that you go to the town of Jirush in the desert to the west and see if any of the townsfolk there know Balakhad's location.","Talk to residents of Jirush who can tell you about Balakhad's location (2/3)","Sadûkh eyes you warily, and you ask him what happened to Balakhâd","Go to the north-eastern entrance of Ghalbûru and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> for some sign of Sadûkh","Assure Sadûkh that you will protect him","Talk to Sadûkh in the caves of Ghalbûru","Talk to Rahâzi in Jirush","Townsfolk of Jirush can be found throughout the city.","Bring the sharp jackal teeth to Erinesh in Jirush","Corudan asked you to go to the north-eastern entrance of Ghalbûru and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> for some sign of Sadûkh.","Chapter 11.3: Knives Everywhere","There is no sign of Sadûkh at the south-western entrance, but a guard beckons to you","Erinesh stands in the centre of Jirush.","Erinesh may know something about Balakhad's location, but he wants you to collect jackal teeth for him before he tells you anything. Jackals can be found throughout Khûd Zagin.","Corudan is outside the entrance to the caves of Ghalbûru, in the heights on the eastern side of the village.","Rahâzi is in the centre of Jirush.","Urugal has beckoned for you to speak with him.","Sadûkh is resting in the caves of Ghalbûru.","Talk to Rahâzi in Ghalbûru","Talk to Khôltekh in the caves of Ghalbûru","Travel to the entrance of Jirush, located in the desert to the west"}},
[2887]={nameES="Chapter 11.3: The Voice of the Dragon",objectivesES={}},
[2888]={nameES="Chapter 11.4: Shadows In Jirush",objectivesES={"Rahâzi is by the water in Ghalbûru.","Khôltekh is at the north-west entrance to Ghalbûru, east of Jirush.","Talk to Rahâzi in Ghalbûru and infiltrate the fortress above Jirush","Sigileth is in the centre of Jirush.","Chapter 11.4: Shadows In Jirush","Rahâzi is by the water in Ghalbûru, waiting to go with you to the fortress above Jirush.","Talk to Khôltekh at the north-west entrance to Ghalbûru","Talk to Sigileth in the centre of Jirush","Return to the north-west entrance of Ghalbûru, east of Jirush","Talk to Sigileth on the western side of Ghalbûru","Khôltekh greets you as you approach. 'Well?' he prompts you","Sigileth is on the western side of Ghalbûru.","Sigileth suggested you return to Ghalbûru, but that you keep the information you learned about Balakhad to yourself.","Rahâzi is prepared for the two of you to assault the fortress above Jirush, but Corudan and Sigileth want to accompany you, hoping to find Balakhad before the Dumûri warrior alerts the Ordâkhai.","Talk to Rahâzi in Ghalbûru"}},
[2889]={nameES="Chapter 11.4: The Last Greymaul",objectivesES={"The cheers seem to shake the mountain itself: 'Gundabad is ours!'","Gorgar has been defeated and Hrímil Frost-heart has fled on injured wings, abandoning the high places to Durin's army. You have achieved victory!","Durin has entrusted you with accompanying Mótsog to the peak, there to face Hrímil Frost-heart. The prince and all of the Gabil'akkâ will create a path through the enemy forces so you can achieve your mission!","Talk to Durin on the mountain-side","At the Thing-fold in the Welkin-lofts, Durin prepares for the battle to come.","Chapter 11.4: The Last Greymaul","Talk to Durin and accompany Mótsog to the peak... and to Hrímil Frost-heart"}},
[2890]={nameES="Chapter 11.4: The Sons of Isildur",objectivesES={"King Isildur of Gondor shakes his head disapprovingly, and calls you to him","Ontamo believes that he has been personally insulted by Isildur's decision to send his sons to inspect the defences at Díngarth, rather than come himself, and he has decided that you should meet with them instead.","Isildur is at the Gondorian encampment of Adambel.","Vëamacil is waiting to speak to you, now that Tárandil has given you no suggestions for his birthday present.","Vëamacil is at Díngarth, waiting to take a meal with you before he conducts the inspection of the encampment's defences.","Tárandil is at Díngarth.\
\
Vëamacil has decided that you should come with them to Adambel, but that you should first ask his foster-brother Tárandil what he wants as a present for his birthday.","Talk to King Isildur at Adambel","Find Tárandil at the encampment of Adambel","Tárandil nods in greeting as you approach","Give the trophies to Tárandil as a birthday present","Tárandil has gone to the primary Gondorian encampment of Adambel.\
\
Vëamacil asked you to slay Orcs and wargs and bring trophies of your victories to his foster-brother Tárandil as a birthday present.","Orcs and wargs can be found throughout Arandor in Mordor Besieged.\
\
Vëamacil asked you to collect trophies from Orcs and wargs to give to Tárandil for a birthday present.","The sons of Isildur have conducted their inspection, and now Vëamacil wishes to speak with you.","Tárandil is in the primary Gondorian encampment of Adambel.","Ontamo feels insulted by Isildur's decision to send his sons to conduct the inspection of Díngarth's defences, and has asked you to speak with them instead.","Talk to one of Isildur's sons at Díngarth","Talk to Vëamacil and complete 'Instance: The Sons of Isildur'","Talk to Vëamacil at Díngarth","Talk to Tárandil at Díngarth","Chapter 11.4: The Sons of Isildur"}},
[2891]={nameES="Chapter 11.5: Deception and Departure",objectivesES={"Rahâzi is by the water in Ghalbûru.","Sigileth is by the north-western entrance to Ghalbûru.","Khôltekh is by the north-western entrance of Ghalbûru.","<rgb=#00FF00>Wave</rgb> to Rahâzi in Ghalbûru","Having received tidings of Balakhad's death, Khôltekh is ready to leave Khûd Zagin behind, taking most of the travelling company with him.","Sigileth stands by the road south-east of Jirush in Khûd Zagin.","Sigileth planned to meet with you along the road south-east of Jirush.","Talk to Belondor in Ghalbûru","<rgb=#00FF00>Wave</rgb> to Corudan in Ghalbûru","Sigileth is by the north-western entrance of Ghalbûru.","Chapter 11.5: Deception and Departure","Talk to Corudan in Ghalbûru","You should <rgb=#00FF00>wave</rgb> to your departing companions, and say your farewells to them. Sirgon is by the north-western entrance to Ghalbûru.","Talk to Sirgon in Ghalbûru","Meet with Sigileth along the road south-east of Jirush, in Khûd Zagin","Talk to Sigileth by the road south-east of Jirush","<rgb=#00FF00>Wave</rgb> to Sirgon in Ghalbûru","You should <rgb=#00FF00>wave</rgb> to your departing companions, and say your farewells to them. Rahâzi is by the water in Ghalbûru.","Corudan is by the water in Ghalbûru.","Talk to Khôltekh in Ghalbûru","Sirgon and Belondor are by the north-western entrance to Ghalbûru.","Talk to Sigileth in Ghalbûru","Rahâzi watches you silently.","You should <rgb=#00FF00>wave</rgb> to your departing companions, and say your farewells to them. Corudan is by the water in Ghalbûru.","Sigileth nods at your approach","Talk to Rahâzi in Ghalbûru"}},
[2892]={nameES="Chapter 11.5: Gundabad Is Ours!",objectivesES={"Talk to Prince Ingór","Habla con Bróin","The Gabil'akkâ celebrates its victory in Gundabad.","Mótsog gazes at the western horizon","Habla con Bori","The dwarves have achieved victory in Gundabad, and the Gabil'akkâ celebrates on the mountainside.","Talk to Stáli the Hewer","Mótsog gazes toward the western horizon.","Chapter 11.5: Gundabad Is Ours!","Talk to Imák","Talk to Fastrith","Durin is up the slope to the east, celebrating the victory of the dwarves.","Find Mótsog down the slope to the west","Talk to Venko","Talk to Durin high above Gundabad","Talk to Mótsog high above Gundabad","Habla con Glóin","Mótsog has stepped away, unnoticed, from the celebrating throng.","Mótsog stands on the slope, watching the setting sun.","Habla con Bósi."}},
[2893]={nameES="Chapter 11.5: The Storm in the East",objectivesES={"Vëamacil is at Adambel.\
\
Now that you have trained with the soldiers, High King Elendil expects you to convey his reprimand to his grandson Vëamacil.","A crate of whetstones can be found by the camp-fires to the north in Adambel, the primary Gondorian encampment in Mordor Besieged.","King Isildur of Gondor is at the encampment of Adambel.","Deliver whetstones to idle soldiers and the sons of Isildur (5/6)","Collected the crate of whetstones","Magoldir is at Adambel, the primary Gondorian encampment in Mordor Besieged.","Elendil stares at you sternly","King Isildur of Gondor worries that his sons have allowed the length of the siege to dull their wits and their weapons, and wants them each made sharp again.","Magoldir nods at you pleasantly","High King Elendil has commanded that you train with soldiers at the encampment of Adambel and remind them not to relax their guard despite the length of the siege.","Idle soldiers can be found throughout Adambel.\
\
Isildur asked you to deliver whetstones to idle soldiers of the Alliance, as well as to his sons.","The shade of Isildur has interrupted the telling of his tale with a brief aside.","Talk to Isildur at Adambel","Chapter 11.5: The Storm in the East","Give Magoldir a whetstone at Adambel","Delivered a whetstone and a warning (5/6)","Talk to the shade of Isildur at Adambel","Deliver a whetstone and a warning to High King Elendil at Adambel","High King Elendil can be found somewhere within Adambel, the primary Gondorian encampment in Mordor Besieged.","Find a crate of whetstones in Adambel","Talk to Vëamacil at Adambel"}},
[2894]={nameES="Chapter 11.6: Tales of the Bright Company",objectivesES={"Talk to Glorfindel at Echad-in-Edhil","Talk to Magoldir on the northern slope of Amon Amarth","Find the location east of Adambel that Magoldir wishes to scout","Magoldir wishes to report to Glorfindel of the Bright Company at the encampment of Echad-in-Edhil, north-west of Adambel in Mordor Besieged.","Magoldir surveys the surrounding terrain from the slope of Amon Amarth","Glorfindel, leader of the Bright Company, is waiting to speak with you in the Elf-camp of Echad-in-Edhil.","Chapter 11.6: Tales of the Bright Company","Talk to Magoldir and complete 'Instance: Tales of the Bright Company'","Magoldir stands at the entrance of Echad-in-Edhil, waiting for your readiness to report to Glorfindel, leader of the Bright Company.","Magoldir has come to Adambel on behalf of the Bright Company, and seeks your help.","Find the entrance to Echad-in-Edhil","Talk to Magoldir at the entrance to Echad-in-Edhil","Magoldir desires to scout a location to the east of Adambel for Glorfindel of the Bright Company."}},
[2895]={nameES="Chapter 11.6: Unsafe Sanctuary",objectivesES={}},
[2896]={nameES="Chapter 11.7: Anárion's Guess",objectivesES={"Anárion asked you to bring his message to soldiers in the field east of Adambel, nearer to the Dark Tower. He also charged you with defeating servants of Sauron and the beasts that stalk among the crags of Mordor.","Vëamacil is at Díngarth.\
\
Tárandil told you that his brothers may have found some clue to the mystery of the missing soldiers.","Anárion has been summoned to an urgent council and is unavailable. Isildur's foster-son Tárandil has called you over and wishes to speak with you.","Talk to Tárandil at Adambel","You came too late to deliver Anárion's hopeful message, for Astondor has been slain.","Bring Anárion's message to Tumbomehtar","Return to Anárion at Adambel","Bring Anárion's message to Martore","Glorfindel of the Bright Company has collected a number of scouting reports from his Elves in the field, and wishes for you to investigate what they might signify.","Bring Anárion's message to Astondor","Chapter 11.7: Anárion's Guess","Talk to Vëamacil at Díngarth","You have done as Anárion asked, and should return to him at Adambel.","Bring the scouting reports to either Isildur or Anárion at Adambel","Glorfindel asked you to deliver the scouting reports to either Isildur or Anárion at the Gondorian encampment of Adambel."}},
[2897]={nameES="Chapter 11.7: The Oasis at Shonith",objectivesES={"Talk to Sigileth at Shonith","Sigileth is on the leader's rise in south-western Shonith.","Tharashil is on the leader's rise in south-western Shonith.","Chapter 11.7: The Oasis at Shonith","Sigileth has sought out the leader of the Kintai who dwell at Shonith","Sigileth is on the leader's rise in the south-western reaches of Shonith.","Talk to Tharashil at Shonith","Talk to Tharashil in south-western Shonith","Meet up with Sigileth far to the south-east at the Oasis of Shonith","Walk closer to the edge of the overlook and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> out over Shonith","Tharashil asked you to leave the meat and feathers you collected in the coffer north of the water in Shonith.","Sand-sifters and birds can be found throughout the desert regions of Khûd Zagin.","Shonith is green and thriving, in stark contrast to the desert beyond the encircling rocks","Shonith is an oasis far away in south-eastern Khûd Zagin.","Leave the meat and feathers in the coffer north of the water in Shonith","Talk to Sigileth in south-western Shonith","Although your investigation at Nirgambâr did not find what Sigileth expected, she believes you should continue on to Shonith as you told your travelling companions you intended.","You leave the sand-sifter meat and bird feathers in the coffer","Tharashil asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> out over Shonith and consider the work of the Kintai."}},
[2898]={nameES="Chapter 11.8: The Fading of the Kintai",objectivesES={"Wait for Aitárshun to turn his attention to you","The Kinta Elf Aitárshun sways slightly within the bole of his red-leafed Sarlásh","Tharashil falls silent and gathers her thoughts","Tharashil is on the leader's rise in south-western Shonith.","Talk to Silirtas at Er-atûr","Talk to Tharashil at Shonith","Aitárshun is on the easternmost island in the water in Shonith.","Talk to Tharashil in south-western Shonith","Er-atûr is to the north-west of Shonith.","At last Aitárshun speaks to you","You and Sigileth have found Silirtas, the Kinta of whom Tharashil spoke","Tharashil wants you to learn about her people, the Kintai of Ikorbân.","You introduce yourself to Aitárshun and await his response.","The attention of Aitárshun has moved away from you, and it may be some time before it returns.","Tharashil has much to tell you about her people, the Kintai.","Meet with Aitárshun on the easternmost island in the water in Shonith","Silirtas is at Er-atûr, north-west of Shonith.","Talk to Sigileth at Er-atûr","Find Silirtas at Er-atûr, north-west of Shonith","Aitárshun is on the easternmost island in the water in Shonith, reachable by the bridges.","Sigileth is at Er-atûr, north-west of Shonith.","Talk to Aitárshun in Shonith","Chapter 11.8: The Fading of the Kintai"}},
[2899]={nameES="Chapter 11.8: Tûka's Wisdom",objectivesES={"Isildur's son Vëamacil can be found at Díngarth.","Talk to Tûka, leader of the Hól-budlan, on the outskirts of Díngarth","Tûka, matriarch of the Hól-budlan, has made a discovery concerning the missing soldiers, and the sons of Isildur want your help to track down a solution to the mystery.","Talk to Vëamacil at Díngarth","Chapter 11.8: Tûka's Wisdom","Isildur's son Ornaher can be found in Díngarth with the Hól-budlan matriarch Tûka.","Tûka, leader of the Hól-budlan, may have some clue as to what befell the missing soldiers. She can be found in Díngarth.","Talk to Ornaher at Díngarth"}},
[2900]={nameES="Chapter 11.9: All Is Quiet",objectivesES={"Talk to Vëamacil and complete 'Instance: All Is Quiet'","Isildur's foster-son Tárandil is at Ram Raedas.","Chapter 11.9: All Is Quiet","Talk to Meldaran at Ram Raedas","Isildur's son Meldaran has come to Ram Raedas with worrying tidings.","Isildur's son Vëamacil is at Díngarth.","Stirred to action by the discovery that the missing soldiers were abducted by Mordorrim cultists, Vëamacil and Ornaher are eager to attempt a dangerous rescue in the heart of Amon Fuin.","Talk to Tárandil at Ram Raedas"}},
[2901]={nameES="Chapter 11.9: Silirtas and the Great Dearth",objectivesES={"Silirtas stands in the dry river-bed where the River Usâl once flowed.","Defeat lizards or avanc in south-western Khûd Zagin (3/4)","The sand falls through your fingers","Silirtas has agreed to tell you about her people and what they have learned about the lands of Khûd Zagin.","Silirtas falls silent in the middle of her thought","Silirtas asked you to investigate the river-bed where once the River Usâl ran through Khûd Zagin. To the north-west you see some water remains in the channel.","Continue further to the north-west and examine some of the sand among the tumbled rocks","Lizards and avanc can be found in the south-western corner of Khûd Zagin.","Sigileth has found something among the southern sands of Khûd Zagin.","Talk to Silirtas in the dry river-bed where the River Usâl once flowed","Silirtas stares blankly forward, seemingly unaware of your presence.","Sigileth calls for you to join her among the southern sands","This is one of the few places where water still collects where the River Usâl once flowed","Silirtas turns her head to you, apparently aware of you and Sigileth once again","Sigileth has found something in southern Khûd Zagin.","Sigileth has found the body of a dead man","Examine sand in the dry river-bed where the River Usâl once flowed","Silirtas asked you to investigate the dry river-bed where the River Usâl once ran through Khûd Zagin. To the north-west a tumble of stones fills the channel.","Sigileth waits politely for Silirtas to resume her story, but the Kinta remains silent.\
\
'What happened following the invasion of the Ordâkhai after the Great Dearth?' Sigileth prompts her.\
\
'Silirtas?'","Silirtas stands in the dry river-bed where the River Usâl once flowed, but she says nothing.","Chapter 11.9: Silirtas and the Great Dearth","Talk to Sigileth in southern Khûd Zagin","Examine sand further to the north-west, alongside the little water that remains in the channel of the River Usâl","Silirtas asked you to investigate the dry river-bed where once the River Usâl ran through Khûd Zagin, to the west.","Silirtas watches the sand fall from your fingers onto the dry ground","Join Sigileth and Silirtas in the desert of southern Khûd Zagin","Talk to Sigileth in the dry river-bed where the River Usâl once flowed","Sigileth is in the dry river-bed where the River Usâl once flowed.","Silirtas is in the dry river-bed where the River Usâl once flowed. She again seems aware of both you and Sigileth."}},
[2902]={nameES="Capítulo 11: Forjada de nuevo",objectivesES={"Snár, el Maestro de la Forja, puede encontrarse junto a las Forjas de Rivendel.\
\
Tu arma posee un potencial oculto que puede desbloquearse reforjándola con un Maestro de la Forja. Este proceso aumenta el daño del arma y revela su potencial.","Dithalion está junto a las Forjas de Rivendel.\
\
Ahora que has reforjado el arma, deberías volver con Dithalion para demostrar su progreso.","Capítulo 11: Forjada de nuevo","Ráthwald está en el arco en ruinas cerca del campamento de Echad Dúnann, en Eregion.\
\
Tu arma se ha vuelto realmente poderosa, quizá lo bastante como para usarla en combate contra el Guardián ante las Puertas de Durin.","Habla con Snár, el Maestro de la Forja, en las Forjas de Rivendel","Diathalon desea ver tu arma reforjada de nuevo."}},
[2903]={nameES="Chapter 11: Grief and Insight",objectivesES={"Chapter 11: Grief and Insight","The distant expression that Nár usually wears has been replaced with a shrewd glare. He is still under the effect of the strange-smelling brew, but that clarity may not last long.","Talk to Nár at Zudrugund","Devastated by the losses suffered by the Grey Company on the Forsaken Road, Halbarad wants you to tell Corunir it is time to leave.","Corunir is at Zudrugund.\
\
Halbarad wants you to tell Corunir to come back to Lhanuch.","Corunir is at Zudrugund.\
\
You have spoken with Nár about a number of topics of interest to Corunir and should tell the Ranger what you have learned.","Talk to Corunir at Zudrugund","Talk to Corunir in Zudrugund","Nár is in Zudrugund.\
\
Corunir, angered by the loss of his friends along the Forsaken Road, has forced Frithgeir to give Nár the strange-smelling brew once again, in order for dwarf to give clear answers about his knowledge."}},
[2904]={nameES="Capítulo 11: El Enfoque hacia Dol Guldur",objectivesES={"Habla con Ningloril en Thangúlhad","Capítulo 11: El Enfoque hacia Dol Guldur","Ningloril está en Thangúlhad, al este de Ost Galadh, en Gathbúrz.\
\
Gruingalas te ha enviado para ofrecer tu ayuda a Ningloril, ahora que la misión de la Guardia Oculta ha fracasado.","La misión de la Guardia Oculta ha fracasado, y ahora las esperanzas restantes de Celeborn y Galadriel dependen únicamente del brazo principal de la Hueste Dorada."}},
[2905]={nameES="Chapter 11: The Blockade",objectivesES={"Saeradan is at his camp, Echad Saeradan, in the Windfells, in Enedwaith. His camp can be found on a hilltop in the Windfells, south-west of Echad Dagoras.\
\
Lothrandir has sent you into the Windfells to assist Saeradan.","Bring the report and the ancient sword to Saeradan","Chapter 11: The Blockade","Talk to Saeradan at Echad Saeradan","Inside the coffer you find a report and a sword with ancient markings","The road that runs north through Dunland and Enedwaith has been troubled by hostile Dunlending clans, and the Grey Company is worried by these reports.","Investigate the road north of Echad Saeradan for evidence of a blockade","Saeradan is at his camp south of the blockaded road in Fordirith.\
\
You found a report and a sword with ancient markings in the coffer at the blockaded road and should bring them to Saeradan.","The road north of Echad Saeradan may have been blockaded by forces of Saruman.\
\
Saeradan has asked you to investigate the road north for signs of blockade."}},
[2906]={nameES="Capítulo 11: Valor inconmensurable",objectivesES={"Capítulo 11: Valor inconmensurable","Lleva tu nueva arma a Wafi o a Dithalion","Tu nueva arma tiene un potencial de valor inconmensurable, pero aún debes blandirla en combate.","Wafi está en la Sala de Forja de la Mansión de Thorin, en Ered Luin, y Dithalion está junto a las Forjas de Rivendel.\
\
Ahora que has combatido a muchos enemigos con tu nueva arma, deberías volver con Wafi o con Dithalion para demostrar tu progreso."}},
[2907]={nameES="Chapter 12.1: The Approaching Storm",objectivesES={"Words are no more use to the despairing soldiers of the Great Alliance. Better now to collect the weapons they cast aside with the hope that they will still be of use to those who remain to fight.","The Longbeard and Thíuda armies that engaged with the Ghâzab Bôron, the Rhúnhoth Storm of Wrath, have been utterly defeated, and now nothing stands between the flank of the Great Alliance and the onrushing horde.","Chapter 12.1: The Approaching Storm","Speak inspiring words to fearful soldiers at Ram Raedas (0/8)","Talk to Ornaher at Díngarth","Frightened Men and Elves can be found at Díngarth.\
\
Ornaher believes tales of Elendil's sword Narsil and Gil-galad's spear Aiglos may inspire the frightened Men and Elves to stand against the Ghâzab Bôron.","Fearful soldiers can be found at Díngarth, despairing at the news of the approaching Rhúnhoth horde.","Deliver abandoned weapons to Ornaher at Díngarth","Tárandil is at Díngarth, and he desires to speak with you.","Talk to Tárandil at Díngarth","You have gathered many weapons cast aside by despairing soldiers at Díngarth, and should bring them to Ornaher for distribution to those who may still wield them.","Isildur's son Ornaher is at Díngarth."}},
[2908]={nameES="Chapter 12.1: The Hungry Fire",objectivesES={"Dampen the cloth and fill the jar with water from the deepest part of the oasis","Talk to Idhraid by the northern pavilion","Silirtas is waiting for you to return to her with the damp cloth and water jar she requested of you.","Talk to Tharashil in south-western Shonith","Silirtas suggested that you speak with Idhraid about what it will take to heal Balakhâd of his injuries, and also that you fill a jar with water from the deepest part of the oasis. Jars for this purpose can be found at the front of the pavilion in northern Shonith.","You inform Tharashil of Balakhâd's condition and his vow to depart from Shonith as soon as he is able to walk. You also ask for her permission to allow Silirtas to accompany you and Sigileth on your journey eastward.\
\
'I am the warden of this grove, but I have not the power to keep Silirtas from doing as she wishes. Had I that power, she might have already entered Tróthul and begun to safely fade within a Veróth of her own! But I do not, and she insists upon fighting the process.\
\
'If she truly wishes to go with you, I hope you will keep her safe. She fights the fading, but I understand the fight is painful, and even one so strong-willed as Silirtas cannot achieve victory in every battle. It is the lot of her people to fade, though she wishes otherwise.'","Sigileth is at the northern pavilion in Shonith.","Help Balakhâd drink from the jar of water","You help Balakhâd hold the jar you filled with clean water from the oasis, and he manages to drink. After a few moments, he looks up at you with a guarded expression.\
\
'We are... not friends. These Elves are alien to me, and I do not trust them. As soon as I am... well enough to walk... I will leave this place, and never return.\
\
'But you and these Elves are... you are right about something. If the Kindred finds the hidden cache of Narghâk they seek...'\
\
Balakhâd falls silent, mopping his forehead with the damp cloth you brought from Idhraid.\
\
'In Gondor they named it \\qUmbari Fire,\\q for they knew not of its long use in these lands, and only learned of it when it was used against them. But my father knew. He dreamed of harnessing it against his enemies, but even with all the men at his command he could find no stores of it. He believed it gone from the world.\
\
'It should be gone. Azagath and Nakási must not find... the hidden stockpile they seek. They will set the world aflame.'","Talk to Sigileth at the northern pavilion in Shonith","Silirtas believes that Balakhâd knows more about Narghâk, the Hungry Fire, than he is letting on. He may speak further on the subject if his hurts are healed.","You should dampen the cloth given to you by Idhraid and fill the jar you collected with water from the deepest reaches of the oasis in Shonith.","Idhraid gives you a cloth to dampen in the water","Silirtas has begun trying to ease Balakhâd's hurts with the damp cloth.","Balakhâd is at the northern pavilion in Shonith.","Bring the damp cloth and water jar to Silirtas at the northern pavilion in Shonith","Wait for Silirtas to soothe Balakhâd's burning skin with the damp cloth","You dampen the cloth and fill your jar with water from the deepest part of the oasis","Chapter 12.1: The Hungry Fire","You pick up the jar","Tharashil is in south-western Shonith.","Collect a jar front the northern pavilion to fill with water for Balakhâd"}},
[2909]={nameES="Chapter 12.2: The Council of Kings",objectivesES={"Collected a Mordorrim badge of rank","Bring the patrol badges to Tárandil at Adambel","Vëamacil is at Adambel, dismayed by the result of the council of the kings.","Chapter 12.2: The Council of Kings","Talk to Tárandil and complete 'Instance: The Council of Kings'","Tárandil is at Adambel, hoping to attend the council of the kings.","Talk to Elendil at Adambel","Collect a badge from an Easterling hopeful","Tárandil wants to attend the council of the kings, but he fears it will not be permitted without some evidence that he is deserving.","Collected an Orkish badge of rank","Collect a badge from a Mordorrim hopeful","Collected an Easterling badge of rank","Collect a badge from a hopeful Orc patrol-leader","High King Elendil is at Adambel, and has asked to speak with you.","Patrol leaders, and others who intend to lead such excursions, can be found throughout Parth Daenath. Mordorrim hopefuls gather west of the entrance to Amon Fuin, and hopeful Orcs can be found in and around Mokh Darga. Look for Easterling hopefuls south of the road halfway between Mokh Darga and Barthost.\
\
Tárandil believes that proof of your value to the Great Alliance will gain the two of you entrance to the council of the kings, and he wants you to collect badges of rank belonging to hopeful patrol leaders as proof of that value.","Talk to Vëamacil at Adambel"}},
[2910]={nameES="Chapter 12.2: The Dead Forest",objectivesES={"Thórvilon, leader of the Kintai at Vartúlin is in southern Imhûlar.","Tharashil has suggested that when you depart from Shonith, you visit the grove of Vartúlin in Imhûlar before meeting up with the rest of your travelling company.","Diseased boars, servals, and deer can be found throughout Imhûlar.","Silirtas is just inside the entrance to Imhûlar.","Sigileth calls a halt at the entrance to Imhûlar","Talk to Thórvilon in Vartúlin","Talk to Silirtas by the road into Imhûlar","Find Thórvilon, leader of the Kintai at Vartúlin, in southern Imhûlar","Talk to Sigileth by the road into Imhûlar","Cross the River Barûg into Imhûlar from Khûd Zagin, north of Shonith","Silirtas stares blankly forward, her awareness once again untethered.","Sigileth stands just within the entrance to Imhûlar.","The leader of the Kintai at Vartúlin is named Thórvilon, and can be found in southern Imhûlar.","Chapter 12.2: The Dead Forest","Thórvilon glances at Silirtas with understanding","The road into Imhûlar crosses the River Barûg north of Shonith.","Silirtas stands by Thórvilon in Vartúlin.","Give the hooves, fangs, and hides to Thórvilon","Talk to Silirtas in Vartúlin","You have found Thórvilon, leader of the Kintai at Vartúlin","Thórvilon, leader of the Kintai at Vartúlin, is in southern Imhûlar."}},
[2911]={nameES="Chapter 12.3: A Bad Birthday",objectivesES={"Glorfindel catches your attention, a sorrowful look on his face","Tûka is outside the tunnel of Halroth, which the Bright Company hopes to use to infiltrate Barad-dûr.","Glorfindel is on Tol Send.\
\
Glorfindel has interrupted the shade of Isildur in his telling of the tale, and wishes to speak with you.","Talk to Vëamacil and complete 'Instance: A Bad Birthday'","Tûka is outside the entrance of Halroth, a tunnel carved in the rocks of Mordor.","The shade of Isildur is on Tol Send, waiting to tell you more of the tale of the Great Alliance.","Talk to the shade of Isildur on Tol Send","Talk to Tûka outside the entrance to Halroth","Talk to Glorfindel on Tol Send","Lendelen of the Bright Company has suggested a dangerous mission to overcome Sauron's domination of the Ghâzab Bôron, and a number of preparations must be made before it can be attempted.","Chapter 12.3: A Bad Birthday","Find Tûka outside the entrance to the tunnel of Halroth","Vëamacil is at Adambel, and he wishes to speak with you.","Talk to Gandalf on Tol Send","Glorfindel closes his eyes, and nods with reluctant agreement","Defeat enemies in the vicinity of the entrance to the tunnel of Halroth, in Emyn Duir.\
\
Tûka thinks you should defeat watchful eyes near the entrance to Halroth, not too many and not too few.","Defeat just the right number of enemies outside Halroth, in Emyn Duir","Gandalf is on Tol Send. He has listened with interest to the tale told by the shade of Isildur, but does not understand the need for Glorfindel's interruption.","Glorfindel is on Tol Send, and he has volunteered to complete the tale begun by the shade of Isildur, despite his misgivings.","Talk to Vëamacil at Adambel"}},
[2912]={nameES="Chapter 12.3: The Encroaching Darkness",objectivesES={"Place a boundary stone on the slope to the southern pavilion in Vartúlin","Travel toward Kûr Anzar, to the north of Vartúlin","Sigileth is outside Adakûr in Imhûlar.","You pick up a number of stones from the pile","Having satisfied Thórvilon's request, you should return to the centre of Vartúlin and check on Silirtas.","Placed boundary stone","Sigileth calls for a halt and says you should defeat the wights near Adakûr","You arrive at an ideal location for scouting Kûr Anzar","Pick up boundary stones from the pile across the bridge in Vartúlin","Chapter 12.3: The Encroaching Darkness","That should be enough stones to fulfil Thórvilon's request.","Sigileth is in Vartúlin.","Sigileth wants to rejoin the rest of your travelling company at Kûr Anzar, to the north of Vartúlin.","Kûr Anzar is filled with soldiers and cultists. Your companions cannot have gone there","Thórvilon has enlisted your help to protect Vartúlin and the Kintai from the encroaching darkness that threatens Imhûlar.","Talk to Silirtas in the centre of Vartúlin","Sigileth wants you to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at Kûr Anzar from a location to the north-east and determine the situation inside the city.","A pile of the boundary stones can be found across the bridge in Vartúlin.","Place a boundary stone at the western entrance to Vartúlin","You should defeat some of the Dead that lurk at Adakûr before they threaten the folk that live in Imhûlar.","Place a boundary stone at the north-eastern entrance to Vartúlin","Talk to Sigileth in Vartúlin","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> at Kûr Anzar from here","Find the location to the north-east from which to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at Kûr Anzar","Talk to Sigileth outside Adakûr","Place a boundary stone north of Thórvilon","Thórvilon has asked you to place boundary stones around the edges of Vartúlin."}},
[2913]={nameES="Chapter 12.4: A Change of Plans",objectivesES={"Your companions within Urmâkh eagerly await the tale of your adventures.","Corudan, Sirgon, and Rahâzi eagerly wait to hear the tale of your adventures","Corudan, Sirgon, and Rahâzi are within Urmâkh.","Sirgon is within the city of Urmâkh.","Sigileth waits for Silirtas to answer.","Your companions consider the tale you have woven","Silirtas is outside Adakûr in Imhûlar.","Talk to Silirtas outside Adakûr in Imhûlar","Rahâzi challenged you to speak with residents of Urmâkh and learn their opinions of Gondor.","Talk to Sirgon within Urmâkh","Corudan, Sirgon, and Rahâzi are within the city of Urmâkh.","With Kûr Anzar occupied by soldiers and cultists of the Church of the All-seeing, your travelling companions must have gone somewhere else.","Tell your companions what befell you while you were apart","Find your travelling companions somewhere in Imhûlar, perhaps in the city of Urmâkh","Talk to Corudan within Urmâkh","Find your travelling companions in the village of Urmâkh, north-west of Adakûr.","Talk to Rahâzi within Urmâkh","Chapter 12.4: A Change of Plans"}},
[2914]={nameES="Chapter 12.4: The Glory of the Bright Company",objectivesES={"Chapter 12.4: The Glory of the Bright Company","Talk to Glorfindel on Tol Send and complete 'Instance: The Glory of the Bright Company'","Talk to Glorfindel on Tol Send","Glorfindel is on Tol Send. He has agreed to finish the tale begun by the shade of Isildur, despite his misgivings.","Glorfindel has volunteered to finish the tale begun by the shade of Isildur, for he fought alongside the Bright Company and remembers both the triumph and the sorrow they encountered within the Dark Tower.","Glorfindel is on Tol Send.","Talk to Gandalf on Tol Send","Gandalf is on Tol Send."}},
[2915]={nameES="Chapter 12.5: Not An Enemy, If Not A Friend",objectivesES={"Rahâzi wants you to defeat cultists throughout Imhûlar, especially in the occupied city of Kûr Anzar.","Sirgon has spoken with the people of Urmâkh and wants you to bring them, on behalf of Gondor, some of the ingredients for which they have asked.","Chapter 12.5: Not An Enemy, If Not A Friend","Bring the ingredients to Sharûkh within Urmâkh","Talk to Sirgon within Urmâkh","Sirgon is within Urmâkh.","Talk to Irnamar within Urmâkh","Sirgon wants to prove that Gondor is not a threat to the people of Shagâna.","Sharûkh is within Urmâkh, waiting for you to bring the ingredients Sirgon promised.","Irnamar is within Urmâkh.","Rahâzi is within Urmâkh.","Talk to Rahâzi within Urmâkh"}},
[2916]={nameES="Chapter 12.5: The End of the Tale",objectivesES={"His memory restored by the words of Glorfindel, much that was hidden from Gandalf has been returned to him: pain, loss, and suffering, but knowledge also.","Elrond is on Tol Send, and he wishes to pick up the tale where Gandalf has left it.","Talk to Elrond on Tol Send","Chapter 12.5: The End of the Tale"}},
[2917]={nameES="Chapter 12.6: Among the Furrows",objectivesES={"Now abandoned by its former occupants, this camp will suit your purpose","The rest of your travelling company has gone ahead to scout the road into Urash Dâr, and you should help them prepare for the next leg of their pursuit.","Light the camp-fire at the abandoned town in Urash Dâr","Talk to Belondor at the road into Urash Dâr","The fire dances, bringing new life to the abandoned town","Talk to Rothog at the road into Urash Dâr","Talk to Silirtas at your new campsite in Urash Dâr","Wait for your companions to arrive","Meet up with the rest of your travelling party in north-east Imhûlar, on the road into Urash Dâr","Belondor stands by the road leading into Urash Dâr.","You have been charged with setting up camp at the abandoned town to the north-west in Urash Dâr.","Talk to Khôltekh at the road into Urash Dâr","Belondor stands by the road that runs into Urash Dâr.","You tell Belondor about your adventures, but make no mention of Balakhad","Belondor is at the road into Urash Dâr, waiting to hear what befell you and Sigileth after you parted in Ghalbûru.","Find the abandoned town to the north-west in Urash Dâr","You have been charged with setting up camp at the abandoned town in Urash Dâr.","Tell Belondor a careful version of what befell you since you parted in Ghalbûru","Belondor sees you approach and calls out a greeting","Khôltekh and Rothog listened to your story, and they have some thoughts of their own.","Chapter 12.6: Among the Furrows","Your companions arrive and try to make themselves at home","A good location for a camp can be found to the north-west in Urash Dâr, at a town recently abandoned by its former occupants.","Silirtas is at your new campsite in Urash Dâr.","The rest of your travelling party should be in north-east Imhûlar, on the road into Urash Dâr."}},
[2918]={nameES="Chapter 12.7: Something Has Awoken",objectivesES={"Silirtas senses that something evil dwells within Urash Dâr, and she is troubled by its presence.","Talk to Mithrandir at your campsite in Urash Dâr","Silirtas wants you to creep closer and <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> for what might be happening within Maurûsh.","Silirtas is at your campsite in Urash Dâr, preparing to go with you to Maurûsh.","Talk to Silirtas at your new campsite in Urash Dâr","Silirtas is at your campsite in Urash Dâr.","Talk to Silirtas at your campsite in Urash Dâr","Mithrandir has come to your campsite in Urash Dâr.","Sigileth coughs apologetically and draws you aside","The sound of Orkish voices, not of the Ordâkhai, drifts from Maurûsh","All seems still within Maurûsh","Silirtas does not speak again, but it is clear she has been deeply hurt. Sigileth begins to say something, but then decides against it.\
\
The three of you prepare to depart for Maurûsh.","Talk to Sigileth at your campsite in Urash Dâr","Silirtas wants you to cross the river to the west and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at the stone keep of Maurûsh.","Sigileth is at your campsite in Urash Dâr.","Cross the river to the west and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> in the direction of Maurûsh","Creep closer and <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> for sounds from Maurûsh","Silirtas is at your new campsite in Urash Dâr.","Talk to Silirtas and go with her into Maurûsh","Chapter 12.7: Something Has Awoken"}},
[2919]={nameES="Chapter 12.8: Friends From the North",objectivesES={"Talk to Mithrandir at your campsite in Urash Dâr","Talk to Elrohir in Urash Dâr","Find Legolas and Gimli to the north-west of your campsite","Whether by chance or plan, friends have come from afar to lend you their aid. Now they must be brought together to face this new danger.","Talk to Gimli in Urash Dâr","Find Glorfindel to the east of your campsite","Talk to Glorfindel in Urash Dâr","Legolas and Gimli greet you warmly","Talk to Legolas in Urash Dâr","Find Elladan and Elrohir to the north-east of your campsite","Mithrandir has sent you to recall the scouts he sent to the north-west and north-east of Urash Dâr.","Glorfindel greets you cordially, but his expression remains solemn","Talk to Elladan in Urash Dâr","Elladan and Elrohir look around curiously, intrigued by the rocks of Urash Dâr","Chapter 12.8: Friends From the North","Mithrandir is at your campsite in Urash Dâr."}},
[2920]={nameES="Chapter 12.9: Legacy of Morgoth",objectivesES={"Hear what Mithrandir has to say about the Elder Orcs","Hear what Mithrandir has to say about the Grim Southron","Mithrandir is at your campsite in Urash Dâr.","Mithrandir has much to say about a number of different subjects.","Mithrandir wishes to tell you what he has learned about the Geas of Morgoth, and what it could mean for Middle-earth.","Talk to Mithrandir at your campsite in Urash Dâr","Hear what Mithrandir has to say about the Kintai","Hear what Mithrandir has to say about the Dark Lord Sauron","Chapter 12.9: Legacy of Morgoth","Hear what Mithrandir has to say about the Thardúth"}},
[2921]={nameES="Capítulo 12: Los ejércitos de Gathbúrz",objectivesES={"Lleva los planes de batalla a Ningloril","Ningloril está en Thangúlhad, el campamento más cercano de la Hueste Dorada a Dol Guldur.\
\
Has derrotado a los comandantes uruk en Búrzkala, Kúfuzg y Hongoi y has recuperado algunos de sus planes de batalla. Ningloril está esperando tu regreso.","Búrzkala, Kúfuzg y Hongoi son campamentos orcos en las regiones del norte de Gathbúrz.\
\
Ningloril te ha pedido que mates a los comandantes uruk de los grandes campamentos del norte de Gathbúrz y que busques en los campamentos planes de batalla.","Has derrotado a un comandante uruk en Hongoi","Derrota a un comandante uruk en Kúfuzg","Derrota a un comandante uruk en Búrzkala","Derrota a un comandante uruk en Hongoi","Los ejércitos orcos de Dol Guldur se están reuniendo en grandes campamentos en las regiones del norte de Gathbúrz.","Has derrotado a un comandante uruk en Kúfuzg","Capítulo 12: Los ejércitos de Gathbúrz","Has derrotado a un comandante uruk en Búrzkala"}},
[2922]={nameES="Chapter 12: The Bearer of the Sword",objectivesES={"Saeradan is at his camp in the Windfells.\
\
You have found the former bearer of the sword, but he was not one of the Rohirrim at all. It was Wadu of the Uch-lûth, and when you arrived he was already dead. You should bring the news to Saeradan.","Find the fallen Man of Rohan along the road and try to save him","Talk to Saeradan at Echad Saeradan","Chapter 12: The Bearer of the Sword","Saeradan has asked you to find the unfortunate bearer of the Rohirrim sword you recovered from the blockade of the road in the Windfells.","Saeradan listens to your account, and his confusion is evident.\
\
'I am sorry indeed to hear that Wadu has been slain, but I cannot understand how he came to possess the sword that was taken from him. It is without doubt a sword of the Rohirrim, and the Men of Rohan are no friend to the clans of Dunland. There is a long history of war between the two, and I fear that if Saruman's plans continue to bear fruit there will be war again.\
\
'Why would Wadu have borne such a sword? And what brought him to that road to die? Was he so o'ermatched in number that even such a well-crafted sword could avail him nothing?'","The former bearer of the Rohirrim sword may be close to death somewhere on the road south of the blockade in the Windfells.\
\
Saeradan wants you to search the road, starting at the blockaded north gate and working your way south, looking for the fallen Rohirrim.","The bearer of the sword was not one of the Rohirrim after all...it was Wadu, and he is dead"}},
[2923]={nameES="Capítulo 12: El Guardián del Agua",objectivesES={"Ráthwald se encuentra en el arco en ruinas cerca de Echad Dúnann, en Eregion.\
\
Has ahuyentado al Guardián del Agua y los enanos han entrado en Moria por fin.","Capítulo 12: El Guardián del Agua","Te has vuelto competente con un arma perdida de los Días Antiguos, y los enanos de la expedición de Bósi están seguros de que ahora puedes enfrentarte al Guardián del Agua.","Ráthwald se encuentra en el arco en ruinas cerca de Echad Dúnann, en Eregion.\
\
Ahora que tienes un arma lo suficientemente poderosa para hacer daño al Guardián del Agua, Ráthwald te espera para llevarte a Bósi.","Habla con Ráthwald y viaja para enfrentarte al Guardián"}},
[2924]={nameES="Chapter 13.1: Evil In The Canyons",objectivesES={"Rahâzi is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","From here you should be able to sketch the map for Khôltekh","Talk to Rothog at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","Rothog asked you to defeat Orcs throughout Urash Dâr.\
Glorfindel asked you to collect jackal teeth and craban claws from creatures throughout Urash Dâr so he can examine them for unusual effects or signs of corruption.\
Khôltekh asked you to draw him a map to the ruins of Ashâgir in north-west Urash Dâr.","The evils that have awoken within Urash Dâr spell an uncertain future for not just the people of Ikorbân, but for all of Middle-earth.","Glorfindel is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","Talk to Khôltekh at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","You sketch a map to Ashâgir for Khôltekh","You hear Rahâzi calling for you from the vicinity of the camp-fire","Chapter 13.1: Evil In The Canyons","Bring the map you sketched to Khôltekh at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","Talk to Rahâzi at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","Talk to Glorfindel at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","Rothog is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","Khôltekh is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","Bring the teeth and claws to Glorfindel at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","Some of your companions at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr have begun to devise plans for combatting the Thardúth and the Elder Orcs that serve them.","Sketch a map to Ashâgir on the parchment Khôltekh gave to you","Find a good place at which to sketch Khôltekh a map to Ashâgir"}},
[2925]={nameES="Chapter 13.1: Two Years of Peace",objectivesES={"Gandalf is on Tol Send, deep in thought.","Talk to the shade of Isildur on Tol Send","After the defeat of Sauron, Isildur faced a number of challenges during the two years preceding his death on the Gladden Fields and the loss of the One Ring.","Chapter 13.1: Two Years of Peace","Gandalf strokes his beard and nods. It is the Wizard's way of asking for attention","Grimbeorn is at the Beorninghús.\
\
Gandalf thinks you should return to the Beorninghús and speak with Grimbeorn.","The shade of Isildur is on Tol Send.","Talk to Grimbeorn at the Beorninghús","Talk to Gandalf on Tol Send"}},
[2926]={nameES="Chapter 13.2: Grimbeorn's Interruption",objectivesES={"Firewood can be found near the base of trees in the Beorning-lands, and Orcs and wargs still threaten the peace of the Beornings.","Thindrif is at the Forest Gate.","Bring the crumpled note to Gandalf inside the Beorninghús","Bring the firewood to Grimbeorn at the Beorninghús","You found the missing Orc's hiding-place. He is dead, but carries a crumpled note","Thindrif invited you to search the corpses of the Orcs for some clue as to why they attempted to pass through the Forest Gate.","You search the Orc but find nothing to explain its presence here","Chapter 13.2: Grimbeorn's Interruption","Gandalf is inside the Beorninghús.","A number of dead Orcs lie near the Forest Gate","Grimbeorn has not forgotten that Gandalf and the Elves are relying upon his hospitality, and he has some chores for you.","This Orc bears the symbol of Ugrukhôr, Captain of the Pit","Thindrif thinks one of the Orcs might have escaped into the Beorning-lands during the commotion.","You find nothing of interest on the dead Orc","You found a crumpled note clutched in the hand of the Orc that fled through the Forest Gate.","This Orc died wielding his sword, but it did not protect him","Go to the Forest Gate on the edge of Eryn Lasgalen","Talk to Thindrif at the Forest Gate","Search the Beorning-lands for the missing Orc's hiding-place","The note speaks of something called 'Falch Gurth' in which Gandalf may be interested","Grimbeorn is waiting for you at the Beorninghús.","Read the crumpled note you found on the missing Orc","Grimbeorn has not heard from the Elves at the Forest Gate in some time, and despite his reticence to restart trade with the Elves, he worries about the silence."}},
[2927]={nameES="Chapter 13.2: The Hour Is Late",objectivesES={"Sigileth is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","Talk to Silirtas at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","Sigileth bids you farewell and leaves on her mission","Rahâzi is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","<rgb=#00FF00>Wave</rgb> to Silirtas at Ilzag Khûl","Wait for the emissaries to depart","<rgb=#00FF00>Wave</rgb> to Rahâzi at Ilzag Khûl","Talk to Belondor at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","<rgb=#00FF00>Wave</rgb> to Belondor at Ilzag Khûl","Silirtas takes a deep breath, and then heaves a sigh","Belondor raises his hand in farewell","<rgb=#00FF00>Wave</rgb> to Sigileth at Ilzag Khûl","You choose not to mention that Sigileth shares this quality with her brother","Mithrandir believes facing the threat posed by the Thardúth will need the strong cooperation of many peoples: the Shagâni, the Kintai, and the Umbari.","Belondor is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","Chapter 13.2: The Hour Is Late","The emissaries have left on their missions.","Talk to Mithrandir at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","Talk to Sigileth at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","Silirtas is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","Rahâzi nods and bids you farewell, for now","Mithrandir is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr."}},
[2928]={nameES="Chapter 13.3: Hidden and Never Found",objectivesES={"Corudan stands outside Ashâgir, atop the north-west cliffs in Urash Dâr.","Khôltekh stands within the undisturbed chamber deep within Ashâgir.","Talk to Khôltekh in the undisturbed chamber deep within Ashâgir","Meet with Khôltekh outside Ashâgir atop the north-west cliffs in Urash Dâr","Khôltekh grins widely at you, his eyes alight","Talk to Corudan in the undisturbed chamber deep within Ashâgir","Can this be the hidden cache of Narghâk sought by Khôltekh?","Chapter 13.3: Hidden and Never Found","Talk to Khôltekh at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","Somewhere inside the depths of Ashâgir, Khôltekh believes you will find a chamber containing a lost, hidden cache of Narghâk.","Mithrandir worries that the secrets buried within Urash Dâr might spell doom for not just the folk of Shagâna, but for all of Middle-earth as well.","Talk to Khôltekh outside Ashâgir in Urash Dâr","Corudan stands within the undisturbed chamber deep within Ashâgir.","Khôltekh can be found at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.\
\
Corudan is concerned about Khôltekh's apparent discovery of a cache of Narghâk, the Hungry Fire.","Talk to Corudan outside Ashâgir in Urash Dâr","Khôltekh stands outside Ashâgir, to the north-west in Urash Dâr.","Khôltekh asked to meet you and Corudan outside Ashâgir, to the north-west in Urash Dâr.","Talk to Corudan at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","Search the depths of Ashâgir for a hidden chamber containing the cache of Narghâk","Corudan is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr."}},
[2929]={nameES="Chapter 13.3: The Picture Painted",objectivesES={"Talk to Gandalf inside the Beorninghús","Chapter 13.3: The Picture Painted","Gandalf is inside the Beorninghús, waiting to divulge what he has learned from his study of the Black Book of Mordor.","Talk to Gandalf and complete 'Instance: The Picture Painted'","Gandalf has continued his study of the Black Book of Mordor, and he has much to tell you.","Gandalf is inside the Beorninghús, shaken by what he has learned from the Black Book of Mordor."}},
[2930]={nameES="Chapter 13.4: A Greater Power",objectivesES={"Talk to Mithrandir during the Dagor Carlanthir","Talk to Legolas to the north within the channel of the River Mûshid","Khôltekh admits, with regret, that the shipping of the Narghâk out of Urash Dâr will have to wait until the threat of the Thardúth has passed, and that will require something he does not relish: a confrontation.","Legolas is to the north within the channel of the River Mûshid that runs through Urash Dâr.\
\
Mithrandir has sent much of your travelling company along the river to the north-east, where he believes the Thardúth dwell. He asked you to speak with them during the approach.","Talk to Glorfindel within the channel of the River Mûshid","Talk to Corudan outside Utug-bûr","Meet with Glorfindel to the north-east within the channel of the River Mûshid","Corudan is outside Utug-bûr, in north-east Urash Dâr.","Most of your travelling party has arrived at the approach to Utug-bûr, to the distant north-east in Urash Dâr.","Mithrandir commands your allied forces during the Dagor Carlanthir, the Battle of the Red Waterfall.","Talk to Mithrandir outside Utug-bûr","Silirtas is outside Utug-bûr, in north-east Urash Dâr.","Chapter 13.4: A Greater Power","Talk to Mithrandir at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","Glorfindel is to the north-east within the channel of the River Mûshid that runs through Urash Dâr.\
\
Mithrandir has sent much of your travelling company along the river to the north-east, where he believes the Thardúth dwell. He asked you to speak with them during the approach.","Talk to Silirtas outside Utug-bûr","Legolas is to the north within the channel of the River Mûshid that runs through Urash Dâr.\
\
Mithrandir has sent much of your travelling company along the river to the north, where he believes the Thardúth dwell. He asked you to speak with them during the approach.","Meet up with the rest of your travelling party to the distant north-east outside Utug-bûr","Mithrandir is outside Utug-bûr, in the north-eastern reaches of Urash Dâr.","Mithrandir is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","Talk to Corudan outside Utug-bûr and stand against Azagath","Meet with Legolas to the north within the channel of the River Mûshid"}},
[2931]={nameES="Chapter 13.4: The Road to the Moon-lands",objectivesES={"Soldiers of Ithilien are hard-pressed at Fennas Gost, the Dread Door","Find the bridge of Gúliant over the Morgulduin, west along the road","The walls of the Dead City tower above you, monumental and menacing","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> at Minas Morgul when you emerge from the trees along the road, by the stone pillar","Beregond asked you to defeat foes throughout Rath Dúath, and to scout the terrain by <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb>ing at several important landmarks within Imlad Morgul.","Faramir, Prince of Ithilien, can be found near the Bridge of Gúliant in Imlad Morgul.","Fennas Gost, the Dread Door on the outskirts of Gorgoroth, provides access to Imlad Morgul.","Talk to Beregond at Echad Uial","Follow the road west of Echad Uial, until you emerge from the trees near a stone pillar","Find Echad Uial in Imlad Morgul","An injured Ranger at Fennas Gost has called to you, hoping to prevent you from suffering as he has.","Beregond is at Echad Uial in Imlad Morgul.","Beregond hails you warmly, welcoming you to Echad Uial","The dark waters of the Morgulduin rush beneath the stones of Gúliant","Chapter 13.4: The Road to the Moon-lands","Talk to Faramir at the Bridge of Gúliant","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> at the environs from the bridge of Gúliant","This is one of the locations Beregond described","Echad Uial is west of Fennas Gost, in Imlad Morgul.","According to Gandalf, the problem posed by Gothmog has become too serious to bear. Your road leads now to Imlad Morgul, where the creature that was once King Eärnur now lurks.","Travel to Fennas Gost on the outskirts of Imlad Morgul","Talk to the injured Ranger at Fennas Gost"}},
[2932]={nameES="Chapter 13.5: The Dagor Carlanthir",objectivesES={"Belondor stands near Mithrandir during the Dagor Carlanthir.","Mithrandir struggles against a distant, invisible foe, and says nothing further to you.","Mithrandir commands the allied forces during the Dagor Carlanthir.","Corudan stands near Mithrandir during the Dagor Carlanthir.","Talk to Corudan during the Dagor Carlanthir and help him seal Utug-bûr","The Dagor Carlanthir rages in Urash Dâr as the servants of the waking Thardúth bring war against the people of Ikorbân and their allies.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>To return to the Dagor Carlanthir in the event you leave it, you can use a banner at your campsite of Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr to return to the fighting.</rgb>","Mithrandir struggles against a distant opponent during the Dagor Carlanthir.","Mithrandir commands the allied forces on the south-western bank of the river during the Dagor Carlanthir.","The Dagor Carlanthir rages in Urash Dâr.","Chapter 13.5: The Dagor Carlanthir","Talk to Belondor during the Dagor Carlanthir","Talk to Corudan during the Dagor Carlanthir","Talk to Mithrandir during the Dagor Carlanthir"}},
[2933]={nameES="Chapter 13.5: The Watch on the Dead City",objectivesES={"Faramir has returned, and another familiar face has also come to Echad Uial","Many foes lie in wait beyond the entrance to the Dead City","Faramir, Prince of Ithilien, has been kept busy maintaining the watch on Minas Morgul.","Mithrandir has made the journey to Echad Uial.","The entrance to Minas Morgul is located at the end of the road south of the Bridge of Gúliant.\
\
Faramir asked you to do battle with the foes you find in the Dead City.","Climb the ramp between the second and third tiers of Minas Morgul, north-west of the Song-house of Lindalírë","Faramir is at Echad Uial, waiting for you to report on what you encountered in the Dead City.","Talk to Nâlunitir on the ramp between the second and third tiers of the city, north-west of the Song-house of Lindalírë","Talk to Mithrandir at Echad Uial","Talk to Faramir at Echad Uial","You found a mortally-wounded Morgul cultist on the ramp between the second and third tiers of Minas Morgul, north-west of the Song-house of Lindalírë.","Return to Echad Uial and find Faramir","Nâlunitir succumbs to her wounds, a smile on her lips","Passage between the second and third tiers of Minas Morgul can be found north-west of the Song-house of Lindalírë.","Find the main entrance to the city of Minas Morgul","Chapter 13.5: The Watch on the Dead City","Suffering from mortal wounds, a Morgul cultist spits curses at you","Faramir intended to return to Echad Uial. You should find him there and tell him what you learned from the dying Morgul cultist."}},
[2934]={nameES="Chapter 13.6: The Madness In His Eyes",objectivesES={"Sirgon has sustained a grievous wound, but his allies still fight to defend him","Corudan stands outside Utug-bûr during the Dagor Carlanthir.","Belondor has returned at the head of a small army of Umbari reinforcements, but even that may not be enough to turn the tide of the battle.","Sirgon has been grievously injured during the Dagor Carlanthir.","Elladan stands his ground against the encircling foes, but says nothing else.","Hoping against hope, you check the Kinta Elf for some sign of life, but there are none to be found. Silirtas is dead.","Talk to Sirgon during the Dagor Carlanthir","Over the sound of fighting you hear Corudan calling for you to the east","Talk to Corudan outside Utug-bûr during the Dagor Carlanthir","Talk to Elladan during the Dagor Carlanthir","Go to the front line of the Dagor Carlanthir, to the north-east","Belondor wants to send some of his soldiers to fight alongside Sirgon at the front line to the north-east.","Talk to Corudan and help him place the caches of Narghâk outside Utug-bûr","Silirtas is dead.","Talk to Corudan in the middle of the river during the Dagor Carlanthir","The Dagor Carlanthir rages all around you","Chapter 13.6: The Madness In His Eyes","Corudan stands in the middle of the river during the Dagor Carlanthir.","Examine Silirtas during the Dagor Carlanthir","The Dagor Carlanthir rages all around you.","Elladan fights by Sirgon's side during the Dagor Carlanthir.","Silirtas lies outside Utug-bûr during the Dagor Carlanthir."}},
[2935]={nameES="Chapter 13.6: The Sword and the Stonemaiden",objectivesES={"Talk to Faramir at Echad Uial","Chapter 13.6: The Sword and the Stonemaiden","Talk to Mithrandir in Echad Uial and complete 'Instance: The Sword and the Stonemaiden'","Beregond is at Echad Uial.","Unwilling to remain behind in the Vales of Anduin, Mithrandir has come to Echad Uial with the Black Book of Mordor.","Faramir is at Echad Uial.","Mithrandir is at Echad Uial, waiting to discuss what else he has learned from the Black Book of Mordor.","Talk to Beregond at Echad Uial"}},
[2936]={nameES="Chapter 13.7: Searching for Something",objectivesES={"Annoth may have climbed the stairs leading to Cirith Ungol. But when did he pass this way, and did he survive?","Beregond charged the soldier Annoth with some tasks around Echad Uial, but Annoth has set his own plan in motion.","Annoth is among the rocky crags within sight of the bottom of the Winding Stair.","Search for some sign of Ugrukhôr among the crags to the north-east of Annoth","Bring the report to Annoth not far from the base of the Winding Stair","Talk to Annoth among the crags not far from the base of the Winding Stair","Look for Annoth further along the rocky path","The location Annoth marked on the map is north-west of Minas Morgul, up in the mountains. That may be where he has gone.","Bring the report to Mithrandir at Echad Uial","Annoth's dagger is embedded in the map, marking a location north-west of Minas Morgul","Annoth waves a greeting. He does not seem surprised to see you","You found a crumpled parchment in the hand of Ugrukhôr's captain. What secrets lie within?\
\
The soldier Annoth will be interested to see the report you found.","Travel to the location Annoth marked on the map, north-west of Minas Morgul, up in the mountains","Examine the map on the table to the west in Echad Uial","This dead Orc bears Ugrukhôr's symbol, and carries a report for his master","Dagoras catches your eye and calls you over","Beregond charged Annoth with a number of duties to perform by the tent surrounded with crates in Echad Uial, to the north-west of his position.","Talk to Dagoras at Echad Uial","You found a crumpled parchment in the hand of Ugrukhôr's captain. What secrets lie within?\
\
Gandalf will be interested to see the report you found. Return to the Wizard at Echad Uial.","Booted footprints lead to the south-east. Did Annoth come this way?","Dagoras saw Annoth studying the map in Echad Uial, to the west.","Look for Annoth by the tent north-west of Beregond in Echad Uial","Annoth asked you to search for signs of Ugrukhôr up the path to the north-east, among the crags.","Dagoras is in Echad Uial.","Chapter 13.7: Searching for Something"}},
[2937]={nameES="Chapter 13.7: Sigileth In The Darkness",objectivesES={"Talk to Mithrandir at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","Corudan has begged you to rescue Sigileth from within Utug-bûr before it is too late.","Corudan stands outside Utug-bûr during the Dagor Carlanthir.","Talk to Corudan and go with him into the darkness of Utug-bûr","Chapter 13.7: Sigileth In The Darkness","Mithrandir is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr."}},
[2938]={nameES="Chapter 13.8: Guardians of the Tower",objectivesES={"Faramir is at his camp of Echad Uial.","Talk to Mithrendan in the centre of the tier troubled by merrevail, in Minas Morgul","A watchful presence stands guard at the entrance to the tower, barring your passage","Mithrandir is waiting for you to return to Echad Uial with word of what guards the entrance to Barad Cúron.","Foes sworn to many different masters stalk the various levels of Minas Morgul.\
\
Faramir asked you to defeat enemies throughout the Dead City and to meet up with the Rangers Mithrendan and Culang on the upper levels.","The entrance to Barad Cúron is guarded by a watchful presence. Culang warned you to be careful, but if you are to gain access to Gothmog's lair inside the tower you will need to dare the guardians.","The watchful presence is unmoved by your need, and bars your passage","The watchful presence regards you coldly, its malice coalescing before you, a solid wall of impassability. You are reminded of the spirit in the watching-stone outside the cavern of Nargroth, but this presence has a different feeling than Zaghárog. There was a mischievous bent to Zaghárog's evil; here there is order, a reverence for rules and commands that the other spirit of your acquaintance did not possess.\
\
'None but Gúrzyul and their servants may pass,' the spirit whispers in your mind, and you see an image of Gothmog standing before the tower, making known his pronouncement before the watching-stone. The spirit in the stone serves Gothmog, and will carry out his command.","Talk to Mithrandir at Echad Uial","Culang will be interested to hear what guards the entrance to Barad Cúron.","Talk to Faramir at Echad Uial","A watchful presence stands guard at the entrance to Barad Cúron.","Investigate the entrance to Barad Cúron, the Tower of the Crescent Moon, south of Culang's position","Talk to the watchful presence that bars entrance to Barad Cúron","Talk to Culang on the uppermost tier of Minas Morgul","Chapter 13.8: Guardians of the Tower","Mithrandir wants you to adventure once again in Minas Morgul and investigate the enchantments that must bar the path to the Tower of the Crescent Moon."}},
[2939]={nameES="Chapter 13.8: Last Words",objectivesES={"The Dagor Carlanthir has ended, but the cost of victory was high and left its mark upon those who were there.","Sigileth is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","Jaith stands guard outside the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja.","Húrshauk rumbles at you appreciatively","Talk to Rothog at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","Talk to Girhâzi at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","Talk to Belondor at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","Sirgon embarks upon his final voyage, and speaks no more","Girhâzi and Rahâzi are at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","Talk to Khôltekh at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","Chapter 13.8: Last Words","Sigileth says nothing further.","Rothog's lion Húrshauk is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","Return to Hármelak in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja, in Umbar Baharbêl","Húrshauk waits for you to <rgb=#00FF00>pat</rgb> him","Corudan is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","Talk to Rahâzi at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","Hármelak is in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja, in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.","Rothog's lion Húrshauk looks at you pointedly","Belondor is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","Talk to Jaith outside the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja","Talk to Corudan at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","Rothog is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","Talk to Mithrandir at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","Khôltekh is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","Talk to Hármelak in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja","Talk to Sigileth at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","Sirgon is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr.","Hármelak watches as you approach her dais","Talk to Sirgon at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr","Mithrandir is at Ilzag Khûl in Urash Dâr."}},
[2940]={nameES="Chapter 13.9: The Warrior Remade",objectivesES={"Talk to Mithrandir at the Eagle and Star","A familiar figure nods in greeting","Mithrandir has come to the Eagle and Star.","Investigate the mysterious figure in the darkened corner of the tavern","Aragorn is at the Eagle and Star, and he wishes to tell you the story of Eärnur's last days.","Aragorn is at the Eagle and Star.","The door of the tavern swings open and Mithrandir enters","Ayorzén watches you guardedly, and with suspicion","Ayorzén says nothing, his eyes still fixed upon the mask of Karazgar.","Ayorzén does not know the disguise you had in mind","Talk to Aragorn at the Eagle and Star","Talk to Ayorzén at the Eagle and Star","Talk to Aragorn and complete 'Instance: The Warrior Remade'","Find Ayorzén at the Eagle and Star, in Minas Tirith","Ayorzén's eyes widen in surprise","Mithrandir has a plan for you to deceive the guardians of Barad Cúron, but it will require some outside help.","Meldir told you that Ayorzén might be found at the Eagle and Star, a tavern south-west of the entrance to Minas Tirith.","Talk to Meldir just inside the entrance to Minas Tirith","Place the mask of Karazgar on the table in front of Ayorzén","Ayorzén is at the Eagle and Star in Minas Tirith.","You should place the mask of Karazgar on the table in front of Ayorzén, and enlist him to help you.","Ayorzén the Wily is at the Eagle and Star in Minas Tirith.","Talk to Ayorzén the Wily at the Eagle and Star","Mithrandir has directed your attention to a darkened corner in the room furthest from the entrance.","Aragorn has come to the Eagle and Star to meet with you, wearing a disguise that hides his identity.","Chapter 13.9: The Warrior Remade","The gossipmonger Meldir is just inside the entrance to Minas Tirith.\
\
Mithrandir has sent you to Minas Tirith seeking the assistance of Ayorzén, but first you need to find him."}},
[2941]={nameES="Capítulo 13: ¡Khazad-dûm al fin!",objectivesES={"Tulk está justo al otro lado de las Puertas de Durin, junto al lago inmóvil donde luchaste contra el Guardián del Agua.\
\
Te han dicho que hables con Tulk sobre los enanos que han entrado en Moria.","Capítulo 13: ¡Khazad-dûm al fin!","Los enanos por fin han entrado en Moria, pero su labor no ha hecho más que empezar. Tendrás que ayudarles en su lucha si quieren lograr algún éxito en las salas olvidadas de Khazad-dûm."}},
[2942]={nameES="Capítulo 13: Los estudiantes de Gorothúl",objectivesES={"Ningloril está en Thangúlhad, en Gathbúrz.\
\
Has derrotado a los espíritus crueles en los Pasajes de Cenizas y has recuperado los libros de hechizos utilizados por los estudiantes de Gorothúl para atarlos a su servicio.","Ningloril ha estudiado los planes que recuperaste y ha aprendido que los hechiceros bajo la tutela de Gorothúl están invocando espíritus crueles en los Pasajes de Cenizas.","Lleva los libros de hechizos a Ningloril para que sean destruidos","Los espíritus crueles y los hechiceros que los invocan se encuentran en Sâd Doldúr y en los Pasajes de Cenizas.\
\
Ningloril te ha pedido que derrotes a los espíritus crueles que están siendo atados al servicio de los estudiantes de Gorothúl en los Pasajes de Cenizas y que prives a los hechiceros de sus libros de hechizos.","Capítulo 13: Los estudiantes de Gorothúl"}},
[2943]={nameES="Chapter 13: The Sword Returned",objectivesES={"Find Wadu's sister Nona at Lhanuch and give her the ancient sword","Chapter 13: The Sword Returned","Find Wadu's father at Lhanuch and give him the ancient sword","Wadu's father Suvulch can be found somewhere within the Uch-lûth village of Lhanuch.\
\
You need to find the father of Wadu and bring him the sad news of his son's death. Additionally, he should be given the ancient sword of the Rohirrim that was taken from Wadu when he was slain.","Wadu's sister Nona can be found somewhere within Lhanuch, the village of the Uch-lûth, in Nan Laeglin.\
\
Suvulch has coldly dismissed the death of his son Wadu, calling him a coward. You should bring the news of Wadu's death and the ancient Rohirrim sword to his sister Nona instead.","The sword that was taken from Wadu should be returned to his family at the village of Lhanuch, in Nan Laeglin.","Nona listens sorrowfully as you recount your discovery of her brother's death. There is the briefest trembling within her deep eyes, then it is gone. The emotion mastered, Nona stares at you sternly.\
\
'Wadu was not the fighter our father Suvulch wanted him to be, and when he spoke to him, which was rarely, Suvulch was cruel. I tried to give Wadu the lessons he needed, lessons in the sword and the axe and the ways of fire, but I could not teach him the courage he needed. My words to him were harsh. If they drove him to his death I would have them back!'"}},
[2944]={nameES="Chapter 14.10: One People",objectivesES={"Glorfindel is in Sul Madásh.","Cúridwan is in Sul Madásh.","Chapter 14.10: One People","Talk to Sigileth in Sul Madásh","Inkanûsh is in Sul Madásh.","A hush has fallen over Sul Madásh.","A hush has fallen over Sul Madásh","In the aftermath of the Utûgi raid on Sul Madásh, Cúridwan has surprising news to share with the Kintai.","Talk to Cúridwan in Sul Madásh","Talk to Ulishár in Sul Madásh","Talk to Inkanûsh in Sul Madásh","<rgb=#00FF00>Sing</rgb> or <rgb=#00FF00>mourn</rgb> in your own way.","Ulishár is in Sul Madásh.","Sigileth is in Sul Madásh.","<rgb=#00FF00>Sing</rgb> or <rgb=#00FF00>mourn</rgb> in your own way","Talk to Glorfindel in Sul Madásh"}},
[2945]={nameES="Chapter 14.11: The Raiders Pursued",objectivesES={"Since you have returned to the grove of Laivárth, you should speak to Shadalith and see if everything is all right.","Examine the corpse of the dead Utûgi warrior","This warrior of the Utûgi died not to blade or arrow, but to something else","Inkanûsh is waiting in Sul Madásh for you to return with news of the raiding-party of Utûgi.","Find the fleeing Utûgi warriors near Laivárth","The creature that slew the Utûgi warriors has come back for you!","Shadalith wanted you to see what happened to her bucket in Laivárth.","Talk to Shadalith in Laivárth","Shadalith is in the grove of Laivárth.","The remaining Utûgi warriors escaped to the north-west, heading for the grove of Laivárth.","Inkanûsh asked you to pursue the Utûgi raiders before they cause further harm to the Kintai of Adagím.","Follow the escaping Utûgi north-west to the Hill of the Mother","Shadalith's bucket has fallen apart, spilling its water everywhere","Examine Shadalith's bucket in Laivárth","The other Utûgi warriors perished outside the grove of Laivárth.","One of the Utûgi succumbed to its wounds not far from the Hill of the Mother.","Something slew the last of the fleeing Utûgi outside Laivárth","One of the Utûgi, at least, succumbed to his wounds","Examine the corpse outside Laivárth... and survive","Talk to Inkanûsh in Sul Madásh","Chapter 14.11: The Raiders Pursued","The Utûgi escaped to the north-west. That way lies the Hill of the Mother!","Irsinith may have seen what befell the Utûgi raiding-party as it approached the Hill of the Mother.","Talk to Irsinith on the other side of Amûma at the Hill of the Mother","You survived your encounter with the spawn of Badharál"}},
[2946]={nameES="Chapter 14.1: The Closing Net",objectivesES={"Talk to Beregond in Echad Uial","Ayorzén has agreed to help you gain access to Barad Cúron, but even with the Easterling's aid this mission will not be free of danger.","Beregond is at Echad Uial, in Imlad Morgul.","Talk to Ayorzén at the Eagle and Star","Talk to Ayorzén on the uppermost tier of Minas Morgul","Chapter 14.1: The Closing Net","Ayorzén is on the uppermost tier of Minas Morgul.","Talk to Ayorzén at Echad Uial","Ayorzén has come to Echad Uial, in Imlad Morgul.","Ayorzén is at the Eagle and Star in Minas Tirith.","Mithrandir has returned to Echad Uial, in Imlad Morgul.","You tell Ayorzén how to get to Echad Uial","Orcs and other foes remain a danger within Minas Morgul, and you should thin their numbers before setting Mithrandir's plan into motion.","Culang is standing watch near the entrance to Barad Cúron on the uppermost tier of Minas Morgul.","Mithrandir calls you to speak with him","Talk to Culang on the uppermost tier of Minas Morgul","Talk to Mithrandir in Echad Uial"}},
[2947]={nameES="Chapter 14.1: Whispers of Wizardry",objectivesES={"Stand by the small knot of people to the south of Tasâdi and <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> to their conversation","Despite the claims of the Umbari that they would know the Wizard when he entered the city, just such a person has already arrived.","Some folk just past the fountain south of Phârex are discussing the effect a Wizard could have on the political situation of Umbar Baharbêl. You should <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> to their conversation.","Talk to Inkanûsh beside the Fathomwell beyond the archway","Stand by the small group of people to the south past the fountain and <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> to their conversation","Talk to Phârex at the Waterway Market","Ushrin has his own opinions concerning the effect of a Wizard on these lands.","Talk to Ushrin at the Waterway Market","Talk to Tasâdi at the Waterway Market","Tasâdi usually holds court at the Waterway Market to the south-east of Dâr Laja.","Phârex has caught your eye.","During a gap in the argument, you hear a familiar chuckle from beyond the archway","A small knot of people to the south of Tasâdi seem to be discussing what they have heard. You should <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> to their conversation.","A small knot of people to the south of Ushrin loudly discuss the rumours concerning a Wizard's powers. You should <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> to their conversation.","Chapter 14.1: Whispers of Wizardry","Umbar Baharbêl is alive with rumour that a Wizard will soon arrive to speak with the Kindred of the Coins about the many threats facing the city.","The opinions of these folk are split concerning the value a Wizard might provide","They notice you listening to their talk and quickly fall silent","Stand by the small group of people to the south of Ushrin and <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> to their conversation"}},
[2948]={nameES="Chapter 14.2: Gothmog's Rage",objectivesES={"Talk to Ayorzén on the uppermost tier of Minas Morgul and complete 'Instance: Gothmog's Rage'","The nearby presence of Isildur's bones has allowed his shade to assume physical form in Barad Cúron.","Talk to the shade of Isildur in Barad Cúron","Chapter 14.2: Gothmog's Rage","Ayorzén is on the uppermost tier of Minas Morgul, willing to help you gain access to the Tower of the Crescent Moon.","The time has come to deal with Gothmog. With Ayorzén's help, you hope to gain access to the Tower of the Crescent Moon and your long-time foe hiding within."}},
[2949]={nameES="Chapter 14.2: The Wizard, the Queen, and the Kindred",objectivesES={"Talk to Inkanûsh beside the Fathomwell and go with him to investigate the nearby commotion","The Wizard Inkanûsh wishes to go with you to investigate the nearby commotion. Speak with him beside the Fathomwell on the eastern side of the city.","Chapter 14.2: The Wizard, the Queen, and the Kindred","Inkanûsh stands by the stable-master at the Fleet-gate in south-eastern Umbar Baharbêl.","Talk to Inkanûsh by the stable-master at the Fleet-gate","The situation in these lands will demand careful handling by all of the affected parties: rulers, Wizards, soldiers, and common people alike."}},
[2950]={nameES="Chapter 14.3: A Casket of Dust",objectivesES={}},
[2951]={nameES="Chapter 14.3: Young Soldiers of Old Wars",objectivesES={"Chapter 14.3: Young Soldiers of Old Wars","Inkanûsh has come to the Kinta grove of Vartúlin in Imhûlar.","Inkanûsh believes your journey south alongside Shâra Mizâdi should begin in Imhûlar with stops at Urmâkh and Vartúlin.","Soldiers weary from battle slowly make their way up the road to Urmâkh","Inkanûsh coughs meaningfully, drawing your attention","Stand by the eastern gate of Urmâkh and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> for Mizâdi's returning soldiers","Glorfindel has arrived at Urmâkh, and wishes to speak with you about the next leg of your journey.","Soldiers that fought for Mizâdi at Kûr Anzar slowly climb the road to Urmâkh.","The Kinta Thórvilon tends the grove of Vartúlin, to the south-east of Urmâkh.","Talk to Shâra Mizâdi at the town of Urmâkh in Imhûlar","Shâra Mizâdi intends to rejoin her army near the town of Urmâkh in Imhûlar, and Inkanûsh asked you to speak with her there about her plans.","Talk to Thórvilon at Vartúlin, south-east of Urmâkh","Talk to Glorfindel inside the eastern gate of Urmâkh","Draw forth your foe and defeat him in the dead woods of Imhûlar outside Vartúlin","Search for some sign of the Utûgi to the north or north-east of Vartúlin","Inkanûsh fears that the Utûgi have drawn near to the grove of Vartúlin, and he wants you to search the dead woods nearby for some sign of their presence.","Shâra Mizâdi invited you to stand by the eastern gate of Urmâkh and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> for her returning soldiers.","Inkanûsh waits for the report of your scouting at the Kinta grove of Vartúlin in Imhûlar.","You feel hostile eyes upon you from somewhere close by","The Utûgi falls to the ground, defeated, but your fears are confirmed","Talk to Inkanûsh at the Kinta grove of Vartúlin in Imhûlar","Hostile eyes study you from nearby. You need to draw this foe out of hiding!"}},
[2952]={nameES="Chapter 14.4: A Vengeful Heart",objectivesES={"Talk to Culang in the throne room of Barad Cúron","Culang is in the throne room of Barad Cúron, concerned about the sound of newcomers approaching.","Culang is in the throne room of Barad Cúron.","Gothmog believes he is most deserving of Thuringwath's secrets, but his enemies encircle the tower and wish to challenge him for them.","Talk to Culang in the throne room and complete 'Instance: A Vengeful Heart'","Chapter 14.4: A Vengeful Heart","Gothmog stirs"}},
[2953]={nameES="Chapter 14.4: Calling On Cúridwan",objectivesES={"Chapter 14.4: Calling On Cúridwan","Inkanûsh has returned to the Kinta grove of Vartúlin in Imhûlar and wishes to speak with you.","Talk to Inkanûsh at Vartúlin","Inkanûsh has many questions to ask of the mysterious woman Cúridwan who dwells near Vartúlin.","Inkanûsh waits at Vartúlin for you and Glorfindel to go with him to speak with Cúridwan.","Talk to Inkanûsh at Vartúlin and go with him to speak with Cúridwan"}},
[2954]={nameES="Chapter 14.5: A Final Escape",objectivesES={"Ayorzén is waiting for you on the uppermost tier of Minas Morgul.","There is no sign of Ayorzén here either","Gothmog is in the throne room of Barad Cúron, trying to speak despite his wounds.","Talk to the shade of Isildur in the throne room of Barad Cúron","You should leave the tower and meet up with Ayorzén on the uppermost tier of the city","The shade of Isildur has asked you to bring the casket containing the dust of his bones out of Barad Cúron.","Chapter 14.5: A Final Escape","Mithrandir is at Echad Uial.","There is no sign of Ayorzén at the meeting-place. Perhaps he returned to Echad Uial?","Gothmog presses a broken key into your hand, and dies at last","You did not find Ayorzén at the meeting-place, and should look for him at Echad Uial.","Talk to Gothmog in the throne room of Barad Cúron","The shade of Isildur is in the throne room of Barad Cúron.","Meet up with Ayorzén outside Barad Cúron, on the uppermost tier of Minas Morgul","Death has come to Barad Cúron and claimed two of the masters of Mordor. How many countless others have perished in that cruel throne room over the years?","Talk to Mithrandir at Echad Uial","Talk to Faramir at Echad Uial","Prince Faramir is at Echad Uial.","Look for Ayorzén at Echad Uial","Pick up the casket of dust in the throne room","Bring the casket of dust and the broken key to Mithrandir at Echad Uial"}},
[2955]={nameES="Chapter 14.5: Rot of the Moulder-wood",objectivesES={"Shadalith is at the grove of Laivárth.","Talk to Athgai at the border with Adagím","Mauthark and Mokh Grazádh can be found among the swamps of Adagím.","Talk to Shadalith in Laivárth","Athgai told you to seek the grove of Laivárth, north-east along the path in Adagím.","Collect sample of the rot west of Laivárth","Talk to Glorfindel in Laivárth","Collected a sample of the rot north-east of Laivárth","Chapter 14.5: Rot of the Moulder-wood","Collected a sample of the rot north-west of Laivárth","Thórvilon is at the Kinta grove of Vartúlin, in Imhûlar.","Athgai stands at the border with Adagím.","Shadalith is in Laivárth.","Shadalith stands nearby in the grove of Laivárth.","Shadalith asked you to retrieve samples of the rot at locations to the north-east, north-west, and west of Laivárth.","Shadalith placed a bucket of water to the west. She wants you to add the samples of the blight you collected to the water so she can see if there is any effect.","Eager to speak with the mysterious Cúridwan, Inkanûsh wishes to travel with you into Adagím, the Moulder-wood, where a terrible blight has taken hold.","Collect sample of the rot north-west of Laivárth","You add the blight to the water and a noxious fume rises into the air","Collect sample of the rot north-east of Laivárth","A Kinta woman standing nearby murmurs her agreement","Add the blight samples to the water bucket in Laivárth","Glorfindel stands in the grove of Laivárth.","Collected a sample of the rot west of Laivárth","Find the grove of Laivárth in Adagím"}},
[2956]={nameES="Chapter 14.6: Beside the Weeping Mother",objectivesES={"Irsinith is at the Hill of the Mother in Adagím.","Irsinith is at Tûl Ama, the Hill of the Mother.","Talk to Glorfindel at the Hill of the Mother","Talk to Glorfindel at Tûl Ama","Talk to Irsinith at the Hill of the Mother","Irsinith asked you to collect venom-sacs, sickly wings, and damaged leaves from creatures located not far from the Hill of the Mother in Adagím.","Find Tûl Ama to the south-east of Laivárth","Fungal rot has already crept up the trunk of Amûma, the Old Mother of Adagím","Bring the venom sacs, wings, and leaves to Irsinith at the Hill of the Mother","Glorfindel stands sorrowfully by Amûma, the Old Mother of Adagím.","Tûl Ama, the Hill of the Mother, is to the south-east of Laivárth.","Chapter 14.6: Beside the Weeping Mother","The Kinta woman turns sorrowful eyes upon you","Grateful for the help you provided, Shadalith has suggested that you visit Tûl Ama, the Hill of the Mother, on your way to Sul Madásh.","Glorfindel is at the Hill of the Mother in Adagím."}},
[2957]={nameES="Chapter 14.7: Visitors to Sul Madásh",objectivesES={"Talk to Corudan in Sul Madásh","Corudan stands in the centre of Sul Madásh.","Kintai within Sul Madásh told you that the Kinta Ulishár might know of Cúridwan's whereabouts.","Inkanûsh stands at the southern entrance to Sul Madásh.","Find Ulishár to the east","The Kinta Ulishár has overheard your conversation and might have some advice for you.","Kintai within the grove of Sul Madásh may know of recent visitors.","Travel to the southern entrance of Sul Madásh","Talk to Inkanûsh at the southern entrance to Sul Madásh","The Kinta guardsman Baharúd stands at the southern entrance to Sul Madásh.","Talk to a Kinta of Sul Madásh north-east of the entrance","Talk to Ulishár in Sul Madásh","Talk to Baharúd at the southern entrance to Sul Madásh","Talk to another Kinta of Sul Madásh further into the grove","One of the Kinta coughs politely and holds up a questioning hand","The Kinta grove of Sul Madásh remains a bastion of health and beauty among the dead or dying trees of Adagím. Did Cúridwan come this way?","Chapter 14.7: Visitors to Sul Madásh","You have found a familiar face, if not the one you sought","A Kinta guardsman of the grove calls to you in greeting","Sul Madásh lies to the south-east of the Hill of the Mother, in Adagím."}},
[2958]={nameES="Chapter 14.8: Wandering Cúridwan",objectivesES={"Baharúd gazes away into the distance.","You see no sign of Cúridwan, but many dangers lurk that way","Cúridwan is at the Elderwell in Adagím.","Baharúd suggested that you travel west through the swamps to continue your search.","This would be a good place to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> for Cúridwan","Baharúd is at the southern entrance to Sul Madásh.","Talk to Cúridwan at the Elderwell","Talk to Sigileth in Sul Madásh","Travel west through the swamps to continue your search for Cúridwan","Cúridwan came to Adagím, but she never reached Sul Madásh. Where wandered the Golden Maiden?","Baharúd is in the swamps west of Sul Madásh, in Adagím.","Return to Sul Madásh and look for Cúridwan","Travel south-east of Sul Madásh through the swamp-land","Talk to Baharúd in the swamps south-east of Sul Madásh","Baharúd calls for a halt","Talk to Baharúd at the entrance to Sul Madásh","Baharúd is in the swamps south-east of Sul Madásh in Adagím.","Your search for Cúridwan now leads south-west to the Elderwell.","Cúridwan asked you to collect crocodile teeth and samples of the blight north-west of the Elderwell.","Baharúd stares around in disbelief.","At last you have located Cúridwan!","You have found Cúridwan!","Cúridwan is no longer at the Elderwell","Chapter 14.8: Wandering Cúridwan","Baharúd agreed to travel south-east of Sul Madásh and to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> with you for Cúridwan.","Cúridwan is waiting at the Elderwell for you to return with the things she requested.","Baharúd believes that Cúridwan may have gone to Sul Madásh. You hope he is right!","You have found Sigileth again!","Sigileth has finished speaking with the elders of Sul Madásh.","Baharúd stands among the blighted trees, deep in thought.","Travel south-west to the Elderwell in search of Cúridwan","Baharúd is at the Elderwell in Adagím.","Talk to Baharúd at the Elderwell","Bring the crocodile teeth and blight samples to Cúridwan at the Elderwell","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> for Cúridwan","Talk to Baharúd in the swamps west of Sul Madásh","Sigileth waves and calls you over to her"}},
[2959]={nameES="Chapter 14.9: A Shared Mission",objectivesES={"Talk to Cúridwan in Sul Madásh and ask that she explain herself","You have finally managed to track down Cúridwan. If fortune smiles, she will have the answers to Inkanûsh's questions.","Talk to Inkanûsh in Sul Madásh and go with him to speak to Cúridwan","Talk to Sigileth in Sul Madásh","Inkanûsh is in Sul Madásh and ready to speak to Cúridwan.","The Utûgi have been driven away from Sul Madásh, but they leave sorrow in their wake.","Inkanûsh is in Sul Madásh.","Chapter 14.9: A Shared Mission","Talk to Ulishár in Sul Madásh","Talk to Inkanûsh in Sul Madásh","Her words hang on the air","Ulishár weeps for his brother, and you go unnoticed.","Cúridwan stands in Sul Madásh."}},
[2960]={nameES="Capítulo 14: Thangulhad en peligro",objectivesES={"La Hueste Dorada está en peligro, ya que los ejércitos de Gathburz están a punto de ser desatados sobre Thangulhad.","Habla con Ellunen en Thangulhad","Capítulo 14: Thangulhad en peligro","Ellunen está en Thangulhad, preparando su defensa.\
\
Ningloril te ha pedido que vengas a la defensa de Thangulhad y te ha dirigido a hablar con Ellunen.","Ellunen te espera para que participes en la defensa de Thangulhad.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión implica una escaramuza que se puede completar en tamaños de grupo Solitario, Duo, Pequeña Comunidad, Comunidad o incursión usando el Panel de Escaramuzas. Esta escaramuza tiene un nivel mínimo de 60.</rgb>","Ellunen está en Thangulhad, el campamento de la Hueste Dorada en Gathburz.\
\
Has ayudado a defender Thangulhad y deberías ir a informar a Ellunen ahora.","Completa la escaramuza: Los protectores de Thangulhad"}},
[2961]={nameES="Chapter 14: The Distant Dwarf",objectivesES={"The ingredients needed by Frithgeir to make the brew can be found throughout Thrór's Coomb. He gave you a list of the ingredients and their locations to study.\
\
Frithgeir can make a brew that brings Nár back to awareness.","Chapter 14: The Distant Dwarf","Talk to Frithgeir at Zudrugund","Frithgeir is in Zudrugund, the once-abandoned dwarf-hall in Thrór's Coomb.\
\
You have collected the ingredients needed by Frithgeir to make the brew that will restore Nár's awareness of his surroundings.","Explore the dwarf-hall in Thrór's Coomb","The dwarf-hall is located among the northern mountains of Thrór's Coomb, far to the east of Lhanuch, the Uch-lûth village in Nan Laeglin.\
\
Nona has asked you to journey to the dwarf-hall in Thrór's Coomb to learn what Wadu saw there that brought him to Fordirith and then to his death.","Bring the list and ingredients to Frithgeir","Something Wadu saw in the abandoned dwarf-hall in Thrór's Coomb brought him to his death, and his sister Nona wants to learn what it was.","Two dwarves make their home in Zudrugund, the dwarf-hall in Thrór's Coomb, within Nár's Peak.\
\
One of the dwarves in the hall seems unable to focus upon you, but the other may be able to tell you what is going on."}},
[2962]={nameES="Chapter 15.10: A Brigand-Haunted Road",objectivesES={"The road to An Shêru leads north-west of Zajâna.","Brigands appear to have tampered with this signpost as well","The Hold of Jalkhíla is located to the east in Kighân.","Brigands may have tampered with the signpost north of Zajâna as well.","Travel north-east of Zajâna on the road to An Shêru","Repair the brigand-tampered signpost north of Zajâna","Repair the brigand-tampered signpost","Amêsh leaps from hiding, unaware of your lack of surprise","The road to An Shêru has a reputation for danger, but that is the way you must go.","There is something suspicious about this signpost","Shouting defiantly, a brigand leaps out of hiding!","Rahâzi has arrived in the company of two Hamâti soldiers.","The road to An Shêru runs by Zajâna. You should begin by going to the north-east.","You should repair this signpost north of Zajâna as you repaired the other.","Continue further north-west along the road to An Shêru","Something strikes you as suspicious about the signpost north-east of Zajâna.","You survived Amêsh's ambush, and should repair this signpost as well","As you step back to admire your work, you feel eyes upon you","You survived, but he may have allies; if you repair the signpost you may save others","Examine the suspicious signpost north of Zajâna","Rahâzi asked you to meet up with her party at Gadim-ûn in An Shêru.","If Dagûrum had allies, leaving the signpost as it is may help them ambush other travellers. You should repair the signpost and ruin their plans.","Bring the blades and bows to Rahâzi at Gadim-ûn in An Shêru","Examine the suspicious signpost north-east of Zajâna","Chapter 15.10: A Brigand-Haunted Road","You repair the signpost, making the road more safe for travellers","Talk to Rahâzi north of Zajâna"}},
[2963]={nameES="Chapter 15.1: Ulishár",objectivesES={"Talk to Corudan in Sul Madásh","Corudan has regretfully decided he cannot accompany you.","Wait for Corudan to depart","Chapter 15.1: Ulishár","Ulishár has joined your travelling companions for the journey south.","Ulishár takes a deep breath as he stares down the southward road","Ulishár stands here.","Talk to Ulishár in Sul Madásh","Corudan is by the southern entrance to Sul Madásh.","Ulishár stands where the road leads south-west into Kighân.","Ulishár agreed to show you where the road passes from Adagím into Kighân, south-west of Sul Madásh.","Baharúd's brother Ulishár has agreed to guide you on your road south into Mûr Ghala.","Ulishár is by the southern entrance to Sul Madásh.","Find the entrance to Kighân, south-west of Sul Madásh","Talk to Ulishár on the road into Kighân"}},
[2964]={nameES="Chapter 15.2: Tendrils of the Blight",objectivesES={"Talk to Glorfindel at Sormedân","Ulishár asked you to collect unblighted seed-pods from trees and defeat their corrupted roots at Shádhag, in Kighân.","Reassured villagers (1/2)","Inkanûsh is at the village of Sormedân.","Ulishár has come with you to Kighân, the Shornvale, but so too have tendrils of the blight that have taken root in Adagím.","Khâwaz at the village of Sormedân is reluctant to speak to you, but might be convinced.","Ulishár said he would wait for you at the village of Sormedân, to the south.","Reassure villagers of Sormedân (0/2)","Travel to Shádhag in Kighân","Khâwaz at the village of Sormedân has something to say to you.","Reassure villagers of Sormedân (1/2)","The trees at Shádhag may have been corrupted by the blight creeping into Kighân from Adagím.","Talk to Khâwaz at Sormedân","It is as Ulishár feared: the trees have been corrupted by blight from Adagím","Talk to Inkanûsh at Sormedân","Glorfindel is at the village of Sormedân.","Reassured villagers (2/2)","Bring the seed-pods to Ulishár at the village of Sormedân, to the south","Chapter 15.2: Tendrils of the Blight","Villagers of Sormedân are frightened of Glorfindel, and need reassurance that he is a friend and can be trusted."}},
[2965]={nameES="Chapter 15.3: Grazing Danger",objectivesES={"Defeat spirits at Badrasâg (4/5)","Talk to Mizâdi at Ingar-garâsh in southern Kighân","After some thought, you decide Mizâdi will be reasonable","Mizâdi stands at Ingar-garâsh in southern Kighân.","The spirits at Badrasâg should be defeated to ensure the safety of Sormedân.","The farmers of Sormedân are worried for one of their own, Rôkhasar, who may have strayed into danger.","Mizâdi's eyes flash angrily","Mizâdi and her advisors stand in the centre of much activity","Consider how Mizâdi will react to this situation","Chapter 15.3: Grazing Danger","Look for Rôkhasar near Badrasâg to the south-east of Sormedân","Talk to Rôkhasar below the Blade-horn","Find Mizâdi at Ingar-garâsh in the southern reaches of Kighân","Someone calls for you from below the Blade-horn","Talk to Rahâzi at Ingar-garâsh","Standing nearby, Rahâzi grunts in disapproval","Khâwaz fears that Rôkhasar may have strayed too near Badrasâg, the Blade-horn south-east of Sormedân, in pursuit of his cattle.","Spirits dwell at Badrasâg and pose a danger to Sormedân","You heard someone calling for you below the Blade-horn. Could it be the missing farmer Rôkhasar?","Mizâdi will be at Ingar-garâsh to the south-west, deep within Kighân.","Rôkhasar is below the Blade-horn, in Kighân.","You consider how Mizâdi will react to this situation.","Rahâzi stands at Ingar-garâsh in southern Kighân."}},
[2966]={nameES="Chapter 15.4: Nothing For Nothing",objectivesES={"Rahâzi is at Ingar-garâsh in southern Kighân.","Rahâzi believes the Shâra's response to this situation involving her soldiers will greatly impact the future of Renewed Hamât. How will Mizâdi respond?","Mizâdi stands at Ingar-garâsh in southern Kighân.","Mizâdi has charged you with the tasks her soldiers would have accomplished if they did not now need to provide aid and recompense to the farmers of Sormedân. These tasks include collecting eggs from nests at Khatzâla and collecting meat from creatures throughout Kighân.","Talk to Mizâdi at Ingar-garâsh","The provisioner Dunaïl stands at Ingar-garâsh.","Bring the meat and eggs you collected to Dunaïl at Ingar-garâsh","Chapter 15.4: Nothing For Nothing","Talk to Rahâzi at Ingar-garâsh","Mizâdi is at Ingar-garâsh in southern Kighân."}},
[2967]={nameES="Chapter 15.5: The Road To Zajâna",objectivesES={"Ulishár suggested that you travel to the cross-road north-west of the war-camp.","Ulishár stands by Khab Antâx, the Overgate, considering the city beyond.","Talk to Ulishár at the cross-road north-west of Ingar-garâsh","Ulishár stands here, observing the distant city.","Talk to Ulishár at Khab Antâx, the Overgate outside Zajâna","Ulishár suggested that you continue on into Zajâna itself.","Ulishár motions for you to halt","Travel to Khab Antâx, the Overgate outside Zajâna","Ulishár stands within the city, considering the buildings nearby.","Ulishár is inside the city of Zajâna.","Ulishár stands beside the road that leads south-west to Zajâna.","Ulishár has come to Ingar-garâsh in southern Kighân.","Chapter 15.5: The Road To Zajâna","Talk to Ulishár at Ingar-garâsh","Meet up with Ulishár at the cross-road north-west of Ingar-garâsh","Talk to Ulishár inside Zajâna","Ulishár stands by Khab Antâx, the Overgate outside Zajâna.","Continue on into Zajâna and meet up with Ulishár","Ulishár has come to Ingar-garâsh in search of you, bearing tidings about your companions' next road.","Ulishár suggested that you continue to the south-west until you reach Khab Antâx, the Overgate outside Zajâna."}},
[2968]={nameES="Chapter 15.6: City of Gates, City of Keys",objectivesES={"Climb the stairs west to the commons of Zajâna","Chapter 15.6: City of Gates, City of Keys","Ulishár taps you apologetically on the shoulder","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> at the commons to learn the layout of the city","Ulishár suggested that you climb the stairs to the west and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at the commons of the city, so you might learn the layout of Zajâna.","Glorfindel told you that Inkanûsh went to inspect Khab Kitâx, the Nethergate south of Zajâna.","Inkanûsh is at Khab Kitâx, the Nethergate south of Zajâna.","Walk north into the scholar's district and find the stage","Find Inkanûsh at Khab Kitâx, the Nethergate south of Zajâna","A bridge to the Ordâkhai-controlled district is beyond the arch to the south. The scholar's district is north","Zajâna the Splendid towers over Kighân, and visitors to the city are drawn to its libraries and cultural centres. Even so, peaceable travellers must avoid the presence of Ordâkh, which still attempts to control the city as it did before.","Glorfindel sees you approach and calls a greeting","Talk to Ulishár at Khab Kitâx, the Nethergate","Glorfindel is by the stage in north-western Zajâna.","North of the commons lies the scholar's district of the city. Ulishár recommended that you go there and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at the various sights of Zajâna.","Talk to Inkanûsh at Khab Kitâx, the Nethergate","Talk to Glorfindel by the stage in north-west Zajâna","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> at the stage in the scholar's district","You have caught up with Inkanûsh and Ulishár at Khab Kitâx, the Nethergate","Ulishár is at Khab Kitâx, the Nethergate, and is very interested in something you have said."}},
[2969]={nameES="Chapter 15.7: The Day's Entertainment",objectivesES={"Talk to Inkanûsh at the Nethergate","Talk to Inkanûsh when you are ready to find the theatre troupe","Ulishár has asked for permission to see the theatre troupe that has come to Zajâna.","Chapter 15.7: The Day's Entertainment","Talk to Ulishár by the stage in Zajâna","Ulishár is by the stage in Zajâna.","Inkanûsh is at the Nethergate south of Zajâna."}},
[2970]={nameES="Chapter 15.8: Têrkar's Travellers",objectivesES={"Talk to Jêsamin in Zajâna","Ulishár is at the western market in Zajâna.","Retrieve the coin-purse from the Ordâkh-controlled district","Talk to Glorfindel at the western market in Zajâna","Asharmûl is outside the Ordâkh-controlled district in south-east Zajâna.","Asharmûl and Zimêlkha asked you to retrieve from the Ordâkhai the coin-purse containing the money Têrkar's Travellers earned from their performance.","Zimêlkha stands with Asharmûl in Zajâna.","Talk to Imalêkh in Zajâna","Talk to Satagêra in Zajâna","Talk to Atâlsi in Zajâna","Chapter 15.8: Têrkar's Travellers","Talk to Zimêlkha in south-east Zajâna","Asharmûl hands you a much heavier purse than the one you retrieved","You found the rest of Têrkar's Travellers outside the Ordâkh-controlled district","Talk to Mashkânu in Zajâna","Talk to Ulishár at the western market in Zajâna","Bring the empty coin-purse to Asharmûl in south-east Zajâna","Ulishár is delighted to have encountered the theatre troupe that aided him during his escape from captivity, but he is troubled by their fewer numbers.","Têrkar's Travellers are at the western market in Zajâna.","Find Asharmûl and Zimêlkha in the residential district of Zajâna to the south-east","Bring the heavy coin-purse to Atâlsi at the western market in Zajâna","Find Têrkar's Travellers at the western market in Zajâna","The playwright Satagêra is at the western market in Zajâna.","Asharmûl and Zimêlkha went to the residential district of south-east Zajâna.","The coin-purse feels empty, but you should return it all the same","Glorfindel is at the western market in Zajâna.","Zimêlkha is outside the Ordâkh-controlled district in south-east Zajâna.","Atâlsi is at the western market in Zajâna.","Ulishár stands by his friends in Zajâna.","The coin-purse you were sent to retrieve has been emptied of its contents by the Ordâkhai, but you should return it to Asharmûl in south-east Zajâna.","Ulishár has spoken with his friends, and wears a mournful expression","Talk to Asharmûl in south-east Zajâna","Têrkar's Travellers may be in the western market of Zajâna."}},
[2971]={nameES="Chapter 15.9: A Wizard In His Natural Environment",objectivesES={"Chapter 15.9: A Wizard In His Natural Environment","Inkanûsh stands in the Kalmakhíla.","Find Glorfindel at the Overgate outside Zajâna","Glorfindel is at the Overgate north of Zajâna.","You hear angry approaching footsteps","Inkanûsh has selected a tome and some pages for you to study in the Kalmakhíla.","Inkanûsh is in the Kalmakhíla in Zajâna.","Mashkânu of Têrkar's Travellers has arrived in a rage","Without warning, Mashkânu bursts into tears","Mashkânu of Têrkar's Travellers has come to the Kalmakhíla, his weapon raised in anger.","If you are able to <rgb=#00FF00>calm</rgb> Mashkânu, you might avoid the violence he intends in the Kalmakhíla.","\\qThe sound was terrible and heard by all, but the devastation in the wake of the Urash-zâl was worst of all, and it changed the face of the land: cliffs crumbled, boulders fell from the height, great chasms opened in the earth along the whole of the Mûr. Even the great northern gate of Jajân cracked, so widespread were the effects of the tremors of the Urash-zâl.\\q","Glorfindel and Ulishár wait for you by the Overgate","Someone approaches, and they sound angry.","Remain on guard, just in case","Inkanûsh has gone to the Kalmakhíla, one of the most famous scholarly archives in all of Zajâna.","Glorfindel is at the Overgate outside Zajâna.","Talk to Inkanûsh in the Kalmakhíla","Someone approaches, and their anger is evident","Ulishár is at the Overgate outside Zajâna.","Talk to Mashkânu in the Kalmakhíla","Mashkânu's rage has been replaced with sorrow.","Read the open book on the table in the Kalmakhíla","<rgb=#00FF00>Calm</rgb> Mashkânu in the Kalmakhíla","Have your efforts borne fruit?","Talk to Inkanûsh in the Kalmakhíla in north-west Zajâna","Inkanûsh is in the Kalmakhíla in north-west Zajâna, beside the commons.","Read the pages on the table in the Kalmakhíla","Talk to Glorfindel at the Overgate","Talk to Ulishár at the Overgate","The pages of the open book are weathered and faded, but still legible.\
\
\\q...would not have believed it ever ran so deep had I not seen it myself only months before, but the flow of the river was greatly diminished. By the third day following the great tremors it had slowed to a trickle. My friend insists that the Usâl and the Agâl too will never flow again as they had, and even the lake of Idagâl is now a cracked and dry basin. He named it Khadagâl, the Dry-whelm, but the herdsmen insist that is a name of ill omen and the lake must return. I think they are both right and wrong: I believe the name is ill-starred, but the waters of the lake have gone forever.\
\
'Were the great tremors of the Urash-zâl a natural event, like the rising and setting of the sun or the passing of the seasons, or was it inflicted upon us by the whim of the Ghursâti? What could we have done to incur such wrath and vengeance?\
\
'My friend thinks Shurash Hûl of Ordâkh is somehow to blame for the Urash-zâl, for the drying of the rivers has removed the last barrier to the northern progress of his armies. I say it must be happenstance, for the quakes were felt along the entirety of the Mûr. How could one man so change the face of the land, even one so ambitious as the Hûl?\\q","In Mashkânu's eyes you see more than rage. You see fear"}},
[2972]={nameES="Chapter 15: An Echo of Days Past",objectivesES={"Talk to Corunir in Zudrugund","You have brought the ingredients Frithgeir needs to make a brew that will restore Nár's awareness of you so you can ask him what he said to Wadu.","Talk to Frithgeir at Zudrugund","Corunir is at Zudrugund.\
\
Frithgeir wants you to speak to Corunir and assure him that Nár means no harm.","Chapter 15: An Echo of Days Past","Frithgeir is in Zudrugund, the once-abandoned dwarf-hall in Thrór's Coomb.\
\
Frithgeir is preparing to make the brew that will restore Nár's clarity so you can ask him questions.","Talk to Frithgeir and wait for him to make the brew for Nár","Frithgeir is in Zudrugund, the once-abandoned dwarf-hall in Thrór's Coomb.\
\
You have travelled with Nár into the mine beneath Zudrugund and witnessed some peculiar things that the Dúnedain are hard-pressed to explain."}},
[2973]={nameES="Capítulo 15: Asalto a Dol Guldur",objectivesES={"Habla con Ningloril en Thangúlhad","Completa la Escaramuza: Forzar la Puerta del Nigromante","Los Elfos de la Hueste Dorada están preparados para lanzar su asalto a la fortaleza de Dol Guldur.","Goldagnir está en Thangúlhad.\
\
Se te ha dicho que hables con Goldagnir sobre los detalles del plan para atacar la fortaleza de Dol Guldur.","Goldagnir está en Thangúlhad, esperando para comenzar la segunda etapa del asalto a Dol Guldur.\
\
Has participado en la escaramuza en la puerta de la fortaleza y ahora deberías hablar con Goldagnir para conocer sus planes para la siguiente etapa de la batalla.","Ha llegado el momento de lanzar el ataque contra Dol Guldur. La primera escaramuza tendrá lugar en la puerta de la fortaleza.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión implica una escaramuza que se puede completar en tamaños de grupo: Solitario, Dúo, Pequeña Comunidad, Comunidad o Incursión utilizando el Panel de Escaramuzas. Esta escaramuza tiene un nivel mínimo de 60.</rgb>","Goldagnir está en Thangúlhad.\
\
Has participado en la segunda escaramuza en Dol Guldur y deberías informar a Goldagnir.","Completa la Escaramuza: Asalto a la Guarida de los Espectros del Anillo","Capítulo 15: Asalto a Dol Guldur","Ningloril está en Thangúlhad, el campamento de la Hueste Dorada en Gathbúrz.\
\
Ningloril te ha pedido que vuelvas a verla sobre un encargo secreto.","Habla con Goldagnir en Thangúlhad","La batalla por Dol Guldur continúa, con la próxima escaramuza teniendo lugar detrás de las murallas de la ciudad.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión implica una escaramuza que se puede completar en tamaños de grupo: Solitario, Dúo, Pequeña Comunidad, Comunidad o Incursión utilizando el Panel de Escaramuzas. Esta escaramuza tiene un nivel mínimo de 60.</rgb>"}},
[2974]={nameES="Chapter 16.10: The Great Triumph of Mordor and Ordâkh",objectivesES={"Talk to Asharmûl in south-east Ahâba","It is time for Têrkar's Travellers to perform Satagêra's masterpiece, and for you to complete your mission and learn how the plans of Ordâkh and the Thardúth intertwine.","Talk to Asharmûl and go with Têrkar's Travellers into Emax Dûl","Asharmûl is in south-east Ahâba.","Chapter 16.10: The Great Triumph of Mordor and Ordâkh","The time has come for you to go with Asharmûl and the rest of Têrkar's Travellers into the guarded fastness of Emax Dûl.","Inkanûsh must be told what you have discovered.","Talk to Inkanûsh on the island in the centre of the oasis of Ahâba"}},
[2975]={nameES="Chapter 16.11: A Journey Into Danger",objectivesES={"Talk to Rahâzi in Khanâg Valoyar","Chapter 16.11: A Journey Into Danger","Ulishár will remain in Idagâl to stand alongside Têrkar's Travellers","Rahâzi stands here.","Glorfindel will remain in Idagâl to stand against the Thardúth","Your companions assemble in Ahâba to discuss these fresh dangers.","With dangers looming in two directions, the time has come to make a difficult choice: some must remain in Idagâl to oppose the Thardúth, and some must return north to combat this last evil of Sauron.","Talk to Rahâzi outside the waggon that brought you to Sûg Nidar","According to what you learned in Emax Dûl, supply-waggons for Sûg Nidar depart from Khanâg Valoyar, south of Jiret-menêsh, in An Shêru.","Fortunately, there is no sign of the Temámir who accosted you during your last visit","Rahâzi will journey with you and oppose this last evil of Sauron","Return to Khanâg Valoyar in An Shêru","<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Fearwater by using the banner at Khanâg Valoyar, in An Shêru.</rgb>\
\
Rahâzi is outside the waggon that brought the two of you to Sûg Nidar, the Fearwater.","Talk to Glorfindel in Ahâba","Talk to Ulishár in Ahâba","Rahâzi is at Khanâg Valoyar in An Shêru.","Talk to Rahâzi in Ahâba","Talk to Rahâzi in Khanâg Valoyar and sneak aboard the next waggon to depart","Rahâzi is at Khanâg Valoyar, in An Shêru. She has identified the next waggon to depart, and is prepared to sneak aboard it with you."}},
[2976]={nameES="Chapter 16.1: Hallows In The Height",objectivesES={"You have come to An Shêru, the Height of the Sky, and must now brave the dangers of this inhospitable land.","Wights stalk Naxar Dâl in northern An Shêru.","Wights stalk the heights of Naxar Dâl","It would appear Mashdagâl has something he wants to say.","Talk to Shenzâmin in Naxar Dâl","Chapter 16.1: Hallows In The Height","The man leaning against a nearby wall snorts in derision","Talk to Shenzâmin at Gadim-ûn","You hear one of the Hamâti soldiers calling for you within Naxar Dâl","You picked up a parchment covered in a sorcerer's mad ravings.","Defeat wights at Naxar Dâl (5/6)","Examine the corpse of the sorcerer of Ordâkh in Naxar Dâl","Read the parchment you recovered from the sorcerer of Ordâkh","Shenzâmin discovered the corpse of a man of Ordâkh wearing sorcerous robes in Naxar Dâl.","Mashdagâl told you that if you want to help so badly, you might deal with creatures of evil at Naxar Dâl.","Rahâzi has introduced you to the Hamâti soldiers with whom she travels. They can be found at Gadim-ûn in An Shêru.","Find Naxar Dâl to the north of Gadim-ûn","You find a parchment covered in mad ravings","Shenzâmin is in Naxar Dâl. What has he discovered?","Talk to Mashdagâl in Gadim-ûn","Glorfindel will want to see the writings of the sorcerer of Ordâkh. The Elf-lord waits for you in Gadim-ûn.","Talk to Kishâtal at Gadim-ûn","Bring the parchment you found to Glorfindel in Gadim-ûn"}},
[2977]={nameES="Chapter 16.2: Something Else Inside",objectivesES={"You picked up another parchment covered in a sorcerer's mad ravings.","Read the mad scratchings of the sorcerer of Ordâkh","Travel to the Crypts of Khâb Daku south-west of Gadim-ûn","You discover a parchment covered in rantings and ravings","Ulishár is at Gadim-ûn, and wishes to speak to you.","Glorfindel will want to see the writings of this sorcerer of Ordâkh as well. The Elf-lord waits for you in Gadim-ûn.","Talk to Ulishár at Gadim-ûn","You heard the cries of hyenas and a scream to the east, near Spoiler's Crag.","The Dead walk at the Crypts of Khâb Daku, as they did at Naxar Dâl","Defeat wights and shades at the Crypts of Khâb Daku (5/6)","Hurry east to Spoiler's Crag and find the source of the scream","Search the body of the slain sorcerer at Spoiler's Crag","It is your duty to face the wights at the Crypts of Khâb Daku, and wherever you find them.","A sorcerer of Ordâkh has fallen victim to the hyenas of Spoiler's Crag","Talk to Mashdagâl at Gadim-ûn","The slain sorcerer at Spoiler's Crag may have something of interest on his person, as did the other you found.","Mashdagâl has become increasingly agitated by the talk in Gadim-ûn.","The Crypts of Khâb Daku are south-west of Gadim-ûn.","The ravings of a slain sorcerer of Ordâkh point to the presence of the Thardúth in An Shêru.","Chapter 16.2: Something Else Inside","Bring the parchment you found to Glorfindel in Gadim-ûn","You hear the cries of hyenas to the east, followed by a piercing scream!"}},
[2978]={nameES="Chapter 16.3: Investigations In An Shêru",objectivesES={"Glorfindel stands here.","Investigation completed: 'A Difficult Step'","Work with Glorfindel and complete 'The Madness at Damudûr'","Glorfindel believes that terrible evils slept within An Shêru, but they must now be awake. You must determine the dangers lurking within the Height of the Sky and aid your companions with their duties.","Your companions within Gadim-ûn have a number of investigations with which they need your help.","The Hamâti soldier Kishâtal in Gadim-ûn has something he wishes to say to you.","Talk to Rahâzi on the road toward Idagâl","Investigation completed: 'A Song of Shurug-nîn'","Work with Rahâzi and complete 'A Song of Shurug-nîn'","Rahâzi is on the road toward Idagâl.","Talk to the Hamâti soldier Kishâtal in Gadim-ûn","Meet with your companions on the road toward Idagâl","Work with Shenzâmin and complete 'Emissaries to Jiret-menêsh'","Investigation completed: 'Emissaries to Jiret-menêsh'","Talk to Glorfindel on the road toward Idagâl","Chapter 16.3: Investigations In An Shêru","Having aided your companions with their investigations, you should now meet them where the road leads toward Idagâl.","Work with Ulishár and complete 'A Difficult Step'","Glorfindel is on the road toward Idagâl.","Investigation completed: 'The Madness at Damudûr'"}},
[2979]={nameES="Chapter 16.4: The Vultures Circle",objectivesES={"Ulishár stands by the road into Idagâl.","Rahâzi is at Ahâba in Idagâl.","Your next destination is the small village of Ahâba located by the oasis in Idagâl.","Travel to the village of Ahâba by the oasis in Idagâl, and introduce yourself to Malgârzor","Talk to Ulishár on the road into Idagâl","Talk to Malgârzor in Ahâba","The herdsman Malgârzor in Ahâba asked you to defeat \\qvultures\\q of different kinds.","Your companions are prepared to advance further into the Ordâkhai-held territory of Idagâl.","Chapter 16.4: The Vultures Circle","Talk to Rahâzi at Ahâba","The oasis-village of Ahâba is green and pleasant","The herdsman Malgârzor in Ahâba eyes you cautiously.","The herdsman Malgârzor in Ahâba will be interested to hear that you dealt with the vultures, as well as the \\qvultures.\\q"}},
[2980]={nameES="Chapter 16.5: A Reminder of Ancient Days",objectivesES={"Glorfindel stands here.","The Dawn-warden towers over the surrounding lands of Idagâl","Rahâzi stands here.","Rahâzi stares at the dragon-bones in awe","Bring the sacred stones to Kindrígi at the Dawn-warden","Talk to Bâlamar at the Dawn-warden","Kindrígi asked you to defeat the creatures at the Tombs of Khâb Ishil and recover the stones they stole from the site of the Dawn-warden.","Talk to Rahâzi by the dragon-bones in the Dry-whelm","Kindrígi is waiting to hear news of your success, and to accept delivery of the sacred stones the kergrim stole from the Dawn-warden site.","Travel to the feet of the Dawn-warden statue north-west of the Dry-whelm","Talk to Glorfindel at the Dawn-warden","Glorfindel is in the Dry-whelm.","Talk to Kindrígi at the Dawn-warden","Chapter 16.5: A Reminder of Ancient Days","A number of wayfarers have made pilgrimages to the Dawn-warden statue in Idagâl.","Glorfindel is interested in seeing the Dawn-warden statue to the north-west of the Dry-whelm up close.","Rahâzi stares at the dragon-bones in the Dry-whelm.","Rahâzi wants to examine the dragon-bones said to lie within the Dry-whelm, west of Ahâba.","Glorfindel is at the Dawn-warden statue in Idagâl.","The lake-bed in the centre of Idagâl has borne witness to a great deal of history, some tragic and some triumphant.","Meet with Rahâzi by the dragon-bones in the Dry-whelm, west of Ahâba","Talk to Dimûzga at the Dawn-warden","Talk to Glorfindel by the dragon-bones in the Dry-whelm"}},
[2981]={nameES="Chapter 16.6: Making Connexions",objectivesES={"Satagêra is in north-east Ahâba.","Talk to Ulishár in north-east Ahâba","Chapter 16.6: Making Connexions","Talk to Rahâzi by the dragon-bones in the Dry-whelm","Listen to what Inkanûsh has discovered","Inkanûsh stands here.","Talk to Glorfindel at the Dawn-warden","Rahâzi is by the dragon-bones in the Dry-whelm.","Ulishár stands here.","Inkanûsh is at the village of Ahâba.","Talk to Satagêra in north-east Ahâba","Return to the village of Ahâba in Idagâl, and meet your companions on the central island of the oasis","Inkanûsh suggested you join your companions at north-east Ahâba.","The situation in Idagâl merits further investigation, particularly the relationship between the Ordâkhai of Emax Dûl and the Thardúth of Damudûr.","Inkanûsh waits at the village of Ahâba, eager to tell you what he has discovered.","Rejoin your companions in north-east Ahâba","Ulishár is in north-east Ahâba.","Glorfindel is at the Dawn-warden in Idagâl.","A familiar face wears a familiar expression: kindness tempered by impatience","Inkanûsh has come to Ahâba.","Talk to Inkanûsh at Ahâba","Your companions agreed to meet back at the village of Ahâba in Idagâl, on the central island in the oasis."}},
[2982]={nameES="Chapter 16.7: The Lies",objectivesES={"Satagêra is in north-east Ahâba.","Satagêra gave you another part of the script she has written.","Talk to Ulishár in north-east Ahâba","Imalêkh is in north-east Ahâba.","Chapter 16.7: The Lies","Read the script Satagêra gave to you","Talk to Satagêra in north-east Ahâba","Satagêra gave you part of the script she has already written.","Talk to Imalêkh in north-east Ahâba","Satagêra has some thoughts about the play she has been tasked with writing.","Read another part of the script Satagêra gave to you","You have read portions of Satagêra's script and should return them to her.","Ulishár is in north-east Ahâba.","Jêsamin is in north-east Ahâba.","Return the pages she gave you to Satagêra in north-east Ahâba","Talk to Jêsamin in north-east Ahâba"}},
[2983]={nameES="Chapter 16.8: A Guarded City",objectivesES={"Talk to Ulishár in north-east Ahâba","Glorfindel has also come to scout the defences of Emax Dûl.","Scout the approach to the main entrance to Emax Dûl","With regret, Ulishár has bid farewell to Têrkar's Travellers so you can continue your urgent errand: scouting the approaches to the Ordâkhai-held Emax Dûl.","Glorfindel quietly arrives as you survey the approach to Emax Dûl","Chapter 16.8: A Guarded City","Jêsamin claps her hands together","The approach to the main entrance of Emax Dûl must be scouted for some weakness in the defences.","Talk to Zimêlkha in north-east Ahâba","Glorfindel fears that fighting your way in to Emax Dûl may be the only option available to you, but Inkanûsh in north-east Ahâba will not like that answer.","Talk to Inkanûsh in north-east Ahâba","Study the main entrance of Emax Dûl from the low wall atop the hill","Emax Dûl looms high above the cliffside","The approach to Emax Dûl must be scouted for some weakness in the defences.","Talk to Glorfindel outside Emax Dûl","Scout the approach to Emax Dûl above the cliffside","Talk to Mashkânu in north-east Ahâba","Mashkânu in north-east Ahâba has an idea.","Study the defences of Emax Dûl from the low wall by the cliffside","Ulishár is in north-east Ahâba.","Zimêlkha is in north-east Ahâba.","The main entrance to Emax Dûl appears heavily-guarded","Jêsamin in north-east Ahâba knows what needs to be done.","Talk to Jêsamin in north-east Ahâba","It will be difficult, if not impossible, to enter Emax Dûl from this side","Mashkânu clears his throat, drawing your attention"}},
[2984]={nameES="Chapter 16.9: Satagêra's Masterpiece",objectivesES={"Satagêra is in north-east Ahâba.","You have only known Têrkar's Travellers for a short time, but you are reasonably certain they would want you to <rgb=#00FF00>point</rgb> at the largest of the mûmakil.","Find Inkanûsh in south-east Ahâba","Satagêra is in north-east Ahâba, waiting for your response to her script.","<rgb=#00FF00>Point</rgb> at the mûmak you want from the Scardelve","Satagêra hands you some fresh pages of her script","Return the script to Satagêra in north-east Ahâba","Talk to Inkanûsh in south-east Ahâba","Talk to Shâdugan Gânda at the Scardelve","Inkanûsh stands here.","Inkanûsh stands in south-east Ahâba, deep in thought","Têrkar's Travellers are willing to help you gain access to the inner keep of the guarded city of Emax Dûl, but the plan is not without its dangers.","No... not big enough!","Talk to Satagêra in north-east Ahâba","They said big, but that one is TOO big, and equipped for war!","Inkanûsh has gone to south-east Ahâba to think about the plan.","Read the new portion of the script Satagêra gave to you","Talk to Mashkânu in south-east Ahâba","Atâlsi hands you a pass with a wax seal to give the mûmak-keeper","Shâdugan Gânda gives you a grim smile","Inkanûsh stands in south-east Ahâba, deep in thought.","Bring the pass to Shâdugan Gânda, the keeper of the mûmakil, at the Scardelve","Talk to Ulishár in south-east Ahâba","Ulishár is in south-east Ahâba.","Talk to Atâlsi outside the western entrance to Ahâba","Shâdugan Gânda, the keeper of the mûmakil, is at the Scardelve, south of Ahâba.","Satagêra has given you some fresh pages of her script to read.","Atâlsi is outside the western entrance of Ahâba.","Mashkânu is in south-east Ahâba.","Chapter 16.9: Satagêra's Masterpiece"}},
[2985]={nameES="Capítulo 16: Las Mazmorras de Dol Guldur",objectivesES={"Habla con Ningloril en Thangúlhad","Habla con Ningloril e infiltrate en las mazmorras de Dol Guldur","Bori está dentro de Nothgar, la torre central de Thangúlhad.\
\
Bori te espera para agradecerte por su rescate.","Capítulo 16: Las Mazmorras de Dol Guldur","Ningloril está en Thangúlhad, el campamento de la Hueste Dorada en Gathbúrz.\
\
Has rescatado a Bori de las mazmorras de Dol Guldur y ahora deberías hablar con Ningloril, quien organizó el esfuerzo de rescate.","Habla con Bori en Nothgar, en Thangúlhad","En las profundidades de las mazmorras de Dol Guldur, Bori sigue cautivo en una celda de prisión. Es hora de liberarlo.","Ningloril está en Thangúlhad, el campamento de la Hueste Dorada en Gathbúrz.\
\
Ningloril te espera para viajar contigo a las mazmorras de Dol Guldur y rescatar a Bori de su cautiverio."}},
[2986]={nameES="Capítulo 17.1: Extraños Desde Lejos",objectivesES={"The Temámir Habâti has set up a shop for the Ordâkhai in the central tent of Khomar Bóha.\
\
Your Suspicion Level is: <rgb=#FFFF00>MEDIUM</rgb>.","You should walk calmly out of Khomar Bóha without arousing further suspicion.\
\
Your Suspicion Level is: <rgb=#00FF00>LOW</rgb>.","A map just to the north seems promising.\
\
Your Suspicion Level is: <rgb=#FFFF00>MEDIUM</rgb>.","The Ordâkhai camp of Khomar Bóha is to the north-west of the waggon in which you arrived.","You should walk calmly out of Khomar Bóha without arousing further suspicion","The soldiers at Khomar Bóha do not seem suspicious of you... yet","You have no choice but to go inside the central tent of Khomar Bóha","Rahâzi is outside the Ordâkhai camp of Khomar Bóha.","You should see what is being stored in the amphorae located on the eastern side of Khomar Bóha.\
\
Your Suspicion Level is: <rgb=#00FF00>LOW</rgb>.","Walk calmly out of Khomar Bóha and arouse no further suspicion\
\
Your Suspicion Level is: <rgb=#00FF00>LOW</rgb>","Even as you commit the map to memory, a woman calls out to you!","Talk to Rahâzi outside the Ordâkhai camp of Khomar Bóha","Report to the vendor inside the central tent of Khomar Bóha\
\
Your Suspicion Level is: <rgb=#FF0000>HIGH</rgb>","Examine the amphorae to the east\
\
Your Suspicion Level is: <rgb=#00FF00>LOW</rgb>","Onúkho is in the centre of Khomar Bóha.\
\
Your Suspicion Level is: <rgb=#00FF00>LOW</rgb>.","Capítulo 17.1: Extraños Desde Lejos","Jóla has caught you examining the map of Sûg Nidar, and she demands to hear your explanation!\
\
Your Suspicion Level is: <rgb=#FF0000>HIGH</rgb>.","Talk to Onúkho in Khomar Bóha\
\
Your Suspicion Level is: <rgb=#00FF00>LOW</rgb>","Travel north-west to the camp of Khomar Bóha","Talk to Jóla and explain yourself\
\
Your Suspicion Level is: <rgb=#FF0000>HIGH</rgb>","Examine the nearby map of Sûg Nidar\
\
Your Suspicion Level is: <rgb=#FFFF00>MEDIUM</rgb>","You and Rahâzi have arrived at Sûg Nidar, the Fearwater, and must now learn of some way to prevent the Song of Waves and Wind from setting sail.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Fearwater by using the banner at Khanâg Valoyar, in An Shêru.</rgb>","A line has formed inside the central tent","The amphorae contain fresh, easily-transportable water for the use of the Ordâkhai","Talk to Habâti in the central tent of Khomar Bóha\
\
Your Suspicion Level is: <rgb=#FFFF00>MEDIUM</rgb>","You have no choice but to go inside the central tent of Khomar Bóha.\
\
Your Suspicion Level is: <rgb=#FF0000>HIGH</rgb>."}},
[2987]={nameES="Capítulo 17.2: No Estás Solo",objectivesES={"Rahâzi stands alongside an unexpected friend near the outer palisade of Drushkála.","Corudan stands outside the Orc-encampment of Drushkála, a good distance from where last you saw him.","Having slain many Orcs at Drushkála, you should return to the entrance of the Orc-encampment and see if you have drawn the attention of your potential ally.","Capítulo 17.2: No Estás Solo","You and Rahâzi have learned that the various groups working to complete the Song of Waves and Wind are not as unified as they might be.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Fearwater by using the banner at Khanâg Valoyar, in An Shêru.</rgb>","Talk to Corudan near the entrance to Drushkála","Rahâzi asked you to descend the slope and approach the Orc-encampment of Drushkála, remaining alert for anything out of the ordinary.","What slew this Orc so near to the entrance of Drushkála?","An Orc lies dead a short distance from the outer palisade of Drushkála","Rahâzi has suggested that you travel east toward the Orc-encampment of Drushkála so that you might learn more.","Rahâzi stands alongside a familiar figure","Rahâzi stands west of the Orc-encampment of Drushkála and stares at the ships of the Song moored off the shore.","This Orc was slain by an Elf-arrow. Might you have allies hereabout?","Return to the entrance of Drushkála and look for your potential ally","Approach Drushkála and remain alert for anything out of the ordinary","Talk to Rahâzi west of Drushkála","You should slay Orcs at their encampment of Drushkála and look for signs of your potential ally.","Rahâzi slows to a halt and stares out at the ships of the Song","Talk to Rahâzi near the entrance to Drushkála","Travel east in the direction of the Orc-encampment of Drushkála","Search the Orc for some sign of what killed him"}},
[2988]={nameES="Capítulo 17.3: Tras los Pasos de su Padre",objectivesES={"Talk to Rahâzi south-east of the Haven of Bâkhridar","Corudan asked you to search supply crates within the Haven of Bâkhridar and then meet him and Rahâzi on the other side.","This crate is packed with stoppered glass jars, currently empty","Corudan and Sigileth have come to the Fearwater, bolstering your ability to destroy the Song of Waves and Wind.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Fearwater by using the banner at Khanâg Valoyar, in An Shêru.</rgb>","You have travelled with Corudan to the opposite shore, very near to the Haven of Bâkhridar, an encampment of Heirsworn within Sûg Nidar.","This crate contains wrapped portions of ship's biscuit","This crate contains several folded maps showing navigable rivers","Rahâzi and Corudan agreed to meet up with you south-east of the Haven of Bâkhridar.","Capítulo 17.3: Tras los Pasos de su Padre","Talk to Corudan outside the Haven of Bâkhridar, in Sûg Nidar","Meet with Rahâzi and Corudan south-east of the Haven of Bâkhridar","Corudan stands south-east of the Haven of Bâkhridar.","Rahâzi stands south-east of the Haven of Bâkhridar.","Talk to Corudan south-east of the Haven of Bâkhridar"}},
[2989]={nameES="Capítulo 17.4: A la Sombra de Kasukhín",objectivesES={"Your allies have returned to Fearwater Notch","You have found Sigileth's encampment in the Fearwater","Talk to Cúridwan north-east of Fearwater Notch","Sigileth is by the camp-fire at Fearwater Notch, on the island of Kasukhín.","Sigileth stands at Fearwater Notch, awaiting news.","Sigileth and Cúridwan intended to set up camp on the island that holds the ruins of Kasukhín, but the bridge leading there lies beyond Starkhaven.","You should return to Fearwater Notch with news of Cúridwan's investigation.","Find Cúridwan north-east of Fearwater Notch, by the shore of Kasukhín","You have found Cúridwan, standing by a small, sunken row-boat","Return to Fearwater Notch with news of Cúridwan's potential solution","Talk to Sigileth at Fearwater Notch","Make your way to the island on which stands the ruins of Kasukhín, and find Sigileth","Cúridwan went to perform an investigation north-east of Fearwater Notch, on the shore of Kasukhín.","Cúridwan stands by the water's edge north-east of Fearwater Notch.","Before you can confront the Song of Waves and Wind, you must rejoin Sigileth and Cúridwan.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Fearwater by using the banner at Khanâg Valoyar, in An Shêru.</rgb>","Capítulo 17.4: A la Sombra de Kasukhín"}},
[2990]={nameES="Capítulo 17.5: Silenciar la Canción",objectivesES={"Talk to Cúridwan at Fearwater Notch and complete 'Evil's Uses'","Talk to Corudan at Fearwater Notch and complete 'The Stockpile'","Your companions at Fearwater Notch on the island of Kasukhín have several objectives you must achieve if you are to prevent the Song of Waves and Wind from endangering Middle-earth.","Sigileth is at Fearwater Notch on the island of Kasukhín.","Capítulo 17.5: Silenciar la Canción","Talk to Sigileth at Fearwater Notch","Talk to Rahâzi at Fearwater Notch and complete 'Even A Single Sword'","In order to prevent the Song of Waves and Wind from threatening Middle-earth, you and your companions must achieve several important objectives.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Fearwater by using the banner at Khanâg Valoyar, in An Shêru.</rgb>"}},
[2991]={nameES="Capítulo 17.6: En la Cima de la Isla",objectivesES={"Talk to Rahâzi on the island of Kasukhín","Talk to Sigileth at Fearwater Notch and go with her to confront the leaders of the Song","Capítulo 17.6: En la Cima de la Isla","Rahâzi is atop the island of Kasukhín.","If you and your companions can defeat Nakási and Balakhâd, you will deprive the Song of Waves and Wind of its leaders and its purpose.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Fearwater by using the banner at Khanâg Valoyar, in An Shêru.</rgb>","Sigileth is waiting for your signal to confront Nakási and Balakhâd atop the island of Kasukhín."}},
[2992]={nameES="Capítulo 17: Recuerdos de Mithrandir",objectivesES={"Habla con Ningloril en Thangúlhad","Encuentra y recorre el pasaje secreto hacia los cimientos de Dol Guldur","Bori ha recordado la mención de Gandalf, hace mucho tiempo, de un camino secreto hacia los cimientos de Dol Guldur, y cree que si se pudiera encontrar, podría ser utilizado en beneficio de la Hueste Dorada.","Sigileth está en Nothgar, la torre situada dentro del campamento de Thangúlhad.\
\
Bori ha recordado algo que podría ser útil: un camino secreto hacia Dol Guldur utilizado por Gandalf hace mucho tiempo.","Habla con Sigileth en Nothgar en Thangúlhad","Ningloril está en Thangúlhad.\
\
Has descubierto el camino secreto utilizado por Mithrandir para entrar en Dol Guldur hace mucho tiempo y deberías informar ahora a Ningloril.","Capítulo 17: Recuerdos de Mithrandir","El misterioso camino secreto hacia los cimientos de Dol Guldur que Gandalf debió haber utilizado se encuentra seguramente en algún lugar del espolón rocoso sobre el que se encuentra la fortaleza."}},
[2993]={nameES="Chapter 18.10: A Knife in the Smoke",objectivesES={"Talk to King Elessar in the graveyard and learn how he was wounded","You have encountered Tatháta by the docks. She may have seen Aphadaer","Pursue Aphadaer to the northern docks of the burning Harlond","Aphadaer will seek to join Balakhâd by the Heirsworn ship moored at the docks!","Tatháta is by the northern docks of the burning Harlond, near the flagship of the Song.","Talk to Tatháta by the northern docks of the burning Harlond","The King has been wounded!\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Harlond in Flames by using the banner east of the Beacon-gate, in Umbar Baharbêl.</rgb>","King Elessar lies in the graveyard, wounded. What happened while you were away?","Aphadaer ran for the docks, intending to join Balakhâd and be rewarded for the death of King Elessar.","Chapter 18.10: A Knife in the Smoke"}},
[2994]={nameES="Chapter 18.11: Nakási Wave-reaper and the Heirs of Castamir",objectivesES={}},
[2995]={nameES="Chapter 18.12: First Verse, Last Verse",objectivesES={}},
[2996]={nameES="Chapter 18.13: The Peace Restored",objectivesES={"Talk to Ioreth in the Harlond infirmary","Queen Arwen and the healer Ioreth arrive at the King's bedside","The threat posed by the Song of Waves and Wind has been met, and now those wounded during the attack must work to recover their wounds and rebuild their homes.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Harlond in Flames by using the banner east of the Beacon-gate, in Umbar Baharbêl.</rgb>","Jajax is in the Harlond infirmary.","Talk to Jajax in the Harlond infirmary","Queen Arwen smiles at you and turns her attention to her injured husband.","Queen Arwen and Ioreth the Healer have come to the Harlond infirmary.","Ioreth sputters to herself with disbelief.","Chapter 18.13: The Peace Restored","Talk to King Elessar in the Harlond infirmary","Talk to Queen Arwen in the Harlond infirmary","King Elessar recovers from his wound in the Harlond infirmary."}},
[2997]={nameES="Chapter 18.1: Outrun the Wind, Outrun the Waves",objectivesES={}},
[2998]={nameES="Chapter 18.2: The River Gate",objectivesES={"Talk to Tasâdi the Rumourmonger","Talk to Daxamat by the pool","The guardsman would not listen. You should hurry to the Waterway Market and <rgb=#00FF00>beckon</rgb> for the folk by the pool to heed you.","Ride west to Umbar Baharbêl and give your warning to the guardsmen at the White Gate","Chapter 18.2: The River Gate","Daxamat hurries off to warn the folk of the city about the approaching threat.","Jajax stands at the forum of Bith Gabâr in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.","Talk to Mother Phúrsi","The folk near the Waterway Market must be warned of the approaching danger!","Daxamat and the others run off to warn the folk of the city!","<rgb=#00FF00>Beckon</rgb> the people nearby to heed you","The people of Umbar Baharbêl must be warned about the danger that approaches them from the east!","According to his brother, you will find Jajax at the forum of Bith Gabâr.","Find Jajax at the forum of Bith Gabâr and warn him of the danger","Will they heed you?","Talk to Guardsman Phârex by the fountain","You can waste no time. Warn the folk at the Waterway Market!","Talk to Itûr within the refuge he has offered you","At last some of the folk give you their attention","A familiar voice calls to you as Daxamat pushes through the crowd","Phârex stands at attention, worried by the tidings you have brought to his city.","<rgb=#00FF00>Daxamat's Refuge is just west of the Waterway Market in Umbar Baharbêl, behind an unassuming door.</rgb>\
\
Itûr has given you a place to shelter until you can learn what happened to your brother and your friend within Dâr Laja.","Talk to Ushrin the Purchaser","Daxamat stands by the fountain, a worried expression upon his face.","You must hurry to the eastern gate of Umbar Baharbêl and warn the guardsmen there of the approaching danger.","Talk to Jajax and go with him to warn the Kindred of the Coins about the approaching danger","Pass through the gate and hurry to the court by the nearby pool"}},
[2999]={nameES="Chapter 18.3: Daxamat Takes The Lead",objectivesES={"Two residents of the city have come to the refuge. But why?","Talk to Itûr in the left storage room","Talk to Khâsha in the entrance to the refuge","Talk to Phêlex in the entrance to the refuge","Until he can learn what happened to his brother and his adventuring friend, it is up to Daxamat to make sense of things!\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Daxamat's Refuge is just west of the Waterway Market in Umbar Baharbêl, behind an unassuming door.</rgb>","Chapter 18.3: Daxamat Takes The Lead","Explore the cellar beyond the southern hallway of the refuge","You have never met this Temámir before. Why does he ask for you?","Birûk nods pleasantly at the boat in the water.","Itûr told you about a useful feature of the refuge: a cellar beneath a trapdoor at the far end of the south hall.","You hear Itûr's footstep behind you as he enters the storage room","Talk to Itûr by the entrance to the refuge","A Temámir dwarf has come in search of you. But why?","You hear the sound of a door closing in the distance, and voices drift from above","Itûr stands in the entrance to the refuge, awaiting your answer.","A small boat bobs in the water beside the platform","Itûr told you a Temámir dwarf has come to the refuge asking for you.","What would they do if they were here?","Return to the entrance of the refuge to speak with the new Temámir arrival","Leave your belongings in a corner of the left storage room","Itûr clears his throat, surprising you. He has a knack for moving unseen!","Itûr has returned to the entrance of the refuge, and has some information for you and the Temámir Birûk.","Have more people come to the refuge? You should return to the entrance and learn who has arrived and for what purpose.","Itûr stands in the entrance to the refuge, assessing the new arrivals.","Itûr has followed you into the left storage room. He has a worried expression on his face.","Return to the entrance of the refuge and learn the identity of the new arrivals","What would they do in this situation, if they were here?","They would fight. They would fight!","Itûr offered you a place in the left storage room of the Refuge. He said to open the southern door and then the storage room would be on the left side of the hall.","More new arrivals: a man and a woman you have not met before","Talk to Birûk, the newly-arrived Temámir dwarf","Talk to Itûr in the entrance to the refuge","Talk to Birûk in the cellar of the refuge"}},
[3000]={nameES="Chapter 18.4: The Cage and the Captives",objectivesES={"Itûr stands in the planning room to the right of the refuge's entrance.","Itûr wonders what has befallen the prisoners.","Nakûr, another recent arrival, sits in the entrance to the refuge.","Talk to Nakûr in the entrance to the refuge","Set up chairs in the room to the right of the entrance","With the heroes imprisoned, it falls to Daxamat to take up the struggle!\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Daxamat's Refuge is just west of the Waterway Market in Umbar Baharbêl, behind an unassuming door.</rgb>","Talk to Itûr in the planning room","Chapter 18.4: The Cage and the Captives","If you are to lead a rebellion against traitorous powers, you will need to prepare. The room to the right of the refuge's entrance should serve."}},
[3001]={nameES="Chapter 18.5: Catching Sparks",objectivesES={"The last time Nakûr checked there were no messages, but perhaps now there will be. If so, the shopkeeper Sekét will have slipped them under the door at the top of the stairs on the left side of the entrance to the refuge.","Return to the entrance of the refuge and learn what has happened","Rothog the Storm stares at you carefully.","Talk to Nakûr in the entrance to the refuge","Something has happened by the entrance to the refuge. You hear the sound of voices raised in anger!","Chapter 18.5: Catching Sparks","You should spread out the papers on the table in the planning room to the right of the entrance to the refuge.","You heave a sigh of relief as they lower their weapons","Two leaders of the Kindred of the Coins stand ready to fight!","Shêsha and her cat Rûmina study the papers in the planning room.","Perhaps Birûk has returned from Umbar-môkh with tidings?","You collect the messages slipped under the door by an ally to Ilma-ghôli's cause","Kinsman Belondor appraises you.","With the heroes imprisoned, it falls to Daxamat to take up the struggle!\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Daxamat's Refuge is just west of the Waterway Market in Umbar Baharbêl, behind an unassuming door.</rgb>","Talk to Belondor in the entrance to the refuge","Check if there are any messages atop the stairs on the left side of the entrance to the refuge","Nakûr will be pleased to see the arrival of these new messages.","Can bloodshed be avoided?","Spread out the papers on the table in the planning room","Two leaders of the Kindred stand ready to fight!","Talk to Shêsha in the planning room","Go down to the cellar and see if Birûk has returned","Talk to Rothog in the entrance to the refuge","Birûk was due to arrive sometime soon. You should go down to the cellar and see if the Temámir has returned.","You hear voices from above... voices raised in anger!"}},
[3002]={nameES="Chapter 18.6: The Uprising Begins",objectivesES={"The assembled fighters of Ilma-ghôli listen to your directives","<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Harlond in Flames by using the banner east of the Beacon-gate, in Umbar Baharbêl.</rgb>\
\
You have arrived at the Harlond in time of war, the port-city wreathed in flames.","With the heroes imprisoned, it falls to Daxamat to take up the struggle!\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Daxamat's Refuge is just west of the Waterway Market in Umbar Baharbêl, behind an unassuming door.</rgb>","Give your allies their orders in the planning room of the refuge","Your gathered allies await their orders in the planning room to the right of the entrance to the refuge.","Use the table in the planning room to address the gathering","Talk to Belondor and stay behind while he goes to rescue the prisoners","Chapter 18.6: The Uprising Begins","Talk to Belondor and go with him to rescue the prisoners","The time has come for you to use the table and address the gathering in the planning room to the right of the entrance.","Belondor awaits the word to begin the rescue mission.","Talk to Tatháta while the Harlond burns"}},
[3003]={nameES="Chapter 18.7: The Song In Gondor",objectivesES={"King Elessar stands atop the overlook, preparing for the counter-attack","You have sailed in haste to Gondor, but the Song arrived before you, and the Harlond is in flames.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Harlond in Flames by using the banner east of the Beacon-gate, in Umbar Baharbêl.</rgb>","Find more defenders north-west of the Harlond, past the graveyard","A soldier of Gondor greets you by the southern side of the burning Harlond, desperate hope written on his face.","Make your way north-west in search of Gondorian defenders","Talk to King Elessar at the overlook north-west of the burning Harlond","A soldier of Gondor beckons you to him","King Elessar prepares for the counter-attack from the overlook north-west of the burning Harlond.","Borndir calls out in greeting as you approach the upward slope","Borndir told you that King Elessar has gathered a number of soldiers on the overlook at the top of the sloping path north-west of the burning Harlond, and prepares to make a counter-attack against the invaders.","You should make your way north-west past the reeds in search of Gondorian defenders.","Talk to the soldier of Gondor by the south-western edge of the Harlond","King Elessar stands here.","Borndir stands on the slope north-west of the burning Harlond, past the graveyard.","Chapter 18.7: The Song In Gondor","King Elessar turns to face you, his expression brightening as he recognizes your return from distant lands.\
\
'You return to Gondor in its time of need, my friend; I deem that is no coincidence. Tell me everything you know of this fleet and the villains who captain it!'","Talk to Borndir on the slope north-west of the graveyard outside the Harlond","Find King Elessar at the overlook atop the sloping path north-west of the graveyard outside the burning Harlond","Defenders of Gondor fought bravely against the assault of the Song, but were pushed back to a slope north-west of the Harlond, beyond the graveyard."}},
[3004]={nameES="Chapter 18.8: Taking Back the Harlond",objectivesES={"Aphadaer urgently calls you to him","Chapter 18.8: Taking Back the Harlond","Leave the weapons you collected in the barrel by the graveyard","Agladal has been sent to safety","With the tasks given to you by King Elessar's attendants now completed, you should return to the graveyard outside the burning Harlond and prepare to push back the invaders.","Talk to King Elessar at the graveyard","The weapons you collected can now be used again in defence of Gondor","King Elessar is at the graveyard outside the burning Harlond, preparing to strike back against the invaders.","Talk to Belondor at the graveyard","Gaeranor has been sent to safety","King Elessar has asked you to speak to his attendants on the overlook north-west of the burning Harlond to learn what must be done for the counter-attack to begin.","Talk to Aphadaer at the graveyard","Aphadaer stands here.","Talk to Lornion on the overlook","Return to the graveyard outside the burning Harlond","Aphadaer has called you to him at the graveyard outside the burning Harlond.","Find the horse Gaeranor along the main street and send him to safety","Gondor has suffered a defeat, but now it is time for the counter-attack to begin.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Harlond in Flames by using the banner east of the Beacon-gate, in Umbar Baharbêl.</rgb>","Talk to Glindor on the overlook","Find the horse Agladal along the main street and send him to safety","The King motions to the man standing nearby, a man once of Gondor but now of Umbar.\
\
'Belondor tells me Nakási has broken with the Kindred of the Coins, and I believe him.'","The King's expression is already greatly-changed from when you first encountered him today. His weariness has been replaced with determination.\
\
'This is the hour in which we fight back against the invaders,' he says.\
\
'Belondor tells me that Nakási has broken with his Kindred, and is an enemy too of Umbar. I believe him. He counts himself no longer a man of Gondor, but today we will fight side by side to prevent Nakási and her allies from endangering our lands and our homes, though they be not shared.'","Gondorian swords were dropped on the sloping path when the soldiers retreated to the overlook north-west of the burning Harlond.","You were told to leave the swords you retrieved in a barrel by the graveyard outside the burning Harlond, rescue frightened horses that fled in the direction of the main street, and defeat Orcs and Ordâkhai that threaten the port.","Belondor is at the graveyard outside the burning Harlond.","Talk to Aphadaer on the overlook"}},
[3005]={nameES="Chapter 18.9: The Lesson of the Flames",objectivesES={"Jajax stands here.","Jajax is on the eastern side of the port-city, preparing to storm the docks.","The King has been wounded! What happened while you were away?","Talk to Borndir at the graveyard","Jajax stands bravely among the flames not far from the docks","Find Jajax on the eastern side of the burning Harlond, preparing to storm the docks","Talk to Borndir at the graveyard and learn what happened to the King.","Chapter 18.9: The Lesson of the Flames","As long as the Song possesses its Narghâk weapons, every shore in Middle-earth remains at risk.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Harlond in Flames by using the banner east of the Beacon-gate, in Umbar Baharbêl.</rgb>","The day is not yet won. You must return to the graveyard outside the burning Harlond and learn what next can be done.","Return to the graveyard and talk to King Elessar","Talk to Jajax and go with him to sabotage the Narghâk weapons of the Song"}},
[3006]={nameES="Capítulo 18: La Batalla en la Torre",objectivesES={"Goldagnir está en Thangúlhad, el puesto avanzado de la Hueste Dorada más cercano a Dol Guldur.\
\
Ningloril te ha dicho que hables con Goldagnir, quien está organizando el último asalto a la torre.","Completa la Escaramuza: La Batalla en la Torre","La Hueste Dorada inicia su asalto final sobre Dol Guldur y se te ha pedido que luches junto a los Malledhrim durante la batalla.","Capítulo 18: La Batalla en la Torre","Habla con Goldagnir en Thangúlhad","Tienes tu propio papel que desempeñar en la escaramuza en la torre, el asalto final de la Hueste Dorada sobre Dol Guldur.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión implica una escaramuza que puede ser completada en solitario, en dúo, en pequeña comunidad, en comunidad o en grupo de incursión utilizando el panel de escaramuzas. Esta escaramuza tiene un nivel mínimo de 60.</rgb>","Goldagnir está en Thangúlhad, el puesto avanzado de la Hueste Dorada más cercano a Dol Guldur.\
\
Con una pequeña victoria en mano, deberías regresar a Goldagnir."}},
[3007]={nameES="Chapter 1: A Council Waiting",objectivesES={"Talk to Lady Galadriel","Chapter 1: A Council Waiting","Legolas seems as if he also wishes to talk with you.","Talk to Thranduil and experience 'Session: the Battle Under the Trees'.","You should talk to Haldir at the entrance to the Court of Lothlórien.","Having spoken to Celeborn and Galadriel, you should talk to King Thranduil as well.","Habla con Galadriel","Find Legolas in Dor Amarth","Hear what the Council of War has to say after Thranduil's recounting of the Battle Under the Trees.","Legolas can be found at the Ruins of Díngarth in Dor Amarth.\
\
You should bring word to Legolas in Dor Amarth of his father's visit to Lothlórien.","Talk to Thranduil","Talk to Lord Celeborn","What has brought King Thranduil of Mirkwood to the Court of Lothlórien?","Having arrived at the Council of War, you should talk to the lord and lady of the court first.","Habla con Legolas.","Approach the Council of War in the Court of Lothlórien.","Habla con Haldir","Approach the War Council","Hear Thranduil's tale of the events in Mirkwood and Lothlórien."}},
[3008]={nameES="Capítulo 1: Un lugar para los hobbits",objectivesES={"Capítulo 3: El paso de la Compañía Gris","Capítulo 1: Un lugar para los hobbits","Capítulo 11: La Batalla de los Campos del Pelennor","Capítulo 17: El Mago y el Rey","Habla con Gandalf","Capítulo 4: Los Senderos de los Muertos","Capítulo 13: El Último Debate","Capítulo 18: El Retorno del Rey","Capítulo 9: El Rey y el Senescal","Capítulo 12: Las Casas de Curación","Capítulo 6: La Batalla de Pelargir","Capítulo 8: La Ciudad de las Torres Blancas","Capítulo 2: El último de la Compañía","Capítulo 10: La Defensa de Minas Tirith","Capítulo 21: Los Puertos Grises","Capítulo 5: La reunión de la Compañía Gris","Capítulo 19: La Boda","Capítulo 20: Los Juicios del Rey","Capítulo 14: La Puerta Negra"}},
[3009]={nameES="Chapter 1: Beneath the Lonely Mountain",objectivesES={"This area of the hall has been set aside for treating the wounded and infirm","King Thorin is currently meeting with his advisors, and is not free for an audience. Foldgráf recommended that you make yourself familiar with the Hall under the Mountain while you wait.","During the siege, this area was used for storage of provisions and other perishables","Foldgráf stands ready to welcome you to the Hall under the Mountain.","King Thorin is meeting with adventurers about opportunities in Mordor","Chapter 1: Beneath the Lonely Mountain","Talk to Foldgráf at the entrance to the Hall under the Mountain","Thorin III, King under the Mountain, is at his throne in Erebor.","Foldgráf is at the entrance to the Hall under the Mountain.","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to Durin's Folk and fight on their behalf in Mordor.","Talk to Dómor by the throne","Talk to Margald in the Hall under the Mountain","Talk to Hrostyr, the personal guard of King Thorin III","Three adventuring dwarves stand by the throne in the Hall under the Mountain. They have been charged by King Thorin III with the same task as you.","Talk to Laurík in the Hall under the Mountain","Talk to Mogi by the throne","Travel to the Hall under the Mountain, in Erebor","Thorin III, King under the Mountain, is at his throne in Erebor. You should present yourself to Hrostyr, his personal guard.","Talk to Bróthi in the Hall under the Mountain","King Thorin should now be ready to meet with you.","Talk to Eirek by the throne","After a long journey, you have arrived at Erebor and gained entrance to its halls","Weapons and armour-pieces were brought to this area for accessibility during the siege","Talk to Foldgráf","Find King Thorin III, in the Hall under the Mountain","Thorin III is now King under the Mountain, and rules Durin's Folk from Erebor. Now that you have pledged to aid the dwarves as they adventure in Mordor, Dori believes you should meet with Thorin at the Lonely Mountain.","Talk to King Thorin III at his throne in the Hall under the Mountain"}},
[3010]={nameES="Capitulo 1: Manteniendo la cadena de suministro",objectivesES={"Thórgnyr se encuentra fuera de Moria, cerca de las Puertas de Durin, junto a la laguna tranquila.\
\
Slóthi quiere asegurarse de que la ruta de suministro fuera de Moria permanezca abierta y que haya suficiente comida dentro de las minas para que los enanos puedan sobrevivir a un largo asedio.","Capitulo 1: Manteniendo la cadena de suministro","Slóthi se encuentra en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, en la entrada sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Thórgnyr te ha dado la primera de varias entregas de comida para Slóthi, que se encuentra en la Cámara de la Encrucijada.","Slóthi está preocupado de que cuando los Orcos ataquen, los enanos puedan quedar aislados del mundo exterior y no puedan sobrevivir a un largo asedio.","Lleva suministros de comida a Slóthi"}},
[3011]={nameES="Capítulo 1: Planes de la Hueste Dorada",objectivesES={"Alfirimbes está esperando para hablar contigo en Echad Sirion, el campamento en las orillas del Anduin, en la frontera del Bosque Negro.\
\
Has conocido a la compañía responsable de llevar a Mazog en secreto a Dol Guldur, y han cruzado al Bosque Negro. Ahora deberías hablar con Alfirimbes.","Habla con Braiglinn en Imlad Lalaith","Habla con Alfirimbes en Echad Sirion","Braiglinn está en Imlad Lalaith, en el lado de Lothlórien del río Anduin.\
\
Alfirimbes está complacido de que la primera travesía haya sido exitosa y te ha enviado a Braiglinn para notificar al grupo responsable de llevar a Mazog a Dol Guldur que ha llegado el momento de su propio cruce.","La primera travesía del Anduin por los Malledhrim ha sido un éxito, y ahora es hora de que la compañía encargada de transportar a Mazog también cruce.","Habla con Braiglinn y viaja para encontrarte con los miembros de la compañía","Capítulo 1: Planes de la Hueste Dorada"}},
[3012]={nameES="Capítulo 1: Explorando las vías de acceso",objectivesES={"Sporr está esperando fuera de la Cámara de la Encrucijada.\
\
El primo de Sigdan, Sporr, va a hacer una exploración de las vías de acceso a la Cámara de la Encrucijada, buscando cualquier Orco que pueda estar preparándose para atacar.","Has acompañado a Sporr en su ronda","Habla con Sporr","Capítulo 1: Explorando las vías de acceso","Sigdan te ha pedido que ayudes a su primo Sporr a hacer una exploración de las vías de acceso a la Cámara de la Encrucijada para detectar cualquier actividad relacionada con los Orcos.","Sigdan se encuentra en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, en la entrada sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Has acompañado a Sporr en su ronda para detectar Orcos en las vías de acceso a la Cámara de la Encrucijada, y ahora deberías informar a Sigdan."}},
[3013]={nameES="Capítulo 1: El fondo del pozo",objectivesES={"El fondo del pozo probablemente se encuentre en algún lugar de las Obras Hidráulicas, en las profundidades de Moria, al suroeste del imponente acueducto. El enano Melmar podría estar en algún lugar cerca del fondo.\
\
Thálfi está preocupado por la posibilidad de que los Orcos puedan trepar desde el fondo del pozo, y quiere que investigues para asegurarte de que eso no sea posible.","Encuentra el fondo del pozo","A Thálfi no le gusta el pozo que se encuentra en el centro de la Cámara de la Encrucijada, y le preocupa que los Orcos puedan trepar por él si las centinelas no están alerta.","Capítulo 1: El fondo del pozo","Thálfi se encuentra en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, en la entrada sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Has encontrado el fondo del pozo pero descubriste que estaba bien protegido, y ahora deberías regresar con Thálfi.","Has defendido a Melmar de sus enemigos."}},
[3014]={nameES="Chapter 1: The Eve of Battle",objectivesES={}},
[3015]={nameES="Chapter 1: The King and the Steward",objectivesES={"You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to Aragorn and the Kingdom of Gondor, and to fight on their behalf in Mordor.","King Elessar is in his throne room atop Minas Tirith.","Talk to King Elessar in his throne room","Chapter 1: The King and the Steward","Talk to Prince Imrahil and return with him to the White City","Prince Imrahil is outside the Black Gate, waiting to return with you to Minas Tirith."}},
[3016]={nameES="Chapter 1: The Rightful Claim",objectivesES={"Talk to Prince Ingór","Explore the balcony","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you.","The hall of Vérnozal was built over, and is powered by, this underground river","Explore the living quarters","Talk to the Zhélruka Clan Quartermaster","Chapter 1: The Rightful Claim","Talk to Zóva","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
Prince Ingór wishes for you to explore Vérnozal.","Explore the waterway","Many coming to Gundabad could seek a comfortable shelter here in Vérnozal","Habla con Hórin","Talk to the Gundabad Missions Quartermaster","From this seat many proclamations were made by the lords of Gundabad","The view from the balcony over the court is truly impressive","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to the Zhélruka and to fight on their behalf in Gundabad.","Explore the throne"}},
[3017]={nameES="Chapter 2 - Call and Response",objectivesES={}},
[3018]={nameES="Chapter 2 - Lost Ledger",objectivesES={"Chapter 2 - Lost Ledger","Zarai provided a general area east along the mountains where a courier lost their delivery. She requires that the satchel reaches Aphamâr, the ledger-keeper of Rakhatâb.","Zarai has a concern that she needs to address. Speak with her in Jax Phanâl.","Find Aphamâr in Râhal Ghol, the upper ward of Umbar Bahârbel.","Find the satchel along the foot of the mountains to the south-east","The Ledger-keepers maintain the Books of Balance informing the Kindred of the Coins of the honour gained by the citizens of Umbar Baharbêl. Your name is now entered in the Books of Balance.","Deliver the runed satchel to Aphamâr at Rahâl Ghol in Umbar Baharbêl","Speak with Núrut in Rakhatâb","Aphamâr is not here; speak with the foreman","Speak with Zarai at her post in Jax Phanâl","Deliver the runed leather satchel to Aphamâr in Rakhatâb","With the satchel recovered you should deliver it to the ledger-keeper Aphamâr in Rakhatâb. You were told she usually stands across the path from the stable-master.","Aphamâr is not where you expected to find her. Núrut of Rakhatâb likely knows her whereabouts. Find and speak with the dwarf near their office at the crest of Rakhatâb.","You collected the runed leather satchel"}},
[3019]={nameES="Chapter 2.10: Caebar",objectivesES={"Caebar made a list of the most common complaints of Linhir's townsfolk: foes in Dor-en-Ernil, pests in the town, burned timbers in Linhir, and listening to the concerns of the people.","Examine the sketch of Barad Rill given to you by Caebar","Hear the concerns of Nimdol","Caebar gave you a sketch of the lighthouse of Barad Rill, seen in happier days.","Talk to Uilin at the entrance of Ethring, in King's Gondor","Caebar hands you a time-weathered sketch of the lighthouse of Barad Rill","Caebar is by the eastern entrance of the town of Linhir, in King's Gondor.","Travel to the southern entrance of Ethring, in the Ringló Vale, King's Gondor","Return Caebar's sketch of Barad Rill to him","Uilin stands at the entrance of Ethring, glaring at you and Caebar.","Talk to Caebar by the eastern entrance of Linhir, in King's Gondor","Maeriel is worried that some of her neighbours have disappeared","A villager of Ethring glares at you and Caebar with distrust","Chapter 2.10: Caebar","Barad Rill is located to the south-west of Linhir, at the southern point of the peninsula of Dor-en-Ernil, in King's Gondor.","Nimdol is concerned about the increase in pests around Linhir","Caebar's hometown of Ethring is located in the Ringló Vale, north of Dor-en-Ernil, in King's Gondor.","Travel to Barad Rill, the grand lighthouse in Dor-en-Ernil, in King's Gondor","Caebar has a renewed interest in facing the foes of Gondor that prowl Dor-en-Ernil or the Ringló Vale, in King's Gondor.","Hear the concerns of Forcharn","Talk to Caebar in view of Barad Rill, in King's Gondor","Forcharn is not really worried about anything. He's just lonely","Hear the concerns of Maeriel","Caebar stares at the ruin of Barad Rill with great sadness","Caebar stares at the ruin of Barad Rill at the southern peninsula of Dor-en-Ernil, in King's Gondor.","King Elessar and Queen Arwen's journey westward will next pass into Dor-en-Ernil and the Ringló Vale."}},
[3020]={nameES="Chapter 2.11 Welcome and Unwelcome",objectivesES={"A man stands in front of the door to Sirdis's home","Find the home of Caebar's mother, Sirdis","Talk to Galengam inside his shop in Calembel, King's Gondor","Garthaben calls excitedly to you south-east of the entrance to Calembel.","Caebar has returned home to Ethring, but it is not a pleasant homecoming.","She glares at you suspiciously, and says nothing","Travel to the entrance of Calembel in Lamedon, King's Gondor","Talk to Caebar outside his mother's house in Ethring, in King's Gondor","Chapter 2.11 Welcome and Unwelcome","Caebar has returned to his hometown of Ethring at the King's direction, but the homecoming is not a pleasant one.","She stares at you with cold eyes, and refuses to say anything","Galengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts is in the south-west corner of Calembel, in King's Gondor.","Garthaben excitedly calls you over to him","Talk to Caebar at the entrance of Ethring","Talk to Garthaben south of Calembel, in King's Gondor","Talk to Carlong in front of Sirdis's house","Enter Galengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts in the south-west corner of Calembel, in King's Gondor","Caebar's mother's house is to the north across the bridge and to the right, in the village of Ethring, in King's Gondor.","The town of Calembel is north-west of the Ringló Vale, in Lamedon, King's Gondor.","Galengam is inside his crowded shop in the south-west corner of Calembel, in King's Gondor.","He murmurs that the best way to help Ethring is for you to leave","Caebar wants you to listen to the concerns of Ethring's villagers.","The man spoke true: the shop is very crowded with King Elessar's retinue","Carlong blocks the way into the home of Caebar's mother, Sirdis.","Caebar stands outside his mother's house in Ethring, in King's Gondor."}},
[3021]={nameES="Chapter 2.12: In the Palace of the Swan",objectivesES={"Chapter 2.12: In the Palace of the Swan","Queen Arwen is inside Galengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts, in Calembel, King's Gondor.","Talk to King Elessar in Galengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts","Talk to Queen Arwen in Galengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts","The Swan-knight Rossaran stands at the western entrance south of Dol Amroth, in King's Gondor, waiting to bring you to Prince Imrahil.","The Swan-knight Rossaran waves you to him","Talk to Prince Imrahil in the Palace of the Swan in Dol Amroth, King's Gondor","King Elessar and Queen Arwen have crossed into Lamedon, and now their sights are set upon Dol Amroth and the Palace of the Swan.","Travel to the western entrance south of Dol Amroth, in King's Gondor","Prince Imrahil is inside the Palace of the Swan in Dol Amroth, in King's Gondor.","Rossaran will meet you and the rest of the company at the western entrance south of Dol Amroth, in King's Gondor.","Talk to Rossaran at the western entrance south of Dol Amroth and travel with him to see Prince Imrahil","King Elessar is inside Galengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts, in Calembel, King's Gondor."}},
[3022]={nameES="Chapter 2.1: Elf-queen of Gondor",objectivesES={"Talk to Lady Vanyalos in her hall, in King's Gondor","Lady Vanyalos is in her hall in Imloth Melui, King's Gondor.","King Elessar is in the tower guard-house in the centre of Imloth Melui, in King's Gondor.","Queen Arwen hands you a small ceramic bowl","Fill the bowl with water from a fountain outside the Hall of Lady Vanyalos","Talk to King Elessar in the Imloth Melui guard-house","Talk to Ioreth in the Hall of Lady Vanyalos","The Hall of Lady Vanyalos is to the east of the tower guard-house in Imloth Melui, King's Gondor.","King Elessar and Queen Arwen have begun to tour their kingdom so the wounds inflicted during the War of the Ring might be healed.","King Elessar is inside the tower guard-house in the centre of Imloth Melui, in King's Gondor.","Chapter 2.1: Elf-queen of Gondor","Enter the Hall of Lady Vanyalos in Imloth Melui, King's Gondor","Talk to Lady Vanyalos in her hall","Return the ceramic bowl filled with water to Queen Arwen in the Hall of Lady Vanyalos, in King's Gondor","Talk to Queen Arwen in the Hall of Lady Vanyalos","Ioreth must have seen something in Arwen's expression, for she falls silent","Queen Arwen is in the Hall of Lady Vanyalos, in Imloth Melui, King's Gondor.","Fill the bowl with water from the falls in the north-western reaches of Imloth Melui","Arwen asked you to fill the ceramic bowl she gave you with water from one of the fountains outside the Hall of Lady Vanyalos and with water from one of the falls in the north-western reaches of Imloth Melui.","The healer Ioreth is deep in discussion with Lady Vanyalos and Queen Arwen","Talk to King Elessar in the tower guard-house in the centre of Imloth Melui, in King's Gondor"}},
[3023]={nameES="Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of Cardolan",objectivesES={"Defeat evil-fascinated wights outside Haudh Nogbenn (2/3)","Bring the Sceptre of Cardolan to Elrond in Rivendell","Talk to Newbold Leafcutter in the Scholar's Stair Archive","Mithrandir has studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang, and believes that if it might be cleansed of its corruption it could be empowered with a force for Good.","A fallen wooden shield catches your eye outside the entrance to the barrow of Haudh Nogbenn.","Séca is on Weathertop.\
\
You have defended Cythred from an attack, and now his assistant Séca wishes to thank you.","Examine the wooden shield and search Haudh Nogbenn for its owner","Newbold Leafcutter is in the Scholar's Stair Archive in the Town of Bree.","Talk to Séca on Weathertop","The low hum of conversation stops as the sceptre's presence is felt","This small wooden shield is scored with many dents and cracks, and tracks lead toward the entrance to the barrow. Whoever dropped the shield here may be in trouble!\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","You catch sight of a battered shield, just outside the entrance to the barrow","Séca of the Eglain told you to consult with Newbold Leafcutter in the Scholar's Stair Archives in the Town of Bree.","Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of Cardolan","Elrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House.\
\
You have cleansed the corruption from the Sceptre of Cardolan, and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.","Cythred is on the hill of Weathertop, in the Lone-lands.","Talk to Frideric the Elder in Ost Guruth","Talk to Cythred on Weathertop","Frideric the Elder is in Ost Guruth, the Ruin-hold in the Lone-lands.\
\
Mithrandir believes the Eglain of the Lone-lands may know something about the corrupted heirloom of Cardolan you discovered.","Find the Scholar's Stair Archives in Bree-town","Haudh Nogbenn is at the southern tip of the Northern Barrow-downs.\
\
Newbold Leafcutter thinks that evils will be drawn to the sceptre when you bring it to Haudh Nogbenn."}},
[3024]={nameES="Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of Khazad-dûm",objectivesES={"Greith told you of a number of doors south-west of the Twenty-first Hall that the corrupted key might unlock.","The key does not fit in the lock","The key fits cleanly in the lock, and turns! The door is unlocked","Bring the Key of the Forgotten to Elrond in Rivendell","Talk to Greith in the Twenty-first Hall, in Khazad-dûm","Elrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House.\
\
You have cleansed the corruption from the Key of the Forgotten, and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.","Unlock the door south-west of the Twenty-first Hall with the Corrupted Key","Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of Khazad-dûm","Talk to Greith outside the unlocked door and explore beyond","Greith is outside the unlocked door in Khazad-dûm, south-west of the Twenty-first Hall and down many levels.","Talk to Greith outside the unlocked door south-west of the Twenty-first Hall and down many levels","The key almost fits in the lock... but not quite","Greith is outside the unlocked door south-west of the Twenty-first Hall and down many levels, in Khazad-dûm.","Mithrandir has studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang and believes that if it might be cleansed of its corruption it could be empowered with a force for Good.","Greith in the Twenty-first Hall considers himself a master of locks and keys and is always telling people so.\
\
Mithrandir thinks that finding the door unlocked by the corrupted key might cleanse the heirloom of its evil."}},
[3025]={nameES="Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of Osgiliath",objectivesES={"Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of Osgiliath","Find a sailor in Osgiliath who knows about the corrupted rigging-hook","Talk to Nathlad in Osgiliath and learn what he knows of the corrupted rigging-hook","Nathlad in Osgiliath is waiting for to agree to help him with his work before he tells you what he knows of the rigging-hook you recovered from Mordor.","Elrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House.\
\
You have cleansed the corruption from the Anchor of the Past, and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.","Mithrandir has studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang and believes that if it might be cleansed of its corruption, it could be empowered with a force for Good.","Mithrandir believes you should ask sailors in Osgiliath if they know the story of the rigging-hook you found in Mordor.\
\
Now that soldiers of the Host of the West have passed through Osgiliath, the city should be reasonably safe for you to search for such a sailor.","Bring the Anchor of the Past to Elrond in Rivendell"}},
[3026]={nameES="Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of Rhudaur",objectivesES={"Elrond is in his library in Rivendell, waiting to advise you about your journey to the Lost Temple to cleanse the cup of Rhudaur.","Elrond can be found in the library of the Last Homely House, in Rivendell.","Talk to Elrond in his library in Rivendell","Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of Rhudaur","Elrond is in the library of Rivendell.","The course of the Bruinen in the Misty Mountains falls in three levels before it comes out of the mountains.\
\
Elrond asked you to fill the cup of Rhudaur with cold, clear water from waterfalls in the Misty Mountains, and to defeat any creatures drawn by its corruption.","Talk to Elrond and travel to the Lost Temple to cleanse the Cup of Rhudaur","Elrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House.\
\
You have cleansed the corruption from the Cup of Sacrifice and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.","The beast falls, free of the evil that compelled it to attack","You fill the cup with cold water, but the corrupting evil remains","Bring the Cup of Sacrifice to Elrond in Rivendell","Mithrandir has studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang and believes that if it might be cleansed of its corruption it could be empowered with a force for Good.","Talk to Elrond in the library of Rivendell"}},
[3027]={nameES="Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of the Earth-kin",objectivesES={"Bring the Seeds of Defiance to Elrond in Rivendell","Talk to Rhothlas and hear his tale","A pack of hunting Wargs has been drawn to you by the evil emanating from the corrupted pouch.","You hear a curious creaking sound coming from the south-west side of the pond","There is a pond in the North Downs, in the south-east corner of Nan Amlug East, where the Rauta-lehmä gather. Santtu told you Trotsiv was going to go there, but he is worried that something happened to him because the pond is very near to Kar Lak, war-camp of the Rauta-lehmä.","Find the pond revered by the Rauta-lehmä near Kar Lak, in Nan Amlug East","Defeat evil-fascinated Wargs at the pond near Kar Lak (2/3)","Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of the Earth-kin","Talk to Chief Tuokki at Lehmä-koti","Elrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House.\
\
You have cleansed the corruption from the Seeds of Defiance, and should bring them now to Elrond in Rivendell.","Chief Tuokki is at the Earth-kin village of Lehmä-koti, in the Ram Dúath, south of Angmar.","Talk to Aarnikka in Lehmä-koti","You hear the snarls of a pack of hunting Wargs, drawn by the corruption","Talk to Santtu in Lehmä-koti","Rhothlas is standing among the trees near the pond in Nan Amlug East, below Kar Lak.","Talk to Rhothlas by the pond near Kar Lak","You have found an Ent near a pond in the North Downs.","Mithrandir has studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang and believes that if it might be cleansed of its corruption it could be empowered with a force for Good.","Aarnikka and Santtu can be found in the village of Lehmä-koti and may know something about the corrupted pouch."}},
[3028]={nameES="Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of the Eglain",objectivesES={"Talk to Morhald in Haragmar","Talk to Aric the Stone-speaker and travel to the Spring of the Red-maid","Talk to Walgar in Haragmar","Morhald and Cólbyr search the Haragmar east of Ost Guruth for artifacts such as the one that has come into your possession.","Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of the Eglain","Aric the Stone-speaker is at Ost Haer, far to the south of Haragmar.","Elrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House.\
\
You have cleansed the corruption from the Image of the Champion, and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.","Frideric the Elder is in Ost Guruth, the Ruin-hold in the Lone-lands.\
\
Mithrandir believes that the corrupted heirloom you have recovered has some connexion to the Eglain of the Lone-lands.","Talk to Cólbyr in Haragmar","Bring the Image of the Champion to Elrond in Rivendell","Habla con Aric el Intérprete de Piedras en Harloeg","Mithrandir has studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang and believes that if it might be cleansed of its corruption, it could be empowered with a force for Good.","Talk to Frideric the Elder in Ost Guruth","Aric the Stone-speaker is in Harloeg, far south of Ost Guruth.","More of the Eglain may be imperiled in the swamp of Haragmar."}},
[3029]={nameES="Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of the High King",objectivesES={"Talk to Gwíniel in Annúminas","Techeron sent you to find the Steadfast Sisters in Annúminas, to see if they have seen any badges identical to the one that came out of Mordor.","Talk to Línneth in Annúminas","Bring the Badge of Ariant to Elrond in Rivendell","Colm Fettering is a tomb-robber of some notoriety on the island of Rantost, in Lake Evendim, and may tell you more about the corrupted badge.","Techeron returned to Echad Garthadir in Annúminas following the War of the Ring.\
\
Mithrandir believes that the corrupted badge came at first from Annúminas in the days of High King Elendil.","Talk to Techeron and walk with him to the Bridge of Ariant","Gwíniel is near the gate of Adannon, in Annúminas.","Mithrandir has studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang and believes that if it might be cleansed of its corruption it could be empowered with a force for Good.","Talk to Colm Fettering on Rantost","Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of the High King","Techeron is at Echad Garthadir, in Annúminas.","You take back the corrupted badge","Talk to Techeron at Echad Garthadir, in Annúminas","Elrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House.\
\
You have cleansed the corruption from the Badge of Ariant, and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.","Talk to Carastír in Annúminas"}},
[3030]={nameES="Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of the Ordinary",objectivesES={"Elrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House.\
\
You have cleansed the corruption from the Necklace of the Ordinary, and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.","Bring the Necklace of the Ordinary to Elrond in Rivendell","Anlaf told you that Umín just left the Forsaken Inn, and if you hurry you might see him outside somewhere.","Anlaf the Forlorn tends the bar of the Forsaken Inn, in the Lone-lands.","Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of the Ordinary","Habla con Anlaf el Despojado en la Posada Abandonada","Bring the corrupted necklace to Umín somewhere outside the Forsaken Inn","Mithrandir has studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang and believes that if it might be cleansed of its corruption, it could be empowered with a force for Good.","Talk to Umín and return to the ship in the caverns beneath the Forsaken Inn","Umín has struggled greatly since his encounter with the spirit of the necklace in the caverns beneath the Forsaken Inn."}},
[3031]={nameES="Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of the Riddermark",objectivesES={"Elrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House.\
\
You have cleansed the corruption from the Vengeance of Folca and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.","Talk to Eldmath north-east of Aldburg","Talk to the expert jeweller in Snowbourn","One jeweller sent you to another. Perhaps the expert jeweller in Snowbourn, the city of Rohan in the Sutcrofts, will be able to read the markings on the corrupted tusk-shard.","Bring the Vengeance of Folca to Elrond in Rivendell","Eldmath has run into some trouble","Eldmath ran off during the fighting, and you should find him. He cannot have gone far.","Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of the Riddermark","You should defeat the Wargs drawn by the corruption of the tusk-shard, or they might prove a danger to Eldmath or the people of the Eastfold.","An expert jeweller in Minas Tirith may be able to use his tools to read the markings on the corrupted shard for you. Such a jeweller plies his trade on the southern side of the Fourth Circle, after the battle.","The jeweller in Snowbourn sent you to the village of Aldburg, in the Eastfold, to ask a Bard of Rohan about the tusk-shard.","Talk to the expert jeweller in Minas Tirith, on the southern side of the Fourth Circle, after the battle","Eldmath has been captured by a raiding party of Orcs.","Talk to the bard in the tavern in Aldburg","Catch up with Eldmath","Talk to Tharbag and look for an opportunity to rescue Eldmath","Eldmath has gone ahead into the field, inspired by the promise of adventure and planned to meet you north-east of Aldburg.","Mithrandir has studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang and believes that if it might be cleansed of its corruption it could be empowered with a force for Good.","The tusk-shard's corruption draws evils to it"}},
[3032]={nameES="Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of the Snowmen",objectivesES={"Search for the missing Lossoth warriors east of Sûri-kylä","Talk to Terho","Talk to Lothrandir in Sûri-kylä, in Forochel","Elrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House.\
\
You have cleansed the corruption from the Brooch of Bone, and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.","Lothrandir returned to Sûri-kylä in Forochel following the War of the Ring.\
\
Mithrandir believes that the corrupted brooch came from Forochel and returning it there may help cleanse the corruption that befell it in Mordor.","Terho is south-east of Sûri-kylä, calling for help!","Bring the Brooch of Bone to Elrond in Rivendell","Lothrandir asked you to search east of Sûri-kylä while he showed the corrupted brooch to folk in the city.","Lothrandir returned to Sûri-kylä in Forochel following the War of the Ring.","Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of the Snowmen","You found some of the missing Lossoth. Suddenly, you hear shouts from the south-east!","Lothrandir returned to Sûri-kylä in Forochel following the War of the Ring.\
\
Lothrandir gave the corrupted brooch to its rightful owner, but he fears that if the corruption remains it might do her some harm.","Mithrandir has studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang and believes that if it might be cleansed of its corruption it could be empowered with a force for Good.","Talk to Lothrandir in Sûri-kylä and go to see the widow"}},
[3033]={nameES="Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of the Tribes",objectivesES={"An expert tailor in the Hall of Making in Lhanuch may know something about the needle that came into your possession.","Lhunog is on a hill outside the village of Lhanuch.","Talk to Helû outside the village","Hûdh of the Caru-lûth and Cufrus of the Avanc-lûth are in Galtrev and may know more of the bone fragment you carry.","Bring the Needle of Many Leagues to Elrond in Rivendell","Talk to Lhunog on a hill outside Lhanuch","Talk to Suvulch in the village of Lhanuch","Helû has come out of the village for further investigation of the bone fragment.","Talk to Cufrus of the Avanc-lûth, in Galtrev","Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of the Tribes","Elrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House.\
\
You have cleansed the corruption from the Needle of Many Leagues, and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.","Talk to Hûdh of the Caru-lûth in Galtrev","Mithrandir has studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang and believes that if it might be cleansed of its corruption it could be empowered with a force for Good.","With a sudden coughing laugh, an old woman demands your attention","Talk to the expert tailor in the Hall of Making, in Lhanuch","Talk to Helû in Lhanuch","Talk to Frestang of the Uch-lûth, in Galtrev","Helû is a warrior of Lhanuch on the highest rise of the village.","Talk to Raiglud and listen to her tale of long ago","Raiglud, the oldest woman in Lhanuch, has drawn your attention. She is in the Hall of Making, and has a story to tell.","Suvulch is in the village of Lhanuch, in Enedwaith.","Suvulch was not much help, but others in the village might know more","Frestang of the Uch-lûth is in Galtrev.","Talk to Raiglud in the Hall of Making, in Lhanuch"}},
[3034]={nameES="Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of the Wild Men",objectivesES={"Bring the Memento of Bhai-buri-Ghân to Elrond in Rivendell","Talk to Ghân-buri-Ghân at Drû Bhûta","Talk to Khôr-buri-Ghân by the river and travel with him to the island cave","Talk to Khôr-buri-Ghân at the Blood-cloak, in Drû Bhûta","Look for Orcs north of the road by Drû Bhûta, in Taur Drúadan","Khôr-buri-Ghân suggested that you look for Orcs at another place in Taur Drúadan, north-west over a hill.","Mithrandir has studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang and believes that if it might be cleansed of its corruption it could be empowered with a force for Good.","Look for Orcs further north-east in the woods, in Taur Drúadan","Khôr-buri-Ghân is at the Blood-cloak, east of the great waterfall in Drû Bhûta, atop a large rocky cliff. It is the location where the Wild Men perform their funerary rites.","Khôr-buri-Ghân has remembered a cave that his brother told him about and wants to find it. He is by the island in the river, waiting for you to speak with him.","Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of the Wild Men","Elrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House.\
\
You have cleansed the corruption from the Memento of Bhai-buri-Ghân, and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.","Khôr-buri-Ghân suggested that you look for Orcs at two places in Taur Drúadan, forth of Drû Bhûta and further north-east of there, in the woods.","Ghân-buri-Ghân is the leader of the Drúedain and may know the origins of the corrupted carving. He is at Drû Bhûta, in Taur Drúadan.","Look for Orcs to the north-west, over a hill and by an island in the river, in Taur Drúadan"}},
[3035]={nameES="Chapter 2.1: The Settling Fog",objectivesES={"This camp-site location is shaded by dense vegetation, but might serve","Chapter 2.1: The Settling Fog","Talk to Venko at the entrance of the pass to Misthallow","Explore potential camp-site location east of Hlithseld","Your travelling companions have found a suitable camp-site south-east of Hlithseld in Misthallow.","In order to find a safe camp-site, you will need to slay aggressive beasts in Misthallow and scout for possible places to shelter out of the wind.","Imák has pointed out a spot that might make for a suitable camp-site.","It is time for you and your travelling companions to cross into Misthallow, the foggy basin in the northern reaches of the Wells of Langflood.","You have been given a task to complete, and although your companions are not pleased to be travelling together, the four of you intend to see it successfully done.","Imák nods appreciatively. 'This will do,' he says","Cross into Misthallow, the northern reaches of the Wells of Langflood","Your companions suggested that you find a safe place to camp in Misthallow","Explore potential camp-site location south-east of Hlithseld","Imák and Venko are at the entrance to the pass that leads to Misthallow, east and south of the broken Rushgate.","Explore potential camp-site location beside the rocks south-east of Hlithseld","This camp-site location is sheltered on one side by sheer rock","Talk to Imák at the entrance of the pass to Misthallow"}},
[3036]={nameES="Chapter 2.2: Like And Yet Unlike",objectivesES={}},
[3037]={nameES="Chapter 2.2: The Light of Eärendil",objectivesES={"Talk to Mithrandir outside the Black Gate","Elrond has imbued the artifact that came out of Mordor with the Light of Eärendil and gave you a powerful gift.","Chapter 2.2: The Light of Eärendil","Mithrandir is outside the Black Gate."}},
[3038]={nameES="Chapter 2.2: Without Their Lord",objectivesES={"King Elessar has decided to travel next to the town of Arnach, south of Imloth Melui.","King Elessar is working in the village of Arnach, in King's Gondor.","Berry bushes can be found to the south-east of Arnach, in King's Gondor.","Arwen hands you the bow she borrowed from her brother Elrohir","Talk to King Elessar in Arnach, King's Gondor","The hunter who brought down this deer steps out from behind a rock","The folk of Arnach stare at King Elessar and his travelling companions","Queen Arwen is hunting south-east of Arnach.","Chapter 2.2: Without Their Lord","Elladan stands picking berries to the south-east of Arnach, in King's Gondor.","Elrohir is working alongside King Elessar in the village of Arnach, in King's Gondor.","Talk to Baranor in the centre of Arnach, in King's Gondor","Bring Elrohir's bow and quiver to him in Arnach, King's Gondor","Folk of Arnach gather in the main square of the village, staring at the King and his party.","Elladan asked you to begin preparing the meat of the slain deer just to the south-east.","Prepare meat of the slain deer to the south-east of Elladan","The town of Arnach is located to the south of Imloth Melui, in King's Gondor.","Talk to Queen Arwen south-east of Arnach, in King's Gondor","Baranor is in the centre of Arnach, in King's Gondor.","Travel to the main square of Arnach, south of Imloth Melui, in King's Gondor","King Elessar is in the main square of the village of Arnach.","Talk to Elessar in the main square of Arnach","Talk to Elladan south-east of Arnach, in King's Gondor"}},
[3039]={nameES="Chapter 2.3: A Life of Battle",objectivesES={"Talk to Glóin at your camp-site in Misthallow","Imák and Venko are at your camp-site in Misthallow, and they have some thoughts about Glóin's tale.","The conversation ebbs once again, and your companions eat and drink in silence","Talk to Imák at your camp-site in Misthallow","Silence has fallen upon your camp-site, and your companions eat and drink in silence.","No stranger to the adventuring life, Gimli's father Glóin reflects upon his past campaigns and eagerly awaits the next.","Chapter 2.3: A Life of Battle","Talk to Venko at your camp-site in Misthallow","Drink in silence, leaving your companions to their thoughts","Eat in silence, leaving your companions to their thoughts","Glóin is at your camp-site in Misthallow."}},
[3040]={nameES="Chapter 2.3: High Walls, Closed Doors",objectivesES={"Talk to King Elessar on the eastern docks of Pelargir, in King's Gondor","Imladir asked you to find the dwarves from Furukzahar where he saw them last, to the south-east.","A nearby resident of Tumladen stares at the dwarves with anger in his eyes.","King Elessar has asked you to proceed on to Tumladen in order to learn of the situation there before meeting up with the rest of the travelling party in Pelargir.","Talk to Asitám in Tumladen","Talk to Captain Imladir in the centre of Tumladen, in King's Gondor","Talk to Captain Imladir in Tumladen, King's Gondor","An expedition of dwarves has come from Furukzahar with a proposal for the people of Tumladen.","Setényil curses but does not attack","Find the dwarves from Furukzahar to the south-east of Captain Imladir, in Tumladen","The dwarves stare at you warily.","Defári scowls angrily at you and the Tumladen resident","The dwarves from Furukzahar stand in Tumladen, waiting for a friendly <rgb=#00FF00>bow</rgb> of greeting.","You have prevented violence between the dwarves from Furukzahar and residents of Tumladen, and should now speak to Asitám.","Survey debris within Tumladen further up the slope to the north-west","<rgb=#00FF00>Bow</rgb> to the dwarf-expedition from Furukzahar","The dwarves from Furukzahar intend to survey the debris deeper within Tumladen to the north-east.","King Elessar would not appreciate any violence between the Dwarves of Furukzahar and the residents of Tumladen.","Asitám shakes his head and clucks his tongue as he studies the debris","A nearby resident of Tumladen mutters something under his breath","Survey debris within Tumladen up the slope to the north-east","Survey debris deeper within Tumladen to the north-east","Captain Imladir is in the centre of the refuge of Tumladen, located to the west of Arnach, in King's Gondor.","Captain Imladir is in the centre of Tumladen, in King's Gondor.","The dwarves from Furukzahar eye you cautiously","The dwarves from Furukzahar intend to survey the debris within Tumladen, further up the slope to the north-west.","Talk to Asitám in Tumladen, King's Gondor","King Elessar stands by the eastern docks of Pelargir, in King's Gondor.","A nearby resident of Tumladen sighs loudly as the dwarves study the debris","The dwarves from Furukzahar intend to survey the debris within Tumladen, up the slope to the north-east.","Chapter 2.3: High Walls, Closed Doors"}},
[3041]={nameES="Chapter 2.3: Lands of Doom",objectivesES={"The Isenmouthe is guarded, but when has that ever proved a hindrance to you?","Brungos is on the other side of the Isenmouthe, in Dor Amarth.","You have found Covadil, staring up at the Spire of Lûghash","Pass through the Isenmouthe and find Brungos in Dor Amarth","Covadil asked you to search among the old ash piles outside Lûghash for some sign of the Gondorian presence.","Travel to the Isenmouthe in the fortress of Carach Angren","Find Covadil near Lûghash, in Dor Amarth","Talk to Brungos in Dor Amarth","Talk to Covadil near Lûghash","Chapter 2.3: Lands of Doom","Now that you have acquired the Light of Eärendil, Mithrandir has asked you to press further into Mordor.","Bring the broken metal pieces to Covadil near Lûghash","The Isenmouthe is the gate between Udûn and Dor Amarth, and it is built into the fortress of Carach Angren.","The Gondorian scholar Covadil is near the Spire of Lûghash, in Dor Amarth.","Brungos is in a small ruined settlement in Dor Amarth.","You have found Brungos in the Doomfold","Fierce enemies stalk the Doomfold of Dor Amarth, and Brungos asked for your help defeating them.","Covadil went north-east in Dor Amarth, intending to see Lûghash."}},
[3042]={nameES="Chapter 2.4: A Home Long Abandoned",objectivesES={"Glóin directed you to meet up with him on the rocky spur to the west, on which stands the old town of Framsburg, from where the forebears of the Rohirrim once hailed.","These ruins are filled with worm nests, but no sign of the raiding-party","Explore the northern ruins on the Framsburg promontory","Find some disturbed earth among the ruins of Framsburg","Find more tracks somewhere to the south, along the river","Glóin is on the rocky spur on which stands the ruins of Framsburg.","Drakes, worms, and other creatures have taken up residence within the ruins of Framsburg, and Glóin thinks you should defeat the creatures while you search within Framsburg for some sign of the Gundabad raiding-party.","Bring the thundercloud badge to Glóin on the eastern side of the Framsburg promontory","Wind whistles among the cracked stones, but there is no sign of the raiders","Glóin thinks the raiding-party from Gundabad may have passed near Framsburg, and the old dwarf believes you should begin your search near its abandoned ruins for the Orkish threat.","Talk to Glóin on the Framsburg side of the bridge","Chapter 2.4: A Home Long Abandoned","The raiding-party descended from Framsburg and came south, following the river","Imák stands by the tracks he found south of Framsburg.","Glóin is on the rocky spur on which stands the ruins of Framsburg. The old dwarf will be interested in the metal badge you discovered.","Meet up with Glóin at the rocky spur on which stands the ruins of Framsburg","From the mud you pry a metal badge marked with a thundercloud symbol","Glóin believes the Orc raiding-party scouted its path from the Framsburg promontory and continued south, following the river.","Talk to Imák by the tracks south of Framsburg","The town of Framsburg has long since fallen into disrepair","Explore the north-east side of the Framsburg promontory"}},
[3043]={nameES="Chapter 2.4: Low Tide",objectivesES={"King Elessar and Sirgon are overseeing ship repairs in south-eastern Pelargir, King's Gondor.","Faltharan is to the north-west of the auction house in Pelargir, King's Gondor.","Talk to King Elessar at the dry dock in Pelargir, King's Gondor","Sirgon stands along the eastern docks of Pelargir, in King's Gondor.","King Elessar and Sirgon, Lord of Lebennin, consider the poor state of the Gondorian navy following the events of the War of the Ring.","Chapter 2.4: Low Tide","Talk to Sirgon on the eastern docks of Pelargir, in King's Gondor","Brigand toughs on the western side of Pelargir have made problems for Sirgon's shipbuilders, and he wants you to help his son Faltharan deal with them.","Talk to Faltharan north-west of the auction house in Pelargir, King's Gondor","King Elessar and members of his travelling party observe the repairs","King Elessar is at the dry dock in south-eastern Pelargir, King's Gondor.","Find King Elessar and Sirgon at the dry dock in south-eastern Pelargir, King's Gondor"}},
[3044]={nameES="Chapter 2.4: Madness at Barad-dûr",objectivesES={"Rhogrin shakes his head and seems to see you for the first time","A tremendous feeling of evil emanates from the bones of Barad-dûr and adversely affects those unready for its touch.","Mithrandir is outside the Black Gate.","Covadil is on the road east of Lûghash.","A number of soldiers are hurrying down the road towards Lûghash.","Chapter 2.4: Madness at Barad-dûr","Talk to Thorvíl on the road east of Lûghash","Talk to Covadil on the road east of Lûghash","Find Rhogrin on the road to the great abyss east of Lûghash","Covadil has come up to the group of soldiers on the road east of Lûghash.","Rhogrin stands near the great abyss in Dor Amarth.","Talk to Rhogrin on the road to the great abyss","Talk to Fairanc on the road east of Lûghash","Rhogrin stands on the road to the great abyss, unaware of your presence","Talk to Mithrandir outside the Black Gate","Rhogrin is near the great abyss east of the Spire of Lûghash, in Dor Amarth.","Rhogrin is standing on the road to the great abyss in Dor Amarth, and seems to be himself again."}},
[3045]={nameES="Chapter 2.5: Being Neighbourly",objectivesES={"Queen Arwen is at the dry dock in south-eastern Pelargir, in King's Gondor.","Sékhel stands guard outside the entrance to Furukzahar.","Gimli has grown impatient and is not pleased at being made to wait outside the entrance to Furukzahar.","Another dwarf emerges from the stronghold and speaks quietly to Sékhel","Travel to the entrance of Furukzahar in the White Mountains north of Pelargir, in King's Gondor","King Elessar stands outside the entrance to the Temámir fortress of Furukzahar, in the White Mountains.","King Elessar has decided to answer the invitation of the Dwarves of Furukzahar, stronghold of the Temámir in the White Mountains.","A dwarf of the Temámir stands guard at the entrance to Furukzahar","Talk to Kutúkh at the entrance to Furukzahar","Bring the gifts of meat to Sékhel at the entrance to Furukzahar","Talk to Gimli outside the entrance to Furukzahar","The Dwarves of Furukzahar expect a gift from those who visit them, and the guard Sékhel suggested that you hunt the game to be found in the valley for that purpose.","The dwarf Sékhel stands guard at the entrance to Furukzahar.","Talk to King Elessar outside the entrance to Furukzahar, in King's Gondor","Gimli is at the dry dock in south-eastern Pelargir, in King's Gondor.","Talk to Queen Arwen at the dry dock in Pelargir, King's Gondor","Talk to Sékhel at the entrance to Furukzahar","Wait until Sékhel says King Elessar is permitted inside Furukzahar","Talk to Gimli at the dry dock in Pelargir, King's Gondor","Chapter 2.5: Being Neighbourly","Sékhel, the guard outside Furukzahar, has regretfully informed you that King Elessar is not yet permitted inside. He will have to wait a little longer.","Kutúkh has emerged from the stronghold of Furukzahar."}},
[3046]={nameES="Chapter 2.5: Danger Downriver",objectivesES={"Travel toward the town of Limlók, to the north-east","Imák wants you to follow the river southward in search of the raiding-party.","Continue southward along the river in search of more tracks","Talk to Venko in view of Limlók","The Beorning village of Limlók lies peacefully to the north-west","Thrúgord spoke of a village of 'Bear-folk' to which the raiding-party planned to go. He must have meant the town of Limlók, to the north-east.","As Thrúgord dies, he bares his fangs at you in a mocking smile","You find more tracks in the dirt by Hengi's Leap","The blood and the footprints both lead eastward","You find more tracks, but these are speckled with blood","If the raiding-party intended to cross the river here, the broken bridge prevented it","You and your companions discovered evidence that the raiding-party travelled south from the ruins of Framsburg. Where has it now gone?","Venko looks out upon the Beorning village of Limlók, the obvious question on his lips: where is the raiding-party?","Chapter 2.5: Danger Downriver","By Hengi's Leap you found more tracks left by the raiding-party, but the broken bridge likely prevented them from crossing the river. They may have continued south instead.","Continue following the river south in search of more tracks","Bloody tracks led eastward, away from the river.","Find the source of the blood-spattered tracks"}},
[3047]={nameES="Chapter 2.5: Mouth of Gondor",objectivesES={"An emissary from Dulgabêth has come to treat with Gondor.","Yadêphal is at the Black Gate, waiting to bring Aragorn to treat with his master.","Aragorn is at the Black Gate.","Chapter 2.5: Mouth of Gondor","Talk to Yadêphal and meet with Dulgabêth","Yadêphal has come to the Black Gate, an emissary from his master.","Aragorn is waiting at the Black Gate to hear the terms of Dulgabêth's peace.","Talk to Yadêphal at the Black Gate","Talk to Aragorn at the Black Gate","Yadêphal, emissary of Dulgabêth, is at the Black Gate."}},
[3048]={nameES="Chapter 2.6: Dwarves of Furukzahar",objectivesES={"Talk to Asitám in Furukzahar","Hámisar smiles at King Elessar indulgently","Talk to King Elessar in the throne room of Furukzahar","King Elessar and Hámisar of the Temámir speak together in the throne room of Furukzahar.","Explore the armoury of Furukzahar","Talk to Hámisar inside the throne room of Furukzahar","Curiously, you feel a strange sensation of dread as you approach the door","Chapter 2.6: Dwarves of Furukzahar","The armoury bustles with activity and the sound of dwarves working at the forges","Find Hámisar in the throne room of Furukzahar","Hámisar has invited you to meet the people of Furukzahar while he speaks with King Elessar.","The ruler of Furukzahar awaits you and the King of Gondor in his throne room in the north-western reaches of the fortress.","Talk to Zimikál in Furukzahar","The delicious aroma of cooking food fills the kitchens of Furukzahar","Talk to Gúlkhu in Furukzahar","Explore the kitchens of Furukzahar","Explore the rooms south of the throne room in Furukzahar","Hámisar rules Furukzahar from his throne room in the north-western reaches of the fortress.","Talk to Hámisar in the throne room of Furukzahar","King Elessar has been invited to visit Furukzahar, a stronghold of the Temámir dwarves in the White Mountains.","Hámisar nods his head to Elessar in greeting"}},
[3049]={nameES="Chapter 2.6: Limlók Under Attack",objectivesES={"Venko does not believe that Limlók is safe, and the Zhélruka warrior wants to investigate.","Chapter 2.6: Limlók Under Attack","Imák stands in the centre of Limlók, satisfied with the day's fighting.","You have come to the Beorning village of Limlók with your travelling companions, but there is no sign of the raiding-party from Gundabad.","Talk to Imák in Limlók","Talk to Venko and search Limlók for the vanished raiding-party"}},
[3050]={nameES="Chapter 2.7: A Thirst for Blood",objectivesES={"Chapter 2.7: A Thirst for Blood","Glóin barely notices your approach. What troubles the old dwarf?","Talk to Glóin at the edge of Limlók","Runerik Knotbeard stands in the village of Limlók.","Return to Runerik Knotbeard in the village of Limlók","Talk to Runerik Knotbeard in Limlók.","Talk to Glóin in Limlók","Talk to Imák in Limlók","Join Glóin at the edge of Limlók","Imák stands in the village of Limlók.","Glóin has walked away from your companions and stands now at the edge of Limlók, deep in thought. What troubles the old dwarf?","The Blade-feast raiding-party has been defeated and the village of Limlók is safe, but the news that Gundabad has a new lord can only mean further troubles ahead for the region washed by the Langflood.","Glóin remains silent, contemplating the words of Natsatúg.","Talk to Venko in Limlók","Runerik looks pleased with himself and with the bravery of his folk","Glóin has returned to Limlók.","Glóin has walked away from your companions and stands now at the edge of Limlók, deep in thought."}},
[3051]={nameES="Chapter 2.7: Khôltekh the Cunning",objectivesES={"Talk to Gimli in the guest rooms of Furukzahar","King Elessar is in the throne room of Furukzahar.","Gangur Farwend, a Longbeard visiting from the north, has quietly called for your attention.","King Elessar is in the guest rooms of Furukzahar on the eastern side of the fortress.","Caebar is in the guest rooms of Furukzahar.","Talk to Gangur Farwend by the suspicious door in Furukzahar","The guest rooms of Furukzahar are on the eastern side of the fortress.","Investigate the suspicious door south of the throne room in Furukzahar","Talk to King Elessar in the throne room of Furukzahar","Elessar hands you a parchment on which Caebar has sketched a portrait","Hámisar has provided comfortable rooms for Elessar and his companions","Elessar gave you the sketch Caebar made of Khôltekh the Cunning from Gangur's description.","Find the guest rooms provided for Elessar's party on the eastern side of Furukzahar","A member of the Kindred of the Coins brought a proposal to Hámisar of Furukzahar in recent weeks.","Chapter 2.7: Khôltekh the Cunning","Examine the sketch of Khôltekh the Cunning","Talk to Gangur Farwend inside the armoury of Furukzahar in the north-eastern reaches of the fortress","Talk to Caebar in the guest rooms of Furukzahar","Return the sketch of Khôltekh the Cunning to Caebar in the guest rooms of Furukzahar","Gangur Farwend has information for you, but he will only share it if you meet with him inside the armoury of Furukzahar.","King Elessar's small travelling party waits in the guest rooms provided by Hámisar.","As you approach the suspicious door, a nearby dwarf seeks to attract your attention","You experienced a sensation of dread near a door located south of the throne room in Furukzahar, and King Elessar thinks you should investigate further.","Talk to King Elessar in the guest rooms of Furukzahar"}},
[3052]={nameES="Chapter 2.8: Snakes in the Grass",objectivesES={"Talk to King Elessar in the throne room of Furukzahar","Talk to Hámisar in the throne room of Furukzahar","Something has gravely upset Glindor and others of the travelling party","King Elessar is in the throne room of Furukzahar.","Chapter 2.8: Snakes in the Grass","Rejoin Elessar's travelling party outside the Hall of Ost Anglebed","The time has come for Elessar and his companions to leave Furukzahar and rejoin the larger company.","Talk to Glindor outside the Hall of Ost Anglebed","The Hall of Ost Anglebed is to be found south-west of Furukzahar, in King's Gondor.","Hámisar is in the throne room of Furukzahar."}},
[3053]={nameES="Chapter 2.9: The Queen Is Gone",objectivesES={"You found Queen Arwen deep in conversation with Roamingstar","Roamingstar stands beside Queen Arwen, north-west of Ost Anglebed, in King's Gondor.","King Elessar has arrived","Learn where Queen Arwen has gone","Queen Arwen has disappeared, and none know where she might be found.","Talk to Roamingstar, Maiden of the Gilrain","Queen Arwen is deep in conversation with Roamingstar, north-west of Ost Anglebed, in King's Gondor.","Talk to King Elessar north-west of Ost Anglebed, in King's Gondor","Talk to Queen Arwen","Find Queen Arwen in King's Gondor","Chapter 2.9: The Queen Is Gone","You should ask around Ost Anglebed and learn if anyone knows where the Elf-queen has gone.","King Elessar has rejoined his Queen north-west of Ost Anglebed, in King's Gondor.","Wait for a new arrival","Ioreth told you she saw someone wearing a cloak much like Queen Arwen's walking to the north-west of Ost Anglebed, in the direction of the river."}},
[3054]={nameES="Chapter 2: A First Furtive Foray",objectivesES={"<rgb=#FF00FF>Listen</rgb> to the half-orcs","You should talk to Pippin and Merry in Bâr Thorenion.","Three travel-worn half-orcs stand on the ledge above you, north of the main road in Udûn, talking amongst themselves. You should <rgb=#FF00FF>listen</rgb> to hear some more.","Pippin and Merry are north of the main road in Udûn.\
\
You should talk to Merry and Pippin about the trio of half-orcs you just overheard.","Three travel-worn half-orcs stand on the ledge above you, north of the main road in Udûn, talking amongst themselves. You should continue to listen <rgb=#FF00FF>listen</rgb> to their conversation.","Look for a northward path ahead","You should talk to Pippin, who says his stomach is growling.\
\
If you should get separated from Pippin or Merry, use their horns to call them back to you.","Habla con Merry","You have only begun eating when Merry looks up, startled","Habla con Gandalf","Merry has suggested going a bit further along the main road in the Udûn valley, and then look for a way that turns north.\
\
If you should get separated from Pippin or Merry, use their horns to call them back to you.","Habla con Pippin","Blow Merry's horn to call him back","Explore to the soldiers' camps","Return to Merry and Pippin","<rgb=#FF00FF>Sit</rgb> down and share in the meal","You should explore further along the main road in the Udûn valley, where the mass of soldiers' tents begins.\
\
If you should get separated from Pippin or Merry, use their horns to call them back to you.","Habla con Aragorn","You should talk to Merry, at the picnic spread in Udûn, and find out what startled him.","Habla con Éomer","Pippin has suggested moving to a flat spot just north of the main road in Udûn, and stopping to eat some and rest up.\
\
If you should get separated from Pippin or Merry, use their horns to call them back to you.","Merry and Pippin persist in their determination to venture into Mordor.","You should return to Merry and Pippin in Bâr Thorenion with word that they have Aragorn and Éomer's blessings to go into Mordor.","Find Pippin in Bâr Thorenion","Look for the source of the sound","You hear a gruff, familiar throat being cleared behind you","Explore to the cross-roads","You should explore down in the Udûn valley, as far as the first cross-roads, with Merry and Pippin.\
\
If you should get separated from Pippin or Merry, use their horns to call them back to you.","Chapter 2: A First Furtive Foray","The two hobbits quickly lay out a considerable amount of food on a thin Gondorian quilt","Both Aragorn and Éomer can be found outside of the Black Gate, in the area of the Slag Hills.\
\
Merry and Pippin have asked you to ask Aragorn and Éomer for permission to venture into Mordor.","Go up the northern path from the hobbits' picnic in Udûn and see if you can find what Merry heard.","Merry looks uncharacteristically pale.\
\
'I have lost my appetite for food, and adventure, and any promise of treasure or gold, Pippin. Let us call it a day and head back, shall we?'","Stop for a bite to eat","DNT YOU FIND SOME THINGS","You should <rgb=#FF00FF>sit</rgb> down with Pippin and Merry at their Mordor picnic spread, off the main road in Udûn, and share in the meal.","You should meet Merry and Pippin at the Foothold encampment in Udûn.","DNT merry returns","DNT summon merry","Meet at the Udûn Foothold","Gandalf has appeared nearby to Aragorn and Éomer, outside the Black Gate in the Slag Hills, and has made it clear that he wishes to talk to you."}},
[3055]={nameES="Capítulo 2: Un poder mayor",objectivesES={"Glúmur tiene curiosidad por las últimas palabras de los sirvientes de Mazog, sus leales guardias Pûlpum, y quiere que descubras si hay algo de verdad en sus últimas palabras.","Capítulo 2: Un poder mayor","Bori se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo, cerca de la sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Has recuperado algunos cofres del tesoro de Zabadgathol y deberías llevarlos a Bori para que los examine.","Lleva los cofres del tesoro a Bori","Zabadgathol se encuentra en Nud-melek.\
\
Glúmur te ha pedido que regreses a Zabadgathol, la fortaleza de Mazog en Nud-melek, y que busques cofres del tesoro que puedan revelar la identidad de su misterioso aliado."}},
[3056]={nameES="Capítulo 2: Lejos de casa",objectivesES={"Capítulo 2: Lejos de casa","Los Orcos se pueden encontrar por todo Zelem-melek y las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo de Moria.\
\
Brogur te ha pedido que derrotes a los Orcos por todo Zelem-melek y las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo, sin importar a qué tribu pertenezcan.","Brogur se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo junto a la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Has derrotado a muchos Orcos en Moria, y deberías informar ahora a Brogur de tu éxito.","Brogur está preocupado porque un uruk de la Mano Blanca ha estado explorando cerca del campamento de los enanos."}},
[3057]={nameES="Capítulo 2: A lo largo del Sirannon",objectivesES={"Se pueden encontrar crebains espías a lo largo de las orillas del Sirannon seco, al sureste de la puerta en ruinas en el área cerca de los Muros de Moria.\
\
Tulk te ha pedido que derrotes a los crebains espías a lo largo de las orillas del Sirannon y que le traigas sus garras, que se pueden usar para varios propósitos.","Lleva las garras irregulares a Tulk","Capítulo 2: A lo largo del Sirannon","Has ofrecido tus servicios a la expedición de enanos que ha venido a Acebeda para reclamar las salas de Khazad-dûm bajo las montañas.","Tulk se encuentra al este de la puerta en ruinas en el área cerca de los Muros de Moria.\
\
El enano Tulk espera tu regreso con las garras que has recogido de los crebains espías a lo largo del Sirannon."}},
[3058]={nameES="Capítulo 2: Enemistad con los orcos los Orcos",objectivesES={"Has derrotado suficientes orcos en Moria para satisfacer a Haldir","Completa la hazaña 'Azote de orcos' en Moria","Haldir se encuentra en su campamento en la frontera de Lothlórien.\
\
Has completado dos grandes hazañas dentro de Moria, y podría ser que el recuento de tus victorias sobre los Orcos y los trasgos de Moria sea suficiente para satisfacer a Haldir sobre tus intenciones.","Capítulo 2: Enemistad con los orcos los Orcos","Completa la hazaña 'Azote de trasgos' en Moria","Has derrotado suficientes trasgos en Moria para satisfacer a Haldir"}},
[3059]={nameES="Chapter 2: At the Stone of Erech",objectivesES={"Candaith is at the camp-site of the Grey Company in a grove of trees east of the Uch-luth village of Lhanuch, in Nan Laeglin.\
\
You have listened to Candaith relate the tale of the Oath-breakers and the Paths of the Dead and should now speak with him.","Chapter 2: At the Stone of Erech","Talk to Candaith at the grove east of Lhanuch and experience 'Session: At the Stone of Erech' or read the shortened account instead","Candaith is at the camp-site of the Grey Company in a grove of trees to the east of the Uch-luth village of Lhanuch, in Nan Laeglin.\
\
Candaith has decided to tell you the story of the Oath-breakers and the Paths of the Dead.","In the Second Age, the Men of the Mountain swear an oath at the Stone of Erech to fight the forces of Sauron, but when they break their promise, Isildur levies a curse against them. They will never know rest until they fulfil their oath....","Talk to Candaith at the grove east of Lhanuch","Candaith wishes you to know the story of the Oath-breakers and the Paths of the Dead, so you can appreciate why the Rangers are so disturbed by the words of Nár."}},
[3060]={nameES="Capítulo 2: La recomendación de Bósi",objectivesES={"Bósi está satisfecho de que hayas ayudado a sus enanos con los preparativos, y quiere que hagas lo mismo por los enanos del Corazón de Fuego.","Capítulo 2: La recomendación de Bósi","Stóthkell es el enano a cargo del Corazón de Fuego, ubicado cerca de la Vía de los Herreros, entre las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata.\
\
Bósi quiere que prestes tu ayuda a los enanos que trabajan en el Corazón de Fuego para que estén preparados si los orcos atacan la Vía de los Herreros."}},
[3061]={nameES="Chapter 2: Candaith's Hidden Cache",objectivesES={"Candaith is at his camp in the Lone-lands, at the foot of Weathertop.\
\
Elrohir has told you to bring word to the Dúnadan Candaith of the Grey Company's preparations.","The Dúnadan Candaith has a camp near the foot of Weathertop, in the Lone-lands. He must be told the mission of the Grey Company.","Locate Candaith's hidden cache at Echad Sûl","Orskdulug falls, his robbery a failure, and you retrieve Candaith's goods","An unsavoury gentleman stands where you thought to find the hidden cache","Candaith is at his camp below Weathertop, in the Lone-lands.\
\
You have recovered the supplies from the hidden cache that were taken by Orskdulug and ruined his plan to rob you with them.","Talk to Candaith at Weathertop","Candaith's hidden cache is north-east of his encampment, atop a small rise called Echad Sûl, in the shade of a tree.\
\
The Ranger Candaith has asked you to recover a hidden cache of supplies he prepared some time ago, as he will have need of its contents on the journey of the Grey Company.","Return to Candaith with the equipment you took from Orskdulug","Candaith's hidden cache at Echad Sûl seems to be gone, and an unsavoury gentleman stands there instead.\
\
Candaith sent you to recover a cache of supplies, but it may now be missing.","Chapter 2: Candaith's Hidden Cache","Talk to Orskdulug at Amon Sûl"}},
[3062]={nameES="Chapter 2: Embassies from Many Lands",objectivesES={"You have found the emissaries from Harad","The delegation of Elves are just north of the prow, in the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.","Find the Haradrim delegation to Minas Tirith","You have found the Elf emissaries from Lothlórien","The delegation of Haradrim is on the south-eastern side of the Third Circle of Minas Tirith.","Talk to Lalornil of the delegation from Lórien","The delegation of dwarves is on the north-east side of the Fifth Circle in Minas Tirith.","Talk to Mauthoi of the delegation from Harad","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to Elessar and the Kingdom of Gondor, and to fight on their behalf in Mordor.","You have found the dwarf emissaries from Erebor","The emissaries from Erebor are on the north-east side of the Fifth Circle in Minas Tirith.","King Elessar is in his throne room atop Minas Tirith.","Talk to Olphadon of the delegation from Lórien","Talk to Hálsi of the delegation from Erebor","Find the dwarf delegation in Minas Tirith","Chapter 2: Embassies from Many Lands","Find the Elf delegation to Minas Tirith","Talk to Hasong of the delegation from Harad","Talk to King Elessar in his throne room","Talk to Vígmath of the delegation from Erebor"}},
[3063]={nameES="Chapter 2: Loyalty for the New King",objectivesES={"King Thorin III has asked you to deliver news of his ascension to the throne to the following dwarf-leaders throughout Eriador and the Misty Mountains:\
\
Dwalin in Thorin's Hall, Ered Luin.\
Mathi Stouthand at Gondamon, Ered Luin\
Hannar at Othrikar, North Downs\
Avar at Gabilshathûr, East Angmar\
Bósi in the Twenty-first Hall, in Moria\
\
After you have delivered his words to each of these dwarf-leaders, you are to return to the King under the Mountain.","Bósi gives you a stone containing a very small portion of mithril","Thorin III, King under the Mountain, is at his throne in Erebor.","Talk to Dwalin in Thorin's Hall, in Ered Luin","Talk to Avar at Gabilshathûr, in East Angmar","Talk to Bósi in the Twenty-first Hall of Khazad-dûm","Talk to Mathi Stouthand at Gondamon, in Ered Luin","Chapter 2: Loyalty for the New King","Hrostyr gives you King Thorin's proclamations for delivery to several dwarf outposts","Talk to Hannar at Othrikar, in the North Downs","Talk to King Thorin III at his throne in the Hall under the Mountain","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to Durin's Folk and fight on their behalf in Mordor."}},
[3064]={nameES="Capítulo 2: El descanso del Portador del Anillo",objectivesES={"Capítulo 2: El descanso del Portador del Anillo","Frodo Bolsón está en la cima de la colina de Cerin Amroth con algunos miembros de su compañía.\
\
Milwen te ha pedido que hables con Frodo Bolsón, uno de los ocho visitantes que han llegado a Lórien en los últimos días. La doncella elfa está segura de que las noticias de Eriador le interesarán.","Boromir está vagando por los alrededores noroeste del claro donde se alza Cerin Amroth, en el centro de Lórien.\
\
Merry se pregunta si una conversación contigo podría animar a Boromir, quien no parece estar contento con la presencia de la compañía en Lothlórien.","Gimli está en la plataforma en la cima de Cerin Amroth, en el centro de Lórien.\
\
Boromir, algo molesto por la creciente confianza de Gimli en los Elfos, te ha pedido que hables con el enano.","Samsagaz Gamyi está de pie en la cima de la colina de Cerin Amroth junto a Frodo.\
\
Frodo te ha pedido que le cuentes a él y a Sam las noticias de Eriador.","Meriadoc Brandigamo está dando un paseo en los alrededores de la colina de Cerin Amroth, y puede que ahora esté descansando en un jardín privado cercano.\
\
Frodo y Sam se alegraron mucho de verte en Lothlórien y saben que Merry también lo estará.","Milwen te ha hablado de varios visitantes de Lórien que estarán interesados en hablar contigo."}},
[3065]={nameES="Capítulo 2: Rumor de Mazog",objectivesES={"Encuentra un cofre que contenga información sobre Mazog en Maudhûl-ulur o Ashurz Maufulug","Lleva el informe sobre Mazog a Alfirimbes","Capítulo 2: Rumor de Mazog","Alfirimbes cree que el éxito de la misión de la Guardia Oculta depende de mantener la presencia de Mazog en secreto frente a los Orcos del Bosque Negro.","Dentro del cofre encuentras una carta dirigida a Mazog","Alfirimbes está en Echad Sirion, el campamento de la Hueste Dorada en los Lindes Oscuros, al norte de Maudhûl-ulur y Ashúrz-maufulug.\
\
Has encontrado un comunicado destinado a Mazog en el cofre de un jefe orco y deberías llevarlo ahora a Alfirimbes.","Buscas en el cofre, pero no encuentras nada que mencione a Mazog.","Habla con Lúth Martillogrís en Echad Sirion","Orcos Taughâsh y viles trasgos pueden encontrarse por todos los Lindes Oscuros. Cofres que pueden contener mensajes orcos pueden encontrarse dentro de los campamentos de Maudhûl-ulur y Ashúrz Maufulug, al sureste de Echad Sirion.\
\
Alfirimbes te ha pedido que busques en las fortificaciones orcas de los Lindes Oscuros para saber si los Orcos del Bosque Negro se han enterado de la presencia de Mazog.","Alfirimbes está en Echad Sirion, supervisando cautelosamente la defensa del campamento.\
\
Luth Martillogrís ha exigido que un miembro de su familia sea asignado como centinela para vigilar al líder orco cautivo.","Luth Martillogrís está mostrando sus malos sentimientos mientras deambula por Echad Sirion.\
\
Alfirimbes quiere que tranquilices a Luth Martillogrís diciéndole que se están tomando las medidas necesarias para garantizar que la misión de la Guardia Oculta se lleve a cabo de manera segura y que la cautividad de Mazog no esté amenazada.","Habla con Alfirimbes en Echad Sirion"}},
[3066]={nameES="Capítulo 2: Almacenes de las Galerías Occidentales",objectivesES={"La Cámara del Conocimiento, la Cámara de la Sabiduría y la Cámara de la Reflexión Profunda se pueden encontrar en algún lugar dentro de la Gran Excavación de Moria.\
\
Bósi te ha pedido que busques en tres antiguos almacenes de la Gran Excavación páginas, tabletas o tomos que le permitan aprender más sobre los Días Antiguos.","Encuentra y busca en la Cámara del Conocimiento","Encuentras una tableta rota dentro del cofre fuerte; su inscripción aún se puede discernir","Lleva los registros históricos a Bósi","Encuentras algunas páginas marchitas dentro del cofre fuerte; la escritura aún es legible","Encuentras un tomo desgastado dentro del cofre fuerte; parte de su texto aún se puede descifrar","Encuentra y busca en la Cámara de la Sabiduría","Capítulo 2: Almacenes de las Galerías Occidentales","Bósi te ha pedido que busques tres almacenes dentro de la Gran Excavación de Moria e intentes recuperar cualquier registro o historia que haya sobrevivido.","Bósi se encuentra en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, en la entrada sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación de Moria.\
\
Has reunido antiguos registros de Moria de tres almacenes en la Gran Excavación y deberías llevárselos a Bósi.","Encuentra y busca en la Cámara de la Reflexión Profunda"}},
[3067]={nameES="Chapter 2: The Assault on Azanulbizar",objectivesES={"Chapter 2: The Assault on Azanulbizar","Talk to the Iron-folk messenger at Ashmargathâl","Talk to Hermáth Stormhammer at Khur Azan","Dwarves of the Landorrim, Narfanghoth, and Temámir can be found at Zirakazhâr on the slopes of Zirakzigil to the north-west of Amdân. Dwarves of the Kámbrada, Zhélruka, and Abnúzhu can be found at Ashmargathâl, far to the north of Amdân on the slopes of Bundushâthur.\
\
Dáin has asked you to aid the other Dwarves of the Haban'akkâ. You should aid the dwarves in Amdân, as well as those who have battled to Zirakazhâr and Ashmargathâl.","Aid the Dwarves of the Landorrim, Narfanghoth, and Temámir at Zirakazhâr","As you continue to read Hermáth Stormhammer's account of the Battle of Azanulbizar, you begin the second chapter in which the Dwarves of the Haban'akkâ of Thráin wake to a dark winter's day and the battle is joined.","Hermáth Stormhammer can be found at Khur Azan, the Dim-crossing.\
\
After learning of how Hermáth Stormhammer aided the dwarves who battled upon the slopes of Zirakzigil and Bundushâthur, Hermáth Stormhammer interjects and calls your attention to events at Khur Azan, the Dim-crossing.","An Iron-folk messenger can be found at Zirakazhâr or Ashmargathâl.\
\
After aiding the Dwarves of the Haban'akkâ, a messenger of the Iron-folk has arrived bearing urgent news for you.","Talk to the Iron-folk messenger at Zirakazhâr","Aid the Dwarves of the Kámbrada, Zhélruka, and Abnúzhu at Ashmargathâl"}},
[3068]={nameES="Chapter 2: The Grey Company in Rivendell",objectivesES={"Chapter 2: The Grey Company in Rivendell","The Grey Company prepares to depart from Rivendell for the wide southern lands and needs your help to make sure that all is ready.","Habla con Elrohir","Habla con Golodir","Candaith is outside the gate by the stables in Rivendell.\
\
You have spoken with several of the Rangers of the Grey Company in Rivendell and should now speak with Candaith.","Golodir, Lothrandir, Radanir, and Elrohir are preparing to depart in and around the stables of Rivendell.\
\
Halbarad has asked you to check with several members of the Grey Company about their final preparations.","Talk to Candaith in Rivendell, outside the gate by the stables","Talk to Lothrandir","Talk to Radanir","Aragorn's standard will remain furled until the time is right"}},
[3069]={nameES="Chapter 2: The Mountain-home",objectivesES={}},
[3070]={nameES="Chapter 2: The Time Before Travelling",objectivesES={"Some Elves sing as they work, their voices sweet and strange and also, somehow, sad","Bring parcels to Tordúril","You should visit Elrond Half-elven. He stands in the library of his house in Rivendell.","Carry the goods down to the Rivendell Forges","Chapter 2: The Time Before Travelling","You should bring the parcels you gathered to Tordúril in the Rivendell Market.","Find Arwen in Imlad Gelair","You should help Elves packing throughout Elrond's house in Rivendell.","Elrond stands in his customary spot, brow furrowed, directing Elves in all manner of packing, provisioning, and planning","Elrond has suggested you visit Bilbo, who can be found in the Hall of Fire in the Last Homely House in Rivendell.","Talk to Hammadelen","Talk to Galdor","Talk to Pethelen outside Elrond's House","Parcels delivered","Lindir can be found in the Hall of Fire in Elrond's house in Rivendell.\
\
You should ask Lindir how you can help with the preparations.","Lady Arwen has asked that you visit her in Imlad Gelair, below the falls in Rivendell.","You should go to Rivendell's Market and gather provisions and goods requisitioned for the journey. You will need to ask among the merchants and artisans and also look for some requisitions left lying around.","Arwen and Eliaril stand in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell.\
\
Hear Arwen's response to Eliaril.","Talk to Eliaril","Arwen and Eliaril stand in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell.\
\
You should talk to Eliaril, Arwen's maid-in-waiting, and see if you can calm her down.","Habla con Elrond","Return to Pethelen","You find Arwen flanked by maids-in-waiting","Talk to Arwen","Judging on the piles and number of busy hands, no few Elves are going on this journey","You should bring the pile of parcels next to Tordúril from the Market down to the Rivendell Forges.","You should return to Pethelen, before Elrond's house in Rivendell, now that you have gathered the parcels as he asked.","You should talk to Elrond Half-elven. He stands in the library of his house in Rivendell.","Talk to Anornaneth","Visit Bilbo Baggins","Talk to Dúrvenel","You have helped a number of packing Elves and should return to Lindir in Elrond's house.","Lindir suggested you look for Pethelen outside Elrond's house in Rivendell, to help with more preparations for the journey.","Lindir laughs.\
\
'It is true, you cannot plead infirmity and age as Master Bilbo here does! We will indeed not turn away help that is offered, for we wish to set out on our journey with some happy haste. Anywhere within these walls you see packing, you are welcome to lend a hand!'","Return to Lindir","Talk to Ladrochan, the Stable-master","You should check in on Elrond in his library in Rivendell to see if he is ready to talk to you.","Habla con Lindir","Pay a visit to Rivendell. Learn what has happened there, what Elrond knows of Glorfindel, and why the house prepares for travel.","Even from outside, the Last Homely House is astir with a new kind of bustling life","Arwen has asked you to find several books in Elrond's library in Rivendell.","Visit Elrond in Rivendell"}},
[3071]={nameES="Capítulo 2: Lo que dejó Gorothúl",objectivesES={"Issuriel se preocupa de que las palabras de Mazog puedan revelar una amenaza oculta para los Elfos de Lothlórien y los Enanos de Moria.","Lenglammel y Forglinn se encuentran en Gwathrendath, el puesto avanzado de los Elfos en las profundidades de las Fundaciones de Piedra, en Moria.\
\
Issuriel cree que Gorothúl puede haber puesto en marcha algún mal que podría devastar Moria de tal manera que incluso Mazog esté buscando otro reino para gobernar.","Habla con Lenglammel en Gwathrendath","Habla con Forglinn en Gwathrendath","Capítulo 2: Lo que dejó Gorothúl","Habla con Bróin en la Senda Pacífica","Bróin se encuentra en la Senda Pacífica, ubicada junto al Camino de Durin.\
\
Los Elfos de Gwathrendath están de acuerdo con la evaluación de Issuriel de que Gorothúl puso en marcha algún mal antes de partir hacia Dol Guldur. Bróin debe ser notificado de esto, ya que concierne a la Guarnición de Hierro y puede afectar sus planes para el rescate de Bori."}},
[3072]={nameES="Chapter 3 - A Formal Meeting with Aphamâr",objectivesES={}},
[3073]={nameES="Chapter 3 - Meeting Achardis",objectivesES={}},
[3074]={nameES="Chapter 3.10: Enemies of Anfalas",objectivesES={"Caebar is in the central yard of Lond Cirion. He seems worried about something.","Talk to Caebar in the central yard of Lond Cirion","Return to Lond Cirion to report of your successes","Borion thanks you for the help","King Elessar has offered the help of his companions in the defence of Anfalas, and that includes any assistance you can provide to Lady Marra's scouts.","Galleth thanks you for the help","Talk to Borion north of Lond Cirion","Talk to Galleth on the beach south of Lond Cirion","Gilvenel thanks you for the help","Chapter 3.10: Enemies of Anfalas","Now that you have aided the scouts, you should return to Lond Cirion.","Caebar calls you over to him. He seems worried","Talk to Gilvenel on the hill east of Lond Cirion","Lady Marra's scouts can be found outside Lond Cirion to the north, east, and south."}},
[3075]={nameES="Chapter 3.11: Last Wishes of the Lord of Langstrand",objectivesES={"Talk to Caebar in the central yard of Lond Cirion and accompany him to the King","King Elessar is in the main hall of Lond Cirion.","Talk to King Elessar in the main hall of Lond Cirion","Chapter 3.11: Last Wishes of the Lord of Langstrand","Talk to Marra in the main hall of Lond Cirion","King Elessar has called upon Caebar to provide a service for Lond Cirion, and the scribe is worried about it.","Marra stares forward and says nothing.","Lady Marra is in the main hall of Lond Cirion.","Caebar is in the central yard of Lond Cirion, where he has confided in you that he is worried about the service King Elessar has asked him to provide."}},
[3076]={nameES="Chapter 3.12: Grief and Duty",objectivesES={"Talk to Orgolas outside the keep of Lond Cirion","Daeram is outside the keep of Lond Cirion.","Talk to Marra in the main hall of Lond Cirion","Orgolas is outside the keep of Lond Cirion.","Talk to Daeram outside the keep of Lond Cirion","Lady Marra has entreated the King to forbid her son from leaving Lond Cirion.","Lady Marra is in the main hall of Lond Cirion.","Chapter 3.12: Grief and Duty","Talk to Queen Arwen in the main hall of Lond Cirion","Queen Arwen has something she wishes to say to Lady Marra."}},
[3077]={nameES="Chapter 3.1: A Matter of Survival",objectivesES={"The bear cub snorts in your direction, but you cannot guess at its meaning. Is this Vídar? You hope so, both for your sake and his!","Glóin has made his decision: he must send message-ravens to Skarháld and to the Lonely Mountain bearing word of this new Lord of Gundabad.","The dwarves have gathered behind Runerik and Yrsa's lodge to release the messenger-ravens.","Talk to Vídar","Watch the departure of the messenger-ravens","The messenger-ravens will bear word of the new Lord of Gundabad to Durin at Skarháld and to King Thorin in the Lonely Mountain.","Runerik Knotbeard is outside his lodge in the village of Limlók.","Glóin grunts without commitment","Chapter 3.1: A Matter of Survival","Find Glóin and his ravens in the centre of Limlók","Talk to Imák behind Runerik's lodge","The bear cub hurries away in triumph!","The dwarves have gathered to watch Glóin release the ravens","The box of scrolls is near the task board in Limlók.","Yrsa Spearwife is in south-east Limlók.\
\
According to her son Vídar, Yrsa has tasked him with scouting outside the village once a week.","Yrsa Spearwife is in south-east Limlók.","Bring the small parchments to Glóin in Limlók","Yrsa told you to scout the wild lands south of Limlók with her son Vídar. You will find the Beorning boy at one of three different spots: to the south-east, south, or south-west of the village.","Take some small parchments from the box of scrolls","Talk to Yrsa Spearwife in Limlók","Imák is behind Runerik's lodge to watch the release of the messenger-ravens.","Glóin is in the centre of the village, preparing his ravens to carry messages to Skarháld and the Lonely Mountain.","You remove suitable papers from the box, leaving some for the folk of Limlók","Find the dwarves behind Runerik and Yrsa's lodge","Glóin is focused on preparing the ravens. He has not noticed you.","Talk to Vídar at one of his three favourite scouting locations","Talk to Runerik Knotbeard outside his lodge in Limlók","Talk to Runerik Knotbeard in Limlók","A young Beorning child stands nearby, fascinated by Glóin and the messenger-ravens.","Glóin has attracted some attention while he readies his ravens"}},
[3078]={nameES="Chapter 3.1: The Dread Lands",objectivesES={"Mithrandir is in Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate.","Aragorn believes that you learned two useful pieces of information from Dulgabêth that should guide your further adventures in Gorgoroth.","Mithrandir has asked you to follow both of the leads you have uncovered, accompanying Atli into Lhingris and Harthalín into Talath Úrui.","Complete 'Chapter 3.3: The Gúrzyul' in Talath Úrui","Chapter 3.1: The Dread Lands","Complete 'Chapter 3.2: The Second Garrison' in Lhingris","Complete 'Chapter 3.2: The Valley of Webs' in Lhingris","Ayorzén the Wily is in Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate.","Talk to Mithrandir in Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate","Complete 'Chapter 3.3: Fate of the Stonemaiden' in Talath Úrui","Talk to Ayorzén in Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate"}},
[3079]={nameES="Chapter 3.1: The Prince's Guest",objectivesES={}},
[3080]={nameES="Chapter 3.2: Runerik's Request",objectivesES={"Venko is at the north-western point of the White Mare.","Runerik Knotbeard followed you to the White Mare with some of his people. Why?","Add the flood-broom to the boiling water in the north room of Runerik's lodge","Bring the unspent arrows to Yrsa Spearwife in Limlók for her inspection","Some unexpected visitors have come north-west of the White Mare, across the river from your dwarf companions. Why have they followed you here?","Bring the flood-broom tea to Runerik Knotbeard inside his lodge","Hjála's wing is broken, pierced by an arrow","Vaka lives, but has lost several feathers and a lot of blood","Talk to Glóin behind Runerik's lodge","Runerik is inside his lodge, tending to the wounded messenger-ravens.","Talk to Runerik Knotbeard inside his lodge in Limlók","Collect the flood-broom tea inside Runerik's lodge","The flood-broom will take some time to steep in the boiling water.","Runerik Knotbeard will meet you inside the lodge to treat the injured messenger-ravens.","The flood-broom tea is now prepared, and waits for you to bring it to Runerik.","Chapter 3.2: Runerik's Request","Yrsa Spearwife is in south-east Limlók.","Some of the ravens were shot from the sky by Orc archers! You have to retrieve them from the White Mare and learn if any of Glóin's messages escaped the Floodfells.","Talk to Runerik Knotbeard north-west of the White Mare","All dwarves everywhere are threatened by the presence of a new Lord of Gundabad. Glóin's warning must reach them!","Retrieve injured message-ravens from the White Mare","Talk to Venko at the north-western point of the White Mare","Glóin is behind Runerik's lodge, and from there you heard a great commotion. What has happened?","Flood-broom can be found alongside rivers and streams throughout the Floodfells. Runerik also wants his wife Yrsa to examine unspent arrows carried by Orcs in the area, and has asked you to collect some.","Wait for the flood-broom tea to properly steep","Runerik stands before some of his assembled people north-west of the White Mare, and demands to speak with you.","Confront the unexpected visitors north-west of the White Mare, across the river","Runerik has prepared a pot of boiling water in the north room, and he wants you to add the flood-broom you collected to it."}},
[3081]={nameES="Chapter 3.2: The Adventures of Jajax and Daxamat",objectivesES={"You have encountered the Corsair Jajax in Dol Amroth and he has a tale to tell.","Chapter 3.2: The Adventures of Jajax and Daxamat","Talk to Jajax in Dol Amroth and hear his story","Talk to Prince Imrahil in the Palace of the Swan, King's Gondor","Prince Imrahil is in the Palace of the Swan in Dol Amroth, King's Gondor.","Talk to Jajax in Dol Amroth, in King's Gondor","Jajax stands on a tree-shaded street in Dol Amroth, King's Gondor."}},
[3082]={nameES="Chapter 3.2: The Second Garrison",objectivesES={"Find a message addressed to Ugrukhôr somewhere in Cirith Ungol","Atli Spider-bane is not far from the approach to Cirith Ungol, in Lhingris.","Bring the message for Ugrukhôr to Atli Spider-bane outside the Tower of Cirith Ungol <rgb=#00FF00>(The message can be read from your inventory)</rgb>","Atli Spider-bane believes that you should enter Cirith Ungol while the Orcs are dealing with the newly-crazed spiders of Lhingris.","This message addressed to Ugrukhôr speaks of loyalties and infighting","Stairs ascend to the higher levels of the tower","Something has stirred up the spiders of Lhingris, and they have begun attacking the Orcs of Cirith Ungol.","You see a crumpled parchment discarded by the fire","Chapter 3.2: The Second Garrison"}},
[3083]={nameES="Chapter 3.2: The Valley of Webs",objectivesES={"This Orc is alive, but he is very near to death","This Orc is not pretending. He is truly slain","An entrance to Lhingris can be found in Durthang or by passes in Udûn or Dor Amarth.","Talk to Atli Spider-bane at the approach to Cirith Ungol","Talk to the mortally-wounded Orc while he yet lives","Spiders can be found throughout Lhingris, to Atli's delight.","Atli Spider-bane is in north-eastern Lhingris, near the pass to Dor Amarth.","Atli was right: the bodies of Orcs and spiders litter the approach to the tower","Atli Spider-bane is not far from the approach to Cirith Ungol.","Atli Spider-bane is within view of the the approach to Cirith Ungol.","Talk to Atli Spider-bane in northern Lhingris","Atli thought you should more closely inspect the approach to Cirith Ungol, ensuring that the Orcs that lie in death before the tower are truly slain.","Atli Spider-bane, with renewed health and vigour, has heard rumours of a spider-infested valley in Gorgoroth and wishes to see it for himself.","One of the Orcs lying on the approach to Cirith Ungol lived still, but he is close to death. What might he tell you of the situation in Lhingris?","Atli calls for you to halt and smells the air","Atli thought you should more closely inspect the approach to Cirith Ungol.","With a final gasp, Sárnazt succumbs to his wounds and can speak no more","Chapter 3.2: The Valley of Webs","Examine the approach to Cirith Ungol","Find Atli Spider-bane in northern Lhingris, east of the Durthang entrance"}},
[3084]={nameES="Chapter 3.3: An Eye for Skill",objectivesES={"Imák wants you to <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> Venko's skills. Venko is by the south-east entrance of Limlók.","Find Glóin in Limlók and <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> his skills","Find Venko by the south-east entrance to Limlók and <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> his skills","Once again <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> Yrsa Spearwife inside the lodge","<rgb=#00FF00>Appraise</rgb> Yrsa Spearwife inside the lodge","Glóin wants you to <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> Imák's skills. Imák is on the western side of Limlók.","Practice makes perfect! Yrsa has asked you to once again try and <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> her skills.","<rgb=#00FF00>Appraise</rgb> Runerik Knotbeard outside the lodge","Talk to Glóin in Limlók","Talk to Imák in Limlók","Yrsa waits for your assessment of her skills and abilities. You consider what you have learned.\
\
<u>Yrsa Spearwife, Beorning Woman of Limlók</u>\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Skin-changing:</rgb> 95\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Observation:</rgb> 90\
\
She sighs as your provide your account, but there is humour in it.\
\
'You say I have great skill at skin-changing? Whatever gave you that idea? Ah, it is only a jest. Try it once again, and perhaps you can notice details you missed before. The signs are there for one who knows what to seek. <rgb=#00FF00>Appraise</rgb> me once again, and concentrate.'","Find Imák on the western side of Limlók and <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> his skills","Yrsa has asked you to try and <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> her skills.","Remembering the words of Yrsa, you decide to next appraise Runerik Knotbeard","Yrsa is inside the lodge, waiting to speak with you.","Glóin is in Limlók, wondering why you have been studying him so closely.","Runerik thinks you may be able to develop one of your latent abilities, and wants you to consult with his wife Yrsa for further instruction along that line.","Talk to Runerik Knotbeard outside his lodge in Limlók","Imák is in Limlók, and he wants to know why you have subjected him to such scrutiny.","Chapter 3.3: An Eye for Skill","The real test of your appraisal ability will be to <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> Runerik Knotbeard outside his lodge.","Talk to Venko in Limlók","Runerik Knotbeard is outside his lodge and interested to know your appraisal of his skills.","Venko is in Limlók, and he is suspicious of the recent attention you have given him.","Yrsa has asked you to try and <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> Glóin's skills. The old dwarf should be somewhere outside in Limlók.","Talk to Yrsa Spearwife inside her lodge"}},
[3085]={nameES="Chapter 3.3: Burning Ships",objectivesES={"Jajax turns to leave, and Prince Imrahil calls for him to halt","Jajax snorts, a rude sound that echoes in the hall","Jajax says nothing further, but he looks very satisfied with himself.","Prince Imrahil is in the Palace of the Swan in Dol Amroth, King's Gondor.","Prince Imrahil calls for everyone to be quiet","Talk to King Elessar in the Palace of the Swan, King's Gondor","Captain Maeral is in the Palace of the Swan in Dol Amroth, King's Gondor.","Talk to Jajax in the Palace of the Swan, King's Gondor","King Elessar is in the Palace of the Swan, in King's Gondor.","Jajax has decided to leave.","Chapter 3.3: Burning Ships","Jajax is in the Palace of the Swan in Dol Amroth, King's Gondor.","A tense situation arises in the Palace of the Swan with the arrival of Jajax.","Talk to Prince Imrahil in the Palace of the Swan, King's Gondor","Wait for Jajax to leave","Talk to Captain Maeral in the Palace of the Swan, King's Gondor"}},
[3086]={nameES="Chapter 3.3: Fate of the Stonemaiden",objectivesES={}},
[3087]={nameES="Chapter 3.3: The Gúrzyul",objectivesES={"Talk to Harthalín outside Fushaum Bal","Talk to Harthalín outside Nargroth","The presence remains within the stone: Zaghárog, watching you silently, waiting.","Talk to the spirit in the stone","You find a scorched parchment clutched in the hand of the fallen Easterling","The sound of raised voices comes from within Fushaum Bal","The lawless settlement of Fushaum Bal is south-west of Orodruin, in Talath Úrui.","You found a crumpled parchment on the body of an Easterling in Talath Úrui.","The spirit in the stone outside Nargroth showed you the location of a scorched skull within a cell in Naerband. If you understood its wish correctly, it has promised to tell you about the Gúrzyul if you return with the skull.\
\
You witnessed that Naerband consists of three large chambers, connected by hallways and subdivided by walls and iron bars. The skull is on the floor of a cell in the south-western corner of the largest, northernmost chamber. The iron door to the cell was half-open, and you saw flame-spirits floating over the fog-covered floor.","Harthalín is outside Fushaum Bal, in Talath Úrui.","A watching-stone outside the Caverns of Fire has taken an interest in you.","Bring the scorched skull to the watching-stone outside Nargroth","A watching-stone outside the Caverns of Fire has taken an interest in you, and awaits delivery of the skull you agreed to bring to it.","The prison that was shown to you is called Naerband","You feel a presence regard you from within the carven stone","Chapter 3.3: The Gúrzyul","Bring the orders concerning Nargroth to Harthalín outside Fushaum Bal <rgb=#00FF00>(The orders can be read from your inventory)</rgb>","Meet up with Harthalín outside Fushaum Bal, in Talath Úrui","Malice emanates from the skull. Scorched by heat, it has neither splintered nor cracked","The images return: you see the prison once again, and know that it is the prison of Naerband, south of the Ghâshghurm. Once again the spirit shows you the certain cell, and the scorched skull in the corner. Then the images recede, but the watchful presence remains.","Nargroth, the Caverns of Fire, can be found on the eastern side of Talath Úrui, beyond the Ghâshghurm.","Find the scorched skull in a cell within the prison of Naerband <rgb=#00FF00>using the information in your quest journal</rgb>","Harthalín wishes to see the slopes of Orodruin again, disbelieving that Sauron is truly gone, and will accompany you as you search Talath Úrui for knowledge of the Gúrzyul.","You place the skull at the base of the stone, and the images return.\
\
Once again you see the prison of Naerband, but something this time is different. It takes you a moment to reconcile what has changed, but held in the grip of the spirit it is impossible to tell how long the moment might have been. The prison stands in the shadow of Orodruin, and then you see it: the southern slope of the Mountain is intact; the Ghâshghurm has not yet been made.\
\
The images flicker behind your eyes, and you see that Naerband is filled with prisoners. Downtrodden Nurnhoth, rebellious Easterlings, and Haradrim deserters rattle the cages of their cells. Their jailors walk the corridors of Naerband, and they tap their weapons on the iron doors, and they scrape their blades on the iron walls, and they tap their boots on the iron floor. You are seized by a sensation of eager anticipation, but it does not belong to you. It comes from the whispering spirit, and fills you with revulsion and dread.\
\
Then the Mountain blazes, and the southern slope explodes in a shower of rock and flame. The torrent flows inexorably down the side of Orodruin, and the rocky plain becomes a lake of fire: the Ghâshghurm.\
\
The images become sharper and more distinct, as if the spirit seeks to draw your attention. At last you understand. As the lava pooled at the foot of Orodruin, the iron prison of Naerband became super-heated by its proximity to the lake of fire. Naerband became more than a prison. It became an oven.\
\
You close your eyes to shut out the sight, and at last the spirit relents, its price paid.\
\
'Zaghárog,' it says to you: the name of the spirit in the stone.","Find the road that leads to Nargroth, on the eastern side of Talath Úrui","Easterlings can be found around Fushaum Bal, in Talath Úrui.","Defeat Easterlings in Talath Úrui (7/8)","Harthalín is by the watching-stone outside Nargroth, on the eastern side of Talath Úrui.","The carven stone is dreadful in form, and it does not seem out of place within Gorgoroth. But there is something else that sets it apart, a cold and watchful presence. And then, there is more: a voice that whispers in your head. Images rise unbidden behind your eyes. They are drained of colour, as if the one who creates them has no knowledge of shade or hue.\
\
You see a place of darkness, and a tiny point of light flickering high above. Then, below, there is a knife held in a cruel fist. It descends in an arc, and blood flows from a wound. The darkness deepens.\
\
The voice in your head speaks no words, but you are suddenly awash on a questioning sea.\
\
You recover your own words enough to reply, 'Yes, the Gúrzyul.'\
\
The interrogative waves vanish as quickly as they had arrived. In their place is an overwhelming sensation: the promise of knowledge and secrets held close for centuries. As you try to express that such knowledge will be welcome, it is whisked cruelly away, dangled just out of reach.\
\
The giving sensation is gone, replaced with a taking desire. You see a prison in your mind's eye, and the details are so clear you know it is a real place. The spirit shows you a certain cell in this prison, and a scorched skull in one corner. The images fade, and the whispering voice returns. It speaks a single word, but the word is enough. The word is 'want.'\
\
You are released from the spirit's hold and the whispering in your head fades away. The presence remains, regarding you silently."}},
[3088]={nameES="Chapter 3.4: A Change of Heart",objectivesES={"Search for Raneleg to the north, west of the road","Talk to Ayorzén at Cirith Gorgor, inside the Black Gate","Learn if Arodrog is alive or dead","You found the adventurers that entered Agarnaith from the northern approach","You found adventurers in Agarnaith, and should hear what they have encountered within the Bloody Gore.","Linadar is just north of the junction with the eastern road, in Agarnaith.","You agreed to meet up with the adventurers again on the road, near where the eastern path leads away into the swamp.","Agarnaith may be approached from either the north or the south.","Mithrandir has heard an unsettling rumour of a threat growing in Agarnaith, the Bloody Gore, on the eastern side of Gorgoroth.","The creatures of Agarnaith seem to draw strength from the foetid air, and you must oppose them for the good of those who adventure in the marsh.","Search for Arodrog just south of the eastern road","Talk to Mithrandir in Cirith Gorgor, inside the Black Gate","Bring Raneleg's sword to Linadar in Agarnaith","Chapter 3.4: A Change of Heart","Ayorzén the Wily is at Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate.","Raneleg and Arodrog ran into trouble off the road to the north and south, and Linadar has asked you to learn if they yet live.","Talk to Linadar on the road in Agarnaith","Talk to the adventurer you found inside Agarnaith","Linadar made it to the meeting location, but where is the other adventurer?","Arodrog's body lies in the muck","Only Linadar met up with you at the arranged meeting place in Agarnaith.","Gain entrance to Agarnaith from the north","Linadar is so shaken that you agree to see him safely out of Mordor","Gain entrance to Agarnaith from the south","Mithrandir is in Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate.","Learn the fate of Raneleg","Raneleg is gone, but his sword remains: sticking straight up in the mud","You found the adventurers that entered Agarnaith from the southern approach","Arodrog has succumbed to his wounds. He is dead","Meet up with the adventurers near the junction with the eastern road, in Agarnaith","Did the sword fall from Raneleg's hand as he was borne aloft?"}},
[3089]={nameES="Chapter 3.4: A Choice of Road",objectivesES={"Travel through Calembel in King's Gondor","Travel through Dínadab in King's Gondor","Your companions look to the summit of the Hill of Erech","Lothgobel has not yet fully recovered from its scars","Hearing about Corsair activity along the coast of Anfalas, King Elessar is more determined than ever that his journey across Gondor should continue.","King Elessar is in the Palace of the Swan, King's Gondor.","Talk to King Elessar in the Palace of the Swan, King's Gondor","King Elessar suggested that you travel to the Hill of Erech in the Blackroot Vale, in King's Gondor.","Chapter 3.4: A Choice of Road","The folk of Dínadab seek to restore their peaceful lives","Calembel seems to have achieved a measure of peace after the war","Legolas stands at the base of the Hill of Erech.","Travel to the base of the Hill of Erech in the Blackroot Vale, King's Gondor","Travel through Lothgobel in King's Gondor","King Elessar has given you a choice of road north into the Blackroot Vale: either to fight your way through Tarlang's Crown, or to take the longer, safer road through Lamedon.","Talk to Legolas at the base of the Hill of Erech, in King's Gondor"}},
[3090]={nameES="Chapter 3.4: Pilgrimage to Sundergrót",objectivesES={"Talk to Venko on the grassy slope east of Sundergrót","Glóin is at Sundergrót, waiting to discuss your companions' exploits at Sundergrót.","Talk to Venko south of the gorge of Sundergrót","Talk to Glóin and climb with him to High Sundergrót","Talk to Durin along the road between the Wells of Langflood and Elderslade","The sound of goblin-cries echoes among the crags near Sundergrót","Glóin is outside the lodge in Limlók.","One of the messenger-ravens bore Glóin's warning to Skarháld, and now the dwarves wish to exercise their skills in preparation for the battles to come.","Talk to Glóin outside the lodge in Limlók","Talk to Imák beyond the bridge of Skerabrygg","Venko is south of the gorge of Sundergrót, eager to discuss his combat training.","Sundergrót is far to the west of Limlók, and your companions are interested in testing their skills among its rocky crags.","Chapter 3.4: Pilgrimage to Sundergrót","Glóin is interested in climbing to the summit above Sundergrót, and he waits for you to speak with him.","You have travelled with Durin to the road that enters Elderslade, where many of his dwarves have begun to prepare for their war on Gundabad.","Venko shouts in triumph and goes in search of more goblins","Meet up with Imák south of the gorge of Sundergrót","Talk to Glóin south of the gorge of Sundergrót"}},
[3091]={nameES="Chapter 3.5: Ruthless",objectivesES={"Examine the arrow embedded in the tree","Gimli stands at the base of the Hill of Erech, in King's Gondor.","Duinhir stands outside his home at the highest point of Morlad, in King's Gondor.","The memory of losses suffered during the War of the Ring remains to trouble the people of the Blackroot Vale.","You hear someone shouting for help from outside the entrance to Morlad","Lady Rosfin looks at you with sad, cold eyes, and says nothing.","Talk to Gimli west of Morlad in King's Gondor","Legolas and Gimli stand at the ready to the west of Morlad.","Talk to Duinhir outside his home in Morlad, in King's Gondor","Their oaths forever broken, the Ruthless Dead now haunt the Blackroot Vale with renewed hatred for the living. Gimli thinks you should inconvenience them, since he isn't certain they can be slain. Ruthless Dead can be found atop the Hill of Erech at night, and on the road to the Paths of the Dead at any time.","It is fortunate this arrow was not loosed with more skill","Talk to Legolas west of Morlad, in King's Gondor","Caebar is south-west of the entrance to Morlad, in King's Gondor.","Talk to Caebar at the base of the Hill of Erech, in King's Gondor","Talk to Gimli at the base of the Hill of Erech, in King's Gondor","Talk to the surly Morlad resident down the hill to the north","Talk to Rosfin outside her home in Morlad, in King's Gondor","Talk to Duinhir in Morlad, in King's Gondor","Chapter 3.5: Ruthless","Caebar thanks you and hurries away to safety","Duinhir stands by his wife Rosfin in Morlad, in King's Gondor.","Legolas and Gimli stand at the ready, their weapons drawn","Find Legolas and Gimli to the west of Morlad in King's Gondor","Talk to Caebar south-west of the entrance to Morlad in King's Gondor","Caebar stands at the base of the Hill of Erech, in King's Gondor.","Talk to the angry Morlad resident down the hill to the east","Rosfin, wife of Duinhir, stands outside their home at the highest point of Morlad, in King's Gondor.","Legolas and Gimli are to the west of the entrance to Morlad, in King's Gondor.","You should hear the concerns of the folk of Morlad, in King's Gondor."}},
[3092]={nameES="Chapter 3.5: The Song of Sweet Lara",objectivesES={"Chapter 3.5: The Song of Sweet Lara","Talk to Ayorzén at Cirith Gorgor, inside the Black Gate","Talk to Ayorzén on the parapet overlooking the city on the south-eastern side of the Fifth Circle","Find a scholar with kingsfoil to spare in the Houses of Lore","Mithrandir is in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, just south of the entrance to the city.","Bring the kingsfoil to Mithrandir in the First Circle, south of the entrance to the city","Mithrandir desires to return to Minas Tirith and spend some time studying one or two matters that trouble him concerning the state of Agarnaith.","A book concerning the Great Plague and a scholar willing to part with kingsfoil must both be found within the Houses of Lore, on the southern side of the Fifth Circle of Minas Tirith.","The waggon-driver Rathnor can be found near the Black Gate.","Talk to Rathnor the waggon-driver","Talk to Mithrandir in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, south of the entrance","Covadil gives you a small packet of kingsfoil and a smile","You learned that athelas was helpful for treating some victims of the Great Plague","Ayorzén is on the parapet overlooking the city on the south-eastern side of the Fifth Circle, in Minas Tirith.","Ayorzén is at Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate.","Talk to Rathnor and travel to the city on his waggon","Find a book about the Great Plague in the Houses of Lore","This musty tome provides a dry account of the Great Plague that ravaged Gondor beginning in the year 1636 of the Third Age. The forgotten scholar that wrote these pages noted that the plague arose somewhere in the East and many of the folk there were consumed by the disease before it spread to the Northmen of Rhovanion.\
\
The account spends slightly longer detailing the effect of the Great Plague on the rule of Gondor, including the deaths of King Telemnar and all of his children, and the abandonment of Osgiliath for lack of men healthy enough to man its defences. The author of these pages mentions in passing that the watches at Minas Ithil, the Morannon, Ost Daethír, and Durthand were severely undermanned as a result of the disease, and you cannot help but wonder if he foresaw the problems that would cause in future days.\
\
The account further notes the discovery that the leaves of the athelas plant were found to have a beneficial effect upon the progression of the plague, and that the disease finally ran its course in Gondor by the year 1637."}},
[3093]={nameES="Chapter 3.5: The War Camp",objectivesES={"Stóthkell's good eye lights up with recognition as you approach","The war camp bustles with activity","The war-camp called Annâk-khurfu is north-west of the bridge between the Wells of Langflood and Elderslade, and serves as a gathering place for the arriving armies of dwarves.","Meet with dwarves on the lower level of Annâk-khurfu","Prince Ingór of the Zhélruka nods at your approach","The war camp is bustling with dwarves preparing for their upcoming assault on Gundabad.\
\
You should speak to the dwarves assembled on the lower level of Annâk-khurfu.","The war camp is bustling with dwarves preparing for their upcoming assault on Gundabad.\
\
You should speak to the dwarves assembled on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu.","Great armies of dwarves have answered Durin's call, and they assemble in Elderslade in preparation for their assault upon Gundabad.","Chapter 3.5: The War Camp","Durin is on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu, addressing the assembled force of the dwarves.","Meet with dwarves on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu","Thettmárr and Líkmund are playing a runic dice game and gambling","Thorgest and Afwald greet you warmly and ask for news of your adventures","Talk to Durin on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu","The upper level is filled with dwarves preparing to undertake missions","Enter the war camp of Annâk-khurfu in one of the old dwarf-keeps"}},
[3094]={nameES="Chapter 3.6: Survivors",objectivesES={"Bróin is just north of Annâk-khurfu.","Bróin did not follow his cousin upstairs. Where did he go?\
\
Bori believes Bróin might be outside, just north of Annâk-khurfu.","Bróin stands alone, gazing into the distance","Talk to Bori on the lower level of Annâk-khurfu","Chapter 3.6: Survivors","Bróin is just north of Annâk-khurfu.\
\
Bróin has asked that you <rgb=#00FF00>agree</rgb> not to tell Durin about his worries.","Talk to Bróin on the lower level of Annâk-khurfu","Bróin smiles nervously, and raises his axe in a pleased salute","<rgb=#00FF00>Appraise</rgb> Bósi on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu","Durin is on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu.","Concerned about the dwarves of the Iron Garrison, Durin wants you to <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> Bósi's mood and skills.\
\
Bósi has followed you to the upper level of Annâk-khurfu.","Talk to Bróin just north of Annâk-khurfu","<rgb=#00FF00>Appraise</rgb> Bróin outside Annâk-khurfu","Talk to Bósi on the lower level of Annâk-khurfu","<rgb=#00FF00>Agree</rgb> not to tell anyone of Bróin's worries","<rgb=#00FF00>Appraise</rgb> Bori on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu","Talk to Durin on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu","Greet more arriving dwarves on the lower level of Annâk-khurfu","Bori is on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu.","Talk to Bori on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu","Bósi is on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu.","Durin has asked you to greet the arriving dwarves on the lower level of Annâk-khurfu.","Dwarves of the Iron Garrison have come to Elderslade to join the great force preparing for the assault on Gundabad.","Talk to Bósi on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu","More dwarves have come to Elderslade for the assault on Gundabad, and Durin is eager to welcome the new arrivals.","Some familiar dwarves have arrived at Annâk-khurfu","Concerned about the dwarves of the Iron Garrison, Durin wants you to <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> Bróin's mood and skills.\
\
Bróin did not follow his cousin upstairs, and now he stands by himself outside Annâk-khurfu.","Find Bróin somewhere outside, just north of Annâk-khurfu","Concerned about the dwarves of the Iron Garrison, Durin wants you to <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> Bori's mood and skills.\
\
Bori has followed you to the upper level of Annâk-khurfu."}},
[3095]={nameES="Chapter 3.6: The Next Great Plague",objectivesES={"Talk to Harthalín just north of the eastward-running road in Agarnaith and collect samples (0/60)","Chapter 3.6: The Next Great Plague","Bring the samples to Harthalín by the road in Agarnaith","Harthalín is by the eastward-running road in Agarnaith.","If Lhaereth the Stained is truly attempting to perfect the Great Plague, Mithrandir wants you to learn how far along she has gotten in the process.","The Orc is dead. You remove a parchment from its hand","Harthalín is north of the eastward-running road in Agarnaith, on the way to Kala-gijak.","Harthalín shot an arrow at an Orc attempting to pass north-east of her location in Agarnaith. She wants you to see if it still lives.","Bring the parchment to Harthalín by the road in Agarnaith <rgb=#00FF00>(The parchment can be read from your inventory)</rgb>","Mithrandir asked you to collect samples from the plants, animals, and water in Agarnaith in order to determine the progress of Lhaereth's experiments.","Examine the Ghâsh-hai shot by Harthalín in Agarnaith, to the north-east"}},
[3096]={nameES="Chapter 3.6: Word of Their Lord",objectivesES={"The time has come for you to rejoin King Elessar on the road to Anfalas.","King Elessar and Queen Arwen greet you warmly as you approach","Chapter 3.6: Word of Their Lord","Talk to King Elessar on the road to Anfalas, in King's Gondor","Talk to Anoradan in Melgobas","The town of Melgobas is to the west along the coast in Anfalas.","Anoradan is in the centre of the fishing village of Melgobas, in Anfalas.","Travel south of the Blackroot Vale in King's Gondor, and rejoin Elessar on the road to Anfalas","You planned to rejoin King Elessar south of the Blackroot Vale in King's Gondor, on the road into Anfalas.","Talk to Queen Arwen on the road to Anfalas, in King's Gondor","The smell of salt and the cries of gulls hang over the fishing village of Melgobas","Travel to the town of Melgobas, in Anfalas","King Elessar is on the road to Anfalas, in King's Gondor."}},
[3097]={nameES="Chapter 3.7: The Cliffs of Langstrand",objectivesES={"The people of Melgobas are endangered by more than just the Corsairs that drew the King to Anfalas.","Daeram is in the centre of the fishing village of Melgobas.","Talk to Anoradan in Melgobas","Corsairs and lynx threaten the folk of Anfalas in the vicinity of Melgobas.","Talk to Daeram in Melgobas","Chapter 3.7: The Cliffs of Langstrand","Anoradan is in the town of Melgobas."}},
[3098]={nameES="Chapter 3.8: The Missing Heir",objectivesES={"It is possible the tracks were left by a child's shoes, but it is hard to say","Daeram asked you to search for Orgolas along the beach to the south of Melgobas.","King Elessar kneels outside Barad Faen, studying the ground intently","Chapter 3.8: The Missing Heir","Daeram says Barad Faen to the west is such a place","Search for Orgolas along the beach to the east","King Elessar kneels outside Barad Faen, studying the ground. It seems the life of a Ranger can be hard to escape!","Meet up with King Elessar outside Barad Faen, in Anfalas","There is no sign of Orgolas along the beach","Search for Orgolas atop Barad Faen","King Elessar stands in Melgobas, considering Orgolas's disappearance.","Daeram is in the centre of the fishing village of Melgobas.","Search along the beach at the bottom of the steps in Melgobas","Daeram was sent from Lond Cirion to search for the missing heir of Anfalas.","Search for Orgolas further east along the beach","Talk to King Elessar in Melgobas","There is no sign of Orgolas here either","King Elessar steps forward to speak","King Elessar has found tracks of some sort outside Barad Faen.","Talk to King Elessar outside Barad Faen","There is no sign of Orgolas here","Barad Faen is west of Melgobas, in Anfalas.","Tracks indicate Orgolas might have climbed Barad Faen.","Daeram asked you to search for Orgolas along the beach to the south, down below the fishing village of Melgobas.","Examine the tracks outside Barad Faen","Talk to Daeram in Melgobas","Daeram asked you to search for Orgolas along the beach to the south."}},
[3099]={nameES="Chapter 3.9: Orgolas",objectivesES={"Find a guardsman on the bridge north-west of Lond Cirion","Find Orgolas by the docks of Lond Cirion","Find the main hall of Lond Cirion","Orgolas watches the soldiers training with sword and with bow","Chapter 3.9: Orgolas","King Elessar is in the main hall of Lond Cirion, speaking with Lady Marra.","The bridge offers a breathtaking view of the water","Talk to Orgolas at the entrance to Lond Cirion","Find the Lond Cirion library inside the keep","Marra suggested you become familiar with the layout of Lond Cirion and those who reside there.","Talk to King Elessar in the main hall of Lond Cirion","Talk to Coruchon in the library of Lond Cirion","Lady Marra is in the main hall of Lond Cirion.","Lond Cirion is to the west of Barad Faen.","Talk to King Elessar at Barad Faen","The library of Lond Cirion smells of dust and candle wax","Talk to Marra in the main hall of Lond Cirion","The main hall of Lond Cirion is located just inside the entrance to the keep.","Talk to Orgolas by the docks","The Lady Marra motions for you to come forward","Talk to Aerhant on the bridge to the north-west of Lond Cirion","Travel to the entrance of Lond Cirion","Daeram clears his throat and calls for your attention","Orgolas is at the entrance of Lond Cirion, in Anfalas.","You have found Orgolas, the son of Golasgil and heir to Anfalas. The question now is what should be done with him?","Daeram is at the entrance to Lond Cirion, in Anfalas.","Orgolas leaps around excitedly","King Elessar stands by Orgolas, at Barad Faen.","Talk to Daeram at the entrance to Lond Cirion"}},
[3100]={nameES="Chapter 3: A Faltering Reflection",objectivesES={"Orophin will take you from the Lothlórien Court to see Lady Galadriel in her garden.","Lady Galadriel wishes to speak to you.","Habla con Legolas.","Talk to Orophin in the Court of Lothlórien","Chapter 3: A Faltering Reflection","Legolas wishes to talk with you in the Court of Lothlórien."}},
[3101]={nameES="Capítulo 3: Una reliquia en Lumul-nar (Grupo)",objectivesES={"Destruye el regalo de Gorothúl en Lumul-nar","Una ola de temor te recorre mientras la reliquia es destruida, luego desaparece.","Habla con Bróin en la Senda Pacífica","La entrada a las Salas de los Espejos de Lumul-nar está afuera, en el lado de Zirakzigil cerca del cráter arruinado donde yace el Balrog aún humeante.\
\
Bróin cree que una de las reliquias que Gorothúl dejó en Moria fue dada a los merrevail que infestan las Salas de los Espejos de Lumul-nar y quiere que la destruyas.","Bróin está en la Senda Pacífica, ubicada entre Zirakzigil y el Camino de Durin.\
\
Has destruido la reliquia que Gorothúl dio a los merrevail en Lumul-nar y ahora deberías regresar con Bróin.","Capítulo 3: Una reliquia en Lumul-nar (Grupo)","Bróin cree que Gorothúl dio una reliquia maligna a los merrevail que infestan los Espejos de Lumul-nar."}},
[3102]={nameES="Capítulo 3: Una reliquia en Lumul-nar (Solo)",objectivesES={"Habla con Bróin y viaja a las Salas de los Espejos de Lumul-nar","La entrada a las Salas de los Espejos de Lumul-nar está afuera, en Zirakzigil, cerca del cráter en ruinas donde yace el Balrog humeante.\
\
Bróin cree que una de las reliquias que Gorothúl dejó en Moria fue dada a los merrevail que infestan las Salas de los Espejos de Lumul-nar y quiere que la destruyas.","Habla con Bróin en la Senda Pacífica","Bróin está en la Senda Pacífica, ubicada entre Zirakzigil y el Camino de Durin.\
\
Has destruido la reliquia que Gorothúl dio a los merrevail en Lumul-nar y ahora deberías regresar con Bróin.","Capítulo 3: Una reliquia en Lumul-nar (Solo)","Bróin cree que Gorothúl dio una reliquia de maldad a los merrevail que infestan los Espejos de Lumul-nar."}},
[3103]={nameES="Capítulo 3: Bósi el Enano",objectivesES={"Lleva el informe de Tulk a Bósi","Tulk te ha pedido que lleves un informe a Bósi, el líder de la expedición de enanos. Los parientes de Bósi han venido a Acebeda con el propósito de entrar en Moria.","Capítulo 3: Bósi el Enano","Bósi supervisa algunos carros a lo largo del camino a través de Acebeda, al sureste de la Puerta y luego girando al noreste.\
\
Tulk te ha dado un informe para que lo lleves a Bósi, uno de los enanos que lideran la expedición a Acebeda."}},
[3104]={nameES="Chapter 3: Death in the Dale",objectivesES={"Dáin can be found at Durin's Stone.\
\
After the defeat of Urro One-hand, the Iron-folk have arrived at Durin's Stone. You should talk to Dáin.","Thromur can be found at Amdân.\
\
After repelling the Orcs at Kamaz-kala, you should find Thromur and investigate what kept him from joining the vanguard.","Ah, Hermáth! Though I tried to convince my father otherwise, he insisted on sending those messengers to find you.\
\
'While you were off aiding the others, there was a bit of tension in the vanguard. It seems King Thráin's son, Frerin, and his esquire had something of an argument, and he sent that dwarf back to Amdân on some errand. Before Thromur could return, Frerin had no choice but to set off with the vanguard. Thromur! That was the esquire's name!\
\
'Lord Grór has asked us to repel the Orcs at Kamaz-kala should we be needed in the dale, but once that is done, you should find out what has been keeping Thromur. He ought to hurry up or the battle will be over!'","Dáin can be found at Khur Azan.\
\
After arriving at Khur Azan, you have spotted your friend, Dáin. You should talk to Dáin.","An uneasy dwarf appears to be searching Amdân for something","As you continue to read Hermáth Stormhammer's account of the Battle of Azanulbizar, you begin the third chapter in which the Dwarves of the Haban’akkâ of Thráin press onward into the dale and the vanguard faces a grave setback.","The Iron-folk can be found at Khur Azan.\
\
You have returned to Khur Azan and should now muster to the Iron-folk waiting in reserve.","Chapter 3: Death in the Dale","Talk to Dáin at Khur Azan","Talk to Dáin at Durin's Stone","Thromur can be found at Amdân.\
\
You have discovered a likely culprit in the theft of Urro's hand. You should aid Thromur.","Thromur can be found at Amdân.\
\
You have found Thromur and should aid him in completing his errand.","Talk to Thromur and forge 'Bonds of Oak and Iron'","Kamaz-kala can be found slightly north-west of Khur Azan at Azanulbizar.\
\
Lord Grór has asked the Iron-folk to repel the Orcs at Kamaz-kala should the battle need to be joined.","Among the many Iron-folk who have marched to Khur Azan, you spot Dáin","Find Thromur at Amdân","Muster to the Iron-folk at Khur Azan","Aid Thromur"}},
[3105]={nameES="Chapter 3: Gimli's Request",objectivesES={"King Thorin beckons for you to approach","Talk to Gimli in the throne room in the Hall under the Mountain","Thorin III, King under the Mountain, is at his throne in Erebor.","Chapter 3: Gimli's Request","Dwarves of Erebor that may wish to accompany Gimli to the Glittering Caves can be found throughout the Hall under the Mountain.","Talk to King Thorin III at his throne in the Hall under the Mountain","Gimli, son of Glóin, has come to Erebor to speak with the King under the Mountain.","Go to Thorin's throne room in the Hall under the Mountain","Gimli beams with pride and accepts the task","Gimli is near the provisioner in the Hall under the Mountain, arranging for the things he will need on his expedition.","Talk to Gimli by the provisioner in the Hall under the Mountain","A familiar figure stands before the throne: Gimli, son of Glóin","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to Durin's Folk and fight on their behalf in Mordor."}},
[3106]={nameES="Chapter 3: High and Low",objectivesES={"Hornblower Pipe-weed, packaged 1 March 3019","<rgb=#FF00FF>Listen</rgb> to Saruman","Hornblower Pipe-weed, packaged 9 August 3017","Saruman wishes only to seize power and rule of Mordor for his own","You discovered many more barrels of pipe-weed than Merry and Pippin had found, and packaged over the course of nearly two years, as well. You should return to Treebeard where he stands before the west face of Orthanc in Flooded Isengard.","Hornblower Pipe-weed, packaged 25 June 3017","Habla con Merry","You should talk to Pippin and Merry in Bâr Thorenion to learn what serious matters they have been discussing.","Hornblower Pipe-weed, packaged 22 Sept 3017","Treebeard and another Ent stand before Orthanc on the western side of Flooded Isengard.\
\
You have heard Saruman's three pleas and seen through each ploy. Now you should return to Treebeard and see what he has to say.","Pippin and Merry have asked you to visit Flooded Isengard and look in after Saruman, the Ents, and anything that will reveal what the three half-orcs were talking about.","Habla con Pippin","Consider the Free Peoples","You should return to Pippin and Merry in Bâr Thorenion with word of all that you have seen and heard.","Consider dethroned Mordor","Saruman stands high upon his tower on the western side of Flooded Isengard.\
\
Saruman has suggested that he could employ his vast wisdom to bring prosperity to the Free Peoples. You should consider how this possibility might turn out.","Return to Pippin and Merry","Habla con Bárbol","Find the other Ents","What Isengard was and the waste it has become swiftly dispel Saruman's lie","Saruman stands high upon his tower on the western side of Flooded Isengard.\
\
You should <rgb=#FF00FF>listen</rgb> one last time to Saruman's plea.","You have found Quickbeam in the waters of Flooded Isengard, who has told you that Treebeard and several other Ents are gathered up ahead on the western side of Orthanc, discussing Saruman.","Merry and Pippin have been pondering the revelations of their last foray into Mordor, and come to some conclusions.","Hornblower Pipe-weed, packaged 11 July 3018","Treebeard suggested that you search for other clues around Flooded Isengard, while you wait for Saruman to emerge from Orthanc.","Hornblower Pipe-weed, packaged 14 May 3018","Saruman stands high upon his tower on the western side of Flooded Isengard.\
\
You should <rgb=#FF00FF>listen</rgb> once more to Saruman's plea.","Saruman stands high upon his tower on the western side of Flooded Isengard.\
\
Saruman has suggested that he could aid in the subjugation and cleansing of Mordor, still covered in the corruptions, lieutenants, and shadow of Sauron as it is. You should consider the dethroned land and what Saruman might do there.","Go back to Treebeard","Return to Treebeard","Hornblower Pipe-weed, packaged 5 July 3018","(A VOICE COMES FROM ABOVE)\
'A VISITOR? OR A RUSE? WILL YOU LISTEN TO MY PLEA WITH A FAIR AND OPEN HEART, TRULY?'","You shudder at the vision of toiling hobbits, whose lives need little improvement, only to be left alone in peace","Return to Flooded Isengard","Hornblower Pipe-weed, packaged 3 August 3018","Saruman stands high upon his tower on the western side of Flooded Isengard.\
\
Saruman has said that if you free him, he will heal, regrow, and make reparations for the wrongs done in his name. You should <rgb=#FF00FF>look around</rgb> to consider the weight of his words.","Chapter 3: High and Low","<rgb=#FF00FF>Look around</rgb> you","You should approach Orthanc from where the Ents stand on the western side of Flooded Isengard and see if Saruman will speak with you.","You have found Quickbeam in the waters of Flooded Isengard, who has told you that Treebeard and several other Ents are gathered on the western side of Orthanc, discussing Saruman.","Saruman stands high upon his tower on the western side of Flooded Isengard.\
\
Saruman has asked you to <rgb=#FF00FF>listen</rgb> to his plea.","Approach Orthanc","Treebeard and other Ents are indeed gathered before Orthanc, talking together"}},
[3107]={nameES="Capítulo 3: Dentro de la Cámara de Mazarbul",objectivesES={"Bósi se encuentra en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, en la entrada sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Brogur se ha mostrado profundamente perturbado por la historia registrada en el Libro de Mazarbul, y te ha pedido que lleves el siniestro tomo a Bósi.","Lleva el Libro de Mazarbul a Brogur","Brogur te ha dicho que los trabajos de excavación de la Cámara de Registros avanzan a buen ritmo, aunque le preocupa la presencia de la Mano Blanca en Moria.","Wárr se encuentra en la Cámara de Mazarbul, situada a la derecha del pasillo norte que sale de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Brogur te ha dicho que Wárr ha estado pidiendo tu ayuda con algo en la Cámara de Mazarbul.","Buscas entre los escombros pero no encuentras nada de interés.","Busca entre los escombros de la Cámara de Mazarbul","Buscando entre los escombros, encuentras un libro dañado.","Brogur se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo, junto a la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Has encontrado un libro misterioso entre los escombros de la Cámara de Mazarbul y deberías mostrárselo a Brogur sin perder un instante.","Capítulo 3: Dentro de la Cámara de Mazarbul","Los escombros cubren la Cámara de Mazarbul, situada a la derecha del pasillo norte que sale de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Wárr te ha pedido que busques entre los escombros de la Cámara de Mazarbul cualquier cosa de interés que pueda ser útil para los enanos.","Lleva el Libro de Mazarbul a Bósi"}},
[3108]={nameES="Chapter 3: Many Voices",objectivesES={"Dúnor is on the south-east side of the Second Circle, in Minas Tirith.","Talk to Legolas in the throne room of King Elessar","Find the gift of the dwarves on the south-east side of the Second Circle, in Minas Tirith","You have found Gimli's gift: a statue carved in the likeness of Boromir, hero of Gondor","Chapter 3: Many Voices","The crowd threatens to become violent. You should try and help Dúnor","Legolas and Gimli have come to the throne room of King Elessar and wish to speak with you.","Dúnor is on the south-east side of the Second Circle in Minas Tirith, and is having trouble dealing with an unruly crowd.","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to Elessar and the Kingdom of Gondor, and to fight on their behalf in Mordor.","Speak to members of the unruly crowd and try to calm them down","The gift of the Elves Legolas brought to Minas Tirith is currently on the south-east side of the Second Circle.","Dúnor has asked for your help in calming the unruly crowd on the south-east side of the Second Circle, in Minas Tirith.","King Elessar is in his throne room atop Minas Tirith.","The gift of the dwarves Gimli brought to Minas Tirith is currently on the south-east side of the Second Circle.","Talk to Dúnor on the south-east side of the Second Circle, in Minas Tirith","Talk to King Elessar in his throne room","Find the gift of the Elves on the south-east side of the Second Circle, in Minas Tirith","Talk to Gimli in the throne room of King Elessar","You found Legolas's gift, but your attention is seized by the sound of an unruly crowd"}},
[3109]={nameES="Capítulo 3: Mazog",objectivesES={"Habiendo aprendido que una fuerza de Dol Guldur se ha aliado con los Orcos de Mazog, Bori está aún más decidido a lanzar un asalto sobre Zabadgathol.","Capítulo 3: Mazog","Habla con Bori y ataca Zabadgathol","Bori se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Bori ha decidido un nuevo plan: atacar la fortaleza de Mazog, empuñando Zigilburk, y matar al malvado Orco antes de que la fuerza de Dol Guldur pueda aprovechar la situación entre los Orcos y los Enanos.","Brogur se encuentra en el Camino Profundo.\
\
Después del asalto fallido de Bori sobre Zabadgathol, Brogur se ha trasladado al Camino Profundo donde llora la pérdida tanto de su sobrino como de Zigilburk."}},
[3110]={nameES="Capítulo 3: Medianoche en el Bosque Ahogado",objectivesES={"Alfirimbes se encuentra en el campamento élfico de Echad Sirion en los Lindes Oscuros.\
\
La Guardia Oculta está lista para comenzar la primera etapa del viaje para llevar a Mazog a Dol Guldur, pasando por el Bosque Ahogado. Alfirimbes te llevará a ellos.","Capítulo 3: Medianoche en el Bosque Ahogado","Habla con Alfirimbes y viaja con la Guardia Oculta","Cúcheron está en el porche de la Posada Embrujada, lamentando la pérdida de Raddir.\
\
Raddir puede haber desaparecido, pero la misión de la Guardia Oculta debe continuar. Cúcheron te dirá qué se debe hacer mientras los Elfos intentan reagruparse tras la pérdida de uno de los suyos.","La misión de la Guardia Oculta comienza cuando llevan a Mazog en la primera etapa del viaje a través del Bosque Negro, trazado por Raddir.","Habla con Cúcheron en el porche de la Posada Embrujada"}},
[3111]={nameES="Chapter 3: Nona's Request",objectivesES={"Wadu's favourite tree is on a rise west of Lhanuch, overlooking the ox-pens.\
\
Nona has asked you to recover the Rohirrim sword she left at Wadu's favourite tree. It was found with Wadu's body and she thought to leave it there as a remembrance, but has changed her mind.","Nona is in the north-eastern corner of Lhanuch.\
\
Candaith has asked you to check on Nona to see how she is dealing with the death of her brother.","Talk to Nona in Lhanuch","Collected Wadu's sword","Chapter 3: Nona's Request","Nona, the Dunlending girl you helped beneath Zudrugund, has been mourning the death of her brother Wadu, and Candaith wants to make sure she is comforted.","Halbarad is in Lhanuch, among the huts on the western side of the village.\
\
Nona has asked to accompany the Grey Company when it departs Lhanuch and travels south.","Nona is in the north-eastern corner of Lhanuch.\
\
You have recovered the sword from Wadu's favourite tree and should now bring it to Nona as she requested.","Talk to Halbarad in Lhanuch","Recover the sword from Wadu's favourite tree","Bring Wadu's sword to Nona in the north-east corner of Lhanuch","Suvulch remains downcast, lost in thought."}},
[3112]={nameES="Capítulo 3: Preparativos para el Corazón de Fuego",objectivesES={"Rink Martillofuerte se encuentra en el Corazón de Fuego, a un lado de la Vía de los Herreros, entre las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata.\
\
Stóthkell te ha pedido que ayudes a su teniente con los preparativos para la defensa del Corazón de Fuego.","Has ayudado a Rink Martillofuerte con sus preparativos","Stóthkell se alegra de contar con tu ayuda para preparar el Corazón de Fuego para la tormenta que se avecina.","Habla con Stóthkell en el Corazón de Fuego, a un lado de la Vía de los Herreros","Capítulo 3: Preparativos para el Corazón de Fuego","Ayuda a Rink Martillofuerte con sus preparativos","Stóthkell se encuentra en el Corazón de Fuego, a un lado de la Vía de los Herreros, entre las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata.\
\
Has ayudado a Rink Martillofuerte con sus preparativos y ahora deberías informarle a Stóthkell sobre tus éxitos."}},
[3113]={nameES="Capitulo 3: Corredores en las profundidades",objectivesES={"Rink Martillofuerte se encuentra en el Corazón de Fuego, cerca de la Vía de los Herreros, en las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata.\
\
Has interrumpido la red de comunicación de los trasgos en las Obras Hidráulicas y ahora debes regresar con Rink Martillofuerte.","Rink Martillofuerte está preocupado por la red de mensajeros que los trasgos han establecido en las Obras Hidráulicas y quiere que la interrumpas.","Los mensajeros trasgos transmiten los planes del enemigo a través de las Obras Hidráulicas.\
\
Rink Martillofuerte te ha pedido que derrotes a los mensajeros trasgos para interrumpir la red de comunicación de estas criaturas en las Obras Hidráulicas.","Capitulo 3: Corredores en las profundidades"}},
[3114]={nameES="Capítulo 3: Rúmil y Orophin",objectivesES={"Habla con Rúmil","Capítulo 3: Rúmil y Orophin","Orophin está a punto de hablar cuando algo lo distrae de repente.\
\
'¡Yrch!' sisea.","Rúmil inclina la cabeza ante ti y señala hacia la distancia, lejos de los límites de Lórien. Luego, se encoge de hombros y pone una mano sobre su arco.\
\
Puede que no hable la lengua común, pero su mensaje es claro: por el momento, su puesto está tranquilo. La amenaza orca se ha ido, por ahora.","Rúmil y Orophin están apostados a lo largo de los límites de Lothlórien. Haldir te dijo que caminaras por la orilla norte del río Nimrodel para encontrar a sus hermanos.\
\
Haldir te ha pedido que les prestes tu ayuda a Rúmil y Orophin. No hablan mucho la lengua común, así que si no puedes hablar con ellos en élfico, tu odio mutuo hacia los Orcos debe trascender la necesidad de palabras.","Haldir se encuentra en su campamento en los límites de Lothlórien.\
\
Has hablado con sus hermanos y repelido un ataque de los Orcos, así que deberías volver ahora con Haldir.","Habla con Orophin","Has defendido con éxito a Orophin"}},
[3115]={nameES="Chapter 3: Saeradan's Watchfulness",objectivesES={"Uchdrud smiles coldly and dismisses your plea for mercy","Talk to Saeradan in Bree-land","Talk to Uchdrud at The Prancing Pony Inn","Meet Uchdrud outside the North-gate of Bree","Barliman Butterbur is the proprietor of The Prancing Pony and can be found by its bar, in the town of Bree.\
\
Saeradan has agreed to travel south with the Grey Company, but he wants you to ask Barliman Butterbur to be careful while the Rangers are gone.","Barliman Butterbur is in the main room of The Prancing Pony.\
\
You have carried several loads of foodstuffs from one of the Pony's parlours out to the main room and should speak now to Barliman.","Uchdrud is waiting somewhere by the North-gate of Bree for you to answer his challenge.\
\
You did as Butterbur asked and told Uchdrud to finish his beer and leave the Pony, and he reacted angrily, challenging you to meet him outside the North Gate of Bree.","Habla con Saeradan en su cabaña","Uchdrud is sitting at a table in the main room of The Prancing Pony.\
\
Barliman Butterbur has asked you to encourage Uchdrud, an unruly and coarse sort, to vacate the premises.","Chapter 3: Saeradan's Watchfulness","Saeradan is at his cabin in Bree-land, east of Thornley's Worksite in the Northern Bree-fields.\
\
Candaith has told you to travel next to tell Ranger Saeradan of the Grey Company's road.","Crates of foodstuffs are waiting in one of the parlours of The Prancing Pony.\
\
Barliman has heard the warning you brought from Saeradan, but he seems to have already forgotten it, and has asked you to carry foodstuffs out to the main room of the Pony.","Uchdrud has challenged you to meet him outside the Pony","Talk to Barliman Buttebur at The Prancing Pony Inn","Habla con Cebadilla Mantecona en la Posada del Poney Pisador","Saeradan is at his cabin outside the town of Bree.\
\
You have done as Saeradan asked and should now return to him at his cabin.","Retrieve foodstuffs from a crate in the Pony","You have brought word to Candaith that the Grey Company assembles, but now Saeradan in Bree-land must be notified.","Uchdrud begs for mercy! Saeradan was right: trouble lies ahead for Bree"}},
[3116]={nameES="Capítulo 3: Rebuscando entre las armas",objectivesES={"Wafi te dio una lista de lugares para buscar entre los escombros que podrían contener armas reutilizables que los artesanos del Corazón de Fuego podrían fundir.\
\
Wafi necesita materias primas para fabricar equipo para la defensa del Corazón de Fuego y te ha pedido que busques entre los escombros de Moria armas reutilizables.","Lleva las armas adecuadas y la lista a Wafi","Wafi se encuentra en el Corazón de Fuego, cerca de la Vía de los Herreros, entre las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata.\
\
Has encontrado muchas armas que pueden ser fundidas en las forjas del Corazón de Fuego.","Wafi quiere que busques entre los escombros de Moria armas reutilizables que puedan ser rescatadas para su uso por los artesanos del Corazón de Fuego.","Capítulo 3: Rebuscando entre las armas","Encontraste algunas armas reutilizables adecuadas para los propósitos de Wafi."}},
[3117]={nameES="Capítulo 3: Hijos de la hoja y la piedra",objectivesES={"Legolas y Gimli han estado caminando por los bosques de Lothlórien, vigilando a los orcos que intentan infiltrarse en los límites.","Gimli está en una plataforma entre los árboles sobre la colina de Cerin Amroth, en el centro de Lórien.\
\
Celeborn ha aceptado ayudar a la Guarnición de Hierro a superar sus problemas en Moria, y deberías hablar con Gimli sobre lo sucedido.","Capítulo 3: Hijos de la hoja y la piedra","Habla con Legolas y viaja con él a través del Bosque de Oro","Legolas está junto a Gimli sobre la plataforma encima de la colina de Cerin Amroth.\
\
Has sido invitado por Gimli a patrullar los bosques de Lothlórien con él y Legolas, y deberías hablar con Legolas cuando estés listo para partir.","Legolas está junto a Gimli sobre la plataforma encima de la colina de Cerin Amroth.\
\
Has sido invitado por Gimli a patrullar los bosques de Lothlórien con Legolas y él mismo, y deberías hablar ahora con el Elfo sobre la excursión."}},
[3118]={nameES="Chapter 3: The Forge and the Gift",objectivesES={}},
[3119]={nameES="Chapter 3: The House of Isildur",objectivesES={"Candaith is by the stables in Rivendell.\
\
You have listened to Candaith describe some of the history of the Dúnedain and should speak to him now for the conclusion.","Talk to Candaith in Rivendell and experience 'Session: The House of Isildur' or read the shortened account instead","Talk to Candaith in Rivendell","The history of the House of Isildur is full of dangerous escapes, glorious triumphs, and near brushes with tragedy, but even after so long the line remains strong. Three thousand years after the death of Isildur, Aragorn, son of Arathorn, is prepared to fulfill his destiny...","Chapter 3: The House of Isildur","Candaith is at the stables of Rivendell.\
\
Candaith has offered to tell you of key moments in the history of the Dúnedain.","Candaith wishes to tell you some of the history of the Dúnedain so you may recognize the importance of the errand upon which you are about to embark."}},
[3120]={nameES="Capítulo 3: Zigilburk el Inigualable",objectivesES={"Capítulo 3: Zigilburk el Inigualable","Habla con Bori","Katûb-zahar, la Cámara de las Palabras de Durin, se encuentra en algún lugar del lado este de la Gran Excavación, al norte de una gran estatua de Durin.\
\
Bori te dijo que si puedes encontrar el lugar llamado Katûb-zahar, podría descubrir la ubicación del misterioso hacha de mithril, Zigilburk.","Esta placa rota está descolorida, pero aún se puede leer 'Katûb-zahar.'","Bori se encuentra en la Cámara de Mando; es la habitación que se encuentra subiendo las escaleras del este en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, en el extremo sur del Camino de Durin. Se puede acceder desde la Gran Excavación.\
\
Has localizado una placa que marca la ubicación de Katûb-zahar y deberías regresar con la noticia a Bori.","Lleva las páginas polvorientas a Bori","Bósi ha descubierto la mención de una poderosa hacha hecha de mithril en uno de los registros que encontraste y busca saber si aún podría encontrarse.","Bori se encuentra en una pequeña habitación en el lado este de la Cámara de la Encrucijada.\
\
Bósi te ha devuelto las páginas polvorientas que contienen pistas sobre la ubicación de Zigilburk, con la esperanza de que tu entrega pueda levantar el ánimo de su hijo.","Encuentra evidencia de Katûb-zahar"}},
[3121]={nameES="Chapter 4.1: Among the Green Hills",objectivesES={"Talk to King Elessar outside the keep of Lond Cirion","King Elessar's travelling party has arrived at Iáphel","Chapter 4.1: Among the Green Hills","Bring the wine bottles to Grethril by the entrance to Iáphel","Iáphel is located north of Thingast, in Tûm Rost.","Gwindir is waiting for you to return with the grapes you picked.","Bring the grapes to Gwindir in Iáphel","Talk to King Elessar at Iáphel","Gwindir is north-west of the entrance to Iáphel.","Vine trellises can be found on the western side of Iáphel.","Grethril is at the entrance of Iáphel in Tûm Rost.","Orgolas is very excited to join King Elessar's travelling party as he journeys into Pinnath Gelin.","King Elessar is in Iáphel.","Grethril will know how best to store the wine bottles. She is by the entrance to Iáphel.","Gwindir offered you three of the wines stored nearby.","Travel to the entrance of Iáphel in Tûm Rost","King Elessar is outside the keep of Lond Cirion.","Talk to Grethril by the entrance to Iáphel","Talk to Gwindir north-west of the entrance of Iáphel","Thingast has a reputation for being haunted, and the folk of Lond Cirion will appreciate if you face some of the dangers there as you journey north."}},
[3122]={nameES="Chapter 4.1: Plans of Attack",objectivesES={"You quickly sketch Caivád Sâr on your map, noting the Angmarim presence","You quickly sketch the Orkish defences at Zarkul-sulûn","Talk to Thálfi at Zudramdân, north-east of the lake that borders the foothills","Thálfi is at Zudramdân, the forward camp of Durin's great force. Zudramdân is north-east of the lake that borders the foothills of Elderslade.","Bring the map back to Thálfi at Zudramdân","You add a brief sketch of the paths of Howlers' Notch to your map","Use the map-ready parchment to add Zarkul-sulûn to the map","You sketch the outside of Shakal-atrâd, but all seems quiet","Thálfi wanted you to add the Angmarim presence at Caivád Sâr to your map, and to defeat any of the cultists that cross your path. Caivád Sâr is to the north of Zudramdân.","Use the map-ready parchment to add Shakal-atrâd to the map","Chapter 4.1: Plans of Attack","Thálfi is at Zudramdân, the forward camp of Durin's great force, south of Caivád Sâr.","Use the map-ready parchment to add Caivád Sâr to the map","The great force of dwarves is ready for the assault, with more arriving every day. Now Durin seeks to formulate a battle plan that will bring this force across Elderslade to Gundabad.","Thálfi is beside the river just north-west of Annâk-khurfu, preparing to scout the mountainous region in advance of the assault.","Talk to Thálfi beside the river just north-west of Annâk-khurfu","Thálfi sent you to add three locations to the parchment he gave you: two old dwarf ruins to the north-west and south-west, and a warg camp further north-west.","Use the map-ready parchment to add Howlers' Notch to the map"}},
[3123]={nameES="Chapter 4.1: The Meeting of the Masters",objectivesES={"You have found record of a sighting of Urudanî","Orcs and evil Men of every variety near the Spire of Lûghash, the settlement of Fushaum Bal, the tower of Cirith Ungol, and the camp outside Naerband may carry messages from their masters to Lhaereth the Stained.","You have found orders for Róglarg","You have found the acceptance from Ugrukhôr","Harthalín is by the eastward-running road in Agarnaith.","You have found the acceptance from Dulgabêth","Intercept a message near Fushaum Bal","Intercept a message from Orodir, the camp outside Naerband","Intercept a message near the Spire of Lûghash","<rgb=#00FF00>All intercepted messages can be read from your inventory</rgb>","Chapter 4.1: The Meeting of the Masters","Bring the intercepted messages to Harthalín by the eastward road in Agarnaith","Intercept a message near the Tower of Cirith Ungol","Harthalín's quick bow-string has slain an Orc carrying word of a meeting of the Masters of Mordor, and she thinks it important to learn more."}},
[3124]={nameES="Chapter 4.2: A Knight of the Green Hills",objectivesES={"You decide to leave the boys to their game, and see if Hebron has any work for you","Find Thorongil's room inside the keep of Ost Arndír","Te doy la bienvenida.","Hebron is outside the northern entrance of the keep of Ost Arndír.","Thorongil and Orgolas run up, shouting and bickering","Thorongil and Orgolas stand uncertainly together","The entrance to Ost Arndír is to the north-east of Iáphel, in Pinnath Gelin.","King Elessar's next destination is to be Ost Arndír in Pinnath Gelin.","Orgolas is in Thorongil's room in Ost Arndír.","According to Hebron, various dangers can be found in the vicinity of Ost Arndír, and the folk of the town would appreciate you helping deal with them.","Talk to Thorongil inside his room in the keep of Ost Arndír","Chapter 4.2: A Knight of the Green Hills","Travel to the northern entrance of the keep of Ost Arndír, north-east of Iáphel","Talk to Hebron in Ost Arndír","Talk to Thorongil outside the keep of Ost Arndír","Hebron nods in welcome","The Lady Nauriel is inside the main hall of Ost Arndír, located upstairs inside the keep.","Talk to Hebron outside the keep of Ost Arndír","Hebron is outside the northern entrance to the keep of Ost Arndír.","Talk to Orgolas in Thorongil's room inside the keep of Ost Arndír","Talk to Lady Nauriel in Ost Arndír","Thorongil is in his room north of the main hall, inside the keep of Ost Arndír.","Thorongil is outside the northern entrance of the keep of Ost Arndír.","Talk to Hebron outside the northern entrance of the keep in Ost Arndír","Hebron is outside the northern entrance of the keep in Ost Arndír.","Nauriel's son Thorongil's room is to the north-east, through the door on the right."}},
[3125]={nameES="Chapter 4.2: No Time To Draw!",objectivesES={"Imák snorts rudely","Thálfi is at Zudramdân in Elderslade.","Extensive palisades and Orkish totems bolster the defences before Gundabad","Imák is at Zudramdân in Elderslade, and he wishes to speak with you.","Talk to Imák at Zudramdân in Elderslade","The Angmarim have established a settlement in the shadow of the three peaks","Thálfi wants you to scout enemy camps nearer to Gundabad and to defeat any Orcs and Angmarim you find on the way. This time he has not asked you to draw the locations on a map, and will rely instead upon your report. Crossing the bridge in front of Gundabad and exploring past the central courtyard on your way to the buildings beyond the entrance should be sufficient.","Thálfi is worried that the forces defending Gundabad need a more thorough scouting, but they will not give you the benefit of leisurely adding their camps to your map.","Scout the central courtyard in front of Gundabad","Chapter 4.2: No Time To Draw!","Scout the bridge in front of Gundabad","Scout the settlement of Dûn Traikh beyond the entrance to Gundabad","Talk to Thálfi at Zudramdân in Elderslade","The bridge before Gundabad crosses a raging river: a defensible position"}},
[3126]={nameES="Chapter 4.2: The Only Place",objectivesES={"Zaghárog told you to walk to the north-west. Will this provide your answer?","Talk to Harthalín by the road to Nargroth","The watching-stone inhabited by the spirit Zaghárog is on the road to the Caverns of Fire, in Talath Úrui.","The creature falls dead. May this be enough for Zaghárog","Mount Doom fills your vision, and you know at once: the Masters will meet on the slopes of Orodruin","There is silence in your mind for so long you begin to doubt that Zaghárog will speak to you. Then, just as you are about to turn away, the presence returns. The questioning sea buffets you as before.\
\
'Where will the Masters seek to meet?' you ask of the spirit. The only reply is silence.\
\
'Have such meetings occurred before?' you try again, but Zaghárog does not reply. The questioning sea recedes, leaving behind only sand and silt. Skeletal fish wriggle madly on the dry bed, gasping and dying.\
\
Then you notice their number: nine fish die in the water's absence. The presence in the darkness that is Zaghárog watches you closely, and the fish are gone. A sudden flash of light blinds you with its brilliance, and you recognize a flat space with sparse trees near many falls, in the southern reaches of Lhingris. Hateful chittering fills your ears, and you know there is a malevolent creature behind you, but you are unable to turn and face it. Then you hear the voice of Atli Spider-bane, and you know he hunts the creature that stalks you.\
\
Zaghárog makes his demand, and his desire fills your mind and echoes in your ears.\
\
'Kill,' he says.","Zaghárog told you to walk to the north-west","Chapter 4.2: The Only Place","The images return. You recognize a flat space with sparse trees near many falls, in the southern reaches of Lhingris. Hateful chittering fills your ears, and you know there is a malevolent creature  behind you, but you are unable to turn and face it. Then you hear the voice of Atli Spider-bane, and you know he hunts the creature that stalks you.\
\
Zaghárog makes his demand, and his desire fills your mind and echoes in your ears.\
\
'Kill,' he says.","Find the area in Lhingris near the falls, and fulfill Zaghárog's demand","Harthalín believes the meeting of the Masters will take place, but if you are to make use of this information you must learn what location each of them might trust.","Unlike your previous visit, Zaghárog does not make you wait this time. He is present immediately, with a hungering and eager need.\
\
'The spider is slain,' you say, and Zaghárog's confusion is apparent. You see the hidden gully in Lhingris once again, and feel the stalking shadow, and hear Atli Spider-bane bellow his battle-cry. A feeling of great insistence spears at you, over and over.\
\
'The spider,' you say once again, and Zaghárog responds at once: 'The dwarf.'\
\
'No,' you respond.\
\
You are buffeted by disappointment and anger. The spirit's rage is a crushing ceiling that presses down on you. It is a cauldron of boiling fire that scalds you. It is a torrent of icy rain that freezes and pierces your skin. It passes, and Zaghárog's rage is replaced with a sullen resentment.\
\
'Where will the Masters meet?' you ask once again, and Zaghárog shows you the nine dying fish, inexplicably and inexorably breathing their last.\
\
Finally, the images fade, and your feet are compelled to walk to the north-west. Zaghárog remains, nursing his disappointment, but you are confident that he has given you what you need.","Harthalín is by the road to Nargroth, on the eastern edge of Talath Úrui.","Zaghárog showed you a particular area in Lhingris and asked you to kill the creature there.","Talk to Zaghárog outside the Caverns of Fire, in Talath Úrui"}},
[3127]={nameES="Chapter 4.3: His Namesake",objectivesES={"The northern entrance to the keep of Ost Arndír is west of the Wave-hunter.","There is no stopping them","Thorongil is high above your head in the rigging of the Wave-hunter.","You should tell someone where they plan to go","Orgolas stands near the Wave-hunter.","Orgolas is near the Wave-hunter, peering up at the rigging.","Daeram is near the Wave-hunter.","The boys have run off on their adventure.","Return to the northern entrance of the keep of Ost Arndír, west of the Wave-hunter","Hebron stares at you with apprehension","Orgolas is outside the keep of Ost Arndír.","Wait for Thorongil to come down","Hebron is outside the keep of Ost Arndír.","From the deck of the Wave-hunter, <rgb=#00FF00>beckon</rgb> for Thorongil to come down","Orgolas and Thorongil intended to go to the Wave-hunter, docked to the east on the lake in Pinnath Gelin.","Talk to Hebron outside the keep of Ost Arndír","Chapter 4.3: His Namesake","Talk to Orgolas near the Wave-hunter","Find Daeram at the keep's kitchens in Ost Arndír and tell him where the boys planned to go","Talk to Orgolas outside the keep of Ost Arndír","Thorongil grudgingly descends to the deck of the Wave-hunter","Find Orgolas and Thorongil near the Wave-hunter","Orgolas peers up at the rigging of the Wave-hunter","Talk to Thorongil on the deck of the Wave-hunter","Thorongil is eager to show his new friend the sights and sounds of Pinnath Gelin, and to make a memorable first impression.","Thorongil stands on the deck of the Wave-hunter.","From the deck of the Wave-hunter you should <rgb=#00FF00>beckon</rgb> for Thorongil to come down.","Daeram is inside the kitchens of the keep in Ost Arndír.","You should cross onto the deck of the Wave-hunter in order to get Thorongil to come down.","Talk to Daeram near the Wave-hunter","High above you, Thorongil clings to the rigging of the Wave-hunter","Cross onto the deck of the Wave-hunter"}},
[3128]={nameES="Chapter 4.3: Raiment of Disguise",objectivesES={"Talk to Mithrandir at Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate","You have found a group of Nurnhoth trying to become used to their new lives","If you are to attend the meeting of the Masters of Mordor in secret, you will need some way to remain hidden: a disguise.","Chapter 4.3: Raiment of Disguise","Talk to Mithrandir in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, south of the entrance to the city","Find the group of freed Nurnhoth on the north-east side of the Third Circle","Ayorzén has followed you to the tailor, and is now on the south-eastern side of the Third Circle, seeking to get your attention.","Ayorzén followed you to the tailor, and now he seeks to get your attention","Hujâ is among a group of freed Nurnhoth on the north-east side of the Third Circle, in Minas Tirith.","Mithrandir is in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, south of the entrance to the city.","The tailor has finished resizing the Nurnhoth garments and bundles them for you","The tailor on the south-eastern side of the Third Circle will be able to fashion a disguise of the appropriate size from the Nurnhoth clothes that were given to you by Hujâ.","Talk to Ayorzén on the south-eastern side of the Third Circle","Bring the Nurnhoth clothes to Lain, a tailor on the south-eastern side of the Third Circle","A group of freed Nurnhoth might be found on the north-east side of the Third Circle, in Minas Tirith.","Mithrandir is in Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate.","With some reluctance but a hopeful smile, Hujâ gives you a bundle of rags","Talk to Hujâ on the north-east side of the Third Circle, in Minas Tirith"}},
[3129]={nameES="Chapter 4.3: Think Like A Goblin",objectivesES={"Talk to Prince Ingór on the lower level of Annâk-khurfu","Thálfi is at Zudramdân in Elderslade.","Imák is at Zudramdân in Elderslade.\
\
You have collected a number of sapper-bombs and loose rocks and should bring them back to Imák.","Durin is on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu.","Goblins carry sapper-bombs that Imák wants for his plan. He also wants you to collect some loose, heavy rocks from the base of cliffs north of Zudramdân in Elderslade.","Talk to Thálfi at Zudramdân","Talk to Durin on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu","Thálfi catches your eye. He seems unhappy about something","Chapter 4.3: Think Like A Goblin","Imák does not believe that the Longbeards are adequately prepared for the assault on Gundabad, and he wants to adopt a different approach.","Prince Ingór is on the lower level of Annâk-khurfu.","Bring the goblin-bombs and loose rocks to Imák at Zudramdân"}},
[3130]={nameES="Chapter 4.4: Raiders In Tûm Rost",objectivesES={"Talk to Nauriel in Ost Arndír","Talk to King Elessar in Ost Arndír","Chapter 4.4: Raiders In Tûm Rost","Talk to King Elessar in the keep of Ost Arndír and join the defence of Tûm Rost","Talk to King Elessar in the main hall of the keep of Ost Arndír","King Elessar hopes to bring his own fighters to join the defence of Tûm Rost against the Corsair raiders.","Talk to Nauriel in the main hall of the keep of Ost Arndír","Nauriel is inside the main hall of the keep in Ost Arndír.","Tûm Rost has been attacked by Corsair raiders, and now the folk of Pinnath Gelin must spring to its defence.","King Elessar is inside the main hall of the keep in Ost Arndír.","King Elessar is inside the main hall of the keep of Ost Arndír."}},
[3131]={nameES="Chapter 4.4: The War of Three Peaks",objectivesES={}},
[3132]={nameES="Chapter 4.4: Union of Evil",objectivesES={"Talk to Mithrandir at Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate","Mithrandir is at Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate.","The Meeting of the Masters is about to commence, and you have arranged for a disguise that should allow you to attend in secret.","Talk to Mithrandir and travel to the meeting of the Masters of Mordor","Chapter 4.4: Union of Evil"}},
[3133]={nameES="Chapter 4.5: Hammer, Axe, and Sword",objectivesES={"Chapter 4.5: Hammer, Axe, and Sword","You hear the sound of many dwarves shouting to the north","Bori, standing nearby, calls your name","Bring the Zhélruka weapons to the weapon crate in the trench to the north-west","Find the retreating dwarves Bósi saw near the trench to the north","You found Trausti in a trench not far from the lakeside while the fighting rages all about him and the War of Three Peaks continues.","Bori is in the trench north-west of Zarkul-sulûn during the War of Three Peaks.","Bori wanted you to look for his cousin Bróin or his father Bósi north-west of his trench. He has not seen them since the fighting began, and he is worried for their safety.","Trausti calls to you as you approach","Bósi told you he saw dwarves retreating from thick fighting to the north. You should search there for Bróin.","Talk to Trausti in the trench not far from the lakeside during the War of Three Peaks","Talk to Bori in the trench north-west of Zarkul-sulûn during the War of Three Peaks","Prince Ingór wants you to pick up weapons dropped by his slain warriors as proof that the Zhélruka are shouldering their own share of the war's burden. You should also slay any enemies that break through the line.","Ingór is furious at Durin's suggestion that the Zhélruka prince kept his forces in reserve during the initial assault of the War of Three Peaks.","Find Bróin or Bósi north-west of Bori's trench","A crate for storing spare weapons can be found in a trench north-west of Prince Ingór's defensive position during the War of Three Peaks."}},
[3134]={nameES="Chapter 4.5: The Chase",objectivesES={"A mighty Ent stares at you from within the curious, deep wells of his eyes.","Search the grove to the south-west for sign of the Corsairs","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> out over the water for the fleeing Corsair ships","Talk to Arasdil on the coast of Thingast","Arasdil stands nearby, and has something to say to you.","Talk to the Ent in the shady grove","You have found a spot from which you might see distant ships","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> out over the water for the fleeing Corsair ships from the coast of Thingast","King Elessar directed you to hurry south along the coast of Anfalas, in pursuit of the fleeing Corsair ships.","There seems to be no immediate sign of Corsairs at this grove","Another location on the coast to the west may allow you to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> out over the water in search of the fleeing Corsair ships.","Examine the high-quality bow on the stone block","Arasdil told you he saw Corsair activity at the haunted grove to the south-west before the ships sailed toward Pinnath Gelin.","You feel the sudden sensation of being watched.","Find a spot further to the west from which you might spy distant ships","You can't quite make out what the distant shapes on the water might be","This is a good spot from which to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> for distant ships","A deep, rumbling sound seems to come from all around you","The hazy sky over the water hides from your sight any retreating ships","Mantente en guardia","From this location on the coast you should <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> out over the water in search of the fleeing Corsair ships.","Travel to the southern coast of Thingast, south-west of Lond Cirion, in Anfalas","This bow is of unusually high quality and is in fine repair","Chapter 4.5: The Chase","A high quality bow rests on a stone within the grove here.","King Elessar wants you to travel with haste to the coast near Thingast, south-west of Lond Cirion, in Anfalas."}},
[3135]={nameES="Chapter 4.6: A Fall of Stones",objectivesES={"Bróin helps Slagvi to safety!","It might be a good idea to check on the goblin-bombs, just in case","The dwarf Afwald stands near the empty crate where Imák stored the goblin-bombs, in Zarkul-sulûn. You should ask him what happened to the explosive devices.","Bróin is trying to help free Slagvi from the rocks that have him trapped","Meet up with Slagvi in a trench to the south while the War of Three Peaks continues.","Slagvi has been trapped by a fall of stones, and Bróin is trying to free him from the heavy rocks.","Meet up with Slagvi several trenches to the south during the War of Three Peaks","With a mighty roar, a ferocious Orc charges forward!","Fighting during the War of Three Peaks has turned against the great force of Durin and Prince Ingór, and their warriors will need to stand together if they are to have the victory. Can they set aside their differences and achieve the triumph they seek?","Collect and defuse the goblin-bombs from the crate where Imák stored them, inside Zarkul-sulûn","Find Imák outside Zarkul-sulûn during the War of Three Peaks","Imák is outside Zarkul-sulûn during the War of Three Peaks, surrounded by an angry group of Longbeards.","Talk to Afwald by the empty crate in Zarkul-sulûn, during the War of Three Peaks","The crate is empty. The goblin-bombs are gone!","As Haukbuz falls, Bróin leads Slagvi to safety!","Trausti last saw Bróin and Slagvi fighting side-by-side to the north, while battle raged on all around them.","Slagvi cannot believe his ears: the trap in which he was caught had been set by the Stout-axe Imák? He demands that you find Imák and ask why he has chosen to fight dwarves and not Orcs.","Find Bróin somewhere to the north, where Trausti last saw him","Talk to Imák outside Zarkul-sulûn during the War of Three Peaks","Help free Slagvi from the stones and defend him from attacking enemies","Slagvi has been trapped by a fall of stones, and Bróin is trying to free him from the heavy rocks.\
\
Bróin wants you to help him free Slagvi from the rocks, and he will need you to defend them while he works!","Talk to Bróin as he works to free Slagvi from the rock trap","Chapter 4.6: A Fall of Stones","Imák is surrounded by a group of angry Longbeards","Imák has reluctantly agreed not to use the goblin-bombs you collected. He sent you to collect the bombs from the crate where he stored them, inside Zarkul-sulûn, and render them unusable."}},
[3136]={nameES="Chapter 4.6: Nestinanessornë",objectivesES={"King Elessar is inside the main hall of the keep of Lond Cirion, and should hear what you learned from Leafshade.","You cannot tell if Leafshade remains awake or if he has heard your words.","The Ent Leafshade is at the grove of Tumbamálë.","Leafshade appears in no hurry to speak any further, so you ask about the Elf-bow in the centre of his glade.\
\
'Hrum, hoom! That is the bow of my friend, Nestinanessornë! He left it here when he... went away.'\
\
The Ent sighs heavily, the breeze of his exhalation rustling the leaves of the trees.\
\
'There was a gathering of my folk some... what is the word your kind would use, hm? Months, hoom. Some months ago. On my return, I came across a dying creature suffering from a poisoned wound. He reminded me of an old friend, an Elf I once knew. Ah, Ferien. Hm, hoom. She lived among the beeches, and sang so beautifully. Hoom...'\
\
Leafshade stands in silence, his story unfinished, and you wonder if you should prompt him to continue.","Chapter 4.6: Nestinanessornë","The Ent Leafshade might know what transpired when the Corsair ships came this way, but getting him to tell you about it might be challenging.","Talk to Leafshade at Tumbamálë","The Ent Leafshade is at Tumbamálë, and he has much to say.","Talk to King Elessar inside the main hall of the keep of Lond Cirion","Talk to Leafshade at Tumbamálë and learn what you can from the Ent"}},
[3137]={nameES="Chapter 4.7: Elderslade Aflame",objectivesES={"Some dwarves remain dangerously close to the path where Eywind has set his stolen goblin-bombs! Eywind will not evacuate them, so it falls to you.","Tremendous explosions thunder behind you, shaking the earth!","Eywind is somewhere near Caivád Sâr as the War of Three Peaks continues.","Durin is inside Zarkul-sulûn while the War of Three Peaks continues.","Eywind's satisfaction has turned to displeasure: for some reason not all of the bombs exploded. Did goblin-sappers recover some of the bombs, and do they now plan to use them against the dwarves? You should try and recover these twice-stolen goblin-bombs, while there is still time. Goblin-sneaks can be found in Eywind's vicinity near Caivád Sâr during the War of Three Peaks.","Return to Eywind south of Caivád Sâr during the War of Three Peaks","You quench the fuse on the goblin-bomb as Eywind hurries to your side","Chapter 4.7: Elderslade Aflame","The goblin-sneak probably set his stolen bomb somewhere near the lakeside trench to the south-west, hoping to do as much damage to the dwarves as possible. You have to find and defuse it as quickly as you can!","Talk to Durin inside Zarkul-sulûn during the War of Three Peaks","Talk to Eywind in the lakeside trench during the War of Three Peaks","Recover twice-stolen goblin-bombs from goblin sneaks (2/3)","Eywind is south of the Angmarim tower of Caivád Sâr, and you should return to him quickly. You do not know how long his goblin-bombs will remain undetonated.","The dwarf Eywind has a long history of setting goblins on fire. But will he prove able to distinguish friend from foe amid the chaos of the War of Three Peaks?","Find and quench the hidden goblin-bomb somewhere near the lakeside trench","Eywind is south of Caivád Sâr, admiring his handiwork.","This goblin's boots are wet with lake-water, but he placed his bomb already!","Talk to Eywind south of Caivád Sâr during the War of Three Peaks","Eywind is in the lakeside trench during the War of Three Peaks.","Talk to Eywind near the Angmarim tower of Caivád Sâr during the War of Three Peaks"}},
[3138]={nameES="Chapter 4.7: What Your Father Would Tell You",objectivesES={"Talk to King Elessar outside the keep of Lond Cirion","You remember Golasgil, Lord of Anfalas and father of Orgolas.","Talk to Orgolas inside the keep of Lond Cirion","Consider your memory of Golasgil in Minas Tirith before the siege of the White City","You remember finding Golasgil on the Pelennor Fields after the great battle, surrounded by the corpses of the Orcs that ambushed him. You recall too the look on his face when he learned how many of his friends perished before the walls of Minas Tirith, but such sorrow did not keep him from marching to the Black Gate with the Men of the West when his King required it.","Find Orgolas in his bedroom, upstairs in the keep of Lond Cirion","Gather your thoughts concerning Golasgil","Consider your memory of Golasgil during the Battle of the Black Gate","Orgolas is inside his bedroom, upstairs in the keep of Lond Cirion.","Wait for Orgolas to consider what you have told him","You remember Golasgil at the Battle of the Black Gate as he stood face to face with the mighty Olog that would give him his mortal wound, and you recall his final words.\
\
'If there is a day to come after this,' he said, 'look to the people of Anfalas. Tell them their lord...'\
\
You cannot say for certain what the Lord of Anfalas intended, for then he died, only moments before the fall of the Dark Lord Sauron and the rout of Mordor's armies. You relay his father's words to Orgolas, and Golasgil's heir rubs at a smudge on the floor with his shoe.","You remember Golasgil standing in the White City before battle was joined on the Pelennor Fields, unafraid of the hard times ahead, trying to remember the words of an old travelling song.","Consider your memory of Golasgil on the Pelennor Fields after the battle","Orgolas is inside his bedroom, upstairs in the keep of Lond Cirion, and he has made up his mind.","You remember Golasgil, Lord of Anfalas,as he was in life","Orgolas considers what you have told him of his father Golasgil, who perished at the Black Gate of Mordor.","King Elessar is outside the keep of Lond Cirion.","Orgolas looks at you with resolve in his eyes","King Elessar has given you an important duty, and he believes your leadership will be crucial in the weeks ahead.","You try to gather your thoughts and tell Orgolas what he needs to hear.","Orgolas looks at you with a crestfallen expression as you arrive","Chapter 4.7: What Your Father Would Tell You"}},
[3139]={nameES="Chapter 4.8: On The Threshold",objectivesES={}},
[3140]={nameES="Chapter 4.8: The King Departs",objectivesES={"Talk to Ioreth at Lond Cirion","Talk to King Elessar outside the keep of Lond Cirion","Talk to Aphadaer at Lond Cirion","Caebar waits for you in the library of Lond Cirion, inside the keep.","Talk to Lady Marra outside the keep of Lond Cirion","Talk to Caebar in the library of Lond Cirion","Caebar is in the library of Lond Cirion, inside the keep.","Talk to Líniel at Lond Cirion","Return to the library of Lond Cirion inside the keep","Talk to Glindor at Lond Cirion","Chapter 4.8: The King Departs","Talk to Grethril at Lond Cirion","You should speak with the members of the travelling party who will leave Anfalas in the company of King Elessar.","King Elessar is outside the keep of Lond Cirion.","Lady Marra is outside the keep of Lond Cirion.","Talk to Queen Arwen at Lond Cirion","King Elessar is about to leave Anfalas with his travelling party, but he has entrusted you with a different mission of grave importance."}},
[3141]={nameES="Chapter 4.9: The Lord of Gundabad",objectivesES={"Chapter 4.9: The Lord of Gundabad","Durin is inside Zarkul-sulûn during the War of Three Peaks, still reeling from the events of his assault on the steps before Gundabad.","Durin's assault up the steps of Gundabad intends to reclaim the Mountain-home from the new Lord of Gundabad, but such a prize cannot be claimed so easily.","Talk to Durin inside Zarkul-sulûn during the War of Three Peaks","Bori is outside Zarkul-sulûn, eager to follow after Durin's assault up the steps. Can victory be close at hand?","Talk to Bori outside Zarkul-sulûn and go with him to confront the Lord of Gundabad"}},
[3142]={nameES="Capítulo 4: Un rencor contra los trasgos",objectivesES={"Has defendido a Sweina de los trasgos","Capítulo 4: Un rencor contra los trasgos","Bósi te ha pedido que te ocupes de un pequeño asunto mientras él lee el Libro de Mazarbul.","Habla con Sweina","Bósi se encuentra en la Cámara de las Encrucijadas, en la entrada sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Has encontrado a Sweina y has luchado a su lado contra muchos trasgos, y deberías regresar ahora con Bósi.","Sweina se encuentra en algún lugar de las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata, probablemente en la parte más al sur de sus vías mineras, cerca de la entrada de las Obras Hidráulicas.\
\
Bósi te ha pedido que busques y rescates a uno de sus enanos que ha decidido tontamente desafiar a los trasgos de las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata. Sweina cree que los trasgos de Gamil Filik tienen su hogar mucho más profundo que las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata, cerca de la entrada de las Obras Hidráulicas."}},
[3143]={nameES="Capítulo 4: Una reliquia en Nalâ-dûm (Grupo)",objectivesES={"Destruye la reliquia de Gorothúl en Nalâ-dûm","Capítulo 4: Una reliquia en Nalâ-dûm (Grupo)","Una ola de temor te recorre mientras la reliquia es destruida, luego desaparece.","Bósi cree que otra de las reliquias de Gorothúl puede encontrarse en el fondo de Nalâ-dûm, donde las grandes ruedas de Khazad-dûm yacen dormidas.","Bósi se encuentra en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, ubicada junto al Camino de Durin.\
\
Bróin te ha dicho que hables con su tío sobre las Ruedas de Agua de Nalâ-dûm.","Bósi se encuentra en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, ubicada junto al Camino de Durin.\
\
Has destruido la reliquia dejada en Nalâ-dûm por Gorothúl y deberías informar de tu éxito a Bósi.","La entrada a Nalâ-dûm se encuentra en las obras hidráulicas de Moria.\
\
Bósi informa que una reliquia de Gorothúl yace entre las Ruedas de Agua de Nalâ-dûm y requerirá un uso cuidadoso de los mecanismos para alcanzarla y destruirla. También recomienda que lleves uno o dos aliados contigo.","Habla con Bósi en la Cámara de la Encrucijada"}},
[3144]={nameES="Capítulo 4: Una reliquia en Nalâ-dûm (Solo)",objectivesES={"Capítulo 4: Una reliquia en Nalâ-dûm (Solo)","La entrada de Nalâ-dûm se encuentra en las obras hidráulicas de Moria.\
\
Bósi informa que una reliquia de Gorothúl se encuentra entre las Ruedas de Agua de Nalâ-dûm y requerirá un uso cuidadoso de los mecanismos para llegar a ella y destruirla.","Bósi cree que otra de las reliquias de Gorothúl puede encontrarse en el fondo de Nalâ-dûm, donde las grandes ruedas de Khazad-dûm yacen inactivas.","Bósi está en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, ubicada en el Camino de Durin.\
\
Bróin te ha dicho que hables con su tío sobre las Ruedas de Agua de Nalâ-dûm.","Habla con Bósi y viaja a las Obras Hidráulicas de Nalâ-dûm","Habla con Bósi en la Cámara de la Encrucijada","Bósi está en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, ubicada en el Camino de Durin.\
\
Has destruido la reliquia que Gorothúl dejó en Nalâ-dûm y deberías informar de tu éxito a Bósi.\
\
Has destruido la reliquia que Gorothúl dio a los merrevail en Lumul-nar y ahora deberías regresar con Bróin."}},
[3145]={nameES="Capítulo 4: Una alianza tensa",objectivesES={"Orvar Martillo de Campana está en Buzun-ghâr, el pasaje recién excavado junto al Camino de Durin, ubicado en la pared sur del extremo sureste de Tharâkh Bazân. Tharâkh Bazân está al noreste de la Cámara de la Encrucijada.\
\
Bósi te ha pedido que ayudes a Orvar, el enano que trabaja más estrechamente con los Elfos enviados por Celeborn a Moria.","Celeborn ha enviado a varios Elfos para ayudar a los enanos en Moria, y has prometido a Gimli que también seguirás prestando tu ayuda en las Minas.","Capítulo 4: Una alianza tensa","Corunothiel está en el campamento dentro de Buzun-ghâr, ubicado junto al Camino de Durin en el extremo sureste de Tharâkh Bazân.\
\
Orvar ha expresado su frustración con los Elfos enviados por Celeborn y quiere que hables con uno de ellos sobre su irritación.","Bósi está en la Cámara de la Encrucijada cerca del Camino de Durin, en Moria.\
\
Gimli te ha pedido que regreses a Moria para hablar con Bósi y decirle que ayudarás a la Guarnición de Hierro con sus problemas."}},
[3146]={nameES="Chapter 4: Charge of the Iron-folk",objectivesES={"Talk to Hermáth Stormhammer at Muru Azog","Iron-folk can be found on the field near Durin's Stone.\
\
Dáin has asked you to command the Iron-folk and send them to aid his father at the gates of Khazad-dûm.","As you continue to read Hermáth Stormhammer's account of the Battle of Azanulbizar, you begin the fourth chapter in which the Dwarves of the Haban’akkâ of Thráin turn the tide of battle and the Iron-folk charge to meet Azog at the gates of Khazad-dûm.","Hermáth Stormhammer can be found at Muru Azog at Azanulbizar.\
\
After the defeat of Azog, Hermáth Stormhammer interjects and calls your attention to events at Muru Azog. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.","Chapter 4: Charge of the Iron-folk","Dáin can be found at Durin's Stone.\
\
You have ordered the Iron-folk to aid Náin Orcsfoe at the gates of Khazad-dûm. You should talk to Dáin.","Talk to Dáin and confront 'The Lord of Moria'"}},
[3147]={nameES="Capítulo 4: Profundo es el Abismo",objectivesES={"El Refugio Sombrío se encuentra entre las Fundaciones de Piedra bajo Nud-melek.\
\
Galadriel le dijo a Haldir que si quieres salvar a los enanos de Moria, debes trabajar junto con los Elfos que envió a las Fundaciones de Piedra para enfrentarse a un gran mal.","Galadriel te ha dicho que al ayudar a los Elfos del Refugio Sombrío, también estarás ayudando a los enanos de Moria.","Capítulo 4: Profundo es el Abismo","Habla con Lenglammel en el Refugio Sombrío"}},
[3148]={nameES="Chapter 4: Deeper In",objectivesES={"Habla con Golodhon","You should talk to Merry and Pippin again in Bâr Thorenion, now that you are all safely returned from Mordor.","Golodhon, Merry, and Pippin can be found in the Foothold camp in Udûn.\
\
You should talk to Golodhon when you are ready to head back into Mordor.","Habla con Merry","Merry and Pippin have grown determined to go back into Mordor once more, this time in search of facts.","Chapter 4: Deeper In","You should meet Merry and Pippin at the Foothold in Udûn.","Habla con Pippin"}},
[3149]={nameES="Capítulo 4: Enemigos en la Oscuridad Eterna",objectivesES={"Bori se encuentra en la Cámara de Mando, la sala en la parte superior de las escaleras del este en la Cámara de los Cruces, en la entrada sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Has descubierto algunas páginas que revelan información sobre Nâr-khelab, el Corazón de Fuego.","Capítulo 4: Enemigos en la Oscuridad Eterna","Busca en Katûb-zahar el secreto para abrir Nâr-khelab","Katûb-zahar, la Cámara de las Palabras de Durin, se encuentra en el lado este de la Gran Excavación, al norte de una gran estatua de Durin.\
\
Bori te ha pedido que regreses a Katûb-zahar para buscar alguna señal del truco para abrir la puerta hacia Nâr-khelab, el Corazón de Fuego.","Lleva las páginas podridas a Bori","Bori te ha hablado de Nâr-khelab, la gran forja en la que podría haberse fabricado el hacha de mithril, Zigilburk. El camino hacia la forja está bloqueado por algún truco secreto, perdido con el tiempo.","Buscas en el nido maloliente, pero no encuentras nada útil."}},
[3150]={nameES="Chapter 4: Ergothorn Elf-friend",objectivesES={"Habla con Halbarad","The mysterious letter is on a crate by Halbarad.\
\
Radanir found a letter addressed 'To the Rangers' stuck in a tree with a knife, and Halbarad wants you to read it and give your opinion on its truthfulness.","Search Lhaid Ogo for the lost Dunlending messenger","To the Rangers:\
\
I am a man of Gondor, a friend of the Elves and of all good folk. Call me Ergothorn. I see the danger growing in the East and want to oppose it.\
\
Lheu Brenin dispatched a messenger from Tûr Morva in Dunland, but the messenger was beset by foes outside Lhaid Ogo in the Lich Bluffs and was dragged within. If he yet lives, he will have information for you.\
\
I cannot reveal myself to you, but trust that I am a friend. I will contact you again when it is safe to do so.\
\
Ergothorn","There are signs of a struggle outside the entrance to Lhaid Ogo","Find the entrance to Lhaid Ogo, in the Lich Bluffs","Chapter 4: Ergothorn Elf-friend","To the Rangers:\
\
I am a man of Gondor, a friend of the Elves and of all good folk. Call me Ergothorn. I see the danger growing in the East and wish to oppose it.\
\
Lheu Brenin dispatched a messenger from Tûr Morva in Dunland, but the messenger was beset by foes outside Lhaid Ogo in the Lich Bluffs and was dragged within. If he yet lives, he will have information for you.\
\
I cannot reveal myself to you, but trust that I am a friend. I will contact you again when it is safe to do so.\
\
Ergothorn","Glynn Brenin is in the Brenin's Hall, atop the hill of Lhanuch.\
\
You have rescued the Dunlending messenger and should return to Glynn Brenin to hear his message.","Talk to Glynn Brenin in Lhanuch","Radanir found a mysterious note from a purported friend: but can Ergothorn Elf-friend be trusted?","Read the letter on the crate by Halbarad in Lhanuch","Somewhere inside Lhaid Ogo, a messenger from Dunland may be in trouble.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an Inspired Greatness bonus, but the challenge will be great.</rgb>","Lhaid Ogo is on the right side of the road that runs through the Lich Bluffs.\
\
Halbarad is not certain that Ergothorn can be trusted, but he wants you to travel to Lhaid Ogo to see if there is any truth to the mysterious letter.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an Inspired Greatness bonus, but the challenge will be great.</rgb>","Halbarad is among the huts on the western side of Lhanuch.\
\
You have read the note from Ergothorn and should now speak with Halbarad about it."}},
[3151]={nameES="Capítulo 4: Primeras Ofensivas",objectivesES={"Completa la Escaramuza: Ataque contra Dannenglor","Habla con Dúndurion en Audaghaim","Las ruinas de Dannenglor son el objetivo de un ataque planificado por Dúndurion.\
\
Dúndurion te ha pedido que participes en el ataque contra las ruinas de Dannenglor ocupadas por los morrovals.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión implica una escaramuza que se puede completar en tamaños de grupo: Solitario, Duo, Pequeña Comunidad, gran Comunidad o Incursión utilizando el Panel de Escaramuzas. Esta escaramuza tiene un nivel mínimo de 60.</rgb>","Cúcheron se encuentra en el porche de la Posada Embrujada, en Audaghaim.\
\
Dúndurion te ha enviado de regreso a Cúcheron. Quizás la Guardia Oculta haya decidido qué camino tomar en la próxima etapa de su viaje.","Dúndurion se encuentra en Audaghaim, fuera de la Posada Embrujada, contemplando el paisaje desde los acantilados.\
\
Cúcheron ha decidido enviarte a Dúndurion para ayudar a la Hueste Dorada con sus asuntos militares mientras la Guardia Oculta decide un plan de acción.","Dúndurion se encuentra en Audaghaim, fuera de la Posada Embrujada, contemplando el paisaje desde los acantilados.\
\
Has participado en el exitoso ataque contra Dannenglor y ahora deberías regresar con Dúndurion.","Habla con Cúcheron fuera de la Posada Embrujada","Capítulo 4: Primeras Ofensivas","La Guardia Oculta está en desorden tras la muerte de Raddir, y Cúcheron ha decidido que deberías ayudar a la Hueste Dorada mientras deciden qué hacer a continuación."}},
[3152]={nameES="Chapter 4: Friends of the Longbeards",objectivesES={"Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
You should collect the care package in Vérnozal.","Talk to Prince Ingór","Collect the care package","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you.","Give the care package to the visiting Longbeard emissary","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
You should pack up all the items into a care package in Vérnozal.","You packed up all the items","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
You should give the care package to the visiting Longbeard emissary in Vérnozal.","Collected the care package","Pack up all the items into a care package","Chapter 4: Friends of the Longbeards","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to the Zhélruka and to fight on their behalf in Gundabad.","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
You should collect some draughts, ales, and bread in Vérnozal."}},
[3153]={nameES="Chapter 4: Halros, Ranger of the Shire",objectivesES={"Talk to Halros and help him decide whether to stay in the Shire or to travel south with the Grey Company","Deal with the trouble-maker in the Green Hill Country","Trouble-makers can be found on the road through Green Hill Country, and in the village of Stock, in the Shire.\
\
Halros has asked you to walk the road through Green Hill Country and to visit the town of Stock to deal with the bold trouble-makers that have appeared there.","Dealt with the trouble-maker in Stock","Halros has a camp in the Greenfields, in the north-east corner of the Shire.\
\
Halros has asked for your help in making the decision whether to travel south with the Grey Company or to maintain his vigil over the Shire.","Dealt with the trouble-maker in the Green Hill Country","Chapter 4: Halros, Ranger of the Shire","Halros has a camp in the Greenfields, in the north-east corner of the Shire.\
\
You have discouraged the trouble-makers in the Green Hill Country and Stock, as Halros asked, and should return now to the Ranger.","Saeradan has sent you to bring word of the Grey Company's errand to Halros, a Ranger currently watching over the Shire.","Halros has a camp in the Greenfields, west of Bree-land, in the Shire.\
\
Saeradan has told you where to find the Ranger Halros and has warned you that Halros may find it difficult to leave the Shire, even for so important an errand.","Deal with the trouble-maker in Stock","Talk to Halros in the Greenfields"}},
[3154]={nameES="Capitulo 4: Apresúrate a la sala Vigesimoprimera",objectivesES={"Capitulo 4: Apresúrate a la sala Vigesimoprimera","Stóthkell está satisfecho con el trabajo que has hecho para ayudar a preparar el Corazón de Fuego para la guerra, y quiere que hagas lo mismo por los enanos de la sala Vigesimoprimera.","Brogur se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo cerca de la sala Vigesimoprimera en Zelem-melek.\
\
Has ayudado a los enanos del Corazón de Fuego a preparar la defensa, y Stóthkell quiere que hagas lo mismo por los enanos de la sala Vigesimoprimera."}},
[3155]={nameES="Chapter 4: Judgements of the King",objectivesES={"Chapter 4: Judgements of the King","King Elessar's guard Malthengil is near the throne.","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to Elessar and the Kingdom of Gondor, and to fight on their behalf in Mordor.","Talk to Malthengil and witness the pronouncements of King Elessar","Talk to King Elessar in his throne room","King Elessar is in his throne room atop Minas Tirith.","King Elessar is about to pronounce his judgements on a number of important matters, and his guard Malthengil has offered that you be allowed to watch.","Talk to Malthengil by King Elessar's throne"}},
[3156]={nameES="Capítulo 4: Fuera de la puerta",objectivesES={"Los trabajadores enanos se encuentran al norte del campamento de Bósi, a lo largo del camino sinuoso que sube a la Puerta de Acebeda.\
\
Bósi te ha pedido que entregues almuerzos a los enanos encargados de desenterrar los escombros frente a la Puerta de Acebeda, y luego que hagas tu reporte a Wárr.","Bósi te ha pedido que ayudes a reabastecer con almuerzos a los trabajadores que intentan desenterrar la Puerta de Acebeda para mantener su ánimo alto.","Lleva los picos rotos a Bósi","Bósi supervisa algunos de los carros cerca de las orillas del Sirannon seco, al sur de la carretera que serpentea hasta la Puerta de Acebeda.\
\
Wárr te ha pedido que entregues un suministro de picos rotos a Bósi y que le pidas que los reemplace.","El enano Wárr se encuentra en la Puerta de Acebeda, supervisando el trabajo de los obreros allí.\
\
Ahora que has entregado los almuerzos a los trabajadores enanos a lo largo del camino que conduce a la Puerta de Acebeda, deberías hablar con Wárr para que te asigne otras tareas.","Capítulo 4: Fuera de la puerta","Has recogido picos rotos"}},
[3157]={nameES="Chapter 4: Riding South",objectivesES={"The first leg of the Grey Company's journey will take them south through the Trollshaws and into Eregion.","Talk to Halbarad at the stables in Rivendell","Saeradan is at Gwingris, in Eregion.\
\
The farrier Londan has thanked you for your aid, and he has asked you to speak with Saeradan.","The Grey Company begins its ride south. Halbarad has determined that the Rangers will rest at Gwingris, in Eregion.\
\
You should ride south to Gwingris, either on your own mount or on one engaged from Rivendell.","Talk to Londan the farrier, who will be waiting for you back at Gwingris","Find Londan the farrier and talk to him","Talk to Saeradan at Gwingris","Chapter 4: Riding South","You have protected Londan the farrier from the uruks","Talk to Saeradan at Gwingris, in Eregion, after riding south","Londan should still be in Eregion. He left Gwingris heading east.\
\
Saeradan has asked you to find the farrier Londan and convince him to return to Gwingris so that he may repair Erebrandir's shoe.","Halbarad is at the stables of Rivendell.\
\
Candaith has asked you to speak with Halbarad to see if he has any final words before you join the rest of the Rangers on their ride south.","Londan the farrier will be waiting for you back at Gwingris, in Eregion.\
\
You have rescued Londan from the Sharkúnakh uruks that he encountered and should return to Gwingris."}},
[3158]={nameES="Capítulo 4: Las penas de Khazad-dûm",objectivesES={"Bósi se encuentra en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, en el extremo sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Brogur te ha pedido que consultes a Bósi para que te dé alguna idea de qué hacer a continuación, ahora que los enanos han perdido gran parte de su esperanza de victoria en Moria.","Brogur no sabe qué hacer tras la pérdida de Bori y Zigilburk, y teme que el tiempo de los enanos en Moria esté cerca de su fin.","Capítulo 4: Las penas de Khazad-dûm"}},
[3159]={nameES="Chapter 4: The Wandering and the Lost",objectivesES={"Return to Legolas in the Court of Lothlórien with the many gifts of seed.","Lady Galadriel suggested you begin by visiting Certhíril in Mirobel and ask her about Glorfindel and a gift of seeds.","Now you should show the record you found in Tham Giliath to Lady Galadriel.","Visit Certhíril in Mirobel","Talk to Lady Galadriel","Look for Glorfindel, or his disciple, at his accustomed spot in Rivendell, below Elrond's House and above the waterfall.","You should ask Legolas about the nature of the request he has for you.","Seek Dorongur in Duillond","Someone is standing in Glorfindel's spot, but it is not he","Show the record to Gildor","Seek Gildor in Tham Giliath","Visit Glorfindel's spot in Rivendell","You should talk to Lady Galadriel in the Court of Lothlórien.","Seek Dorthaneth near Edhellond","Travel to the places where Elves dwell, seeking word of Glorfindel and gifts for Aragorn's taking of the throne.","Gildor has suggested you look around Tham Giliath for a clue as to what Glorfindel found.","Show the record to Lady Galadriel","Deliver the seeds to Legolas","Dorongur has suggested that you travel to the library in Lin Giliath and look for Gildor Inglorion, whom you can ask about Glorfindel and a gift of seeds.","You should talk to Galadriel once more before you go.","You should show the record that you found to Gildor in Tham Giliath.","Dorthaneth suggested that Dorongor, in Duillond, might know something of what Glorfindel seeks and where he has gone. You should ask him about that and also a gift of seeds.","Seek Dorthaneth in the caves of the Avorrim, near Edhellond, in Belfalas, and ask her about Glorfindel and a gift of seeds.","Chapter 4: The Wandering and the Lost","Habla con Legolas."}},
[3160]={nameES="Chapter 4: Treachery in Mordor",objectivesES={"Search near the base of Lûghash for Mogi","Search to the north for Mogi","Thorin III, King under the Mountain, is at his throne in Erebor.","Dómor has gone to the road south of Lûghash. Did he find Mogi?","If Mogi was here, he is gone now","Talk to Dómor south of Lûghash, in Dor Amarth","You found Dómor in Dor Amarth. Does he know where the other dwarf heroes have gone?","There is no sign here of Mogi","You see no sign that Mogi was here","Search near the road for Mogi","You have found Dómor, one of the dwarf heroes Thorin sent into Mordor","Dómor asked you to search to the north, in the direction of Lûghash, for the treacherous Mogi.","Find the missing dwarf heroes in Dor Amarth, in Mordor","The dwarf heroes sent into Mordor by King Thorin have not reported back in some time, and are missing somewhere in Dor Amarth, south of Lûghash.\
\
King Thorin has sent you to find the missing dwarf heroes in Mordor.","Chapter 4: Treachery in Mordor","Talk to Dómor south of Lûghash, near the road","Talk to King Thorin III at his throne in the Hall under the Mountain","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to Durin's Folk and fight on their behalf in Mordor."}},
[3161]={nameES="Chapter 5.1: A Question of Purpose",objectivesES={"Talk to Mithrandir at Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate","Harthalín is west of Faltor Gâm, in Agarnaith.\
\
Mithrandir asked you to find Harthalín in Agarnaith and hear her report.","Thenca is south of Agarnaith, by the road in Talath Úrui.\
\
Mithrandir asked you to find Thenca in Talath Úrui and hear his report.","Talk to Harthalín west of Faltor Gâm, in Agarnaith","Talk to Thenca south of Agarnaith, along the road in Talath Úrui","Talk to Gwedhir south-west of the ruins of Díngarth","Mithrandir is at Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate.","Gwedhir is south-west of the ruins of Díngarth, in Dor Amarth.\
\
Mithrandir asked you to find Gwedhir in Dor Amarth and hear his report.","Chapter 5.1: A Question of Purpose","Unsure of how best to combat the Masters of Mordor in their unification, Mithrandir turns to you to gather the information that will allow him to form a strategy."}},
[3162]={nameES="Chapter 5.1: Many Masters",objectivesES={"Glóin expressed his surprise and dismay at the artists and craftsmen that have answered Durin's call and come to Zarkul-sulûn. You should speak with these new arrivals and learn why they have come to such a place of war.","Talk to Eskil Bloodthumb outside Zarkul-sulûn","Stáli has directed you to speak to his apprentice, Eskil Bloodthumb, outside Zarkul-sulûn.","Stáli the Hewer stands outside Zarkul-sulûn. Why has the sculptor come to such a dangerous place in time of war?","Talk to Prince Ingór downstairs in Zarkul-sulûn","You set the luggage down as Stáli arrives. You notice he carries nothing","Talk to Stáli the Hewer on the upper floor of Zarkul-sulûn","Chapter 5.1: Many Masters","Talk to Glóin outside Zarkul-sulûn","Stáli clearly does not remember you","Stáli the Hewer glances at you imperiously, without recognition","Durin will not be dissuaded from reclaiming the Mountain-home. He commands the Dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ to break through the frozen wall that now blocks the gates of Gundabad.","Stáli the Hewer has ordered that Eskil Bloodthumb carry his master's luggage to the upper floor inside Zarkul-sulûn. You have decided to help Eskil in this task, so the apprentice need not carry everything by himself.","Glóin stands outside Zarkul-sulûn, watching as more dwarves arrive for the conquest of the Mountain-home.","Meet with the new arrivals outside Zarkul-sulûn","Talk to Stáli the Hewer outside Zarkul-sulûn","Pick up some of Stáli's luggage","Stáli the Hewer has arrived on the upper floor of Zarkul-sulûn.","You decide to leave Stáli before you damage the irksome artist himself","Prince Ingór is downstairs in Zarkul-sulûn, waiting to speak with you."}},
[3163]={nameES="Chapter 5.1: The Crew of the Wave-hunter",objectivesES={"Complete 'The Crew: The Boon Companions'","Talk to Caebar in the library of Lond Cirion when you are satisfied with your crew","Chapter 5.1: The Crew of the Wave-hunter","Caebar has written some notes about potential crew-members for the Wave-hunter. Consult the book on the table in the library of Lond Cirion, and let it guide you as you assemble your crew.","Recruit any other members of the crew you wish","Complete 'The Crew: The Sea-longing Lord'","Complete 'The Crew: Knight of the Green Hills'","Complete 'The Crew: The Corsair Jajax'","Elessar has charged you to carry out a dangerous rescue mission to the City of the Corsairs, and for that you will need a willing crew.","Complete 'The Crew: She Who Remained'","Caebar has written some notes about potential crew-members for the Wave-hunter. Consult the book on the table in the library of Lond Cirion, and let it guide you as you assemble your crew.\
\
When you are satisfied with the crew you have assembled, return to the library of Lond Cirion and speak with Caebar."}},
[3164]={nameES="Chapter 5.2: Breaking Through",objectivesES={}},
[3165]={nameES="Chapter 5.2: Making Ready To Depart",objectivesES={"Chapter 5.2: Making Ready To Depart","Sigileth readies for the departure of the Wave-hunter.","Travel to the Wave-hunter where it is docked in Pinnath Gelin","Talk to Sirgon on the deck of the Wave-hunter","Talk to Sigileth beside the Wave-hunter in Pinnath Gelin","Nauriel and others of the crew prepare to depart","Sirgon stands on the deck of the Wave-hunter, lost in his thoughts, as he prepares for the voyage.","The Wave-hunter is docked on the lake outside Ost Arndír.","Nauriel readies for the voyage of the Wave-hunter where the ship is docked in Pinnath Gelin.","Talk to Nauriel beside the Wave-hunter in Pinnath Gelin","The time has come for you and your trusted crew to depart for Umbar on the Wave-hunter."}},
[3166]={nameES="Chapter 5.2: The Warrior Missing",objectivesES={"Talk to Mithrandir at Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate","Find Plákash in Durthang","Lady Galadriel and Lord Celeborn have come with the Golden Host to Dol Guldur, in preparation for the fortress's destruction. You will find them outside the fortress of Thangúlhad in the Gathbúrz area of Southern Mirkwood.","Find Galadriel and Celeborn outside Thangúlhad in the Gathbúrz area of Southern Mirkwood","Plákash can be found somewhere within Durthang. Durkhlát can be found outside Cirith Ungol.\
\
Mithrandir asked you to find one of the Orcs that seek the Weeping Warrior and compel him to divulge the purpose for his search.","You have uncovered a course of investigation that Mithrandir hopes will lead to some means of fighting the Masters of Mordor: Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior, is sought by Ugrukhôr for some unknown purpose.","Talk to Lady Galadriel outside Thangúlhad","Chapter 5.2: The Warrior Missing","The Lord and Lady of the Golden Wood have come to the fortress of Dol Guldur","Find Durkhlát outside Cirith Ungol","Mithrandir is at Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate.","Talk to Lord Celeborn outside Thangúlhad"}},
[3167]={nameES="Chapter 5.3: The Mighty Court of Máttugard",objectivesES={}},
[3168]={nameES="Chapter 5.3: Voyage of the Wave-hunter",objectivesES={"Talk to Caebar by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles","The men stare at you warily","Talk to Daxamat at Voyage's End in the Shield Isles","Caebar stands by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles.","Chapter 5.3: Voyage of the Wave-hunter","You feel eyes upon you from the tree line","Someone watches you from the tree line to the west of the Wave-hunter.","Daxamat has left the ship and awaits your orders.","Talk to Mattân to the west of the Wave-hunter","Confront the men watching you from the tree line to the west","Talk to Ozâl to the west of the Wave-hunter","Now that your preparations have been made, it is time for the voyage of the Wave-hunter and the completion of your secret mission.","Two residents of the Shield Isles watch you with suspicion in their eyes.","Talk to Sirgon and give the order for the ship to set sail to Umbar","Sirgon stands on the deck of the Wave-hunter, eager for the ship to set sail."}},
[3169]={nameES="Chapter 5.3: Whispers from the Long Years",objectivesES={"Talk to Gladhel within Dol Guldur","Chapter 5.3: Whispers from the Long Years","Talk to Sigileth in her hideout","Find Elves of the Golden Host within Dol Guldur","The Lord and Lady of Lórien have joined the Golden Host for the final destruction of Dol Guldur.","Sigileth is in her hideout deep beneath Dol Guldur.","You found some Malledhrim sentries within the walls of Dol Guldur","Talk to Bánoth within Dol Guldur","Explore the room of shadow at the bottom of the secret stair","Elves of the Golden Host can be found within the walls of Dol Guldur.","You found another group of sentries within the walls of Dol Guldur","This must be the entrance of which Bánoth spoke.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","Find Elves of the Golden Host deeper within Dol Guldur","Bánoth asked you to investigate the secret stairway his warriors discovered down the slope, behind the door on the left."}},
[3170]={nameES="Chapter 5.4 She Who Remained",objectivesES={"You have found Sigileth in a secret wing beneath Dol Guldur, and she wishes to help you complete your mission before the fortress is destroyed.","Servants of Sauron and evil relics can be found throughout the halls and chambers of Gostador.","Sigileth is in her hideout at the Sorcerer's Stores, in Gostador.","Bring the relics and tomes to Sigileth in the Sorcerer's Stores, in Gostador","Chapter 5.4 She Who Remained"}},
[3171]={nameES="Chapter 5.4: A Weapon of Light",objectivesES={"Clean the south-western mirror mechanism at Vâr Nuchur","Talk to Bori north-west of Vâr Nuchur","This dirty mirror is covered in filth and no longer reflects light","Bósi directed you to the west, where he spoke of more mirrors in need of cleaning.","You scrub filth from the dirty mirror until it gleams","Searching for mirrors to clean, you have found Bósi's son Bori north-west of Vâr Nuchur.","You scrub the dirt of years from the mirror until it shines once again","Clean the eastern mirror mechanism at Vâr Nuchur","Clean the mirror south-east of Bósi's location","Find the dirty mirror of which Bósi spoke to the south-east","You will find Bósi along the southern side of the great pit in the centre of Máttugard.","Clean the mirror mechanism north-west of Vâr Nuchur, and down a level","Chapter 5.4: A Weapon of Light","Glóin has asked you to aid the dwarves of the Iron Garrison he sent to scout the further reaches of Máttugard.","After a good scrubbing, the mirror mechanism once again reflects light","The mirror mechanism to the south-east once kept the trolls at bay, but now it is filth-covered and non-reflective. Bósi asked you to clean the dirty mirror and restore its troll-hindering potential.","The mirror mechanism south of the great pit once kept the trolls at bay, but now it is filth-covered and non-reflective. Bósi asked you to clean the dirty mirror to the south-east and restore its troll-hindering potential.","As you approach the mirror, you see that someone has already cleaned it of grime","Bósi stands here, studying a troll-shaped stone statue","Look for Bósi south of the great pit in Máttugard","You have found Bósi south of the great pit in Máttugard, studying a troll that has been turned to stone.","Now that you cleaned the mirror as he requested, you should return to Bósi in Máttugard, north-west of the cleaned mirror.","Talk to Bósi south of the great pit in Máttugard","Talk to Bósi to the north-west in Máttugard"}},
[3172]={nameES="Chapter 5.4: The Shield Isles",objectivesES={"Talk to Sirgon by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles","Sirgon has joined you and Caebar by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles.","Talk to Caebar by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles","Complete 'The Isles: Keen-eyed Sigileth'","Complete 'The Isles: The Corsair Daxamat'","Complete 'The Isles: Gimli and Legolas'","Chapter 5.4: The Shield Isles","Complete 'The Isles: The Knight Nauriel'","Complete 'The Isles: Sirgon the Explorer'","Eager to obtain a secure foothold from which to continue the mission, some of the Wave-hunter's crew have scattered across the Shield Isles and must be found.","Think it over","Each member of your crew has gone in search of some way to help, but now many of them are scattered across the various islands that make up the Shield Isles.","Sirgon joins you and calls for your attention","Caebar is by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles.","Sirgon is interested in your conversation with Caebar."}},
[3173]={nameES="Chapter 5.5: Belondor of Langstrand",objectivesES={"Find the location to the west where Sirgon wants to talk with you","Sirgon has asked to meet you to the west so he can discuss something with you.","Sirgon has fallen silent once again.","Sirgon seems ready to conclude his tale","Sirgon is west of Voyage's End, ready to continue his tale.","Sirgon is west of Voyage's End, waiting to speak with you.","Wait for Sirgon to gather his thoughts once again","Chapter 5.5: Belondor of Langstrand","Sirgon seems ready to continue his tale","Sirgon's joy of exploring the Shield Isles has soured a little with the arrival of some new information.","Sirgon has fallen silent.","Wait for Sirgon to gather his thoughts","Talk to Sirgon on the rocky outcropping","Sirgon stands on the rocky outcropping, staring out at the water","Sirgon is west of Voyage's End, ready to conclude his tale."}},
[3174]={nameES="Chapter 5.5: The Walls Brought Down",objectivesES={"Talk to Sigileth on Dol Dhannen, the Hill of Ruin","Talk to Thranduil on Dol Dhannen, the Hill of Ruin","Talk to Galadriel on Dol Dhannen, the Hill of Ruin","Galadriel has cast down the walls of Dol Guldur and laid bare its pits, and now she wishes to speak with you.","Sigileth is on Dol Dhannen, the Hill of Ruin.","Chapter 5.5: The Walls Brought Down","Thranduil the Elvenking has come to Dol Dhannen, the Hill of Ruin.","Galadriel has laid waste to the fortress of Dol Guldur, bringing an end to its capacity to nurture the evils of Sauron."}},
[3175]={nameES="Chapter 5.5: Treasure in a Troll-hoard",objectivesES={"Talk to Líkmund outside the grodbog-infested troll-hoard, to the north-west","You root around in the debris, but find nothing of value","This might also once have been home to trolls and their treasure","Talk to Bróin at Maergrind, the Noble Gate","Bori has two locations in mind that might once have served as troll-hoards full of treasure. The first is a short distance to the south of his position.","Bróin catches your eye, a haunted expression on his face","Bori has two locations in mind that might once have served as troll-hoards full of treasure. The second is far to the east, beyond the great pit in the centre of Máttugard.","A foul reek emanates from an entrance in the western wall: the odour of troll?","This coffer has been emptied of any treasure it might once have held","Find and search the second possible troll-hoard far to the east, beyond the great pit","Líkmund thinks the goblins lurking in the shadowy reaches of Máttugard might have coins they stole during their occupation of Gundabad.","Find and search the first possible troll-hoard to the south of Bori's position","Bróin is at Maergrind, the Noble Gate, in Máttugard.","Bori wonders whether any of the trolls that were turned to stone by the mirror mechanisms throughout Máttugard might have kept treasure-hoards nearby, and wants you to investigate.","This box contains only dust, looted of treasure long ago by Orcs","If the debris of centuries once contained treasure, it does no longer","Bring the coinpurses to Thettmárr south-west of Maergrind in Máttugard","Líkmund is standing by this one-time troll-hoard, waiting to hear of your discoveries.","Líkmund asked you to bring the coinpurses to Thettmárr south-west of Maergrind in partial payment of his gambling debt.","Chapter 5.5: Treasure in a Troll-hoard"}},
[3176]={nameES="Chapter 5.6: A Place for the Lost",objectivesES={"Nauriel believes you should ask the folk who live in Halrax, on the island of Zamarzîr, what they know about the bounty hunters recruited by Saklaphêl.","Talk to Manadhon on the upper level of Halrax and complete 'The Isles: Driftwood'","Nauriel is back at the Wave-hunter, waiting for information about the bounty hunters recruited by Saklaphêl.","Belondor is not the first wayward voyager to return from death among the Shield Isles, and he will not be the last.","Talk to Nauriel at Voyage's End","Nauriel has returned to the Wave-hunter in the Shield Isles and will surely have a plan.","Chapter 5.6: A Place for the Lost","Manadhon, the bartender at Halrax, may be willing to tell you about Driftwood, one of the bounty hunters hired by Saklaphêl.","Talk to Daxamat on the eastern side of Halrax, at the bottom of the hill","Daxamat has come to Halrax in search of more information, and can be found at the bottom of the hill on the eastern side of the city."}},
[3177]={nameES="Chapter 5.6: High Seat of the Dwarves",objectivesES={"Durin is at Maergrind, the Noble Gate, in Máttugard.","Talk to Durin at Maergrind","Durin stands atop the Steepset, considering the progress of his people as they seek to reclaim the halls of Gundabad.","Chapter 5.6: High Seat of the Dwarves","Durin has called for the leaders of the Gabil'akkâ to ascend to the Steepset.","Stáli the Hewer is at the Steepset.","Talk to Durin at the Steepset","Stáli the Hewer waves you over to him","Talk to Durin and ascend to the Steepset with the Gabil'akkâ","With the first foothold of the dwarves in Gundabad assured, Prince Durin calls for the leaders of the Gabil'akkâ to ascend to the Steepset.","Talk to Stáli the Hewer at the Steepset"}},
[3178]={nameES="Chapter 5.7: The Cape of Umbar",objectivesES={}},
[3179]={nameES="Chapter 5: A Meal in Cormallen",objectivesES={"You should talk to Pippin and Merry in Bâr Thorenion to learn what sort of expedition they are setting off on now.","Merry and Pippin propose a very different kind of expedition.","Chapter 5: A Meal in Cormallen","Habla con Merry","You should talk with Merry and Pippin now that you have returned to Bâr Thorenion from your meal, and hear their thoughts on the discussion that took place."}},
[3180]={nameES="Chapter 5: An Ordinary Squabble",objectivesES={"Talk to Prince Ingór","Chapter 5: An Ordinary Squabble","Talk to Víglund","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you.","You question Igrit about both Víglund and Néchek.\
\
'You might find this odd, but they are both telling the truth! Víglund swept up at Hammers and Bones last night, with the goat as the main prize. I could not tell you where the goat came from, however. I think it wandered over and looked quite without an owner, so we all thought the goat would sweeten the pot, you know.'\
\
'Néchek, on the other hand, he never gambles. If that goat does belong to Néchek, you might want to check the stables.'","Search for the missing rope","The rope is tied around some sort of gift","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
You should talk to Víglund in Vérnozal.","Talk to Néchek","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
You should show the gift to Néchek in Vérnozal.","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
You should talk to the arguing dwarves in Vérnozal.","Bring the gift to Igrit","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
You should talk to Igrit in Vérnozal.","You show Néchek the gift tied with missing rope from the stables.\
\
'Oh my, I am such a fool! Not only is that rope indeed the one used to tether my goat, that gift is also mine.\
\
'I have been trying to profess my love to someone special. I procured the perfect gift, but I lacked anything with which to tie it up! In my haste I must have taken the rope from the stalls without thinking and forgot to latch the gate! Oh, this is all my fault... and for all this unpleasantness my love did not even open the present! Please take the gift away! I do not wish to see it again!'","Complete a Gundabad Mission with either Scout-master Ausma or Hórin","This feed is fresh and untouched","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
You should bring the gift to Igrit in Vérnozal.","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to the Zhélruka and to fight on their behalf in Gundabad.","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
You should search for the missing rope in Vérnozal.","These goat droppings are at least a day old","Show the gift to Néchek","Talk to Igrit","Scout-master Ausma and Hórin can both be found at Vérnozal in Máttugard.\
\
You should complete a Gundabad Mission with either Scout-master Ausma or Hórin.","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
You should search for signs of the goat at the stables in Vérnozal.","There should be a rope here to tie up the goat, but it is missing!"}},
[3181]={nameES="Chapter 5: Dhûrto",objectivesES={"The Haven tavern is on the south-east side of the Third Circle of the city.","Talk to Duinhir in King Elessar's throne room","This tavern was once a place of cheer, but now the mood is somber","Find the location where Duinhir believes he last saw his knife","Dúnor is in the Haven tavern.","You found a body and a knife hidden a short distance from the tavern. Is this another victim, or the murderer? Or is he both?","You have found another body! A knife lies at his side","Parthadan, the Warden of the Green, is outside the Dome of the Sun on the north-east side of the Sixth Circle.","Hasong is in King Elessar's throne room.","Talk to Dúnor outside the Dome of the Sun","Chapter 5: Dhûrto","Confront Parthadan outside the Dome of the Sun","Talk to folk near the spot Duinhir described","This Gondorian man was stabbed in the front, and it appears he struggled with his attacker","Duinhir is in King Elessar's throne room.","A Gondorian man seeks to get your attention on the parapet on the north side of the Fifth Circle.","Look for bloodstains outside the tavern and follow them","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to Elessar and the Kingdom of Gondor, and to fight on their behalf in Mordor.","It might be innocent, or the blood might have dripped from the murder weapon!","Bring the knife to Dúnor in the Haven tavern","A tavern-worker has begun to clean up some of the blood. Did he see anything?","Dúnor has come with you to apprehend Parthadan.","Enter the Haven tavern and talk to the guard in charge","Examine the discarded knife","Duinhir may have last seen his knife at the parapet on the north side of the Fifth Circle, but he does not really remember.","Talk to tavern-worker","King Elessar is in his throne room atop Minas Tirith.","Talk to Hasong in the throne room","Examine the second victim","Examine Mauthoi's body","Parthadan is a broken man","You examine the knife, and note a distinctive black circle on the hilt","The tavern-worker has scrubbed blood-stains near the door, but does the trail continue out of the tavern?","Mauthoi's body is on eastern side of the Haven tavern.","A cursory examination is enough to reveal the cause of Mauthoi's death. He was stabbed in the back by a short, bladed weapon, probably a knife or a dagger. It seems that his killer then carefully lowered him to the floor so as not to attract too much attention.\
\
The murderer must have taken the weapon with him, because there is no sign of it.","Several of the people in the Haven might have seen something when Mauthoi was murdered.","Talk to King Elessar in his throne room","Parthadan stares at you with haunted eyes. You have seen many unsettling things in your adventures, but this is among the worst.","This is the location Duinhir described to you"}},
[3182]={nameES="Capítulo 5: Tambores en las profundidades",objectivesES={"Ha llegado el momento de que los enanos se enfrenten a los orcos de Moria, pero Bósi y Brogur han perdido la esperanza de que puedan lograr la victoria bajo las montañas.","Has defendido el Camino Profundo de los ataques","Capítulo 5: Tambores en las profundidades","Stóthkell se encuentra en la Vía de los Herreros.\
\
Ahora que el Camino Profundo ha sido asegurado, deberías ofrecer tu ayuda a Stóthkell.","Has defendido la Vía de los Herreros de los ataques","Habla con Stóthkell y defiende la Vía de los Herreros","Habla con Bósi en la Cámara de la Encrucijada","Bósi se encuentra en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, en el extremo sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Has ayudado a repeler los ataques iniciales de los orcos en las barricadas de los enanos, y deberías informar de tu éxito a Bósi.","Habla con Brogur y defiende el Camino Profundo","Brogur se encuentra en el Camino Profundo.\
\
La supervivencia de los enanos de Moria ahora depende de la capacidad de ti y tus aliados para defender estos lugares de los ataques. Se te pidió que hablaras con Brogur primero.","Has defendido la Sala Vigesimoprimera de los ataques","Wíli se encuentra en la Sala Vigesimoprimera.\
\
Con el Camino Profundo y la Vía de los Herreros asegurados, deberías dirigirte a la Sala Vigesimoprimera y ayudar a Wíli a defenderla.","Habla con Wíli y defiende la Sala Vigesimoprimera"}},
[3183]={nameES="Chapter 5: Flight from Khazad-dûm",objectivesES={"Thorin III, King under the Mountain, is at his throne in Erebor.","Bósi is in the Hall under the Mountain. Khazad-dûm, and much of the Iron Garrison, is lost.","Chapter 5: Flight from Khazad-dûm","Talk to Bósi in the Hall under the Mountain","Talk to Foldgráf in the Hall under the Mountain and go with him to Khazad-dûm","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to Durin's Folk and fight on their behalf in Mordor.","Talk to King Thorin III at his throne in the Hall under the Mountain","Foldgráf is assembling a group to come to the aid of the Iron Garrison, in Khazad-dûm."}},
[3184]={nameES="Chapter 5: Forces at Work in Eregion",objectivesES={"Find the site of the attack on Fúsi and Fúni Gem-cutter","The tracks at the fallen pack lead east. It is in that direction that Fúni Gem-cutter must have been taken.\
\
You have learned in what direction the Ninkoth uruks have taken Fúni Gem-cutter and should follow the tracks.","A confusion of tracks surround the fallen pack and lead off to the east","Fúsi Gem-cutter's father Fúni was attacked somewhere east of Echad Eregion.\
\
Fúsi has asked you to find the site of the attack and determine where his father has been taken by the Ninkoth uruk.","Chapter 5: Forces at Work in Eregion","Talk to Radanir at Echad Eregion","Find information about the Ninkoth uruks east of the fallen pack","The ride of the Grey Company continues, with the Dúnedain travelling further south into Eregion.","Talk to Fúsi Gem-cutter at Echad Eregion","The next leg of the journey will take the Grey Company to Echad Eregion, and it is there that they will meet up with you again.","Fúsi Gem-cutter is at Echad Eregion.\
\
Radanir has asked you to speak with Fúsi Gem-cutter about his serious problem, a problem which has brought the Grey Company to a halt."}},
[3185]={nameES="Capítulo 5: Medio Enigma",objectivesES={"Lleva las páginas podridas a Brogur","Brogur está en la Cámara de Mando, subiendo las escaleras del este dentro de la Cámara de la Encrucijada.\
\
Bori te ha pedido que consultes con su tío Brogur sobre el Corazón de Fuego.","Capítulo 5: Medio Enigma","Has descubierto el secreto para abrir la puerta de Nâr-khelab, la forja donde se fabricó Zigilburk, pero aún no sabes la ubicación de la puerta."}},
[3186]={nameES="Capítulo 5: Manejar la situación",objectivesES={"Has ayudado a Bori con su tarea","Bósi se encuentra al oeste de las escaleras que conducen al lago fétido, que se extiende frente a la Puerta de Acebeda.\
\
Bósi está deseando hablar contigo ahora que se han reunido suficientes materiales para fabricar nuevos picos.","Capítulo 5: Manejar la situación","Las ramas gruesas se pueden encontrar en la base de los árboles en el área alrededor de la Puerta de Acebeda. Es probable que Bori esté hablando con su amigo Bróin en las escaleras al este de Bósi.\
\
Bósi te ha pedido que recolectes ramas gruesas con las que fabricar mangos de picos resistentes y que ayudes a su hijo Bori con la tarea de reunir piedras para afilar.","Ayuda a Bori con la tarea que le dio Bósi","Bósi te ha encargado la tarea de reunir los materiales necesarios para fabricar nuevos picos, para reemplazar las que han sido rotos por los enanos que trabajan en la Puerta de Acebeda.","Lleva ramas gruesas a Bósi"}},
[3187]={nameES="Capítulo 5: En el fuego",objectivesES={"Barras de hierro y listones de madera se pueden encontrar por las Profundidades Llameantes de Moria, donde los orcos de los Ghâsh-haï se preparan para la guerra.\
\
Brogur quiere que recolectes materiales que puedan usarse para hacer barricadas para defender la Sala Vigesimoprimera.","Lleva materiales para barricadas a Brogur","Brogur quiere que acoses a los orcos en las Profundidades Llameantes mientras reúnes materiales para construir barricadas para la defensa de la Sala Vigesimoprimera.","Capítulo 5: En el fuego","Acosar a los orcos de los Ghâsh-haï en las Profundidades Llameantes, al sur de Anazârmekhem.\
\
Brogur quiere que acoses a los orcos después de recoger los materiales que pueden usarse para hacer barricadas para defender la Sala Vigesimoprimera.","Brogur se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo, cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Has encontrado materiales para ayudar a construir barricadas efectivas y has hecho un gran número de víctimas entre los Ghâsh-haï."}},
[3188]={nameES="Capítulo 5: Mantenerse afilado",objectivesES={"Lleva piedras de Eregion afiladas a Bori","Bori se encuentra en la base de las escaleras que conducen al lago fétido frente a la Puerta de Acebeda. Se pueden encontrar piedras a lo largo del lecho seco del Sirannon, pero no todas las piedras son lo suficientemente afiladas.\
\
Bori está esperando que le traigas suficientes piedras para afilar los picos necesarios para los trabajadores que están desenterrando la Puerta de Acebeda.","Capítulo 5: Mantenerse afilado","Bori fue encargado de reunir piedras adecuadas para afilar los picos de los trabajadores de la Puerta de Acebeda.","Se pueden encontrar piedras a lo largo del lecho seco del Sirannon, pero no todas las piedras son lo suficientemente afiladas.\
\
Bori está esperando que le traigas suficientes piedras para afilar los picos necesarios para los trabajadores que están desenterrando la Puerta de Acebeda."}},
[3189]={nameES="Chapter 5: Loose Ends in the North Downs",objectivesES={"Daervunn is in Esteldín, the hidden Ranger-camp in the North Downs.\
\
Halbarad has sent you back to tell Daervunn to gather as many Rangers for the Grey Company as can be spared without jeopardizing the safety of the people of the North Downs.","Talk to Daervunn at Esteldín","Halbarad can be found near the entrance to Tham Úmdúr, in the North Downs.\
\
You have destroyed three of the idols prized by the Angmarim and should return now to Halbarad, as he asked.","Now that Halros has made his decision, it is time to gather more of the Dúnedain to join the ranks of the Grey Company on its mission.","Talk to Halbarad at Tham Úmdúr","Destroyed statue of Amarthiel","Destroy statue of Amarthiel","The Ranger Daervunn can be found in Esteldín, the hidden Ranger encampment in the North Downs.\
\
Halros has told you to next bring your message to Halbarad, but since the Ranger is often away seeing to the elimination of threats, you should speak first to his second-in-command, the Ranger Daervunn.","Destroy statue of Mordirith","Halbarad is in Tham Úmdúr, in the shadow of Ost Crithlanc, far to the east of Esteldín, in Nan Amlug East.\
\
Daervunn told you that Halbarad has gone to investigate a cave where foes fleeing from Carn Dûm following the defeat of the False King hope to create a new Angmar. If you are to enlist Halbarad's help as part of the Grey Company, you will need to travel to Tham Úmdúr.","Three stone idols of great significance to the Angmarim can be found throughout Tham Úmdúr.\
\
Halbarad has already destroyed three of the idols, but three remain, and he wants you to deal with them.","Destroy statue of the Witch-king","Destroyed statue of the Witch-king","Destroyed statue of Mordirith","Chapter 5: Loose Ends in the North Downs"}},
[3190]={nameES="Capítulo 5: Los Buscadores de Mazog",objectivesES={"Los Pûlpum atrapados por la corrupción de los Globsnaga se pueden encontrar por todas las Fundaciones de Piedra, pero especialmente en las cercanías del lago subterráneo en sus profundidades.\
\
Dithaliwenn quiere saber para qué ha enviado Mazog a tantos de sus Orcos a las Fundaciones de Piedra, ya que parece un movimiento poco característico. Quiere que derrotes a los Pûlpum Globsnaga y les arrebates cualquier orden que puedan seguir teniendo.","Dithaliwenn se encuentra en el campamento de Gwathrendath, el Refugio Sombrío en las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
Has recogido órdenes de los Pûlpum Globsnaga corrompidos y deberías llevarlas a Dithaliwenn en Gwathrendath.","Dithaliwenn quiere saber por qué Mazog ha enviado a sus Orcos a las cavernas de las Fundaciones de Piedra.","Lleva las órdenes de los Pûlpum a Dithaliwenn","Capítulo 5: Los Buscadores de Mazog"}},
[3191]={nameES="Chapter 5: News from Dunland",objectivesES={"The Brehur and Brehures can be found in the Brenin's Hall in Lhanuch.\
\
Glynn Brenin has asked you to speak with his advisors about the words of Anirin the messenger and about the events of his rescue.","Halbarad is among the huts on the western side of Lhanuch.\
\
You have spoken with the Brehur and Brehures of Lhanuch and should return to Halbarad with their words as Glynn Brenin wished.","Chapter 5: News from Dunland","Talk to Nona in Lhanuch","Nona is in the north-eastern corner of the Dunlending village of Lhanuch.\
\
Halbarad has remembered that you did not bring his refusal to Nona and wants you to tell her that he cannot allow her to travel with the Grey Company when they depart.","Talk to Halbarad in Lhanuch","The messenger from Dunland has given hope to Glynn Brenin that other Dunlending clans are standing against Saruman."}},
[3192]={nameES="Capítulo 5: Cadenas para Mazog",objectivesES={"Bróin está en la Senda Pacífica, ubicada junto al Camino de Durin.\
\
Has recogido las cadenas que se utilizarán para asegurar a Mazog durante el viaje a la Tierra Media y ahora deberías llevarlas a Bróin.","Capítulo 5: Cadenas para Mazog","Habla con Stóthkell en el Corazón de Fuego","Lleva las cadenas de mithril a Bróin, en la Senda Pacífica","Habla con Lenglammel en Gwathrendath","Bósi te ha enviado a recuperar las cadenas de mithril que se están fabricando en el Corazón de Fuego para contener a Mazog.","Stóthkell se encuentra en el Corazón de Fuego, junto a la Vía de los Herreros, entre las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata.\
\
Bósi te ha pedido que vayas al Corazón de Fuego para ver si las cadenas para Mazog han sido fabricadas.","Lenglammel se encuentra en Gwathrendath, el campamento de los Elfos en las profundidades de las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
Bróin te ha enviado a decirle a Lenglammel que los enanos no llevarán a Mazog a través de Lothlórien en su camino hacia el Bosque Negro, sino que rodearán el bosque. También quiere que expreses su descontento con este requisito."}},
[3193]={nameES="Capítulo 5: La fuente de la podredumbre",objectivesES={"Nimpheleg cree que es posible acabar con la corrupción de la podredumbre marchita dentro de Buzun-ghâr.","Habla con Nimpheleg","Nimpheleg está en Lossathrod, el campamento en las zonas altas de Buzun-ghâr.\
\
Has atraído y derrotado la fuente de la podredumbre dentro de Buzun-ghâr, un espíritu debilitado: Grawulun el Caerog.","Derrotaste a Grawulun el Caerog","Atrae y derrota la fuente de la podredumbre en Buzun-ghâr","Una piedra para colocar el berilo de Nimpheleg se encuentra en la zona más profunda de Buzun-ghâr.\
\
Nimpheleg cree que puedes atraer y derrotar la fuente de la podredumbre en Buzun-ghâr colocando un berilo sobre una piedra en las profundidades de la cueva. Te advirtió que permanecieras cerca del berilo una vez colocado, pues solo la piedra disminuirá la ferocidad del maestro de la podredumbre.","Capítulo 5: La fuente de la podredumbre"}},
[3194]={nameES="Capítulo 5: Tomados por la locura",objectivesES={"Una locura de mente y cuerpo ha afectado a los Orcos del mando de Mazog que han venido a las Fundaciones de Piedra.","Los Orcos del mando de Mazog, corrompidos por el mal enfermizo, se pueden encontrar por las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
Forglinn te ha pedido que derrotes a tantos Orcos corrompidos de Mazog, los Globsnaga, como puedas. Las criaturas parecen no tener mente, pero siguen siendo peligrosas.","Capítulo 5: Tomados por la locura","Forglinn se encuentra en Gwathrendath, el campamento de los Elfos entre las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
Has derrotado a muchos de los Orcos Globsnaga, y deberías volver ahora con Forglinn."}},
[3195]={nameES="Capítulo 5: La batalla del Camino Profundo",objectivesES={"Brogur se encuentra en el Camino Profundo.\
\
Has repelido el ataque de las hordas de orcos, ve a hablar con Brogur sobre la victoria.","Completa la escaramuza: La batalla del Camino Profundo","Defended el Camino Profundo frente a la embestida de los orcos, es el pasaje que conecta la Gran Excavación con las Obras Hidráulicas.","Capítulo 5: La batalla del Camino Profundo","Brogur se encuentra en el Camino Profundo.\
\
Una vez que hayas reunido a tus aliados, ve a hablar con Brogur. No tardarán en llegar los orcos."}},
[3196]={nameES="Capítulo 5: La batalla de la Sala Vigegimoprimera",objectivesES={"Capítulo 5: La batalla de la Sala Vigegimoprimera","Wíli se encuentra en la Sala Vigegimoprimera.\
\
Has defendido con éxito la Sala Vigegimoprimera del ataque de los orcos, y ahora debes hablar con Wíli.","La Sala Vigegimoprimera es un centro importante para la presencia de los enanos en Moria, y debe ser defendida a toda costa.","Wíli se encuentra en la Sala Vigegimoprimera.\
\
Ha llegado el momento de defender la Sala Vigegimoprimera del ataque de los orcos. Habla con Wíli para organizar la defensa.","Completa la escaramuza: La batalla de la Sala Vigegimoprimera"}},
[3197]={nameES="Capitulo 5: La batalla de Vía de los Herreros",objectivesES={"Completa la escaramuza: La batalla de Vía de los Herreros","Stóthkell se encuentra en el Corazón de Fuego.\
\
Has defendido el Corazón de Fuego del ataque de las hordas de Orcos, y ahora deberías hablar con Stóthkell.","Stóthkell se encuentra en el Corazón de Fuego.\
\
Deberías hablar con Stóthkell cuando hayas reunido a tus aliados y estés listo para defender la Vía de los Herreros.","La Vía de los Herreros, en la que se encuentra la entrada secreta del Corazón de Fuego, debe ser defendida contra los Orcos.","Capitulo 5: La batalla de Vía de los Herreros"}},
[3198]={nameES="Chapter 5: The Bitterest Victory",objectivesES={"Talk to King Thráin at Muru Azog","Before the gates of Khazad-dûm, crows pick at Azog's remains","King Thráin can be found at Muru Azog.\
\
You have driven back the Orcs at Muru Azog and found the remains of Azog being picked by crows. You should talk to King Thráin.","Talk to Hermáth Stormhammer at Amdân","Talk to King Thráin and aid in 'A Final Reckoning'","Investigate the gates of Khazad-dûm","Hermáth Stormhammer can be found at Amdân.\
\
You have witnessed the end of the Battle of Azanulbizar. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.","Nud-mekhem, the east-gate, can be found to the west of Muru Azog.\
\
Hoping to rout the last of the Orcs at Azanulbizar, King Thráin has asked you to investigate the gates of Khazad-dûm and defeat Orcs of the Ufúrzrak clan.","King Thráin can be found at Muru Azog.\
\
After the defeat of Azog, King Thráin appears intent on routing the remaining Orcs at Azanulbizar. You should talk to King Thráin.","Chapter 5: The Bitterest Victory","As you continue to read Hermáth Stormhammer's account of the Battle of Azanulbizar, you begin the fifth and final chapter in which the Dwarves of the Haban’akkâ of Thráin must reckon with the cost of victory over Azog."}},
[3199]={nameES="Capítulo 5: El Foso Oscuro",objectivesES={"Has ayudado a Dithaliwenn con su tarea.","Ayuda a Dithaliwenn con su tarea","Lenglammel se encuentra en el campamento de Gwathrendath, entre las Fundaciones de Piedra bajo Nud-melek.\
\
Has ayudado a los Elfos de su campamento y deberías hablar con ella de nuevo.","Ayuda a Forglinn con su tarea","Capítulo 5: El Foso Oscuro","Forglinn y Dithaliwenn se encuentran en el campamento de Gwathrendath, entre las Fundaciones de Piedra bajo Nud-melek.\
\
Lenglammel piensa que quizás descubrirás lo que el destino te depara si ayudas a los Elfos de su compañía a combatir las criaturas de la oscuridad.","Para salvar a los enanos de Moria, has venido a ayudar a los Elfos de Gwathrendath, enviados a Moria por orden de la Dama Galadriel.","Has ayudado a Forglinn con su tarea."}},
[3200]={nameES="Chapter 5: The Return",objectivesES={"You should talk to Glathlírel in the Court of Lothlórien.","You should ask Celeborn in the Court of Lothlórien about the ancient text.","Talk to Lord Celeborn","Chapter 5: The Return","Talk to Lady Galadriel","You should talk to Lady Galadriel in the Court of Lothlórien, and tell her all that happened in the Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu.","Learn the meaning of the ancient text you found and to where it led Glorfindel.","Go with Glathlírel to the Rift","Talk to Glathlírel","Go with Glathlírel and return to the Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu in search of Glorfindel."}},
[3201]={nameES="Capítulo 5: La podredumbre marchita",objectivesES={"Capítulo 5: La podredumbre marchita","Corunothiel está en Lossathrod, el campamento de Elfos y enanos en la cima de Buzun-ghâr.\
\
Has lidiado con la podredumbre marchita dentro de Buzun-ghâr y ahora deberías hablar con Corunothiel sobre tus éxitos.","Orvar Martillo de Campana está en Lossathrod, el campamento dentro del pasaje de Buzun-ghâr, ubicado fuera del Camino de Durin.\
\
Corunothiel dijo que un mensaje para ti fue entregado a Orvar mientras estabas en las profundidades de Buzun-ghâr, y deberías hablar con el enano para conocer su contenido.","Corunothiel y los otros Elfos de Lórien enviados para ayudar a la Guarnición de Hierro están preocupados por la podredumbre corrupta que se extiende en uno de los pasajes recién excavados.","Nimpheleg está en Lossathrod, el campamento dentro de Buzun-ghâr, ubicado fuera del Camino de Durin. Los orcos Globsnaga se encuentran por todo Buzun-ghâr.\
\
Como Orvar se ha negado a sellar el pasaje recién excavado, Corunothiel te ha pedido que trabajes con su amigo Nimpheleg para localizar y destruir la fuente de la podredumbre marchita dentro de Buzun-ghâr, y derrotar a los Globsnaga que han sido afectados o atraídos por la corrupción.","Ejecuta el plan de Nimpheleg para destruir la fuente de la podredumbre marchita","Ejecutaste el plan de Nimpheleg para destruir la fuente de la podredumbre marchita"}},
[3202]={nameES="Capítulo 5: Luces Traicioneras",objectivesES={"Otri Martillogrís está junto a la chimenea en la Posada Embrujada, entre los Troncosombríos.\
\
Has sacado a los hermanos Martillogrís de sus ensoñaciones y ahora deberías regresar con Otri.","Habla con Bróin en la bodega de la Posada Embrujada","Encuentra a Rósar Martillogrís y asegura su seguridad","Cúcheron te ha dado la desafortunada noticia de que la misión de la Guardia Oculta sigue estancada y que los enanos Martillogrís han causado otro retraso.","Bróin está en la bodega de la Posada Embrujada, en los Troncosombríos.\
\
Otri te ha pedido que le digas a Bróin que sus hermanos están a salvo y que verifiques si la Guardia Oculta ya ha decidido una ruta.","Habla con Otri Martillogrís en la Posada Embrujada","Rósar y Stígur Martillogrís están perdidos en algún lugar de los pantanos del Bosque Ahogado, al sur de los Troncosombríos.\
\
Otri Martillogrís está desesperado por que encuentres a sus hermanos, perdidos en los pantanos del Bosque Ahogado.","Al fijar la mirada en los ojos vidriosos del enano, te das cuenta de que no se trata de Rósar Martillogrís, sino de una imagen conjurada por los males del pantano. ¡No dejes que te engañe!","Al fijar la mirada en los ojos vidriosos del enano, te das cuenta de que no se trata de Stígur Martillogrís, sino de una imagen conjurada por los males del pantano. ¡No dejes que te engañe!","Capítulo 5: Luces Traicioneras","Encuentra a Stígur Martillogrís y asegura su seguridad"}},
[3203]={nameES="Capítulo 5: Palabras de precaución",objectivesES={"Bósi ha leído más del Libro de Mazarbul, y está preocupado por la prisa de Brogur.","Brogur se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Bósi está preocupado por lo que ha leído sobre el destino de Balin en el Libro de Mazarbul, y quiere que le adviertes a su primo que sea más cauteloso.","Capítulo 5: Palabras de precaución"}},
[3204]={nameES="Chapter 6.1: The Artist and the Apprentice",objectivesES={"Worried that he lacks the necessary training to successfully investigate Deepscrave, Eskil Bloodthumb has asked you to find a teacher at Maergrind willing to help him hone his skills.","Stáli the Hewer is at Maergrind, the Noble Gate.","Chapter 6.1: The Artist and the Apprentice","Eskil Bloodthumb stands at the entrance to Deepscrave, weaponless and ashamed of his clumsiness.","Eskil has dropped his axe, fumbling it while trying to show off his fighting form for you.","Talk to Eskil Bloodthumb at the entrance to Deepscrave","Pick up Eskil's fumbled axe","Eskil Bloodthumb is still at the entrance to Deepscrave, waiting for the news that you found him a teacher.","Observe Eskil's fighting form","Talk to Stáli the Hewer at Maergrind, the Noble Gate","Stáli the Hewer has charged his apprentice Eskil Bloodthumb with searching the caverns of Deepscrave for the Zabad'ibîn, the lost jewels of the Steepset.","Stáli the Hewer's assistant, Eskil Bloodthumb, stands at the entrance to Deepscrave.","Eskil fumbles his axe, which clatters clumsily to the ground","Give Eskil back his axe","Eskil Bloodthumb has asked you to observe his fighting style so you can give him pointers about his combat form.","Eskil Bloodthumb is at the entrance to Deepscrave from Máttugard, south-west of the Steepset.","Eskil reddens with embarrassment","Eskil Bloodthumb frowns nervously as you approach","Find a teacher at Maergrind willing to instruct Eskil Bloodthumb in the arts of combat and survival","Find Eskil Bloodthumb at the entrance to Deepscrave, south-west of the Steepset"}},
[3205]={nameES="Chapter 6.1: The Halls of the Elvenking",objectivesES={"This is King Thranduil's dining chamber, but there is no feast here today","Gondil smiles sadly, remembering days before she left Caras Tilion","Itheron apologizes for his sudden reticence, but he will say no more","You have come to Felegoth, the Halls of the Elvenking, and should make yourself known to Limlang, the guard at the entrance.","Felegoth, the Halls of the Elvenking, can be found in the north-eastern woods of Eryn Lasgalen.\
\
The steed near King Thranduil outside the ruins of Dol Guldur can take you to Eryn Lasgalen with utmost speed.","The air is cool and damp with mist in this river-channel","Talk to Gondil in the Room of Study, south-east of the throne room","You have found the entrance to the caverns of Felegoth, the Halls of the Elvenking","Talk to Herthír in the dining chamber east of the throne room","Journey to the entrance of Felegoth in the north-eastern reaches of Eryn Lasgalen","Chapter 6.1: The Halls of the Elvenking","Legolas invited you to visit the dining chamber, the Room of Study, and the water-way bridge in Felegoth, and to speak to the Elves you find at those locations.","Herthír smiles, anticipating the day the wood-elves will rule Eryn Lasgalen","Talk to Itheron on the river-bridge, east of the throne room","Thranduil the Elvenking has invited you to visit his halls in the northern reaches of Eryn Lasgalen, where he believes you may find news of Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior.","Talk to Legolas in the throne room of Felegoth","Legolas has come to his father's throne room in Felegoth.","Talk to Limlang at the entrance to Felegoth","This is the Room of Study, where scholars pore over the artifacts from Dol Guldur","King Thranduil is at his throne in the north-eastern chamber of Felegoth.","Legolas is in his father's throne room, in Felegoth.","Talk to King Thranduil at his throne in Felegoth"}},
[3206]={nameES="Chapter 6.1: The Road From Jax Phanâl",objectivesES={"Driftwood, standing nearby, calls for your attention","Retrieve Umbari Book of Romance","Retrieve Umbari Book of Flora","Bring the stolen books back to Jâkin in Jax Phanâl","Talk to Nauriel outside Jax Phanâl","The Haradrim that were pushed out of Jax Phanâl have a camp to the south where they keep the things they stole.","Retrieved Umbari Book of Romance","Jâkin is in the settlement of Jax Phanâl, on the Cape of Umbar.","Chapter 6.1: The Road From Jax Phanâl","The settlement of Jax Phanâl is to the east.","Driftwood has accompanied you to Jax Phanâl, on the Cape of Umbar.","You recovered the stolen books and should bring them back to Jâkin in Jax Phanâl.","You have made the crossing to the Cape of Umbar from the Shield Isles and should now turn your attention toward reaching Umbar Baharbêl.","Nauriel has made the crossing from the Shield Isles to the Cape of Umbar, and you should speak with her outside Jax Phanâl.","Talk to Jâkin in Jax Phanâl","Retrieve Umbari Book of History","Talk to Driftwood in Jax Phanâl","Retrieved Umbari Book of Flora","Retrieved Umbari Book of History","Jâkin eyes you warily as you approach","Enter the settlement of Jax Phanâl"}},
[3207]={nameES="Chapter 6.2: Pillar of the Mountain",objectivesES={"Bring the rusted dagger and dirty gem to Stáli the Hewer at Maergrind in Máttugard","Search debris at the upper extent of the Berg-beam","Stáli the Hewer is at Maergrind, the Noble Gate.","Stáli the Hewer is waiting for you to emerge from Deepscrave and bring him the fruits of your search. He is at Maergrind in Máttugard.","You search the fallen rubble but find nothing of value","This lower portion of the Berg-beam appears wide and sturdy","Beneath the pile of refuse you find a dirt-smeared and cloudy gem","Sign the contract or tell him <rgb=#00FF00>no</rgb>","Search debris at the lower extent of the Berg-beam","Durin asked you to examine the Berg-beam in Deepscrave for signs of weakness and to combat any Orcs you find there. While you are on the prince's business, you may as well keep your eyes open for the jewels sought by Stáli the Hewer.","Talk to Durin at Maergrind in Máttugard","Stáli the Hewer has presented you with a contract requiring you to assist him. It is your choice whether to sign the document or tell him <rgb=#00FF00>no</rgb>.","This middle portion of the Berg-beam still stands strong","Buried within the fallen debris you find an old and rusted dagger","Chapter 6.2: Pillar of the Mountain","Search debris near the midpoint of the Berg-beam","This upper portion of the Berg-beam appears sturdy enough","Durin is at Maergrind, the Noble Gate, in Máttugard.","You shake your head, and Stáli laughs off your refusal","Talk to Stáli the Hewer at Maergrind","Stáli the Hewer believes you convinced Eskil Bloodthumb not to search Deepscrave for the jewels of the Steepset, and he hopes that you will do so on behalf of his assistant.","You sign the contract and Stáli's grin widens"}},
[3208]={nameES="Chapter 6.2: Spies in the Forest",objectivesES={"Talk to Thranduil in his throne room in Felegoth","Thranduil is in his throne room in Felegoth.","Legolas is eager to help you track down the Orc spies that have been seen creeping throughout Eryn Lasgalen and to learn from them what evils they might be planning.","Find Gardelen and Dínellas south-east of Torech Emel, in Eryn Lasgalen","The hunter Dínellas motions quietly to you and Legolas, drawing you near","Show the letter for Karazgar to Legolas near Caras Tilion","You find a filthy parchment among the Orc's possessions","Search the Orc-spy slain by Dínellas","The Elf-scout Gardelen calls to Legolas warmly and waves to you","Legolas is near the ruins of the Elf-hall at Caras Tilion.","The Orc-spy slain by Dínellas can be found by his position near Caras Tilion.","Talk to Legolas near Caras Tilion","Legolas asked you to defeat foes within his old home of Caras Tilion while he considers the meaning of the letter you discovered.","Find Dínellas near Caras Tilion, in Eryn Lasgalen","Chapter 6.2: Spies in the Forest","Thranduil's scouts Gardelen and Dínellas patrol the wood south-east of Torech Emel.","Dínellas is near the ruins of the Elf-hall at Caras Tilion.","Dínellas followed a band of Orc-spies through Eryn Lasgalen. Gardelen believed the Orcs were bound for Caras Tilion, and you should seek the hunter Dínellas by the old Elf-hall there.","Show the letter for Karazgar to Dínellas near Caras Tilion","Foes of the Elves have been stirred up by the passage of Orcs through Eryn Lasgalen, and Gardelen has asked you to defeat them if you can."}},
[3209]={nameES="Chapter 6.2: Whispers In Rakhatâb",objectivesES={"Daxamat motions for you to come speak with him","Daxamat has arrived at your meeting spot south-east of Rakhatâb, and you should show him the evidence you retrieved from the coffer.","Daxamat stands by the crowd in Rakhatâb.","A guard has called for you to step away from the body, and glares at you with distrust.","You agreed to meet with your crew outside Rakhatâb on the south-eastern beach to examine the evidence you retrieved.","Daxamat arrives at the meeting spot. 'Jajax could only have done a little better!' he says","Show the evidence you recovered to Daxamat south-east of Rakhatâb","Examine the body of the victim","Talk to the woman in the crowd","Talk to the man in the crowd","You retrieve the contents of the coffer but should not examine them here","Sirgon is at your meeting spot outside Rakhatâb.","Talk to Daxamat outside Rakhatâb","The body of an aged man lies dead on the ground in Rakhatâb.","Chapter 6.2: Whispers In Rakhatâb","Rakhatâb is located on the southern promontory of the Cape of Umbar.","Talk to the guard in Rakhatâb","A crowd has gathered around someone lying on the ground","Nauriel is eager for you to continue along the coast road toward the City of the Corsairs. Your first stop will be at Rakhatâb along the southern promontory.","Search the evidence coffer outside the keep in Rakhatâb","Daxamat is outside Rakhatâb, waiting to hear what you learned from the Corsairs.","A crowd gathers around a body on the ground in Rakhatâb.","Sirgon waves you over","Before you can learn anything, the guards call for you to step back","Now you can investigate the evidence coffer while Dax distracts the guards","Talk to Sirgon outside Rakhatâb","Wait for Daxamat to run off","Daxamat runs off to distract the guards.","Travel south along the coast to Rakhatâb","Meet up with your crew on the beach to the south-east of Rakhatâb","Folk in the crowd believe one of the Corsairs from the camp to the north-east, up the coastline, may be responsible for the brazen murder in Rakhatâb.","The coffer containing evidence taken from the victim of the murder in Rakhatâb is outside the keep, to the south-east.","Talk to Daxamat by the crowd in Rakhatâb"}},
[3210]={nameES="Chapter 6.3: A Message From Cruel Dancer",objectivesES={"Talk to Caebar outside Rakhatâb","Find the woman Bôdo described atop the rocks north-east of Khûtra","Chapter 6.3: A Message From Cruel Dancer","The bounty-hunter Cruel Dancer may be seeking to eliminate her competition and claim the bounties on the Kindred of the Coins for herself, which endangers Driftwood and any who associate with him.","Bôdo told you a woman was looking for you, and could be found atop the rocks north-east of Khûtra.","Bôdo waits for you to return to him in the village of Khûtra.","Permanece alerta","Talk to the woman north-east of Khûtra","A woman has asked to speak with you atop the rocks north-east of Khûtra.","Talk to Driftwood outside Rakhatâb","You were asked to collect things that may help Khûtra survive the famine with which it has been gripped in recent days.","Caebar is at the meeting spot outside Rakhatâb.","Talk to Bôdo in Khûtra","The village of Khûtra is north-east of Rakhatâb along the coast road that runs to the City of the Corsairs.","Bring the driftwood and crab legs to Bôdo in the village of Khûtra","Travel to the village of Khûtra, north-east of Rakhatâb","You volunteer to do the work and he snorts noncommittedly","Cruel Dancer laughs again, and before you can follow her she is gone","The fisherman stares at you suspiciously, but says nothing","Bôdo is unsure what to make of your arrival to his village.","Driftwood is outside Rakhatâb.","The woman looks familiar to you, but you cannot determine why","Talk to Gimli north-east of the village of Khûtra","Gimli waits for you north-east of the village of Khûtra.","Cruel Dancer moves swiftly, and then she is gone."}},
[3211]={nameES="Chapter 6.3: Hidden in the Hoard",objectivesES={"Ugrukhôr seeks knowledge of the artifact Bugdatish from Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior, and Mithrandir has come to Felegoth seeking the same.","Thranduil is in his throne room in Felegoth.","Talk to Thranduil in his throne room in Felegoth","Return to Thranduil in the throne room of Felegoth","Mithrandir sees you approach and knits his eyebrows together with concern","King Thranduil eyes you carefully as you approach","Mithrandir asked you to inquire of Thranduil if the Bugdatish might have been part of Smaug's treasure-hoard.","Loeglond, the settlement of the Raft-elves, is in the Dale-lands along the river.\
\
Mithrandir suggested that you visit the Raft-elves on your way to Erebor, seeking news of Karazgar and the Bugdatish.","Find Mithrandir and the scholars of Felegoth in the Room of Study, south-east of the throne room","Mithrandir is in the throne room of Felegoth.","Talk to Mithrandir in the throne room of Felegoth","Travel to Loeglond and seek tidings of Karazgar or the Bugdatish","Talk to Nembadeth at Loeglond","Talk to Mithrandir in the Room of Study, south-east of the throne room","Chapter 6.3: Hidden in the Hoard","Mithrandir is meeting with the scholars of Felegoth in the Room of Study, south-east of the throne room."}},
[3212]={nameES="Chapter 6.3: Life on the Bridges",objectivesES={"Durin has asked you to search Durshulot in Deepscrave to learn what you can about Gorgar the Ruthless and his rule of the Orcs.","With a roar of anger, a ferocious Orc rushes to attack!","Durin is at Maergrind, the Noble Gate, in Máttugard.\
\
You have recovered a number of readable documents that may shed light on Gorgar's rule of the Orcs within Gundabad, and should bring them to Prince Durin for his study.","Recover a litany of complaints from Orcs guarding the north-eastern approach to Durshulot","Talk to Durin at Maergrind in Máttugard","Recover a record of the takeover from Orcs guarding the north-western approach to Durshulot","Trausti has suddenly arrived and called for your attention. What has happened?","Chapter 6.3: Life on the Bridges","Bring the readable pages you recovered from Deepscrave to Durin at Maergrind","Among the papers you find a diary containing goblin scribbles","Trausti arrives suddenly and calls for your attention","Search the mess of assorted papers at a camp-fire inside Durshulot","Durin is at Maergrind, the Noble Gate, in Máttugard.","Having searched Deepscrave on behalf of Stáli the Hewer, you should now continue to carry out your work for Prince Durin.","You found a record of the Frost-horde takeover","You found a litany of Orkish complaints","An enraged Orc bellows with fury and moves to attack!","Talk to Trausti at Maergrind in Máttugard"}},
[3213]={nameES="Chapter 6.4: Eskil Ensnared",objectivesES={"Trausti is in a ramshackle dwelling along the north-eastern wall of Deepscrave, searching for Eskil Bloodthumb.","You feel frightened eyes upon you","Trausti is on the north-western side of the Berg-beam in Deepscrave, near the site where Eskil Bloodthumb was left behind.","Trausti believes Eskil may have been brought through the Orc-village of Durshulot, perhaps to dwellings along the north-eastern wall of Deepscrave.","Let loose a mighty <rgb=#00FF00>roar</rgb>!","Trausti has returned from Deepscrave with sad tidings: he and Eskil Bloodthumb were attacked and the inexperienced warrior was left behind.","The site of the attack is north-west of Trausti's location. What clues might it hold for Eskil's fate?","The site of the attack is in Deepscrave, north-west of Trausti's location. What clues might it hold for Eskil's fate?","Talk to Trausti in a ramshackle dwelling along the north-eastern wall of Deepscrave","Talk to the frightened goblin","Talk to Trausti in the ramshackle dwelling on the north-eastern wall of Deepscrave","Search the site of the attack for clues to Eskil's fate","With a frightened squeak, a terrified goblin falls out of hiding","The site of the attack is to the north-west of Trausti's location.","Chapter 6.4: Eskil Ensnared","Trausti is in the ramshackle dwelling along the north-eastern wall of Deepscrave, musing over what you have learned.","The goblin is frightened!","Talk to Trausti at the Berg-beam in Deepscrave","Meet up with Trausti on the north-western side of the Berg-beam, in Deepscrave","Search for Eskil Bloodthumb north-east of Durshulot, among dwellings along the outer wall of Deepscrave","Trausti has urged you to meet him in Deepscrave on the north-western side of the Berg-beam, in sight of where he lost Eskil Bloodthumb.","Orc-blood? Perhaps Eskil managed to injure his attackers","Talk to Trausti on the north-western side of the Berg-beam, in Deepscrave","Trausti is on the north-western side of the Berg-beam, near the site where Eskil Bloodthumb was left behind.","This short length of cord was cut from a longer rope, but for what reason?","Trausti thinks someone is lurking in the ramshackle dwelling, and if you <rgb=#00FF00>roar</rgb> you may be able to frighten him from his hiding-place.","A frightened goblin cowers in the ramshackle dwelling. Does he know anything about Eskil's fate?","The frightened goblin makes good his escape!"}},
[3214]={nameES="Chapter 6.4: The Dragon's Bones",objectivesES={"Kólfith nods at you, a welcome change from the other townsfolk","Your journey to Erebor searching for news of the Bugdatish or Karazgar the Gúrzyul continues through Lake-town.","Authi, the dwarf you befriended in the Dragonbone Inn, is just to the north of the tavern.","The guards stare at you appraisingly","Talk to Authi Gem-cutter just north of the Dragonbone Inn","Kólfith is on the lower level of Lake-town, just above the water.","As before, the townsfolk fall silent and wait for you to move on","Ask around Lake-town for tidings of Karazgar","Várthrek told you to ask the townsfolk of Lake-town for tidings of Karazgar.","Travel to the entrance of Lake-town","Kólfith wants to meet you inside the Dragonbone Inn, in the northern section of Lake-town. He asked you to speak with Fasti outside the inn to arrange a safe meeting.","The townsfolk lower their voices and eye you warily","Habla con Várthrek en la entrada de la Ciudad del Lago","Talk to Kólfith on the lower level of Lake-town, just above the water","Talk to Fasti outside the Dragonbone Inn and meet with Kólfith in secret","Lake-town is to the north-east of Loeglond.\
\
Nembadeth sent you to speak with Várthrek, a guard at the entrance to Lake-town.","Chapter 6.4: The Dragon's Bones"}},
[3215]={nameES="Chapter 6.4: The Temple and the Tower",objectivesES={"Meet up with your crew further ahead, beside the road to Umbar Baharbêl","Travel south-west where you can have a view of the Calatirion's wreckage","Talk to Legolas in view of the wreckage of Calatirion","Atop its hill, the tower of Calatirion has tumbled into several pieces","Your crew plans to meet on the road to Umbar Baharbêl, and you should join them.","Daxamat stands by the road to Umbar Baharbêl with the rest of your crew.","Chapter 6.4: The Temple and the Tower","The Dead that linger near the ruined temple of Sauron to the east will endanger any who travel to the City of the Corsairs.","The wreckage of Calatirion on the hill of Kharn Arâx can be found to the south-west.","Sirgon has come as near to the ruined temple of Sauron as he wishes.","Legolas looks up at the wreckage of Calatirion, musing about what he has been told of its history.","The road to Umbar Baharbêl runs by two places of significance for the region: the temple of Sauron and the wreckage of Calatirion. Either may pose the threat of watchful guards.","Talk to Daxamat by the road to Umbar Baharbêl","Talk to Sirgon outside the ruined temple of Sauron"}},
[3216]={nameES="Chapter 6.5: Decline and Decay",objectivesES={"Travel to the Lonely Mountain, north of Dale, and meet with Authi","Authi Gem-cutter has shared some of his own problems with you and invited you to the Lonely Mountain where you may learn more about your own charge.","Habla con Dwalin","Talk to Gandalf in the Hall Under the Mountain","Talk to King Thorin III at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain","Chapter 6.5: Decline and Decay","Authi is not alone. Gandalf stands nearby, and beckons to you","A number of Thorin Oakenshield's surviving companions have come to Erebor","Gandalf has come to Erebor, and he stands outside the entrance to the Hall Under the Mountain.","Authi Gem-cutter invited you to go to Erebor to consult with King Thorin about the mysterious decline in the craft-skill of the dwarves. He said he would meet you at the Lonely Mountain.","Gandalf is in the Hall Under the Mountain near several dwarves of Thorin's Company who have come to Erebor.","Find the visitors Gandalf mentioned on the way to the throne in the Hall Under the Mountain","Habla con Glóin","Talk to Dori","Authi Gem-cutter invited you to go to Erebor to consult with King Thorin about the mysterious decline in the craft-skill of the dwarves. He asked you to defeat troublesome beasts on the way to the Lonely Mountain.","Talk to Gandalf at the Lonely Mountain","Gandalf hinted that some old friends could be found on the way to the throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.","King Thorin III is at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.","As Gandalf hinted, a number of Thorin Oakenshield's companions have come to Erebor. What has drawn them here?"}},
[3217]={nameES="Chapter 6.5: Eskil's Escape",objectivesES={"Talk to Trausti near the base of the Berg-beam","Talk to Eskil Bloodthumb at Maergrind in Máttugard","Talk to Trausti and attempt to rescue Eskil Bloodthumb","Trausti has suggested that you meet with him at the base of the Berg-beam, at the lowest level of Deepscrave.","Habla con Fastrith Halcomida en Maergrind, en Matugarde","Trausti stands here, surveying the dirt floor of Deepscrave as you approach","Trausti is near the base of the Berg-beam, ready to rescue Eskil Bloodthumb.","Chapter 6.5: Eskil's Escape","You have rescued Eskil Bloodthumb and returned him safely to Maergrind in Máttugard, where he waits to speak with you.","Eskil's sister Fastrith looks at you thoughtfully","Meet up with Trausti by the base of the Berg-beam","Eskil's sister Fastrith Hawkfeast has asked to speak to you.","Trausti is at the base of the Berg-beam, preparing for the rescue of Eskil Bloodthumb.","According to the frightened goblin you discovered, Eskil Bloodthumb may have been brought to Vatug-ronk, the Groaning Pit. Trausti is eager to rescue him without delay."}},
[3218]={nameES="Chapter 6.5: The City of the Corsairs",objectivesES={"You have arrived at Umbar Baharbêl, the City of the Corsairs","Talk to Caebar by the Beacon Gate","Everyone takes their leave and goes to enter the city separately","Complete 'The City: The Eyes of Nauriel'","The crew separates and prepares to enter the city by different paths.","Enter Umbar Baharbêl by the Beacon Gate, which leads to the Sail-haven","Caebar said he would meet you at one of the markets in the Sail-haven when you have learned what your crew discovered.","Talk to Caebar at a market in the Sail-haven","Chapter 6.5: The City of the Corsairs","Your crew has split up to search Umbar Baharbêl for information that will aid in the rescue of Thorongil and the completion of your mission.","Your mission nears its end. Thorongil and Corudan are sure to be held somewhere within Umbar Baharbêl, just down the coast road.","Complete 'The City: The Short Straw'","Complete 'The City: Elves, Dwarves, and Trouble'","Complete 'The City: Sirgon's Wound'","Caebar has entered Umbar Baharbêl by the Beacon Gate on the north-western side of the city.","You will enter the city by the Beacon Gate, which provides entrance to the north-western area of the city.","Wait for your crew to disperse","Complete 'The City: Sigileth's Curiosity'"}},
[3219]={nameES="Chapter 6.6: Lamps In the Night",objectivesES={"Caebar is in the Sail-haven.","Find the lamp nearest the crocodiles, on the rocks to the west","Examine another toppled lamp to the west along the rocks","Cruel Dancer waves you over to her","Cruel Dancer spoke of crocodiles outside the city, and Caebar believes she means the ones that can be found to the south-east.","The toppled lamp to the west of the crocodiles merits some examination.","A lamp lies overturned here upon the rocks","Talk to Caebar in the Sail-haven","Cruel Dancer spoke of lamps in the night, somewhere near the crocodiles.","Another lamp lies to the west.","Find the camp of crocodiles to the south-east of the city","Before this lamp was overturned, it may have guided ships along the river","Caebar has had a close encounter with Cruel Dancer, but did not realize it at the time. What has the dangerous bounty-hunter discovered that may be of use to you?","You feel eyes upon you. Someone watches from the west","Caebar handed you the note he discovered in his pocket, and you should read it.","Cruel Dancer is west of the line of lamps, standing upon the rocks overlooking the river.","Confront the person watching you to the west of the line of lamps","Someone watches you from the rocks to the west of the line of lamps.","Now where are these broken lamps?","Talk to Cruel Dancer by the coil of rope","Read the note Caebar discovered on his person","Examine the toppled lamp","Chapter 6.6: Lamps In the Night"}},
[3220]={nameES="Chapter 6.6: The Fine Print",objectivesES={"Your search proves fruitless, revealing no sign of Eskil's contract","Habla con Fastrith Halcomida en Zarkul-sulûn","Talk to Eskil Bloodthumb in Zarkul-sulûn","This chest contains many papers, but none bearing Eskil's name","You find no sign of Eskil's contract","Section the Third: Ending the Agreement\
==========================\
This agreement shall be binding for each of the listed parties, Apprentice and Sculptor alike, and it shall continue in effect until such time as Sculptor delivers to Dáin II, King Under the Mountain, a signed parchment containing the desire of both parties to terminate it. Without such a delivery, this agreement will continue in perpetuity.\
\
May it be a fruitful and satisfactory apprenticeship for both parties!\
\
Witnessed on this day the Third of October,\
in the Year 3018,\
with seals affixed,\
in the Hall Under the Mountain,\
by Dáin II Ironfoot,\
King Under the Mountain","Fastrith coughs politely","Stáli the Hewer arrives, a shrewd look on his face. Fastrith and Eskil follow at a distance","Examine Eskil's contract","Talk to Stáli the Hewer upstairs in Zarkul-sulûn","Bueno...","Chapter 6.6: The Fine Print","Section the First: Duties of the Apprentice\
===========================\
The duties of the Apprentice shall not be limited in any way by the omission of any particular duty in this section, but shall be deemed to include any such reasonable responsibilities that shall be suggested by the Sculptor. The meaning of \\qreasonable\\q for this section, and for any following section, shall be interpreted as \\qthe course most likely to be favoured by the will of Dáin II, King Under the Mountain.\\q\
\
The duties of the Apprentice shall include, but be not limited to, the following responsibilities:\
\
One (1): Acquisition of materials for the creation of any works of art required by the Sculptor, purchased with supplied coin. Any excess coinage is to be returned promptly and without fail. Upon discovery of such a failure, the excess will be tallied and deducted from the Apprentice's weekly stipend (see Section the Second).\
\
Two (2): Thorough weekly cleaning of workshop space in order to foster creative work on the part of the Sculptor. Any spots missed in the cleaning shall be tallied and a percentage deducted from the Apprentice's weekly stipend (see Section the Second).\
\
Three (3): Timely preparation of meals for the Sculptor, no earlier than eight in the morning for breakfast and no later than six of the clock for dinner; drinks to be made upon request. The Sculptor does not like berries of any kind on his plate, but he is partial to honey and any products made from it, such as mead. The appearance of berries anywhere near the Sculptor's table will be noted, and a deduction made from the Apprentice's weekly stipend (see Section the Second).\
\
Four (4): Praise to be made for the Sculptor's work (when appropriate). Private criticism of such work will be noted, and a deduction made from the Apprentice's weekly stipend (see Section the Second). Public criticism will be noted twice, and count double.\
\
Five (5): In the event of illness or maiming that causes the Apprentice to be unable to carry out his duties, be they daily or weekly in nature, he is to provide a substitute for the day or week in question. If the substitute is found lacking, such deficiency will be noted and a deduction made from the Apprentice's weekly stipend (see Section the Second). Similarly, if the Apprentice is deemed to be contagious and refuses to nominate a substitute, that will also be grounds for a deduction from his weekly stipend.\
\
Six (6): Greeting guests of the Sculptor and assessing who is to be admitted and who is deemed unwelcome. The Sculptor's time is valuable and not to be wasted! Special consideration is to be given to those who bring gifts for the Sculptor, especially mead. The discovery that mead might have been given as a gift should the guest have been informed beforehand by the Apprentice will be met with disappointment, which is worse than anger. Disappointment in this case will take the form of a deduction from the Apprentice's weekly stipend (see Section the Second).","Hmmm....","Stáli brandishes the contract with a flourish","Hmmm?","Stáli the Hewer has returned to Zarkul-sulûn.","Eskil Bloodthumb stands on the upper level of Zarkul-sulûn, looking resigned to his fate.","Talk to Durin on the lower level of Zarkul-sulûn","Fastrith Hawkfeast stands on the upper level of Zarkul-sulûn, seeking to gain your attention.","You hear footsteps approaching.","Section the Second: Duties of the Sculptor\
===========================\
The duties of the Sculptor shall only include responsibilities here listed. This is their full extent:\
\
One (1): The Sculptor shall provide a weekly stipend of coin to the Apprentice, modified as described above in Section the First.\
\
Two (2): The Sculptor shall provide instruction in the art of sculpting and the preparation of fine artwork (as time allows and at the Sculptor's inclination, informed by whether the Apprentice displays a natural propensity for the subject. This propensity is to be assessed by the Sculptor and by no other, save the King Under the Mountain, should the Apprentice choose to frivolously spend the king's time in this manner).","Stáli the Hewer is on the upper level of Zarkul-sulûn.","Stáli the Hewer has returned to Zarkul-sulûn, and he holds Eskil's contract out for your study.","Fastrith Hawkfeast is interested in finding some way to free her brother Eskil Bloodthumb from his apprenticeship to Stáli the Hewer.","Well...?","Talk to Stáli the Hewer in Zarkul-sulûn","Prince Durin is on the lower level of Zarkul-sulûn.","Search Stáli's luggage for Eskil Bloodthumb's contract","With that settled, you should speak with Durin downstairs before returning to Gundabad","Stáli the Hewer's luggage can be found upstairs in Zarkul-sulûn.","You hear footsteps approaching","Preamble and Naming of the Parties\
========================\
Let it be known to all in the Lonely Mountain and its environs, and to every inhabitant of dwarfdom throughout this Middle-earth, that on this the third day of October, Dáin II Ironfoot, King Under the Mountain, did recognize and witness this agreement between two parties come before him.\
\
The parties are named as follows, with due identification presented and accepted in the sight of King Dáin. Party the first: Stáli the Hewer, noted sculptor and artist of great renown, resident of Tumnu-dûm, the dwelling-halls, known herein as the Sculptor. Party the second: Eskil Bloodthumb, noteworthy accomplishments asked for by the first party but none were offered by the second and are therefore omitted; also a resident of Tumnu-dûm, the dwelling-halls, known herein as the Apprentice.\
\
As a matter of course, the King Under The Mountain expressed his opinion that the parties enter into this agreement of apprenticeship of their own free wills, and that no undue influence was exercised upon either party."}},
[3221]={nameES="Chapter 6.6: The Keeper of Raven-hill",objectivesES={"You volunteered to bring water from the well at the base of Raven-hill to Dís.","You offered to clear the brush and stones from the path up Raven-hill for Dís.","Talk to Gandalf by the throne in the Hall Under the Mountain","Pick up the bucket of water at the base of Raven-hill","The King Under the Mountain has agreed to your request to open the tomb of Thorin Oakenshield and ensure the Arkenstone remains within, but he wants you to first obtain permission from Thorin's sister Dís.","Dís is at Raven-hill, south-west of the Lonely Mountain.","Gandalf wishes to speak with you by the throne of King Thorin III, in the Hall Under the Mountain.","Find Dís, the sister of Thorin Oakenshield, at Raven-hill","Chapter 6.6: The Keeper of Raven-hill","Dís, the sister of Thorin Oakenshield, is at Raven-hill.","You volunteered to defeat foes in the vicinity of Dale for Dís.","Talk to Dís at Raven-hill","You set down the bucket of water as more dwarves come up the hill","This must be Dís, the elderly sister of Thorin Oakenshield"}},
[3222]={nameES="Chapter 6.7: Lair of the Beast",objectivesES={"Use the coil of rope and climb down to the secret grotto","Despite your misgivings, you know that this may be your best chance to reach the Kindred's prisoners undetected. You resolve to remain alert in case Cruel Dancer attempts any treacherous action.","You rescued one prisoner from the Kindred of the Coins, and your friends now recover at the amphitheatre east of the city.","Chapter 6.7: Lair of the Beast","The coil of rope by Cruel Dancer will allow you to reach the lair Cruel Dancer discovered.","Talk to Corudan at the amphitheatre east of the city","Cruel Dancer has located the grotto where two members of the Kindred of the Coins seem to harbour their ships: Tatháta the Sea-beast and Nakási Wave-reaper."}},
[3223]={nameES="Chapter 6.7: Wood, Lake, Mountain, and Stone",objectivesES={"Talk to King Thorin III at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain","Talk to Gandalf by the throne in the Hall Under the Mountain","Chapter 6.7: Wood, Lake, Mountain, and Stone","Gandalf is by the throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.","Gandalf is at Raven-hill, waiting to travel with you and the surviving members of Thorin's Company to ensure the Arkenstone remains entombed with the Oakenshield.","King Thorin III is at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.","Dís has given her permission to the dwarves of Thorin's Company to investigate his tomb and learn if the Arkenstone remains within.","Talk to Gandalf at Raven-hill and travel to Mazal Akrâz"}},
[3224]={nameES="Chapter 6.8: One Prisoner Rescued",objectivesES={"Driftwood greets Corudan warmly.","Driftwood steps forward, a smile upon his face","You have rescued a friend from the Kindred of the Coins. Has the experience changed him, or have those he left behind changed in his stead?","Sigileth is at the amphitheatre east of the city.","The silence extends, awkwardly and overlong","Corudan looks at you carefully.","Corudan laughs. 'I am ready for more, my sister. The Kindred is not ready for us.'","Corudan looks around eagerly.","Talk to Driftwood at the amphitheatre east of the city","Chapter 6.8: One Prisoner Rescued","Talk to Sigileth at the amphitheatre east of the city","Talk to Corudan at the amphitheatre east of the city","An awkward silence fills the air","Driftwood remains silent.","Wait for Driftwood to arrive","Corudan is pleased to see his friends again."}},
[3225]={nameES="Chapter 6.8: One Prisoner Rescued",objectivesES={"Corudan laughs. 'I am ready for more, my sister. The Kindred is not ready for us.'","Corudan waits for you to speak.","Think about what to tell Corudan","You have rescued a friend from the Kindred of the Coins. Has the experience changed him, or have those he left behind changed in his stead?","Chapter 6.8: One Prisoner Rescued","How should you tell Corudan about some of the mournful events that transpired?","Sigileth is at the amphitheatre east of the city.","Corudan is eager to hear what befell his friends... but you do not know how to tell him some of the mournful things that transpired.","Talk to Sigileth at the amphitheatre east of the city","Talk to Corudan at the amphitheatre east of the city"}},
[3226]={nameES="Chapter 6: A Mortal Gift",objectivesES={"Arwen has asked you to walk with her in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell. If you get separated, ring the bell.\
\
Talk to Arwen by the statue.","A distant look comes across Arwen's face","Deliver the gift to Arwen in Imlad Gelair","The world opens out before you, a breeze rustling the leaves of the trees","Arwen has asked you to walk with her in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell. If you get separated, ring the bell.\
\
Talk to Arwen upon the second bridge.","The air is sweet and clear, this Elven retreat fine to behold","You should ask Lady Galadriel in the Court of Lothlórien for Arwen's gift.","Ask Galadriel for the gift","Walk with Arwen to the left statue","Arwen has asked you to walk with her in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell. If you get separated, ring the bell.\
\
Go with Arwen onto the second bridge.","Arwen has asked you to walk with her in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell. If you get separated, ring the bell.\
\
Go with Arwen to the left past the bridge, where the statue stands.","Gift in hand, it is time to visit Arwen in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell, once more.","Arwen has asked you to walk with her in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell. If you get separated, ring the bell.\
\
Talk to Arwen under the trees before the second bridge.","Talk to Arwen","Chapter 6: A Mortal Gift","Arwen has asked you to walk with her in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell. If you get separated, ring the bell.\
\
Talk to Arwen upon the bridge.","Arwen has asked you to walk with her in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell. If you get separated, ring the bell.\
\
Go with Arwen to the bridge ahead.","Walk with Arwen a little further","Walk with Arwen some more","Walk with Arwen to the bridge","Arwen looks up at the statue and you are struck by a strong resemblance","Arwen has asked you to walk with her in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell. If you get separated, ring the bell.\
\
Go with Arwen farther down the path, through the narrow pass.","Accept the honour of delivering Glorfindel's betrothal gift to Arwen."}},
[3227]={nameES="Capítulo 6: Armas de la Mordedura Más Afilada",objectivesES={"Bori se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Has reunido muchas piezas del equipo que te ha pedido Bori, y ahora deberías llevárselas.","Bori quiere que recolectes armaduras, armas y escudos que puedan ser reparados o fundidos para equipar a los enanos que ejecutan su audaz plan.","Armaduras abolladas, hojas rotas y escudos agrietados se pueden encontrar en los orcos y dentro de sus campamentos por todo Zelem-melek y las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo.\
\
Bori necesita equipar a los dos equipos que ejecutarán su ataque a Stazgnâkh, y quiere que reúnas los materiales que le permitirán hacer esto.","Lleva armaduras, armas y escudos a Bori","Capítulo 6: Armas de la Mordedura Más Afilada"}},
[3228]={nameES="Capítulo 6: Las sospechas de Bori",objectivesES={"Capítulo 6: Las sospechas de Bori","Bori sospecha que ha dado con algo que permitirá a los enanos darle la vuelta a los amenazantes orcos de Moria.","Bori se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo junto a la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Has explorado las Obras Hidráulicas para encontrar las armerías que buscaba el enano Óin, como se explica en el Libro de Mazarbul. Deberías volver ahora con Bori.","En las Obras Hidráulicas se pueden encontrar criaturas acuáticas peligrosas.\
\
Bori te ha pedido que derrotes a las criaturas que se encuentran entre las ruinas de las Obras Hidráulicas.","Las placas de las habitaciones se pueden encontrar por todas las Obras Hidráulicas, al igual que criaturas acuáticas peligrosas.\
\
Bori te ha pedido que memorices la ubicación de las placas en varias habitaciones diferentes de las Obras Hidráulicas.","Bori se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo junto a la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Brogur te ha dicho que su sobrino Bori quiere hablar contigo sobre algo."}},
[3229]={nameES="Capítulo 6: El primo Brogur",objectivesES={"Capítulo 6: El primo Brogur","Bósi te agradeció tu parte en la recolección de materiales para la fabricación de nuevas piochas, y te envió a Brogur para que puedas prestar tu ayuda a su primo.","El primo de Bósi, Brogur, se encuentra en algún lugar a lo largo del camino que sube a la Puerta de Acebeda, al norte de la posición de Bósi.\
\
Bósi te ha pedido que prestes tu ayuda a su primo Brogur mientras se fabrican las piochas."}},
[3230]={nameES="Capítulo 6: Enanos de gran valor",objectivesES={"Bori necesita que reclutes a algunos enanos para llenar las filas de los dos grupos necesarios para su plan: el grupo de distracción y el grupo de ataque.","La Sala Vigesimoprimera en Zelem-melek está llena de enanos que Bori quiere reclutar para su audaz misión contra la Mano Blanca.\
\
Bori necesita reclutar enanos para completar los dos grupos necesarios: una fuerza de distracción y un grupo de ataque principal.","Capítulo 6: Enanos de gran valor","Bori se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Has intentado reclutar a algunos enanos para el audaz plan de Bori contra la Mano Blanca, pero muy pocos se han ofrecido como voluntarios."}},
[3231]={nameES="Capítulo 6: Maldades bajo el mundo",objectivesES={"Lenglammel se encuentra en el campamento de Gwathrendath, entre las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
Has hecho lo que has podido para contrarrestar la amenaza de las criaturas Sinnombre que acechan entre los Fundaciones de piedra.","Se pueden encontrar grietas en el abismo por todas partes en las Fundaciones de Piedra, no muy lejos de Gwathrendath. \
\
Lenglammel te ha pedido que coloques Piedras élficas frente a las grietas del abismo cerca del campamento para disuadir a las criaturas Sinnombre de acercarse.","Lenglammel está preocupada de que las criaturas Sinnombre buscadas por Mazog se estén acercando demasiado a su campamento.","Capítulo 6: Maldades bajo el mundo"}},
[3232]={nameES="Chapter 6: Farewell to Evendim",objectivesES={"Talk to Calenglad at Tinnudir","Daervunn has sent you to bring word of the Grey Company's mission to Calenglad and the Rangers of Evendim.","Calenglad is at Tinnudir, the Ranger-camp on the shores of Lake Evendim.\
\
Calenglad is waiting to speak with you about taking one more journey into Annúminas to rescue some relics from the Angmarim and tomb-robbers that seek to plunder them.","Chapter 6: Farewell to Evendim","Calenglad is at Tinnudir, the Ranger-camp on the shores of Lake Evendim.\
\
You have done as Calenglad asked, and in his own way, he has bade farewell to the lands of Evendim. He is ready now to travel with the Grey Company, and you should speak with him.","Talk to Calenglad and travel with him to the Flooded Ward","Calenglad is at Tinnudir, the Ranger-camp on the shores of Lake Evendim.\
\
Daervunn has sent you to enlist the aid of Calenglad and the Rangers of Evendim for the Grey Company."}},
[3233]={nameES="Chapter 6: For Wadu",objectivesES={"Radanir is at the camp-site of the Grey Company in a grove of trees to the east of the Uch-lûth village of Lhanuch.\
\
Suvulch told you that Radanir was looking for you about an urgent matter.","Suvulch is by Wadu's favourite tree, on a rise by ox-pens west of Lhanuch, and hostile Dunlendings can be found throughout Enedwaith.\
\
Suvulch has challenged you to a competition to slay hostile Dunlendings in memory of Wadu.","Hostile Dunlendings can be found throughout Enedwaith.\
\
Suvulch has challenged you to a competition to see who can defeat the most Dunlendings of enemy clans in honour of Wadu.","Find Suvulch somewhere near Lhanuch","You last saw Suvulch at Wadu's favourite tree, on a rise by the ox-pens, west of Lhanuch.\
\
Nona is angry at her father Suvulch for his cruel treatment of Wadu while Wadu was still alive, and she wants you to tell Suvulch so.","Defeat hostile Dunlendings throughout Enedwaith, and return to Suvulch when you are satisfied","Talk to Suvulch","Nona is not pleased that Halbarad has refused her request to travel south with the Grey Company and is also angry with her father Suvulch.","Read the letter on the crate by Radanir","A second letter from Ergothorn is on the crate near Radanir, at the camp-site of the Grey Company in the grove of trees east of Lhanuch.\
\
Radanir has found a second letter from Ergothorn and wants you to read it and give your opinion on what the mysterious correspondent has to say.","Talk to Radanir at the grove of trees east of Lhanuch","Defeat hostile Dunlendings throughout Enedwaith","To the Rangers:\
\
I do not have much time to write this; I beg you to move with all possible haste. A group of uruks have come out of Dunland, but instead of passing further north as others have done, these have begun the climb into Thrór's Coomb. I fear they have orders involving the dwarves that still live there, especially the one called Nár.\
\
You must defend this dwarf from the uruks! He knows much that, told to the wrong person, could be hurtful to your errand.\
\
Ergothorn","Chapter 6: For Wadu","Defeated a hostile Dunlending warrior","Find Radanir at the grove of trees east of Lhanuch","Radanir is at the camp-site of the Grey Company in the grove of trees east of Lhanuch.\
\
You have read Ergothorn's second letter, which calls for you to go to the defence of Zudrugund."}},
[3234]={nameES="Chapter 6: Fúni Gem-cutter",objectivesES={"Chapter 6: Fúni Gem-cutter","Fúni Gem-cutter has been taken to the abandoned ruins of Minas Elendúr by the Ninkoth uruks.","Fúni Gem-cutter is being held somewhere within the depths of Minas Elendúr, far to the east of Echad Eregion.\
\
You have learned the location of Fúni Gem-cutter and should now attempt his rescue.","The floor is stained with blood. Will this lead to Fúni Gem-cutter?","Find Fúni Gem-cutter somewhere within Minas Elendúr"}},
[3235]={nameES="Capítulo 6: Trasgos en las galerías occidentales",objectivesES={"Lleva los mapas rudimentarios a Bósi","Capítulo 6: Trasgos en las galerías occidentales","Lleva los mapas rudimentarios a Brogur","Brogur se encuentra en la Cámara de Mando, subiendo las escaleras del este en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, ubicada en la entrada sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Has matado a muchos trasgos y recogido sus mapas mientras buscabas el Corazón de Fuego.","Bósi se encuentra en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, justo afuera de la Cámara de Mando.\
\
Brogur no ha visto nada útil en los mapas rudimentarios de los trasgos que encontraste, pero su primo Bósi podría tener más suerte interpretándolos.","Brogur duda de que el Corazón de Fuego exista, y quiere que al menos hagas algo con el problema de los trasgos mientras lo buscas.","Se pueden encontrar trasgos en las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata, al sur y debajo de la Gran Excavación, y sus mapas se pueden encontrar dentro de Gamil Filik, la mina que han ocupado.\
\
Brogur te pidió que mataras trasgos mientras buscas el Corazón de Fuego, y que estuvieras atento a sus mapas; es posible que hayan descubierto la forja y la hayan incluido en sus mapas rudimentarios."}},
[3236]={nameES="Capítulo 6: Talladores de piedra",objectivesES={"Las Cámaras de Sabiduría, Conocimiento y Reflexión Profunda se encuentran en toda la Gran Excavación, al igual que Katûb-zahar. Cualquiera de estos lugares puede tener los registros mineros que Bróin debía encontrar.\
\
Bróin está insatisfecho con las tareas sin sentido que su padre Brogur le ha asignado, y está extremadamente frustrado de que los enanos hagan este tipo de trabajo mientras Bori sigue prisionero de las fuerzas de Mazog.","Estas estanterías no contienen ningún registro minero.","Bróin está descansando en la Senda Pacífica, ubicada en la Sala de Reunión Militar, al este de Sulnul-dûm y al oeste del Salón de Piedra, en el Camino de Durin. La entrada a la Senda Pacífica está al noreste de Buzun-ghâr.\
\
Bróin ha enviado aviso de que desea hablar contigo de nuevo. Orvar te dijo que trataras a Bróin con amabilidad, creyendo que sus pruebas en la guarida acuática del Vigilante y la pérdida de su primo ante las fuerzas de Mazog pueden haberlo afectado profundamente.","Bróin está en la Senda Pacífica, ubicada en la Sala de Reunión Militar, al este de Sulnul-dûm y al oeste del Salón de Piedra, en el Camino de Durin. La entrada a la Senda Pacífica está al noreste de Buzun-ghâr.\
\
Has recuperado algunos de los registros mineros que el padre de Bróin quería que encontrara, pero incluyen detalles curiosos que interesarán mucho a Bróin.","Capítulo 6: Talladores de piedra","Lleva los registros mineros a Bróin","Has encontrado registros mineros, pero contienen información curiosa.","Este cofre no contiene ningún registro minero.","Bróin no está seguro de qué hacer y quiere que le ayudes a encontrar alguna forma de ayudar a Bori, capturado por las fuerzas de Mazog.","Busca registros mineros para Bróin"}},
[3237]={nameES="Capítulo 6: Honor suficiente para ambos",objectivesES={"Brogur te ha dicho que su sobrino Bori ha propuesto un plan audaz, que podría acelerar la reconquista de Khazad-dûm por los enanos.","Bori se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo, cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Has ayudado a Bori a prepararse para su audaz ataque contra la Mano Blanca, y ahora deberías informarle.","Capítulo 6: Honor suficiente para ambos","Bori se encuentra con Brogur en la Cámara de Liderazgo, cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Brogur te ha dicho que su sobrino Bori ha ideado un plan audaz para dar un golpe a los Orcos de la Mano Blanca en Moria, y quiere que le ayudes con sus preparativos."}},
[3238]={nameES="Capítulo 6: Planificando el ataque más sabio",objectivesES={"Bori se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Has evaluado la fuerza de la fuerza en el cruce vigilado a lo largo de la Carretera Oriental y has encontrado dos entradas a Stazgnâkh, el campamento de la Mano Blanca entre las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo.","Encuentra el cruce vigilado en la Carretera Oriental","El cruce vigilado en la Carretera Oriental se encuentra en Nud-melek, y el campamento de la Mano Blanca de Stazgnâkh está ubicado entre las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo.\
\
Bori te ha pedido que investigues el cruce vigilado a lo largo de la Carretera Oriental, y que recolectes barriles de pólvora negra del campamento de la Mano Blanca de Stazgnâkh para que te familiarices con él.","Capítulo 6: Planificando el ataque más sabio","El plan de Bori llama a un ataque de distracción en la Carretera Oriental para atraer a la fuerza principal de los Orcos de la Mano Blanca fuera de Stazgnâkh para que otro grupo de enanos pueda eliminar al líder.","Lleva los barriles de pólvora negra a Bori","Has evaluado la fuerza de la fuerza en el cruce vigilado"}},
[3239]={nameES="Chapter 6: Return of the Noble Hall",objectivesES={"Talk to Prince Ingór","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
You should place the crystals that you mined in the crystal planters scattered throughout Vérnozal.","Chapter 6: Return of the Noble Hall","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
You should decorate Vérnozal with Zhélruka runners for Prince Ingór.","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to the Zhélruka and to fight on their behalf in Gundabad.","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you."}},
[3240]={nameES="Capítulo 6: Regreso a Azanarukâr",objectivesES={"Habla con Lenglammel para viajar a Azanarukâr","Lenglammel se encuentra en Gwathrendath, el campamento élfico entre las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
Has destruido la reliquia de Gorothúl y enviado a Gwathnor y Grawulun sin forma a las profundidades, por un tiempo. Ahora deberías informar a Lenglammel.","Habla con Lenglammel en Gwathrendath","Habla con Haldir en Talan Haldir","Lenglammel se encuentra en Gwathrendath, el campamento élfico entre las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
Lenglammel está esperando para hablar contigo y llevarte a Magor para un asalto a Azanarukâr.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: La inspiración te ayudará si decides emprender este desafío. Esta instancia solo puede ser completada por un grupo de uno o dos jugadores.</rgb>","Lenglammel te dijo que otra de las reliquias de Gorothúl ha sido encontrada en las profundidades de Azanarukâr y debe ser destruida.","Haldir se encuentra en Talan Haldir, justo fuera de la frontera del Bosque de Oro.\
\
Lenglammel te ha enviado a Haldir para transmitirle un mensaje importante: la expedición de la Hueste Dorada debe llevarse a cabo lo antes posible.","Capítulo 6: Regreso a Azanarukâr"}},
[3241]={nameES="Capítulo 6: Reconocimiento de Emyn Lûm",objectivesES={"Habla con Enedhel en Ost Galadh","Enedhel está en Ost Galadh, en Emyn Lûm.\
\
Te has escondido detrás de las piedras erguidas en el camino hacia Minas Gîl, al este de Ost Galadh, y ahora deberías regresar a Enedhel con lo que has aprendido.","El camino al este de Ost Galadh es la ruta más directa hacia la fortaleza de Dol Guldur.","Se pueden encontrar piedras erguidas a lo largo del camino inclinado hacia Minas Gîl, al este de Ost Galadh.\
\
Enedhel te ha pedido que te escondas detrás de las piedras erguidas en el camino hacia Minas Gîl para aprender qué tan de cerca los Orcos están vigilando el camino oriental hacia Dol Guldur.","Te escondes detrás de la piedra erguida","Capítulo 6: Reconocimiento de Emyn Lûm"}},
[3242]={nameES="Capítulo 6: Reconocimiento de Taur Morvith",objectivesES={"Tomas nota de la presencia de orcos en Krul Lugu","Encuentra a Malendol dentro o alrededor de Krul Lugu","Erymbes se encuentra en el Santuario Verde, al norte de los campamentos orcos de Krul Lugu, en Taur Morvith.\
\
Has explorado los campamentos orcos de Krul Lugu y defendido a Malendol, y ahora deberías regresar con Erymbes para informarle de lo que has aprendido.","Malendol puede estar en algún lugar dentro o alrededor de las fortificaciones orcas de Krul Lugu, en Taur Morvith.\
\
Has evaluado la presencia de orcos en Krul Lugu y ahora deberías buscar a Malendol, que podría estar en problemas.","Capítulo 6: Reconocimiento de Taur Morvith","Has defendido con éxito a Malendol","Krul Lugu es el nombre orco de un par de fortificaciones orcas en el centro de Taur Morvith, al sur del Santuario Verde.\
\
Erymbes te ha pedido que investigues la presencia de orcos en Krul Lugu y que luego busques a su amigo Malendol.","Evalúa la presencia de orcos en Krul Lugu","Habla con Erymbes en el Santuario Verde","Los orcos tienen una fuerte presencia en Taur Morvith."}},
[3243]={nameES="Capítulo 6: Reconocimiento de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas",objectivesES={"Lleva el paño con las muestras de veneno a Gladiel junto al Santuario del Antiguo","Las arañas de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas representan un peligro para todos los que pasan por allí, pero aún queda por determinar cuán grande es la amenaza para la Guardia Oculta.","Habla con Gladiel junto al Santuario del Antiguo","Se pueden encontrar arañas en todas las Hondonadas Enmarañadas.\
\
Gladiel te ha pedido que recojas veneno de las arañas de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas usando el paño que te dio.","Capítulo 6: Reconocimiento de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas","Gladiel está junto al Santuario del Antiguo, en las Hondonadas Enmarañadas.\
\
Has recolectado varias muestras de veneno de las arañas de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas y deberías devolverlas a Gladiel para que las examine."}},
[3244]={nameES="Capítulo 6: La elección de los caminos",objectivesES={"Ayuda a Enedhel en Ost Galadh, en Emyn Lûm","Cúcheron se encuentra fuera de la Posada Embrujada, ubicada entre los Troncosombríos.\
\
Has obtenido las opiniones de los Elfos de la Guardia Oculta sobre qué ruta tomar hacia Dol Guldur y has recibido tres propuestas diferentes.","Cúcheron está fuera de la Posada Embrujada, en los Troncosombríos.\
\
Has hecho lo que Cúcheron te pidió al reunir información sobre las posibles rutas hacia Dol Guldur y ahora deberías regresar con él.","Capítulo 6: La elección de los caminos","Ayuda a Gladiel en las Hondonadas Enmarañadas","Los Elfos de la Guardia Oculta se han encontrado con una dificultad: con la muerte de Raddir, ninguno de ellos sabe con certeza qué ruta había planeado para llevarlos a Dol Guldur en secreto.","Habla con Cúcheron en la Posada Embrujada","Los Elfos de la Guardia Oculta se encuentran en la bodega de la Posada Embrujada.\
\
Bróin te ha pedido que vayas a hablar con los Elfos de la Guardia secreta sobre lo que debe hacerse a continuación.","Ayuda a Erymbes en Taur Morvith","Issuriel se encuentra en la bodega de la Posada Embrujada, situada entre los Troncosombríos.\
\
Basándose en la información que has proporcionado, Cúcheron ha decidido que la ruta propuesta por Issuriel hacia Dol Guldur tiene la mayor probabilidad de éxito. Quiere que le informes que este es el camino que tomará la Guardia Oculta.","Tres exploradores han sido enviados a las Hondonadas Enmarañadas, Emyn Lûm y Taur Morvith.\
\
Cúcheron te ha pedido que hables con los Elfos que envió a investigar las áreas a lo largo de las rutas propuestas por la Guardia Oculta. Gladiel está en las Hondonadas Enmarañadas, al oeste del Santuario del Antiguo, cerca de la frontera de Gathbúrz. Erymbes está en Taur Morvith, junto al Santuario Verde, al sur de la Ruina Salvaje. Enedhel está en Ost Galadh.","Habla con los Elfos de la Guardia Oculta","Habla con Issuriel en la Posada Embrujada"}},
[3245]={nameES="Chapter 6: The King Under the Mountain",objectivesES={}},
[3246]={nameES="Chapter 6: The Last Word",objectivesES={"Habla con Merry","Habla con el Semiorco","You should talk to Pippin and Merry in Bâr Thorenion to hear what, exactly, they are thinking about with regard to Mordor.","There can be no mistaking it: this was one of the two remaining half-orcs, come to a bitter end","Habla con Gandalf","Return to Bâr Thorenion","Habla con Pippin","Pippin and Merry have asked you to go in search of the two half-orcs who fled the last encounter. You have found one of them, come to a bitter end, on the path to Barad-dûr, and should examine the corpse.","You should talk to Merry in Bâr Thorenion to hear his thoughts on where the two remaining half-orcs might be.","Pippin and Merry have asked you to go in search of the two half-orcs who fled the last encounter. Tracks leading from the corpse of the first have led at last to the second, who lives still. You should talk to him and learn what you can.","Chapter 6:  The Last Word","On returning to Bâr Thorenion, Gandalf has appeared and beckoned you over to speak with him.","A look of abject misery and fear is etched across the half-orc's lifeless face. Signs of a struggle on the ground about him clearly show marks of both pursuer and pursued, bearing roughly east.","Although they promised Frodo they would not return to that land, Pippin and Merry find their thoughts turning back towards Mordor once again.","Found the final half-orc","Pippin and Merry have asked you to go in search of the two half-orcs who fled the last encounter. Merry believes they will be found somewhere in Dor Amarth, on the path to Barad-dûr.","Search for the half-orcs","Sigue el rastro","Examine the dead half-orc","Return to Merry and Pippin in Bâr Thorenion with news of what you learned from the dying half-orc.","You should talk to Pippin and Merry in Bâr Thorenion, telling them at least some of the whole truth, as Gandalf counselled you.","Gandalf is here and beckons you over","Pippin and Merry have asked you to go in search of the two half-orcs who fled the last encounter. You should follow the trail leading from the one half-orc, in hopes of finding the other.","The tracks of the final half-orc lead onward"}},
[3247]={nameES="Chapter 6: The Wizard and the King",objectivesES={"Talk to Mithrandir in the throne room and stand guard","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to Elessar and the Kingdom of Gondor, and to fight on their behalf in Mordor.","Mithrandir has come to the throne room of King Elessar, atop Minas Tirith.","Talk to King Elessar in his throne room","King Elessar is in his throne room atop Minas Tirith.","Talk to Mithrandir in King Elessar's throne room","Chapter 6: The Wizard and the King"}},
[3248]={nameES="Chapter 7.1: Asking Questions",objectivesES={"You have found the Hungry Deep Tavern, a popular eating and drinking establishment","Chapter 7.1: Asking Questions","Find the Hungry Deep Tavern that overlooks the Sail-haven","Daxamat is at the amphitheatre outside the city.","The Whelk and Cockle Tavern is not as busy as the Hungry Deep","The folk here seem to be studiously avoiding your gaze.","The Whelk and Cockle Tavern is not as popular as the last one you visited, but patrons here may still know something.","Rothog the Storm is at the Whelk and Cockle Tavern in the Sail-haven.","Talk to Corudan at the amphitheatre","Rothog the Storm has come to the Sail-haven","Part of your mission has been completed... but half of it remains, for Thorongil is still a prisoner of the Kindred of the Coins.","The Hungry Deep Tavern is located up a set of stairs in the Upper Ward, from where it overlooks the Sail-haven.","Patrons of the Hungry Deep Tavern may have information of use to you.","Daxamat suggests you speak with patrons at two taverns in the Sail-haven and Upper Ward","Talk to Rothog the Storm outside the Whelk and Cockle Tavern","The Whelk and Cockle Tavern is located to the west of the Hungry Deep, in the Sail-haven.","Find the Whelk and Cockle Tavern to the west, in the Sail-haven","Talk to Daxamat at the amphitheatre","A hush falls over the people nearby","What has caused this sudden stillness?","Daxamat clears his throat, seeking your attention","Corudan is at the amphitheatre outside the city."}},
[3249]={nameES="Chapter 7.1: Inside the Lonely Mountain",objectivesES={"This is the entrance to the recently-delved New-lodes of Narathâk","Chapter 7.1: Inside the Lonely Mountain","Gandalf was given a residence within the Lonely Mountain and plans to retire there to study while you help the Gem-cutters with their day-to-day work.","Mother Amma has asked you to pick up the finely-crafted necklace and deliver it to Erfith, the customer who requested it. Erfith can be found on the west side of the Dwelling-halls of Erebor, on one of the lower levels.","The entrance to the New-lodes of Narathâk is located east of the Dwelling-halls, beyond the passage that runs from the entryway to the Hall Under the Mountain.","Authi's brother Gráfar Splitstone has asked you to carry a crate of precious stones back to Mother Amma in the Jewelstead. The Gem-cutter family home is located in the south-west corner of the Dwelling-halls.","You have found the entrance to the Jewelstead, home of the Gem-cutter family","Talk to Mother Amma in the Jewelstead","Pick up the finely-crafted necklace and deliver it to Erfith on the west side of the Dwelling-halls","Authi Gem-cutter's brother Gráfar is in the New-lodes of Narathâk.","Someone named Khîl has been spreading rumours about the Gem-cutters","The home of Authi Gem-cutter and his family can be found in the south-western corner of the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.","The New-lodes of Narathâk are crawling with cave-claws and other pests, and Authi's brother Gráfar asked you to help make the mine safe for the miners by thinning out some of the vermin.","Find the home of Authi Gem-cutter in the Dwelling-halls","Mother Amma nods at you, and indicates she has a necklace that needs delivering","Talk to Authi Gem-cutter in the Jewelstead","Talk to Gráfar Splitstone in the New-lodes of Narathâk","Pick up the crate of precious stones by Gráfar Splitstone","Talk to Erfith on the west side of the Dwelling-halls","Mother Amma is in the Jewelstead, the Gem-cutter family home in the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.","Mother Amma strokes her beard and considers you carefully","Authi Gem-cutter is in the Jewelstead, the Gem-cutter family home in the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.","Find the entrance to the New-lodes of Narathâk east of the entryway within the Lonely Mountain","Erfith accepts the necklace and admires its fine craftsmanship","Erfith the Quarrelsome is on the west side of the Dwelling-halls of Erebor, east of the Jewelstead and down the stairs."}},
[3250]={nameES="Chapter 7.1: The Houses of Rest",objectivesES={"Prince Durin has ordered the Gabil'akkâ to push further into Gundabad in opposition to the hostile Orc-defenders.","Bori has agreed to meet you by the upper crypts, further north in the Pit of Stonejaws.","Find Bósi at the entrance to the Pit of Stonejaws, north of Máttugard","A cruel sword of Orc-make is embedded here in the wall","You have found Bósi at the entrance to the Pit of Stonejaws","Durin ordered Bósi of the Iron Garrison to scout the further reaches of the Mountain-home, and has asked you to meet up with them at the entrance to the Pit of Stonejaws, north of Máttugard.","Find and talk to Bori further north in the Pit of Stonejaws","Talk to Bósi at the entrance to the Pit of Stonejaws","Prince Durin has returned with you to Máttugard.","Bósi is at the entrance to the Pit of Stonejaws.","Chapter 7.1: The Houses of Rest","You have caught up to Bori by the upper crypts","Bósi's son Bori has gone to search the crypts in the Pit of Stonejaws, and could use your assistance to the north-west.","Bori asked you to search more of the crypts along the westward path, which eventually turns north and slopes upward.","Bori calls you over to him","Find Bori to the north-west in the Pit of Stonejaws","You try to remove the sword but it is held fast by the rock","Talk to Durin in Máttugard","Search more of the crypts along the north-western path for evidence of the Orcs","Talk to Bori in the Pit of Stonejaws","<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel to Máttugard when you accept this quest.</rgb>\
\
'Then let us return! The conquest of the Mountain-home will wait no longer!'"}},
[3251]={nameES="Chapter 7.2: A Damaging Song",objectivesES={"How can Khîl believe this tale? Thafar-gathol never existed","This machine sounds very implausible","Talk to Khîl and hear his tale","A dwarf named Khîl has been spreading lies about the Gem-cutter family, and Authi wants you to find him and get him to stop.","Thafar-gathol sounds as it always has: a fanciful story with little basis in reality","Valves and pipes? No one else has mentioned such a machine at the battle","What nonsense! There was no such machine at the battle!","This disrespect cannot stand! King Brand and Dáin Ironfoot died before the gates of Erebor!","This must be Khîl. He seems to have attracted an audience","If Thafar-gathol existed, would it not have been found by now?","This story beggars belief. No such machine existed at the battle","Actually, King Brand and Dáin Ironfoot died before the gates of Erebor. Khîl's account is wrong","Demonstrate to Khîl that you are ready to <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> to his tales","It is good the machine was destroyed before the Jangovar plot could be successful","Is that truly how events unfolded?","That is how you remember the last moments of King Brand and Dáin Ironfoot","How can Khîl believe this tale? Lost Thafar-gathol is a tale for children","This dwarf does not know what really happened. King Brand did not die at the river-crossing","Khîl might be found outside the entrance to the Lonely Mountain.","Chapter 7.2: A Damaging Song","Khîl refuses to take back his story about the Gem-cutters","Talk to Khîl outside the Lonely Mountain","That isn't right, is it? King Brand and Dáin Ironfoot died before the gates of Erebor, didn't they?","Find Khîl outside the entrance to the Lonely Mountain","Khîl is wrong. King Brand and Dáin Ironfoot died before the gates of Erebor","Respond to the truthfulness of Khîl's account: <rgb=#00FF00>agree</rgb>, <rgb=#00FF00>yes</rgb>, <rgb=#00FF00>ahem</rgb>, <rgb=#00FF00>angry</rgb>, <rgb=#00FF00>confused</rgb>, <rgb=#00FF00>grumble</rgb>, or <rgb=#00FF00>no</rgb>","The story of lost Thafar-gathol excites your imagination. Can it be found?","The Jangovar machine was truly a complex and forbidding construct","Talk to Authi Gem-cutter in the Jewelstead","You have heard much of the battle, but have seen no evidence of such a machine","Khîl the Tale-spinner is outside the entrance to Erebor, regaling onlookers with his stories.","Did the Jangovar truly assemble such a machine as Khîl describes?","Authi Gem-cutter is in the Jewelstead, the Gem-cutter family home in the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.","Imagine the treasures that must await within lost Thafar-gathol, if it could be found","Such nonsense! Thafar-gathol never existed, and tales of it cannot be believed"}},
[3252]={nameES="Chapter 7.2: An Audience With The Golden Queen",objectivesES={"Find the courtyard in Hármelak's manor","Talk to Hármelak in the office of her manor","Find the garden of Hármelak's manor","Talk to Hármelak by the courtyard","Hármelak arrives in the courtyard","Hármelak arrives in the garden of her manor","Hármelak asked you to wait for her in the garden to the north.","Wait for Hármelak in the garden to the north","Hármelak has arrived in her office.","Chapter 7.2: An Audience With The Golden Queen","Talk to Hármelak in the garden of her manor","Hármelak asked you to wait for her in the office to the north.","Wait for Hármelak in the courtyard of her manor","Find the office to the north in Hármelak's manor","Wait for Hármelak in the office to the north","Hármelak arrives in the office and takes her seat","Rothog the Storm has brought you to speak with Hármelak, the Golden Queen.","Hármelak asked you to wait for her in the courtyard of her manor.","Hármelak asked you to wait for her in the garden to the north of the courtyard.","Hármelak has arrived in the courtyard.","Hármelak has arrived in the garden of her manor.","Talk to Hármelak in her manor","Hármelak is in the main hall of her manor."}},
[3253]={nameES="Chapter 7.2: So Say The Legends",objectivesES={"Bori needs your help to clear the rubble and debris away from the entrance to the south-west.","Together, you and Bori have cleared the rubble away from the room to the south-west, and can now gain entrance.","Bori is in Zul-mazal.","Examine the broken mosaic in Zul-mazal","Bori has asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> out over the Pit of Stonejaws, which contains the crypts of the many dwarf-families that were laid to rest over the years.","Bori needs your help to clear the rubble and debris away from the entrance.","Explore the room you have unearthed from the rubble","Even from this great height, the presence of the Orcs is unmistakeable","Bósi is outside Shakhajât in the centre of the Pit of Stonejaws.","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> out over the Pit of Stonejaws","Talk to Bósi outside Shakhajât in the centre of the Pit of Stonejaws","Chapter 7.2: So Say The Legends","A broken mosaic decorates one wall of this chamber.","Talk to Bori by the upper crypts in the Pit of Stonejaws","Bósi is outside the fortress of Shakhajât in the centre of the Pit of Stonejaws.","Find Bósi outside Shakhajât in the centre of the Pit of Stonejaws","Bori is by the upper crypts in the Pit of Stonejaws.","Bori is interested in the legends and history of Gundabad, and wants your help to learn as much of them as he can.","Clear rubble from the entrance to the south-west","Talk to Bori in Zul-mazal","Many of the stones in this mosaic have been lost to looters and time"}},
[3254]={nameES="Chapter 7.3: Beneath His Notice",objectivesES={"Talk to Ushu on the dock beside the Harbour Warden's tower","Hármelak has given you some information that may help you get past the guards into the Citadel of Winds.","You have accomplished the task set before you by Ushu and Enât","The women eye you suspiciously as you approach","Hármelak told you that every day Azagath's servants can be found on the docks by the Harbour Warden's tower, filling bowls with water to carry to the Citadel of Winds.","Azagath's water-bearers are on the dock beside the Harbour Warden's tower.","Azagath's water-bearers are on a dock by the Harbour Warden's tower.","Pick up the bowl of water on the dock","Rothog the Storm has escorted you from Hármelak's manor. He clearly believes his task is finished.","Talk to water-bearer Ushu on the dock","Talk to water-bearer Enât on the dock","Chapter 7.3: Beneath His Notice","Rothog looks down at you but says nothing.","The water-bearers will only allow you to accompany them into the Citadel if you can prove up to their task.","You should find some of the water-carriers mentioned by Hármelak","Find Azagath's water-carriers on a dock near the Harbour Warden's tower","The servant's companion calls for your attention","Ushu nods at the bowl, challenging you to carry it without spilling any of the water","Talk to Rothog the Storm outside Hármelak's manor"}},
[3255]={nameES="Chapter 7.3: Grievances",objectivesES={"Talk to Authi Gem-cutter in the Jewelstead and go with him to petition the king","Authi Gem-cutter is in the Jewelstead, the Gem-cutter family home in the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.","Authi Gem-cutter is very angry about the gossip Khîl has been spreading about his family, and he wishes to petition King Thorin about the matter.","Chapter 7.3: Grievances","Talk to Authi Gem-cutter in the Jewelstead"}},
[3256]={nameES="Chapter 7.3: Skulls of Shakhajât",objectivesES={"Strakhbuk roars a challenge and rushes to battle!","Talk to the dwarf-woman Bróin saw within Shakhajât","Bósi has asked Imák and Bróin to draw the defenders of Shakhajât out into the open.","The Dwarves of the Iron Garrison plan to combat the denizens of Shakhajât in the Pit of Stonejaws.","Bori is waiting to meet up with you outside Shakhajât.","Bósi has agreed that you can carry out Bróin's part of the plan: climbing either the left or right slope around the fortress and using a discarded horn of battle to draw forth some of the hobgoblins from Shakhajât.","Bróin gives you a relieved smile","Meet up with Bróin inside Shakhajât","You have caused a sufficient distraction for the dwarves to enter Shakhajât","Bróin greets you warmly","Now that you have carried out your part of the plan, you should join the dwarves inside Shakhajât.","Use a horn of battle on one of the slopes to either side of the fortress to draw forth and defeat hobgoblin defenders of Shakhajât","Talk to Bróin outside Shakhajât","Imák is pleased with the plan, and will do his part","Talk to Bróin inside Shakhajât","Bróin is inside Shakhajât and desires to speak with you.","Talk to Bósi outside Shakhajât","Talk to Bori outside Shakhajât","Chapter 7.3: Skulls of Shakhajât","Bróin has seen a dwarf-woman fighting in the fortress and wants you to check on her while you combat the forces inside Shakhajât.","Bori laughs abruptly, drawing your attention","The dwarves have made their presence known to Bósi's satisfaction and are now ready to meet up outside Shakhajât.","You can tell that Bróin is uncomfortable with the plan","Talk to Fastrith outside Shakhajât","Bósi is outside Shakhajât. Given Bróin's discomfort with the plan, perhaps you should volunteer in his stead?","Talk to Imák outside Shakhajât"}},
[3257]={nameES="Chapter 7.4: A Broken Mosaic",objectivesES={"Talk to Fastrith and travel with her to Zul-mazal","Chapter 7.4: A Broken Mosaic","Bori believes that Stáli the Hewer would be interested in the mosaic you found in Zul-mazal, and suggested that his apprentice Fastrith Hawkfeast take a look on behalf of her master.","Talk to Fastrith outside Shakhajât","Imák is standing in Zul-mazal, waiting to speak with you.","Talk to Imák in Zul-mazal","Fastrith is outside Shakhajât, waiting for you and Bori to bring her to Zul-mazal to examine the interesting mosaic.","Fastrith Halcomida se encuentra a las afueras de Shakhajât."}},
[3258]={nameES="Chapter 7.4: Into The Citadel",objectivesES={}},
[3259]={nameES="Chapter 7.4: Iron Road",objectivesES={"Visit Arin, a friend of the Gem-cutters who lives in Járnfast but is likely fishing in the Redwater","King Thorin has given you a task to complete in the Ironfold, and you will accompany Authi Gem-cutter with his own.","Gandalf is in the Wizard-home, east of the Jewelstead and up several stairs","Talk to Khîl at the entrance to Járnfast","Authi is at the entrance to Járnfast.","Meet up with Authi and Khîl outside the entrance to the Lonely Mountain","Visit Méthur, a friend of the Gem-cutters who lives in Hammerstead","Chapter 7.4: Iron Road","Authi and Khîl are waiting for you, but neither seems eager to depart","Find an entrance to the town of Utterby","Talk to Khîl outside the Lonely Mountain","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> from the cliff's edge at Skald's Drop to survey the lands below","Talk to Authi at the entrance to Járnfast","From the high cliff you can see the fair fields of the Bardings, far below","Authi has suggested you help the people of the Ironfold as you travel to Járnfast.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Complete any four of the objectives Authi has suggested as you travel through the Ironfold to Járnfast.</rgb>","Talk to Authi outside the Lonely Mountain","From here you could <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> out over the lands below","Authi planned to meet you outside the entrance to the Lonely Mountain after you prepared for the journey and said good-bye to Gandalf.","The entrance to Járnfast is in the north-east corner of the Ironfold.","Khîl Tale-spinner is at the entrance to the Lonely Mountain.","You have come to Járnfast, the Ironfort of the dwarves","Gandalf is in the room that was given to him in the Dwelling-halls, east of the Jewelstead and up several sets of stairs.","Authi Gem-cutter is at the entrance to the Lonely Mountain.","You have successfully escorted Khîl to Járnfast and should now speak to him.","The town of Utterby was occupied by the Jangovar, who now call it Er Shamol","Travel to the entrance of Járnfast, in the Ironfold"}},
[3260]={nameES="Chapter 7.5: Errands at the Ironfort",objectivesES={"Talk to Náin the Slakeless in Járnfast","Find Náin the Slakeless, Lord of the Ironfort, at his throne","With his steel teeth, a false eye, and a golden ear, Náin is an impressive figure","The Quenching Trough is a low-ceilinged tavern opposite the entrance to Járnfast.","Find Durin in the Quenching Trough opposite the entrance to Járnfast","You have completed the first part of your commitment to King Thorin, and now it is time to undertake the second portion of your responsibility: bringing word to his son Durin that it is time to return to the Lonely Mountain.","Náin the Slakeless, Lord of the Ironfort, can be found at his throne atop the northern ramps.","Durin is in the Quenching Trough, a low-ceiling tavern opposite the entrance to Járnfast.","Durin is in the Quenching Trough, a low-ceilinged tavern opposite the entrance to Járnfast.","Chapter 7.5: Errands at the Ironfort","Talk to Durin in the Quenching Trough","Durin sits up straight, and the change is striking: he stares at you alertly","Talk to Durin (again) in the Quenching Trough","You have found Durin, but he seems unprepared for your tidings"}},
[3261]={nameES="Chapter 7.5: Every River Leads To The Sea",objectivesES={"Your mission to Umbar has reached its successful conclusion, but a number of unresolved questions leave the situation in the city and surrounding lands in some doubt.","Chapter 7.5: Every River Leads To The Sea","The successful completion of your mission to Umbar is the result of those who helped you, and many of them are now by the Harbour Warden's tower and want to speak with you.","Talk to Jajax by the Harbour Warden's tower","Talk to Nimrodel by the Harbour Warden's tower","Nimrodel is by the Harbour Warden's tower.","Talk to Caebar by the Harbour Warden's tower","Talk to your friends by the Harbour Warden's tower about the successful conclusion of your mission","Caebar is by the Harbour Warden's tower, a long way from his home.","Jajax is by the Harbour Warden's tower."}},
[3262]={nameES="Chapter 7.5: The Smell of a Spell",objectivesES={"Talk to Imák at the Witch-gate","Imák has asked if Fastrith and Bróin wish to investigate the dealings of the Angmarim cultists in Câr Bronach.","Imák stands at the Witch-gate between the Pit of Stonejaws and Câr Bronach.","Meet up with Imák at the Witch-gate between the Pit of Stonejaws and Câr Bronach","Imák insists that he can smell the odour of magic about the chamber of Zul-mazal, and believes it may be the doing of Angmarim cultists.","Talk to Bróin in Zul-mazal","Strange runes carved into the Witch-gate lend the passage a foreboding air","Chapter 7.5: The Smell of a Spell","Imák has suggested that you meet up at the Witch-gate, which can be found at the connexion between the Pit of Stonejaws and Câr Bronach.","Talk to Fastrith in Zul-mazal"}},
[3263]={nameES="Chapter 7.6: Danger at the Drop",objectivesES={"Talk to Náin the Slakeless in Járnfast","Durin is at his uncle's throne in Járnfast.","Biraisbij tharâkh: Jangovar tents on the eastern side of Utterby","Chapter 7.6: Danger at the Drop","The prisoner is grateful for your help, and makes his escape!","Biraisbij tharâkh: Jangovar tents on the southern side of Utterby","Durin suggested using dwarf-phrases that will be unfamiliar to the Jangovar in order to confuse your foes and to attain strategic advantage when you move against them:\
\
Biraisbêj tharâkh, \\qscouting the approaches.\\q \
Bini'zêg utrâd, \\qblinding the watchers.\\q \
Mahinsês mamahkhafdân, \\qrescuing the prisoners.\\q \
Isgêr narakakâ, \\qdefeating the reinforcements.\\q \
Ensêkh, \\qsetting a trap.\\q","You study the arrangement of the tents on the eastern side of Utterby","Meet up with Durin east of Utterby, in the Ironfold","Náin the Slakeless hopes that you and his nephew Durin will be able to combat some of the Easterling threat that remains within the Ironfold.","Durin can be found by his uncle's throne in Járnfast.","Talk to Durin at Skald's Drop","Durin eagerly watches the town of Utterby, threatened by the Jangovar","Durin is beneath the rising cliff-face at Skald's Drop.","Talk to Durin in Járnfast","The prisoner thanks you and makes his escape!","You study the arrangement of the tents on the southern side of Utterby","Durin is east of Utterby, in the Ironfold.","Talk to Durin east of Utterby","Náin the Slakeless, Lord of the Ironfort, can be found at his throne atop the ramps."}},
[3264]={nameES="Chapter 7.6: Iron Pass and Narrow Way",objectivesES={"Having scouted the Iron Pass, Imák thinks you should now do the same for the Narrow Way, the southern pass into Elderslade. He also wants you to continue your efforts to make the mountain paths safe for the Gabil'akkâ.","Venko has asked you to show the crumpled parchment to Imák.","Talk to Imák at the Narrow Way","You have met up with Imák at the Narrow Way only to discover that a former companion also shows an interest in the situation at Câr Bronach.","Scout the Narrow Way between Câr Bronach and Elderslade","Imák believes the mountain passes of Câr Bronach have been overrun by Angmarim cultists that threaten the mission of the Gabil'akkâ in Gundabad.","Read the crumpled parchment given to you by Venko","Talk to Venko at the Narrow Way","Chapter 7.6: Iron Pass and Narrow Way","Angmarim cultists fled through the Iron Pass to Gundabad when their kingdom fell","Your former companion Venko has also come to investigate the Narrow Way between Câr Bronach and Elderslade.","Venko is waiting to hear your thoughts at the Narrow Way between Câr Bronach and Elderslade.","Scout the Iron Pass in the north-western reaches of Câr Bronach","Venko hands you a crumpled piece of parchment","The Iron Pass is located in the north-western reaches of Câr Bronach, and Imák wants you to make the road there as safe as you can while investigating the enemy presence on that route to Angmar.","You and Imák are not the only adventurers with an interest in the Narrow Way","Give the crumpled parchment to Imák at the Narrow Way","Venko gave you a crumpled piece of parchment that he wrestled from one of the Angmarim, and is waiting for you to read it.","Talk to Imák at the Iron Pass"}},
[3265]={nameES="Chapter 7.7: The Hidden Chamber",objectivesES={"Talk to Náin in the hidden chamber","Talk to Authi Gem-cutter in the Quenching Trough","Authi Gem-cutter is in the Quenching Trough.","Náin is in the hidden chamber in Khîl's home in Járnfast.","Satisfied with his efforts against the Jangovar in the Ironfold, Durin is now ready to return to the Lonely Mountain with you, but first you need to find Authi Gem-cutter and make sure he is ready to go home.","Talk to Khîl and travel to his father's home","Talk to Khîl in the Quenching Trough","Chapter 7.7: The Hidden Chamber","Khîl is in the Quenching Trough, quite distraught."}},
[3266]={nameES="Chapter 7.7: The Valley of Ghosts",objectivesES={"Venko shivers nervously","Bring the orders from Magith to Venko outside Tâg Fógarrach","You retrieved a set of orders from one of the cultists you faced in Câr Bronach, and should read it to learn what you can of their movements and plans for the mountain passes.","Venko saw something disturbing to the south-east, just behind Tâg Fógarrach, and he has asked you to investigate. Whatever he saw, the vision seems to have shaken the Zhélruka's composure.","Talk to Imák south-west of Tûr Fúar","Someone watches","Chapter 7.7: The Valley of Ghosts","Venko saw something disturbing by the mountainside to the south-east, behind Tâg Fógarrach, and he has asked you to investigate. Whatever he saw, the vision seems to have shaken the Zhélruka's composure.","Talk to Venko outside Tâg Fógarrach","Venko believes there is more to learn from the messages carried hither and yon by Angmarim cultists within Câr Bronach. He wants you to wrest from them any such missives.","Read the orders from Magith","Imák is south-west of Tûr Fúar, stroking his beard thoughtfully.","Defeat Angmarim cultists or Trév Duvárdain in Câr Bronach (7/8)","You find a set of orders on this Angmarim","Venko is outside Tâg Fógarrach. No doubt the Zhélruka will be pleased to see the set of orders you recovered from the Angmarim cultist you defeated.","Ordered by Prince Ingór to learn more about the Angmarim presence in Câr Bronach, Venko is pleased to adventure with you and Imák once again.","The watchful presence departs. You are once again alone","You feel watchful eyes upon you, but otherwise no sign of anyone","Venko is outside Tâg Fógarrach, disturbed by whatever it was he saw.","Investigate the mountainside to the south-east, behind Tâg Fógarrach, and learn what could have shaken Venko's composure"}},
[3267]={nameES="Chapter 7.8: A Silent Presence",objectivesES={"Approaching the gate, you see a figure that cannot be","Talk to Venko north of the Witch-gate","Talk to Imák at the Witch-gate","Someone watches","Once again, the watchful presence departs and you are alone","Chapter 7.8: A Silent Presence","Return to the Witch-gate with Imák and Venko","Venko is at the Witch-gate, waiting to speak with you about what you saw.","Imák stands at the Witch-gate, a haunted expression on his face.","Imák believes that the troubling presence that so disturbed Venko might be the result of a ritual being conducted by the Angmarim in Tûr Fúar, the Drearspire. The Stout-axe thinks the three of you should investigate, despite the danger.","Talk to Venko at the Witch-gate","Talk to Imák and sneak into the Drearspire of Tûr Fúar","Imák and Venko are prepared to depart Câr Bronach, and want to travel with you to the Witch-gate.","You once again feel the watchful presence.","Venko is north of the Witch-gate.","Imák believes that the troubling presence that so disturbed Venko might be the result of a ritual being conducted by the Angmarim in Tûr Fúar, the Drearspire, and he wants you to investigate."}},
[3268]={nameES="Chapter 7: A True Friend of Durin's Folk",objectivesES={"Chapter 7: A True Friend of Durin's Folk","Thorin III, King under the Mountain, is at his throne in Erebor.","Bósi is in the Hall under the Mountain.","Talk to Bósi in the Hall under the Mountain","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to Durin's Folk and fight on their behalf in Mordor.","Talk to Bósi and go with him to see the king","Talk to King Thorin III at his throne in the Hall under the Mountain","Bósi has been instructed to bring you before the King under the Mountain."}},
[3269]={nameES="Chapter 7: A True Friend of Gondor",objectivesES={}},
[3270]={nameES="Chapter 7: Attack on Zudrugund",objectivesES={"Talk to Radanir and travel with him to Zudrugund","Radanir is at the camp-site of the Grey Company in the grove of trees to the east of Lhanuch.\
\
Radanir is waiting to speak with you, and together you will travel to Zudrugund with all haste to try and defend it from the uruks of which Ergothorn wrote.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo, you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.</rgb>","Corunir is in Zudrugund.\
\
You have managed to stave off an attack on Zudrugund by the Grishgúk Uruks led by Núrzumgrat, and should speak now to Corunir.","Chapter 7: Attack on Zudrugund","Talk to Corunir in Zudrugund","Ergothorn has left the Rangers a second letter: a band of uruks has come out of Dunland and is marching towards Zudrugund!"}},
[3271]={nameES="Chapter 7: Bewildering Ruins",objectivesES={"Treasure and Ninkoth uruks can be found throughout the ruins of Minas Elendúr and the Delotham under-cellars.\
\
Fúni Gem-cutter is waiting for you to retrieve as much treasure from the ruins as you can.","Talk to Radanir at Echad Eregion","Fúni Gem-cutter is in Minas Elendúr.\
\
You have done what Fúni asked, and should return to him with the treasures you have gathered.","Bring treasures to Fúni Gem-cutter in Minas Elendúr","Chapter 7: Bewildering Ruins","You have found Fúni Gem-cutter, but he is not content merely to be rescued: he wants you to rescue as much gold from the Ninkoth uruks in Minas Elendúr as you can.","Fúsi Gem-cutter is at Echad Eregion.\
\
You have rescued his father and should bring the news to Fúsi.","Talk to Fúsi Gem-cutter at Echad Eregion","Radanir is at Echad Eregion.\
\
The Rangers have been discussing something with Fúni Gem-cutter, now that he has been rescued, and Radanir may know more about it."}},
[3272]={nameES="Capítulo 7: Más allá de la luz y el conocimiento",objectivesES={"Lenglammel se encuentra en su campamento de Gwathrendath, entre las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
Has buscado en ambos lugares y has encontrado el sombrero quemado de Gandalf en el medio del Lago Negro. La Escalera Interminable está bloqueada por escombros quemados y ennegrecidos. Parece que Gandalf sobrevivió lo suficiente para enfrentarse al Balrog, pero lo que pasó después es desconocido para ti. Ahora deberías hablar con Lenglammel.","Capítulo 7: Más allá de la luz y el conocimiento","Describes tu hallazgo del sombrero quemado de Gandalf en medio del Lago Negro y de los escombros que obstruyen la Escalera Interminable. Lenglammel suspira.\
\
'Tus noticias sobre Mithrandir y la falta de noticias sobre mi amigo Magor me llenan de inquietud, pues aún desconocemos cuál ha sido su suerte. Te lo agradezco, pero podría ser que, al menos, Magor vuelva pronto con nosotros.\
\
'Dithaliwenn encontró algo mientras estabas fuera'.","Busca encima de la sección inferior de la Escalera Interminable","El Lago Negro y el pie de la Escalera Interminable se encuentran entre las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
Lenglammel te ha pedido que busques en varios lugares alguna señal de Mithrandir o del Elfo Magor.","Lenglammel no ha tenido éxito hasta ahora en su misión principal en Moria: localizar y rescatar a Mithrandir, si es que se puede rescatar a un Mago.","Busca el Lago Negro","Estos escombros están quemados y rotos, y bloquean el paso por la escalera","Lleva el sombrero quemado a Lenglammel","Este sombrero está quemado y cubierto de cenizas, pero sin duda perteneció a Gandalf el Gris"}},
[3273]={nameES="Chapter 7: Lothrandir of the Frozen Wastes",objectivesES={"Chapter 7: Lothrandir of the Frozen Wastes","Calenglad has sent you to speak with Lothrandir, a Ranger sent to Forochel, to bring him word of the Grey Company's mission.","Lothrandir is at Sûri-kylä, the major village of the Lossoth in Forochel.\
\
Calenglad has sent you to bring your message to Lothrandir, in Forochel, with the warning that he has lived among the Lossoth for so long that he may have taken on something of their customs and personalities.","Talk to Lothrandir and help him find the screaming shadow","Lothrandir is at Sûri-kylä, in Forochel.\
\
You have found the cause of the Lossoth's hunting troubles and have hopefully ended it. Lothrandir, at least, seems satisfied.","Lothrandir is at Sûri-kylä, in Forochel.\
\
You have given Lothrandir the message, but he seems unsure of the Grey Company's ability to reach Aragorn in time and wants your help with a Lossoth issue.","Talk to Lothrandir at Sûri-kylä"}},
[3274]={nameES="Capítulo 7: Al borde",objectivesES={"Issuriel está preocupada por el sentimiento de terror que se cierne sobre el pueblo abandonado de Audaghaim y por las cosas extrañas que los Elfos han visto allí.","Capítulo 7: Al borde","Los nerviosos Malledhrim se encuentran por todo Audaghaim.\
\
Issuriel te ha pedido que tranquilices a los nerviosos Malledhrim por todo Audaghaim diciéndoles que todo estará bien, a pesar de las cosas perturbadoras que han visto en este pueblo abandonado.","Habla con Issuriel en la Posada Embrujada","Issuriel está en el sótano de la Posada Embrujada, en Audaghaim.\
\
Has tranquilizado a un gran número de nerviosos Malledhrim y deberías volver a ver a Issuriel."}},
[3275]={nameES="Chapter 7: Pitting the Factions",objectivesES={}},
[3276]={nameES="Chapter 7: The Bow is Drawn",objectivesES={"Talk to Lady Galadriel to be released, finally, from your service.","Glorfindel is come to the Council of War in the Court of Lothlórien.","Chapter 7: The Bow is Drawn","Habla con Galadriel","Habla con Orophin","You should talk to Orophin and join the War Council."}},
[3277]={nameES="Capítulo 7: El tesoro sumergido",objectivesES={"Habla con Bori","Bori se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Bori y tú descubrieron a Bróin, todavía vivo a pesar de las grandes dificultades, y lo trajeron sano y salvo del tesoro sumergido donde encontró el hacha de mithril Zigilburk.","Capítulo 7: El tesoro sumergido","Bori se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Bori está esperando para hablar contigo y viajar a la Sala del Mithril, donde cree que encontrarás el hacha de mithril Zigilburk. Te pidió que trajeras aliados.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Se sugiere completar esta misión mientras estás en una comunidad. La inspiración te ayudará si decides emprender este desafío solo o con un grupo más pequeño.</rgb>","Bori cree que has descubierto la ubicación de las armerías que el condenado enano Óin buscaba hace muchos años, y que podrían contener el hacha de mithril Zigilburk.","Habla con Bori y viaja a la Sala del Mithril"}},
[3278]={nameES="Capítulo 7: El Pasaje Vacío",objectivesES={"Bósi cree que ha descubierto la ubicación de Nâr-khelab, la forja donde se fabricó el hacha de mithril Zigilburk.","Habla con Bósi y viaja con él para encontrar Nâr-khelab","Bósi está en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, en la entrada sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación de Moria.\
\
Con la ayuda de Bósi, has descubierto la entrada oculta a Nâr-khelab, el Corazón de Fuego, y ahora deberías hablar con él.","Bósi está en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, cerca de la entrada sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación de Moria.\
\
Bósi cree que ha intuido la entrada oculta a Nâr-khelab, el Corazón de Fuego, y está esperando para viajar allí contigo.","Capítulo 7: El Pasaje Vacío"}},
[3279]={nameES="Capítulo 7: La historia gloriosa de Bróin el Poderoso",objectivesES={"Habla con Bróin","Capítulo 7: La historia gloriosa de Bróin el Poderoso","El hijo de Brogur, Bróin, ha pedido tu ayuda para combatir a los peligrosos huargos de las sombras que merodean más allá de las orillas del Sirannon.","Bróin se encuentra al pie de las escaleras que suben al lago fétido frente a la Puerta de Acebeda, al este de donde viste a Bosi.\
\
Has derrotado a un gran número de huargos de las sombras y ahora deberías volver a ver a Bróin.","Los huargos de las sombras se encuentran al sur de las escaleras que suben al lago frente a la Puerta de Acebeda, del otro lado del lecho seco del Sirannon.\
\
Bróin ha encontrado la manera de endosarte esta tarea, y ahora tienes que enfrentarte a los huargos de las sombras en su lugar."}},
[3280]={nameES="Capítulo 7: El Taller Perdido",objectivesES={"Capítulo 7: El Taller Perdido","Encuentra el taller de Melkólf Tallapiedra y búscalo en busca de menciones de Zurr-thurkh","El pasaje al taller de Melkólf Tallapiedra se encuentra en la ladera de Zirakzigil; toma la salida oeste de la Senda Pacífica, y luego gira al oeste y sube una corta pendiente hasta la entrada.\
\
Bróin te ha pedido que encuentres el taller de Melkólf Tallapiedra y lo busques en busca de cualquier mención de Zurr-thurkh, el camino secreto hacia la sala del trono de Durin que podría haberse construido hace mucho tiempo. Ha decidido no acompañarte al taller.","Bróin cree que has descubierto la mención de un pasaje secreto hacia Rushdurinul, donde Mazog ha establecido su trono, y podría usarlo para rescatar a su primo Bori.","Bróin está en la Senda Pacífica, ubicada en la Sala de Reunión Militar, al este de Sulnul-dûm y al oeste de la Sala de Piedra, a lo largo del Camino de Durin.\
\
Has recuperado unos planos del taller de Melkólf Tallapiedra que revelan un camino secreto hacia Rushdurinul, la sala del trono de Durin, que ahora está ocupada por Mazog y sus orcos."}},
[3281]={nameES="Capítulo 7: La Mano Blanca en la oscuridad",objectivesES={"Capítulo 7: La Mano Blanca en la oscuridad","Ha llegado el momento para que Bori ponga en marcha su audaz plan para expulsar a la Mano Blanca de Moria.","Habla con Bori y pon en marcha su audaz plan para combatir a la Mano Blanca","Bori se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo, cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
El plan de Bori ha sido un éxito, y ahora deberías hablar con él al respecto.","Bori se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo, cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Bori te espera para dar la orden, y luego pondrá su plan en marcha.","Brogur se encuentra con Bori en la Cámara de Liderazgo, cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Bori está preocupado por las últimas palabras de Ashpar, y quiere que le preguntes a Brogur por consejo."}},
[3282]={nameES="Capítulo 7: Voces de lobos en el viento",objectivesES={"Has ayudado a Bróin con su tarea","Brogur está preocupado por el comportamiento inusualmente agresivo de los lobos de la región y quiere que se ocupen de ellos.","Capítulo 7: Voces de lobos en el viento","Encuentra la causa de la locura de los lobos","Bosi se encuentra al sur de donde viste a Brogur, a la vista de las escaleras que suben al lago que se extiende frente a la Puerta de Acebeda.\
\
Has aprendido algo sobre la locura de los huargos de las sombras ayudando a Bróin con su tarea, y ahora debes ir a ver a Bosi.","Ayuda a Bróin con la tarea que le dio Brogur","El cuerpo de este lobo está quemado, su pelaje carbonizado.","La causa del comportamiento temible de los lobos puede encontrarse entre sus guaridas, al sur de donde viste a Brogur y al otro lado del lecho seco del Sirannon. Brogur cree que la cueva de Filgogân podría contener alguna pista sobre la locura de los lobos, en el extremo suroeste de la región. Bróin se puede ver hablando con Bori en la base de las escaleras que suben al lago frente a la Puerta de Acebeda.\
\
Brogur te ha pedido que busques la causa de la creciente locura de los huargos de las sombras, y que ayudes a su hijo Bróin con una tarea. Cuando hayas hecho cada una de estas cosas, te dijo que hablaras con su primo Bosi."}},
[3283]={nameES="Chapter 7: World Behind and Home Ahead",objectivesES={"You should talk to Pippin in Bâr Thorenion, and learn what sort of 'formal invitation' he and Merry are talking about.","Chapter 7: World Behind and Home Ahead","Habla con Merry","The hobbits have issued you a 'formal invitation' to Bâr Thorenion.","You should talk to Pippin and Merry in  Bâr Thorenion.","Habla con Pippin"}},
[3284]={nameES="Chapter 8.1: A Message in Mithril",objectivesES={}},
[3285]={nameES="Chapter 8.1: Azagath Pursued",objectivesES={"Talk to Nauriel and help her pursue the fleeing members of the Kindred","Nauriel stands outside the Harbour-warden's Tower, preparing to pursue the escaping members of the Kindred deeper into the Citadel of Winds.","Nauriel stands outside the Harbour-warden's Tower.","Thorongil has been rescued, but questions remain about the members of the Kindred of the Coin who fled from the Five Sisters.","Sigileth stands outside the Harbour-warden's Tower.","Talk to Sigileth outside the Harbour-warden's Tower","Sigileth hums a tuneless melody, attracting your notice","Talk to Nauriel outside the Harbour-warden's Tower","Chapter 8.1: Azagath Pursued"}},
[3286]={nameES="Chapter 8.1: The Black Book of Mordor",objectivesES={"Gandalf is at his chambers on the upper level of the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.","Talk to Durin among the large Zhélruka force","Pick up the Black Book of Mordor from the table where it lies","The party Durin witnessed from afar reveals itself to be a large band of Zhélruka","Talk to Khîl in the hidden chamber","Meet up with Durin on the road west of Utterby, in the Ironfold","Talk to Durin in the hidden chamber","King Thorin looks at you curiously as you approach without the son he sent you to retrieve","Durin stands among the group of Zhélruka that intends to cross the Dale-lands.","Khîl Tale-spinner is in the hidden chamber in his father's house where you discovered the Black Book of Mordor.","Durin has spied a large party heading west on the road to the Lonely Mountain, and he wants to investigate.","Talk to Gandalf at his chambers in the Dwelling-halls and give him the Black Book of Mordor","Durin wanted to meet up on the road west of Utterby to admire his handiwork.","The black leather binding feels cool to the touch","Durin is in the hidden chamber in Khîl's family home in Járnfast.","Catch up to the large party heading west","Chapter 8.1: The Black Book of Mordor","The Black Book of Mordor is on the table in the hidden chamber in Khîl's family home in Járnfast.","Talk to King Thorin in the Hall Under the Mountain","Talk to Bótuz Frostblood among the large Zhélruka force","Within the rune-covered walls of the secret chamber in the home of Khîl Tale-spinner you found a black-bound book written by his thrice-great grandfather Vóin and hidden long ago.","Hurry to King Thorin in the Hall Under the Mountain","Bótuz Frostblood leads a group of Zhélruka toward the Dale-lands.","King Thorin III is at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.","Durin wears a thoughtful expression as he gazes off to the west"}},
[3287]={nameES="Chapter 8.2: Broken Bones, Broken Hearts",objectivesES={"He scowls and accepts the salve. 'I suppose I need this,' he grumbles","Durin nods solemnly","Slagvi thanks you for the bandage, wincing at the pain in his leg","Prince Ingór refuses the bandage.\
\
'I need it not,' he insists.","Treat as many wounded dwarves at Maergrind as you can","Stóthkell has no further need of your help. The forge-master is dead","Talk to Slagvi at Maergrind","Búkk is at Maergrind.\
\
You have treated the dwarves you could, and should now return the remaining supplies to Búkk.","Bósi refuses the bandage. 'I am merely winded,' he says","Búkk is at Maergrind.\
\
Durin asked you to collect salves and bandages from Búkk with which to heal the hurts of those dwarves who are not already beyond help.","Chapter 8.2: Broken Bones, Broken Hearts","It is too late for any of your supplies to help him. He is dead","Slagvi is at Maergrind.","He smiles weakly and gratefully accepts the bandage","Durin is at Maergrind.","Slagvi limps over and begs the prince's pardon","Durin is at Maergrind, furious at Gorgar's attack and grieving for the slain.","Gorgar's attack has left many dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ dead or wounded. If the conquest of Gundabad is to be successful, Prince Durin and those loyal to him must recover from this defeat, and resist despair.","Talk to Búkk at Maergrind","This Zhélruka warrior is beyond help. He is dead","Longbeards and Zhélruka were wounded during Gorgar's attack, and many of them require treatment for their wounds.","Talk to Durin at Maergrind","Return the remaining supplies to Búkk at Maergrind","Búkk hands you a bundle of salves and bandages","He accepts the bandage with a grateful smile","Glóin thanks you for the bandage"}},
[3288]={nameES="Chapter 8.2: Something Remains",objectivesES={"Corudan has asked you to speak with a distant onlooker down the hill to the east.","Talk to Corudan by his sister east of the Mâkhda Khorbo","Sigileth is beside the road east of the Mâkhda Khorbo, north-west of Umbar Baharbêl.","Corudan stands by the road east of the Mâkhda Khorbo, north-west of Umbar Baharbêl.","Corudan catches your eye","Sigileth stands by the road east of the Mâkhda Khorbo, north-west of Umbar Baharbêl.","Sigileth is waiting for you to return to her east of the Mâkhda Khorbo with the strange objects for which she asked.","Bring the strange items she requested to Sigileth east of the Mâkhda Khorbo","Talk to Corudan beside the road east of the Mâkhda Khorbo","Talk to Sigileth beside the road east of the Mâkhda Khorbo","Meet up with Sigileth and Corudan beside the road east of the Mâkhda Khorbo","Talk to Rukân down the hill to the east","Sigileth is no stranger to the works of Sauron, and she believes that Azagath should be prevented from delving beneath the Mâkhda Khorbo for anything of that sort that may remain there.","The ruins of the Mâkhda Khorbo stand to the north-west of Umbar Baharbêl. Sigileth and Corudan asked to meet up with you there.","Sigileth asked you to retrieve a number of curious objects near the Mâkhda Khorbo so she may examine them.","Corudan is beside the road east of the Mâkhda Khorbo, north-west of Umbar Baharbêl.","Chapter 8.2: Something Remains","Sigileth and her brother Corudan greet you as you approach"}},
[3289]={nameES="Chapter 8.2: The Zhélruka",objectivesES={"Durin stands among the wind-swept grasses of the heights","You have found Durin on the road that climbs into the Grey Mountains.","King Thorin is at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.","Durin has followed the Zhélruka into the Grey Mountains, and at King Thorin's request you should look for him on the road that climbs into Ered Mithrin.","Return to King Thorin with Gandalf's warning about the Zhélruka","Talk to Durin on the road that climbs into the Grey Mountains","Find Durin on the road that climbs into the Grey Mountains","Talk to King Thorin in the Hall Under the Mountain","A band of Zhélruka desires to travel to the Grey Mountains, but its presence near the Lonely Mountain has threatened to spark an incident between the Zhélruka and the Longbeards.","Chapter 8.2: The Zhélruka","Authi Gem-cutter stands before the king. What is he doing here?"}},
[3290]={nameES="Chapter 8.3: An Inhospitable Land",objectivesES={"Durin stands by the Anvil on the Withered Heath.","Durin stares up at the Anvil, preoccupied with his own thoughts","Durin has asked you to defeat some of the worms and drakes that stalk the Withered Heath and Ered Mithrin, and collect their teeth and hides.","Durin beckons you to his side, signaling for quiet","Travel with Durin to the canyons south of Stormwall","Talk to Durin in the canyons south of Stormwall","The old fortress of Skarháld is south and west of the path to Stormwall. Durin is at the eastern entrance of the city, waiting to speak with you.","Durin is in the canyons south of Stormwall.","The Zhélruka stare suspiciously at you and Durin as the two of you approach","Durin asked you to defeat enemies in the Wyrmgap on your way to the Anvil on the Withered Heath.","Now that Durin has seen the Grey Mountains for himself, he has decided he wants to adventure among them for glory and for treasure, rather than remaining at the Lonely Mountain with his father.","Talk to Durin by the Anvil on the Withered Heath","Talk to Durin at the eastern entrance of Skarháld","Durin asked you to defeat enemies in the Vales of Mithrin.","The old fortress of Skarháld is south and west of the path to Stormwall.","Travel to the old fortress of Skarháld, where the Zhélruka planned to encamp","Chapter 8.3: An Inhospitable Land","Travel with Durin to the Anvil on the Withered Heath"}},
[3291]={nameES="Chapter 8.3: In Memory of the Forge-master",objectivesES={"Slagvi wants to honour the memory of Stóthkell by protecting the sacred lake of Gloomingtarn from the Angmarim, and has volunteered to accompany you there.","Examine the White Stone Forge on the island in the lake","Talk to Slagvi on the Stone of Wakening","Cross to the island and find the White Stone Forge and the Black Stone Anvil","Slagvi stands beside the rune-stone wards at the entrance to Gloomingtarn.","The rune's power has been drained by specific lines, carefully etched","Slagvi stands at the entrance to Gloomingtarn, beside the broken wards.","Talk to Slagvi beside the lake in Gloomingtarn","Slagvi stands beside you in silence as you contemplate the distant rocks","Slagvi has come to the Stone of Wakening, and he is not happy.","Talk to Slagvi by the lakeshore","Slagvi grimly observes the rune-stone wards at the entrance to Gloomingtarn","Talk to Slagvi at the entrance to Gloomingtarn","Meet up with Slagvi at the entrance to Gloomingtarn from Deepscrave","The Wakening Stone stands in the middle of the lake in Gloomingtarn.","The White Stone Forge gleams even in the dim light, unaffected by time's passage","Slagvi has asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> toward the Stone of Wakening, the island that stands in the lake.","Studying the stones on either side of the entrance may reveal what happened to the wards that once blocked passage to Gloomingtarn.","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> toward the island that stands in the lake","Chapter 8.3: In Memory of the Forge-master","Slagvi asked you to defeat any Angmarim cultists you find lurking within the cavern of Gloomingtarn.","The White Stone Forge is as Slagvi described, but of the anvil there is no sign","Someone etched further lines upon this rune. Now it feels inert, robbed of power","Slagvi asked to meet with you at the entrance to Gloomingtarn from Deepscrave, where he fears the rune-stones warding passage to that sacred cavern may be threatened.","It is said that Durin himself constructed the White Stone Forge and the Black Stone Anvil in the days after he first awoke.","Slagvi stands beside the lakeshore in the vast cavern, deep in thought."}},
[3292]={nameES="Chapter 8.3: The Words in the Wards",objectivesES={"Gather information from residents in the Lower Ward (2/3)","He falls silent and says nothing further","The rumour was true: Belondor has returned to the Sail-haven","Belondor stands atop one of the piers extending out into the waters of the Sail-haven.","Find the man wearing blue and silver on one of the north-south piers of the the Sail-haven","Belondor says nothing.","Chapter 8.3: The Words in the Wards","Talk to Belondor in the Sail-haven","A man in the Lower Ward told you he saw a well-dressed man in blue and silver walking along one of the north-south piers extending out into the waters of the Sail-haven, north-west of the Lower Ward.","Corudan has asked you to speak with residents of the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl about Azagath and the other leaders of the Kindred that fled with him.","The man says nothing further to you.","Azagath was well-loved by the people of Umbar Baharbêl, and Corudan wants to know if they have learned of his escape from the city.","Corudan has asked you to speak with residents of the Lower Ward of Umbar Baharbêl about Azagath and the other leaders of the Kindred that fled with him."}},
[3293]={nameES="Chapter 8.4: An Insult Never To Be Forgotten",objectivesES={"Bósi greets you warmly","You hear Slagvi calling for you from the Stone of Wakening","Chapter 8.4: An Insult Never To Be Forgotten","Meet up with Bósi and the other Longbeards on the lakeshore","Slagvi has sworn vengeance upon the Angmarim cultists that removed the Black Stone Anvil from the island of Durin's awakening.","Bósi is on the lakeshore in Gloomingtarn.","Bósi and some other Longbeards have come to the lakeshore in Gloomingtarn.","Defeat Angmarim in Gloomingtarn (6/101)","Slagvi has demanded that you slay one hundred and one Angmarim as payment for their theft of the Black Stone Anvil.","Talk to Slagvi on the island in the lake","Slagvi is standing on the Stone of Wakening, the island in the middle of the Gloomingtarn lake.","Talk to Bósi on the lakeshore in Gloomingtarn"}},
[3294]={nameES="Chapter 8.4: Gondor and Umbar",objectivesES={"Talk to Sirgon outside the Harbour-warden's Tower, in the Sail-haven","Chapter 8.4: Gondor and Umbar","Talk to Sirgon outside the Harbour-warden's Tower and go with him to meet with Belondor","Belondor has asked to speak with his one-time friend and long-time foe, if it is true that Sirgon has come to Umbar Baharbêl.","Talk to Hármelak inside her manor","Sirgon stands outside the Harbour-warden's Tower, in the Sail-haven.","Sirgon stands outside the Harbour-warden's Tower, in the Sail-haven, waiting to go with you to meet with Belondor.","Hármelak is inside her manor, waiting to speak with you about the Kindred of the Coins."}},
[3295]={nameES="Chapter 8.4: The Stones of Skarháld",objectivesES={"Leave the keep of Skarháld and learn what transpired outside","Bótuz Frostblood is near the top of the fortress of Skarháld.","Talk to Dóbrokh","Inek eyes the siege defences with disapproval","Talk to Inek the Brash","Dóbrokh stands at the edge, unconcerned by the long drop","Find Inek the Brash at the siege defences","A crowd of dwarves surround a wounded Zhélruka warrior","Kópat assists his brethren with establishing crafting facilities in the keep","Talk to Bótuz Frostblood at Skarháld","Talk to Vútro the West-wind and learn how he was injured","Talk to Durin inside Tharrazhâr, the keep of Skarháld","You and Durin have come to the old fortress of Skarháld, where Longbeards and Zhélruka both attempt to survive in the dangerous Grey Mountains.","You heard raised voices outside the keep. What is happening?","Find Kópat inside Tharrazhâr, the keep of Skarháld","Durin is inside Tharrazhâr, the keep of Skarháld.","Talk to Kópat","A crowd of dwarves surround a wounded Zhélruka warrior on the upper level of Skarháld.","Chapter 8.4: The Stones of Skarháld","Find Dóbrokh at the view from the high eastern arch","Bótuz Frostblood told you to look for his chieftains Inek, Kópat, and Dóbrokh on the upper levels of Skarháld and in the keep."}},
[3296]={nameES="Chapter 8.5: Assault on Clovengap",objectivesES={"Bori is waiting by the lakeshore in Gloomingtarn for you to agree to his plan.","Bori of the Iron Garrison thinks the Angmarim may have hauled the Black Stone Anvil out of Gloomingtarn, and if you hurry you may be able to find and retrieve the ancient artifact before they do it some harm.","Talk to Bori by the lakeshore and travel with him in search of the Black Stone Anvil","Bósi is in Clovengap, north-east of the tunnel to Gloomingtarn.","Fastrith is on the lakeshore in Gloomingtarn.","Talk to Bróin on the lakeshore","Chapter 8.5: Assault on Clovengap","Bori is on the lakeshore in Gloomingtarn.","Talk to Bósi in Clovengap, north-east of the tunnel to Gloomingtarn","Talk to Bori on the lakeshore","Fastrith laughs merrily","Talk to Fastrith on the lakeshore","Bróin is on the lakeshore in Gloomingtarn."}},
[3297]={nameES="Chapter 8.5: Hármelak's Resolve",objectivesES={"Yamin is located just to the north of the Grand Market in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.","Jaith guards the entrance to Dâr Laja, the Meeting-hall, in the centre of the Upper Ward.","Defeated an Heirsworn Corsair in the Sail-haven","Chapter 8.5: Hármelak's Resolve","At last! You have found the keys to Dâr Laja!","Talk to Jaith outside Dâr Laja about opening the Meeting-hall","Bring the keys you recovered to Yamin just north of the Grand Market in the Upper Ward","Dâr Laja, the Meeting-hall, is located in the centre of the Upper Ward.","Hármelak has decided that, in the wake of Azagath's betrayal, the people of Umbar Baharbêl need to be reassured that the Kindred of the Coins are working to ensure their safety and prosperity.","Talk to Jaith outside Dâr Laja in the centre of the Upper Ward","Defeat Heirsworn in the Sail-haven until you find the keys to Dâr Laja","Jaith told you that Heirsworn in the Sail-haven might have absconded with the keys to Dâr Laja, and they must be recovered before the hall can safely be opened to the people."}},
[3298]={nameES="Chapter 8.5: The Warrior Found",objectivesES={"Talk to Bótuz Frostblood and join the search for Karazgar","Talk to Bótuz Frostblood on the upper level of Skarháld","Chapter 8.5: The Warrior Found","Bótuz Frostblood is on the upper level of Skarháld, and he plans to lead a party of dwarves in search of the Weeping Warrior.","Bótuz Frostblood is on the upper level of Skarháld.","Vútro the West-wind ran afoul of the Weeping Warrior and barely escaped with his life."}},
[3299]={nameES="Chapter 8.6: The Beauty of Akrakír",objectivesES={"The Angmarim are here in great numbers, but of the Black Stone Anvil there is no sign","Bósi has asked you to search a number of locations within Clovengap for the missing Black Stone Anvil, and to defeat the wargs charged with protecting the area from intruders.","Investigate the Angmarim presence at Garanashmar","All is silent in the old vineyard, any fruitful pursuit there long abandoned","Investigate the sounds coming from Dashat-zahar","Chapter 8.6: The Beauty of Akrakír","Talk to Bósi in Clovengap","Investigate the old vineyard of Maranazhâr","Hornets have occupied Dashat-zahar. The Angmarim will not trouble to come here","The Longbeards of the Iron Garrison comb the gardens of Akrakír for the missing Black Stone Anvil, hoping to find the ancient artifact before it is put to some terrible purpose by their enemies.","Bósi is at his camp not far from the south-western entrance to Clovengap."}},
[3300]={nameES="Chapter 8.6: Tremors in the Foundation",objectivesES={"Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior, has promised to bring war to Skarháld, and Bótuz Frostblood wants you to ready the defences.","The mountains shake again!","The mountains shake!","Durin asked you to count the weapons and armour currently stored inside the keep of Skarháld, as well as to assess the quality of the siege defences on the upper level outside the keep.","The mountains shake! What is happening?","Talk to Bótuz Frostblood inside Tharrazhâr, the keep of Skarháld","There is a distant rumbling as the keep shakes beneath your feet","Talk to Durin inside Tharrazhâr, the keep of Skarháld","Durin is inside Tharrazhâr, the keep of Skarháld.","This time the rumbling is more pronounced, as the keep shakes again","Chapter 8.6: Tremors in the Foundation","Durin is inside Tharrazhâr, the keep of Skarháld, which has been shaken to its foundations.","Bótuz Frostblood is inside the keep of Skarháld.","Durin has requested that you send Zhélruka craftsmen inside the keep to repair the siege defences."}},
[3301]={nameES="Chapter 8.7: The First Promise",objectivesES={"Bótuz Frostblood wants you to keep an eye on Durin during the defence of Skarháld.","Durin is outside the keep on the upper level of Skarháld.","The death of Bótuz Frostblood threatens to leave the Zhélruka at Skarháld in disarray. One of his lieutenants must rise to lead his fellows.","Chapter 8.7: The First Promise","Talk to Durin inside the keep and defend Skarháld","Find a lieutenant of Bótuz Frostblood to lead the Zhélruka","While surveying the damage, Inek catches your eye","Talk to Durin on the upper level of Skarháld","Karazgar has not given the Dwarves of Skarháld enough time to prepare. He launches the first of his promised attacks, seeking to attain his goals with a single throw."}},
[3302]={nameES="Chapter 8.7: The Rimed Passage",objectivesES={"Bróin has called for your attention in Clovengap.","Investigate the frozen reaches of Clovengap, to the north-west","Crushed into the snow and ice of one booted footprint you find a single red pebble","Bróin has asked to see the red pebble you found.","Bróin calls over to you, seeking your attention","Bróin asked to meet with you atop the terrace to the west, a short distance away from the others.","Bróin looks around nervously, and asks to see the red pebble you found","A disorganized array of Orkish footprints has drawn your attention.","Bósi is in the south-west portion of Clovengap, waiting to hear what you learned during your investigation of the frozen reaches.","Chapter 8.7: The Rimed Passage","Talk to Bósi in the south-western portion of Clovengap","Talk to Bróin and show him the pebble you found in the boot-print","Examine the booted footprints in the icy channel","The northern reaches of Clovengap may have become home to Hrímil Frost-heart, and Bósi wants you to investigate... carefully. He suggested you make your way through Frósthel on the left side of the Ladder-gardens to reach the frozen river-bed.","Talk to Bróin atop the terrace to the west, in Clovengap","A disorganized array of booted footprints in the icy channel draws your attention","Bósi is concerned about the frozen northern reaches of Clovengap, and believes you should investigate to learn if it has become a lair for Hrímil Frost-heart.","Talk to Bróin in Clovengap"}},
[3303]={nameES="Chapter 8.8: A Pouch of Stones",objectivesES={"Found a yellow stone!","Talk to Durin at Maergrind in Máttugard","Durin is at Maergrind in Máttugard.","Found a blue stone!","Found a red stone!","Found a green stone!","Bróin has asked you to collect any colourful stones you find from the enemies you face on behalf of the Gabil'akkâ throughout Gundabad.","Bring the pouch of stones to Bróin at Maergrind in Máttugard","Found a black stone!","Chapter 8.8: A Pouch of Stones","Bróin is at Maergrind in Máttugard, eager to see how many stones you were able to find.","Found a white stone!","Bróin has noticed that the foes of the Gabil'akkâ often pick up these coloured stones scattered throughout Gundabad, and he thinks you might help him with his own goal while still helping the overall effort of his people."}},
[3304]={nameES="Chapter 8: As Near As May Be",objectivesES={"Talk to Halbarad in Echad Eregion","Halbarad has had an idea: to equip each Ranger of the Grey Company with an imitation of the ring of Barahir, in order to confuse any servants of the Enemy in the event a Ranger is captured.","Halbarad is at Echad Eregion.\
\
Halbarad is waiting to travel with you to the forges Fúni will use to craft imitation Rings of Barahir for the Grey Company.","Halbarad is at Echad Eregion, waiting to speak with you.\
\
Fúni Gem-cutter has crafted imitation rings for the Grey Company, and you should speak now with Halbarad.","Chapter 8: As Near As May Be","Talk to Halbarad at Echad Eregion","Talk to Halbarad at Echad Eregion and travel to the forges","Halbarad is at Echad Eregion.\
\
Radanir has told you of Halbarad's plan to have Fúni Gem-cutter craft an imitation ring of Barahir."}},
[3305]={nameES="Capítulo 8: Frente a las Puertas de Durin",objectivesES={"Bósi te espera en su pequeño campamento para acompañarte a las Puertas de Durin.\
\
Los enanos de Bósi han reparado los picos, y ahora quiere que los lleves con él a los trabajadores.","Capítulo 8: Frente a las Puertas de Durin","Los enanos de la expedición de Bósi y Brogur esperan la apertura de las Puertas de Durin.","Ráthwald se encuentra fuera del arco, cerca del campamento de Echad Dúnan, en Eregion.\
\
Los enanos se han retirado en desbandada de las Puertas de Durin, y ahora deben planear para un futuro incierto.","Habla con Bósi y viaja a las Puertas de Durin"}},
[3306]={nameES="Capítulo 8: La historia de Bróin",objectivesES={"Bróin está vivo y se está recuperando de sus pruebas en la Senda Pacífica.","Bróin se está recuperando en la Senda Pacífica, un campamento que se ha establecido a lo largo del Camino de Durin, al noreste de los jardines.\
\
Bori está seguro de que Bróin querrá hablar contigo sobre sus aventuras.","Capítulo 8: La historia de Bróin"}},
[3307]={nameES="Chapter 8: Further Secrets",objectivesES={"Nár is in Zudrugund.\
\
You have searched the book-shelves pointed out to you by Corunir, and should speak to Nár to see if he can shed any light at all on what you found there.","Chapter 8: Further Secrets","(You found a book, of which the cover is missing, as are many of the pages, but it has been recently read and was clearly put back carelessly.)\
\
...but the beast returned that night, and the walls all around shook with the sound of its fury. The doors were barred, but the bars bent with each mighty crash of the creature's bulk, and cracks began to appear along their lengths. \\qWe must return its youngling!\\q cried Selur over the din, and he leapt forward, knocking aside the warriors that braced the door with their bodies. The first bar gone, and then the second! \\qNo, Selur!\\q they shouted, but it was too late: the third bar fell to the floor, and Selur threw open the door.\
\
Old Stonetooth was through the doorway in seconds. Selur was trampled underfoot, along with many good dwarves that spoke against the capture of Pebblewart; it availed them nothing in the end. Stonetooth thundered down the length of the hall, braying for her young. And then, an answering bleat! It drew her down side passages and steep stairways, the flagstones cracking beneath her great weight.\
\
The dwarves freed Pebblewart from his cage, and many of them ran; those that witnessed the reunion of mother and child did not survive to tell of it. But the next day, when the dwarves ventured back to those broken halls, all was empty. Old Stonetooth and Pebblewart were never seen in those caves again, and none know where they went. But it is still said today, when the earth shakes, that Pebblewart is running beneath the mountains, expressing joy at his freedom, carving great channels in the walls of the deepest caves with his golden horn.","(You have found some pages, which have been hastily torn from a larger volume -- perhaps a diary or record of events -- and seem to be only a few years old.)\
\
...surprisingly cold for March. Our friend the Ranger came by again today, and we spoke for a time about the situation in the north. His chief is on some errand to Mirkwood, but it seems to me that Túgonn knows little of it as well.\
\
Nár has been in high spirits lately; I think he likes receiving visitors, though he does not always recognize them for who they are. Still, it seems to me he enjoys the company. He does spend a great deal of time in the mine; I only accompany him occasionally, but there are only so many times I can see Thrór's Stone-house standing empty before the melancholy is too much. Nár sees it as it was, I think, so I am content to let him visit it by himself.\
\
These periods give me time to write in my book, which is fine by this dwarf. I think tomorrow I will walk down to the Coomb and see about picking more of the herbs I have read about. Perhaps I will make that brew after all. It will be nice to have Nár to talk to again.","Talk to Nár in Zudrugund","Corunir is in Zudrugund.\
\
You have spoken with Nár, but yet again he has provided very little with which you can piece together a solution.","(You found a stack of loose papers, yellowed with age, which seem to have been placed back onto the shelf randomly, with no regard for keeping them in order.)\
\
...and in the last month, a great number of the supports have fallen, giving rise to much concern among the dwarves who have stalls in Zigil-jabâl. A dozen of our stone-masons were directed to repair the supports, and trade should resume shortly.\
\
With these stone-masons went several waggons of material, chiefly unearthed stone, but also a number of fine gems: a gift to the dwarves at Kechel. We will see how hotly burn their forges, and if they can work the gem-stones into their craft as well as we are able.\
\
(Judging from the state of the next page, it is even older, and only a few words can still be read.)\
\
...time we lost one of our own to the Forbidden Halls. They should seal it away and forget it was ever delved.","You have repelled an attack on Zudrugund by the Grishgúk uruks, but Nár's curious behaviour before the attack causes Corunir concern.","Talk to Halbarad in Lhanuch","Halbarad is among the huts on the western side of Lhanuch.\
\
You have defended Zudrugund from the uruks, and Corunir now wants you to report of your success to Halbarad.","The book-shelves that so agitated Nár are on the upper level, on the north side of the library in Zudrugund.\
\
Corunir has noted the book-shelves that Nár spent so much time at in the moments before the attack and wants you to search them for information that might be of use.","Talk to Corunir in Zudrugund"}},
[3308]={nameES="Capítulo 8: Mazog en la red",objectivesES={"Issuriel está en Gadorgar, una sala de almacenamiento dentro de las ruinas de Ost Galadh.\
\
Debilitado por los efectos del gwigael, Issuriel tiene algo que decir sobre la misión de la Guardia Oculta.","Issuriel y los Elfos de la Guardia Oculta están ahora listos para llevar a Mazog en la siguiente etapa del viaje a Dol Guldur: una ruta peligrosa a través de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas.","Capítulo 8: Mazog en la red","Habla con Achardor en Ost Galadh","Habla con Bróin en Ost Galadh","Habla con Issuriel en Ost Galadh","Habla con Issuriel y viaja por Râd Iorist con la Guardia Oculta","Issuriel tose débilmente y lucha por hablar.\
\
'Yo... no... quiero que la Guardia Oculta... falle. Mazog... Mazog no puede morir.'","Bróin está en Gadorgar, una sala de almacenamiento dentro de las ruinas de Ost Galadh.\
\
Achardor está al límite de su temperamento, y se necesitará mucho para evitar que mate a Mazog en su frustración. Bróin desea razonar con él.","Achardor está en Gadorgar, una sala de almacenamiento dentro de las ruinas de Ost Galadh.\
\
El viaje a través de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas resultó desastroso: tanto Mazog como Issuriel han sido envenenados por el letal veneno gwigael. Achardor está furioso y debe ser calmado."}},
[3309]={nameES="Capítulo 8: El alcance de Mazog",objectivesES={"Bósi se encuentra en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, en la entrada sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Brogur te ha pedido que le lleves a Bósi noticias de la victoria de su hijo sobre Ashpar y los orcos de la Mano Blanca en Moria.","Capítulo 8: El alcance de Mazog","Brogur te ha pedido que le cuentes a Bósi la victoria de su hijo sobre la Mano Blanca en Moria.","Habla con Bósi en la Cámara de la Encrucijada"}},
[3310]={nameES="Capítulo 8: Nueva Diablería",objectivesES={"Dithaliwenn ha encontrado una pista sobre el paradero del elfo perdido Magor cerca de Azanarukâr, y Lenglammel quiere que lo encuentres.","Habla con Lenglammel y ve a Azanarukâr","Lenglammel se encuentra en su campamento de Gwathrendath, entre las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
Has ganado una gran victoria en las profundidades bajo Moria, y deberías hablar ahora con Lenglammel.","Capítulo 8: Nueva Diablería","Lenglammel se encuentra en su campamento de Gwathrendath, entre las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
Lenglammel quiere que hables con ella sobre tu viaje a Azanarukâr en busca de Magor y el misterioso mal que habita allí.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: La inspiración te ayudará si decides emprender este desafío. Esta instancia solo se puede completar en solitario o en grupo de dos personas.</rgb>"}},
[3311]={nameES="Capítulo 8: Las profundidades del deber",objectivesES={"Corunir is at Aughaire, the settlement of the Trev Gallorg, in Angmar.\
\
You have rescued Golodir from the depths of Nûrz Ghâshu and should speak now with Corunir, your ally on that journey.","Capítulo 8: Las profundidades del deber","Completa la escaramuza: Rescate en Nûrz Ghâshu","Habla con Corunir en Aughaire","The Ranger Corunir is at Aughaire, the settlement of the Trev Gallorg in Angmar.\
\
You must go with Corunir into danger if Golodir is to be rescued.","The Ranger Corunir is at Aughaire, the settlement of the Trev Gallorg in Angmar.\
\
Lothrandir has told you where you might find Corunir, that he may be called to the muster of the Grey Company.","Lothrandir has sent you to speak with Corunir, a Ranger who has lived for many years in the settlement of Aughaire, in Angmar."}},
[3312]={nameES="Chapter 8: The Dreadful Dourhands",objectivesES={"Chapter 8: The Dreadful Dourhands","Talk to Prince Ingór","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to the Zhélruka and to fight on their behalf in Gundabad.","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you."}},
[3313]={nameES="Capítulo 8: El Camino Secreto",objectivesES={"La entrada a Zurr-thurkh, el camino secreto, se encuentra en las profundidades de Buzun-ghâr, donde luchaste contra Grawulun el Caerog.\
\
Orvar ha aceptado encontrarse contigo dentro de Zurr-thurkh, si puedes encontrar la entrada, para montar el rescate de Bori de las garras de Mazog.","Corunothiel está en Lossathrod, el campamento en Buzun-ghâr.\
\
Has salido de Rushdurinul victorioso sobre Mazog, pero has recibido la desafortunada noticia de que Bori y los otros cautivos han sido enviados a Dol Guldur con Gorothúl. Corunothiel espera para hablar contigo.","Encuentra la entrada a Zurr-thurkh y úsala para llegar detrás de los muros de Zabadgathol","Capítulo 8: El Camino Secreto","Has encontrado los planos de un túnel secreto de escape desde la sala del trono de Durin. Si alguna vez fue construido, podría usarse para entrar en secreto a Zabadgathol y rescatar a Bori.","Orvar Martillo de Campana está en Buzun-ghâr, al suroeste de la Senda Pacífica, en la esquina más al sureste de Tharâkh Bazân, por el Camino de Durin.\
\
Bróin te ha pedido que hables con el enano Orvar para que te acompañe por el camino secreto hacia Rushdurinul."}},
[3314]={nameES="Capítulo 8: La Sala Vigesimoprimera",objectivesES={"Animados por su éxito en las minas, muchos de los enanos han seguido a Brogur más al este, hacia la Sala Vigesimoprimera.","Brogur está en la Cámara de Liderazgo, una pequeña sala junto a la Sala Vigesimoprimera en Zelem-melek.\
\
Brogur ha llevado a una compañía de enanos más al este en Moria, y ha establecido una nueva base de operaciones en la Cámara de Liderazgo, junto a la Sala Vigesimoprimera.","Capítulo 8: La Sala Vigesimoprimera"}},
[3315]={nameES="Chapter 9.1: A New Dawn for Umbar",objectivesES={"Act naturally!","Daxamat stands within the entryway of Dâr Laja.","Enter the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja in the Upper Ward","Jajax is keeping an eye on the coffer containing suggestions for those who might join the leadership of the Kindred of the Coins, and he would like you to do the same.","Daxamat told you his brother Jajax has gone to speak with the Kindred in the main hall of Dâr Laja.","Examine the suggestions coffer at the foot of Hármelak's dais in Dâr Laja","Daxamat nods to you in greeting","Vigilant guards keep a watchful eye on the suggestions coffer inside Dâr Laja.","Hármelak has called for you to speak with her in the main hall of Dâr Laja.","Talk to Jajax in the main hall of Dâr Laja","Talk to Hármelak in the main hall of Dâr Laja","The Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl has now been opened to the people of the city so they may bring their concerns before the Kindred of the Coins.","The Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja has been opened at the command of the Kindred of the Coins, and a new dawn rises in Umbar.","Talk to Daxamat in the entryway of Dâr Laja","Hármelak, the Golden Queen, calls for you to attend her","Vigilant guards stand by the coffer, ensuring the rules are followed","Chapter 9.1: A New Dawn for Umbar"}},
[3316]={nameES="Chapter 9.1: The Jailor Jailed",objectivesES={"Trausti stands south-east of the fortress of Shakhajât, pleased to have retrieved his axe.","Talk to Durin north of Maergrind in Máttugard","The goblin Glúrkub has given you information concerning the hobgoblin who took Trausti's axe, but can he be trusted? According to Glúrkub, the hobgoblin can be found living in a dwelling south-east of the fortress of Shakhajât.","Shoshraf emerges from the house, ready to fight!","Eskil and Trausti are keeping watch over the captive goblin north of Maergrind and down one level, in Máttugard.","Talk to the goblin Glúrkub north of Maergrind and down one level, in Máttugard","Talk to Trausti north of Maergrind","Summon and defeat the hobgoblin Shoshraf in Shakhajât","Shoshraf has barely hit the ground before Trausti wrests the axe from his hand","Talk to Glúrkub, the captive goblin north of Maergrind","Trausti is keeping watch over the captive goblin north of Maergrind.","The goblin Glúrkub is encaged north of Maergrind and down one level, in Máttugard.","Talk to Trausti in Shakhajât","Durin is keeping an eye on the captive goblin north of Maergrind and down one level, in Máttugard.","The Dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ have caught a goblin sneaking around Máttugard, and now he is their prisoner.","Chapter 9.1: The Jailor Jailed","The goblin Glúrkub has been imprisoned by the Gabil'akkâ."}},
[3317]={nameES="Chapter 9.1: Withstand and Overcome",objectivesES={}},
[3318]={nameES="Chapter 9.2: An Expedition to the Anvil",objectivesES={"Inek has commanded that Hórin lead an expedition to the Anvil of Winterstith in pursuit of Karazgar, and he invited you to join the raiding party.","Talk to Vútro the West-wind in Skarháld","Chapter 9.2: An Expedition to the Anvil","Durin is on the upper level of Skarháld.","Vútro has reluctantly agreed to stay behind","Vútro the West-wind is south-east of Durin and down two levels, among the tents of the Zhélruka in Skarháld.","Talk to Durin on the upper level of Skarháld"}},
[3319]={nameES="Chapter 9.2: Tatháta Unaccounted",objectivesES={"Chapter 9.2: Tatháta Unaccounted","The Temámir guard asks you for the password","Talk to Birûk in Mekab-kuphâr","Mûluget is waiting for you to speak the phrase Khôltekh gave to you.","Khôltekh told you to go inside the southern entrance to Khabârkhad, where his folk guard an entrance to Umbar-môkh, the caverns and passages beneath Umbar Baharbêl.","Khôltekh will wish to speak with you in Dâr Laja.","Although the leaders of the Kindred of the Coins possess renewed optimism for the future of their city, questions remain about their missing kinswoman Tatháta.","Speak the password to Ayâl through the doors and down the corridor to the north-west","Find the entrance to Umbar-môkh that Khôltekh suggested","Tekûl stares impassively at you but grunts that you may pass his door","Mûluget nods and permits you to pass","Birûk has been assigned the task of helping you while you are within Umbar-môkh. You will find him to the north-west in Mekab-kuphâr.","Speak the password to Tekûl down the stairs","Tekûl is further ahead and down the stairs, waiting for you to speak the phrase Khôltekh gave to you.","Speak the password to Mûluget","Talk to Khôltekh in the main hall of Dâr Laja","Ayâl is beyond the doors and down the hall to the north-west, waiting for you to speak the phrase Khôltekh gave to you."}},
[3320]={nameES="Chapter 9.2: The Divided Loyalties of Glúrkub the Goblin",objectivesES={"Prince Durin is furious, enraged with Glúrkub's story.","Chapter 9.2: The Divided Loyalties of Glúrkub the Goblin","Talk to the prisoner and experience 'The Divided Loyalties of Glúrkub the Goblin'","The goblin Glúrkub has a tale to tell, but whether or not he can be trusted is up to you and to the Dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ.","The goblin Glúrkub wants to tell you his side of the story. He is caged north of Maergrind and down one level, in Máttugard.","Durin seethes with anger","Glúrkub is caged north of Maergrind and down one level, in Máttugard.","Talk to Durin by the cage","Talk to Glúrkub"}},
[3321]={nameES="Chapter 9.3: A Price for Every Answer",objectivesES={"Find the axe that was misplaced somewhere at Sektakhâb","The Temámir dwarf Birûk has been volunteered to help you discover what happened to Tatháta.","Talk to Corudan at Mekab-kuphâr","Because the axe does not fit inside the collection box, you should just lean it against the wall by the notice board.","This must be the axe you learned about from the notice board","Chapter 9.3: A Price for Every Answer","Deliver the old jewellery and the axe to the collection box at Mekab-kuphâr","Birûk told you to examine the notice board to the south-west in Mekab-kuphâr to see how you can busy yourself while he seeks information concerning Tatháta's whereabouts.","Wights stalk the halls of Sektakhâb. Facing them may impress the Temámir","Corudan and Sigileth have arrived at Mekab-kuphâr.","Examine the notice board to the south-west in Mekab-kuphâr","You deposit the old jewellery into the box, but the axe does not fit","Lean the axe against the wall by the notice board","Dealing with the wights at Sektakhâb, located to the west of Mekab-kuphâr, may encourage the Temámir to help you.","The notice board directed you to leave the things you recovered from Sektakhâb in the box back at Mekab-kuphâr.","<rgb=#FFFF00>The Dead That Walk</rgb>\
The bodies of the slain and interred remain not at rest, but are animated by spirits of evil and must be made still. Many can be found at Sektakhâb to the west.\
\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Arms Loosed From Their Bodies</rgb>\
Of great danger to the unwary, grasping arms crawl along by their fingertips and are not to be underestimated. Look for them among the crypts at Sektakhâb to the west.\
\
<rgb=#FFFF00>My Misplaced Axe</rgb>\
I lost my axe at Sektakhâb! Its edge has been dulled due to much use, but it is still of great sentimental value to me and I would have it returned. Leave it in the collection box if you bring it back, because I have business outside the city for several weeks and will not be back for some time.\
\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Valuable Trinkets and Jewelleries</rgb>\
It may be distasteful to some, but the valuables worn by the Dead at Sektakhâb are of no use to them, and might be of great use for the Temámir. Any concerns may be brought directly to Khôltekh, but the valuables should be left in the collection box.","As you lean the axe against the wall, you feel eyes upon you"}},
[3322]={nameES="Chapter 9.3: A Question of Trust",objectivesES={"Durin has ordered you to kill the goblin prisoner.","After a brief moment, Glúrkub speaks up: a thoughtful squeak","Chapter 9.3: A Question of Trust","Glúrkub is encaged in Máttugard.","Durin falls silent at last, his face a mask","Glóin is by the cage in Máttugard.","Glóin is standing by the cage, eyeing Durin warily.","Talk to Glúrkub","Durin has calmed himself somewhat, but the prince still disbelieves the goblin's story.","Durin is by the cage holding Glúrkub.","Durin is furious at the words of Glúrkub and at Glóin's betrayal of his commands.","Talk to Glóin by the cage","Kill Glúrkub","Durin is beside himself with rage at Glúrkub's story, and refuses to believe that he has been made a dragon's puppet.","Talk to Durin by the cage","Glóin catches your arm. 'Do not do this!' he warns you","The prince breathes heavily. Some of his rage departs"}},
[3323]={nameES="Chapter 9.3: Another Way In",objectivesES={"Climb the ladder inside the keep of Skarháld","Rocks fall and seal the exit of the escape tunnel","A tunnel winds into the mountains behind Tharrazhâr, the keep of Skarháld, and Kozun went inside to investigate. Kámat has asked you to find his friend and ensure his safety.","Find the entrance to the tunnel in the back of Tharrazhâr","The cave-mouth has been successfully sealed by rocks","While Inek focuses on taking the fight to Karazgar at the Anvil, Durin wishes to ensure that Skarháld is made ready for his possible return.","Kámat waves to you and calls you over","Gandalf has come to Skarháld with a small party of dwarves!","Chapter 9.3: Another Way In","Durin asked you to investigate the upper levels of Tharrazhâr, the formerly-inaccessible keep of Skarháld.","Talk to Kozun at the bottom of the tunnel","Return to Durin on the upper level of Skarháld","Collapse the cave-mouth at the bottom of the escape tunnel","Talk to Kámat on the upper level of Tharrazhâr","Find the bottom of the winding tunnel behind Tharrazhâr","Durin stands on the upper level of Skarháld among a group of new arrivals, including a familiar Wizard.","Kozun has asked for your help in collapsing the cave-mouth at the bottom of the escape tunnel behind Tharrazhâr.","You have successfully collapsed the exit of the escape tunnel, and should now return to Durin on the upper level of Skarháld.","Talk to Durin on the upper level of Skarháld","Strange sounds echo up from the depths of the winding tunnel","You found the bottom of the tunnel, where it empties onto a sloping path north-west of Skarháld","Kámat and Kozun explored the upper level of Tharrazhâr, the keep of Skarháld, and found a tunnel winding deep into the mountain. Kámat asked you to defeat any enemies you find within the chambers of the keep or in the tunnel."}},
[3324]={nameES="Chapter 9.4: A Look at Lugroz",objectivesES={"Orcs prowl the Welkin-lofts, and Durin has asked you to defeat those you find there.","Talk to Durin by the cage north of Maergrind, in Máttugard","Durin thinks you should investigate the Welkin-lofts and see what you can learn about the relationship between Gorgar the Ruthless and Hrímil Frost-heart.","Find a hiding place nearby, perhaps in the stand of trees to the north-west","Talk to Glúrkub in Máttugard","A number of weapons rest in the rack, but the mithril hammer is missing","Find the path to the summit in the south-east heights of the Welkin-lofts","You need to find a hiding place nearby! Perhaps one could be found in the stand of trees to the north-west.","Chapter 9.4: A Look at Lugroz","Examine the weapon rack by the path to the summit","This place might serve to hide you when Gorgar goes to meet with the dragon","The path to the summit can be found atop a snow-covered terrace in the south-eastern heights of the Welkin-lofts.","Durin is north of Maergrind and down one level, by the cage holding Glúrkub in Máttugard.","A weapon rack stands by the path to the summit, as Glúrkub described.","Defeat Orcs in the Welkin-lofts (5/6)","A weapon rack stands by the path to the summit","Glúrkub is encaged north of Maergrind and down one level, in Máttugard.","You find a pouch of colourful stones on the Orc; Bróin will want to see this"}},
[3325]={nameES="Chapter 9.4: An Unexpected Delivery",objectivesES={"Talk to Gandalf on the upper level of Skarháld","Chapter 9.4: An Unexpected Delivery","Gandalf has come to Skarháld with a small party of dwarves including Hrostyr, the personal guard of King Thorin.","Gandalf has come to Skarháld and stands on the upper level of the fortress."}},
[3326]={nameES="Chapter 9.4: Trail of the Sea-beast",objectivesES={"Chapter 9.4: Trail of the Sea-beast","Sigileth holds her unnamed blade at the ready, eager to keep the Corsairs busy while her brother searches Tatháta's ship.","You have located another entrance to the hidden harbour","Wait for Corudan to depart","Sigileth stands by the entrance to the hidden harbour, staring out at the docked ships.","Corudan stands by the entrance to the hidden harbour.","Corudan listens to your report with growing unease.\
\
'He is gone?'","Talk to Corudan by the entrance of the hidden harbour","Corudan will rely on you to keep the Corsairs busy while he searches the ship","That is peculiar. Birûk is missing","Sigileth surveys the harbour briefly before repeating her original assessment.\
\
'This will make discovering Tatháta's trail more difficult,' she says.","Talk to Sigileth in the hidden harbour","Corudan and Sigileth will want to hear what you learned. They are still at at Mekab-kuphâr, but both of the Elves are eager to depart.","Talk to Corudan at Mekab-kuphâr","Corudan and Sigileth have descended into Umbar-môkh to help you find Tatháta's trail.","Birûk has returned to Mekab-kuphâr and may have learned something that will help you learn what happened to Tatháta.","Corudan and Sigileth suggested that you return to Mekab-kuphâr and ask Birûk what he thinks of the circled areas on the map Corudan retrieved from Tatháta's ship.","Devious Corsairs and their Heirsworn Captains have taken over the hidden harbour in Nakási's absence, and you should keep them busy while Corudan searches Tatháta's ship for some clue to her whereabouts.","Talk to Birûk at Mekab-kuphâr","Corudan and Sigileth have arrived at Mekab-kuphâr.","Return to Mekab-kuphâr and ask Birûk about the map Corudan recovered","Corudan has returned to the entrance of the hidden harbour, but whether he found anything of use remains in doubt.","Corudan hurries away, his feet making little sound on either wood or rock.","Talk to Corudan in the hidden harbour","An entrance to the hidden harbour can be found in the south-eastern corner of Dil-irmíz.","Find an entrance to the hidden harbour in the south-eastern corner of Dil-irmíz"}},
[3327]={nameES="Chapter 9.5: A Theft of Freedom",objectivesES={}},
[3328]={nameES="Chapter 9.5: How Do You Do It?",objectivesES={"You located Birûk, but he needs your help!","Find someone at Mekab-kuphâr who might know what happened to Birûk","<rgb=#FFFF00>Spiders of Nishabêt</rgb>\
Someone should do something about the spiders that have infested the chamber to the north of Mekab-kuphâr in Khabârkhad. They are contained within Nishabêt for now, but who can say how long they will remain there?\
\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Grave-robbers at Lôkhalel</rgb>\
Brigands and grave-robbers are plundering the chambers at Lôkhalel, north-west of Mekab-kuphâr, stealing valuables that belong to us. Someone needs to tell them that this is our territory!","Wait for Birûk to escape","Birûk said he would meet you at Itekh-kên, in the northern reaches of Khabârkhad.","Corudan suggested that you ask dwarves at Mekab-kuphâr if any of them saw where Birûk might have gone.","You have found Birûk, and he is in trouble!","Gêzheg does not know where Birûk has gone, but he did notice the dwarf studying the notice board at some point in the last few hours.","Talk to Corudan at Mekab-kuphâr","Talk to Birûk at Itekh-kên in the northern reaches of Khabârkhad","Examine the notice board at Mekab-kuphâr","Talk to Birûk and help him escape from danger","Search for Birûk at Nishabêt or Lôkhalel","You believe Birûk has gone to complete one of the two tasks posted on the notice board, either to combat the spiders of Nishabêt to the north, or to face the grave-robbers of Lôkhalel to the north-west. Whichever of the locations you do not search will be visited by Corudan and Sigileth.","As you go to leave, you notice the axe you left here is now missing","Birûk has escaped from danger. You should meet up with him at Itekh-kên","Decide between Nishabêt or Lôkhalel, and the Elves will search where you do not","Corudan will want to hear what you think might have happened to Birûk. The Elf has returned to Mekab-kuphâr with Sigileth.","Chapter 9.5: How Do You Do It?","Your Temámir contact Birûk has gone missing from Mekab-kuphâr while you investigated the hidden harbour.","Birûk flees for safety!"}},
[3329]={nameES="Chapter 9.5: Report from Winterstith",objectivesES={"Talk to Dolek on the upper level of Skarháld","Mudro is to the north-east of Gandalf, on the upper level of Skarháld.","Talk to Gandalf inside the chamber that was given to him in the north-east corner of the upper level of Skarháld","Gandalf has come to Skarháld, but before he will share what he has learned from the Black Book of Mordor, he wishes to hear what happened to the dwarf-expedition to the Anvil of Winterstith.","Talk to Ibor on the upper level of Skarháld","Ibor is to the north-west of Dolek, on the upper level of Skarháld.","Talk to Mudro on the upper level of Skarháld","Gandalf is in the chamber that was prepared for him in the north-east corner of the upper level of Skarháld.","Chapter 9.5: Report from Winterstith","Dolek is to the south-west of Mudro, on the upper level of Skarháld."}},
[3330]={nameES="Chapter 9.5: Report from Winterstith",objectivesES={"Talk to Dolek on the upper level of Skarháld","Mudro is to the north-east of Gandalf, on the upper level of Skarháld.","Talk to Gandalf inside the chamber that was given to him in the north-east corner of the upper level of Skarháld","Gandalf has come to Skarháld, but before he will share what he has learned from the Black Book of Mordor, he wishes to hear what happened to the dwarf-expedition to the Anvil of Winterstith.","Talk to Ibor on the upper level of Skarháld","Ibor is to the north-west of Dolek, on the upper level of Skarháld.","Talk to Mudro on the upper level of Skarháld","Gandalf is in the chamber that was prepared for him in the north-east corner of the upper level of Skarháld.","Chapter 9.5: Report from Winterstith","Dolek is to the south-west of Mudro, on the upper level of Skarháld."}},
[3331]={nameES="Chapter 9.6: Painting the Picture",objectivesES={"Talk to Gandalf in his chamber at Skarháld and learn of his discoveries from the Black Book","Gandalf is in the chamber granted to him by Durin at Skarháld, studying the Black Book of Mordor.","Chapter 9.6: Painting the Picture","Gandalf is in the chamber of Skarháld given to him by Durin, waiting to discuss with you the contents of the Black Book of Mordor.","Talk to Gandalf in his chamber at Skarháld"}},
[3332]={nameES="Chapter 9.6: Unseen Ones",objectivesES={"You set down the meal and wine and wait for Tephísa to return","Birûk suggested that you defeat rats and crocodiles within Ilmabiri.","The empty metal plate in the south-eastern corner of Ilmabiri waits for the bread Birûk gave to you.","You hear a girl's voice from the darkness beyond the grate in the south-eastern corner of Ilmabiri.","The Terâsi girl you encountered in Ilmabiri asked you to retrieve a meal of higher quality from the Upper Ward, as well as a bottle of fancy wine, or she will tell you nothing. The tables at the Baths of Ilmai Iforikh in the Upper Ward may have what you need.","The empty metal plate in the south-eastern corner of Ilmabiri waits for the meal and wine you \\qretrieved\\q from the Upper Ward.","Find the metal plate in the south-eastern corner of Ilmabiri","Makhíl agrees to let you go. \\qKindred business,\\q he says with a wink","You set the bread on the plate. If Birûk is right, now you just need to wait","Wait for the Terâsi girl Tephísa to return","Wait and see if you are contacted by one of the Terâsi","You hear someone moving quietly in the darkness beyond the grate","Birûk has given you a curious directive that he insists will help you track down Tatháta's location within Umbar-môkh.","Place the meal and wine on the metal plate in the south-eastern corner of Ilmabiri","Place the crusty bread on the metal plate in the south-eastern corner of Ilmabiri","You hear someone moving about in the darkness","Birûk told you to find a metal plate in the south-eastern corner of Ilmabiri.","Chapter 9.6: Unseen Ones","Once again, Tephísa's voice floats from the darkness.\
\
'This is much better fare, stranger. You have my thanks.\
\
'Now tell me again what you wished to learn.'","Birûk told you that leaving food here should summon one of the Terâsi, the forgotten ones of Umbar-môkh. Now you must wait and see if he was right.","The Terâsi girl you encountered in Ilmabiri asked you to retrieve a meal of higher quality from the Upper Ward, as well as a bottle of fancy wine, or she will tell you nothing. The tables at the Baths of Ilmai Iforikh may have what you need.","Talk to the girl in the darkness beyond the grate in the south-eastern corner of Ilmabiri","Steal an unattended bottle of wine from the Baths of Ilmai Iforikh in the Upper Ward","Talk to Tephísa, the Terâsi girl in the darkness at the south-eastern corner of Ilmabiri","A girl's voice drifts out of the darkness.\
\
'When people leave food out for us, they do not wait. Maybe you did not know this.'\
\
You respond that you were hoping to speak to someone who might know what happened to Tatháta, Kinswoman of the Lower Ward. The silence stretches for so long that it seems possible the unseen speaker has slipped away, but your patience is rewarded at last.\
\
'I might know something, but this bread is not enough. I want a true meal, something fancy. And wine! Bring me a meal and wine from the Upper Ward, and I may tell you what I know.'\
\
A sudden scuffling sound in the darkness tells you the girl is about to leave. You call out, asking how she will know you have fulfilled your side of the bargain.\
\
'Tephísa will know,' she calls back, and then you are certain you are alone again.","Your great ability as a Burglar has allowed you to avoid detection","Steal an unattended meal from the Baths of Ilmai Iforikh in the Upper Ward","Have you been seen?","You must wait once again for the Terâsi girl Tephísa to return.","Tephísa, the Terâsi girl, has returned to the south-eastern corner of Ilmabiri.","This location matches the description given to you by Birûk"}},
[3333]={nameES="Chapter 9.7: The Beast Below",objectivesES={"Corudan and Sigileth have suggested a number of places for you to search throughout Kamrabezûr, and encouraged you to defeat any foes that stand in the way of your investigation.","You explain your intention to learn what befell Tatháta in the days since she was last seen fleeing from the hidden harbour. Silence falls upon Ilmabiri for long moments. At last Tephísa's voice floats back to you.\
\
'Many of us live in the tunnels, stranger: more than you might think. Our eyes see much that the Temámir do not, for we can reach places even they cannot go; perhaps they choose not to go there, but we have not that choice. All of Umbar-môkh is our domain, and while the city is big, Umbar-môkh has vastness of a different kind.\
\
'A friend of mine witnessed Tatháta's flight. By secret paths he followed her, unseen, but he was not her only pursuer. An Umbari warrior-woman chased at her heels, deadly daggers flashing in the torch-light. He pursued them both into Kamrabezûr, but among those vaults he lost their trail. Many abandoned temples to the Church of the All-Seeing can be found in that place; it may be Tatháta gained entrance to one of those, and stays there now in hiding. Of the other, I cannot say. My friend believes Tatháta must have given her the slip as well, leaving her no choice but to return to the city above. That seems most likely to me.\
\
'Good-bye, stranger. I thank you for the food and for the wine! I hope Tephísa has been a help to you.'\
\
There is a brief rustling sound, and you know the girl has disappeared once again into the deeper darkness of Umbar-môkh.","Corudan stands at Kên Taghlim in north-western Kamrabezûr.","Corudan stands beside Galatâni's grave outside the city.","Sigileth stands at Kên Taghlim in north-western Kamrabezûr, prepared to go with you in search of Tatháta's hiding-place.","Corudan and Sigileth have also arrived at Kên Taghlim","Birûk waits for you at Itekh-kên in Khabârkhad, and may be able to guide your search of Kamrabezûr for Tatháta.","Talk to Corudan by the grave","Search the centre of the cultist camp of Jâx Ugikh for Tatháta","Talk to Corudan at Kên Taghlim in north-western Kamrabezûr","Birûk suggested that you go to Kên Taghlim in the north-western reaches of Kamrabezûr, but that you should steer clear of the great beasts rumoured to have escaped from the arena.","Cultists mass in these halls, but there is no sign of Tatháta","The unruly Dead stalk these corridors, but there is no sign of Tatháta","Talk to Sigileth at Kên Taghlim and go with her in search of Tatháta","Hostile veterans of Dahâl Huliz encamp here, but there is no sign of Tatháta among them","Search the centre of Harkhaphâr for Tatháta","Talk to Corudan at Kên Taghlim","Chapter 9.7: The Beast Below","The information you learned from Tephísa guides you to Kamrabezûr in the north-eastern reaches of Umbar-môkh.","Search the centre of Ghâr Mejet for Tatháta","Find Kên Taghlim in north-western Kamrabezûr","Talk to Birûk at Itekh-kên in Khabârkhad"}},
[3334]={nameES="Chapter 9.7: The Wind and the Warrior",objectivesES={"Find frost-drake tracks to the south along the road","Talk to Vútro the West-wind by the hidden path among the rocks","By following frost-drake tracks in the Ered Mithrin, you found a hidden path climbing into the mountains. Did drakes of the Frost-horde come this way in search of Karazgar?","Chapter 9.7: The Wind and the Warrior","Talk to Vútro the West-wind outside Skarháld.","Find frost-drake tracks further south along the road","Someone wants to meet you on the road to the Glimmerdeep, and you should find out who it is.","A steep path climbs north-east to a shadowy cave entrance","A dwarf has come to Gandalf's chamber in Skarháld, and he has a message for you.","Climb the steep hidden path you discovered","Vútro the West-wind leans on his staff and nods in greeting","A partially-hidden path leads up among the rocks to the north-west","Frost-drakes passed this way in great numbers, heading south","You followed frost-drake tracks to a partially-hidden path that winds its way up the mountains. Vútro the West-wind stands at the start of the path, eager to speak with you.","Talk to the Zhélruka messenger in Gandalf's chamber at Skarháld","Vútro the West-wind saw frost-drake tracks to the south, and he thinks following them will lead you to the wounded Karazgar.","Search along the road to the Glimmerdeep to find the message's sender","Vútro the West-wind is on the road leading to the Glimmerdeep.","Vútro the West-wind is inside the shadowy cave you discovered high among the rocks in the Ered Mithrin.","Talk to Vútro the West-wind inside the cave","Gandalf has come to Skarháld with the Black Book of Mordor, but the situation in the Ered Mithrin will not wait for the Wizard to finish his research, and there are other demands on your time."}},
[3335]={nameES="Chapter 9.8: Karazgar Cornered",objectivesES={"These drakes of the Frost-horde were slain by some sharp instrument","Judging from its injuries, this drake engaged in fierce battle before it was slain","Small piles of rust shine in the pale light of the cavern","Vútro the West-wind has entered the large chamber at the rear of Karazgar's lair.","Search the lair for some sign of Karazgar","Steam still rises from the blood, even in the cavern's cold air","You have come with Vútro the West-wind to a cavern in the Ered Mithrin that may have served as Karazgar's lair. But where is the Weeping Warrior now?","Vútro the West-wind has asked you to search Karazgar's lair for some sign of the Weeping Warrior.","Chapter 9.8: Karazgar Cornered","The drake-corpse is warm to the touch. The creature has not been dead for long","The tunnel opens into a large cavern filled with the corpses of worms and drakes","Talk to Vútro the West-wind in Karazgar's lair"}},
[3336]={nameES="Chapter 9.8: Last Dance",objectivesES={"Talk to Hármelak in the main hall of Dâr Laja","You should leave Galatâni's dagger on the grave.","Hármelak waits in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja to hear what you have learned about Tatháta from your time seeking her in Umbar-môkh.","Chapter 9.8: Last Dance","Hármelak waits in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja to hear what you have learned about Tatháta.","Sigileth stands by the grave, deep in thought.","Talk to Sigileth by the grave","You have emerged from Umbar-môkh with tidings of Tatháta for the Kindred of the Coins, but your information may herald trouble on the horizon.","Return to Hármelak in the main hall of Dâr Laja","Leave Galatâni's dagger on the grave","Hármelak eyes you carefully as you approach the dais, her expression unreadable"}},
[3337]={nameES="Chapter 9.9: A Promise Kept",objectivesES={"Gandalf stands on the upper level of Skarháld following his confrontation with Karazgar.","Talk to Gandalf on the upper level of Skarháld","Explore the tunnel with Vútro the West-wind","Talk to Vútro the West-wind outside the cave mouth north-west of Skarháld","Karazgar's lair is filled with dead drakes of the Frost-horde that followed him from Winterstith, but the Weeping Warrior is nowhere to be found. Where can he have gone?","Vútro the West-wind has called for a halt north-west of Skarháld, near a cave entrance.","Chapter 9.9: A Promise Kept"}},
[3338]={nameES="Chapter 9.9: The Name",objectivesES={"Hármelak is in the main hall of Dâr Laja, waiting to speak with you again.","Talk to Jaith outside Dâr Laja","Talk to Rothog in Dâr Laja","Talk to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja","Talk to Belondor in Dâr Laja","Jajax has some words for you in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja.","Chapter 9.9: The Name","Talk to Hármelak in Dâr Laja","The guardsman Jaith stands outside the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja. Hármelak has asked that you warn him to keep watch in case Tatháta assaults the entrance in search of you or the leaders of the Kindred.","Hármelak suggested that you speak with the other leaders of the Kindred of the Coins in the main hall of Dâr Laja about the dangers their people will face in the days ahead.","One name was placed in the suggestions coffer inside Dâr Laja more than any other.","Talk to Jajax in Dâr Laja"}},
[3339]={nameES="Capítulo 9: Un arma de los días antiguos",objectivesES={"Los enanos están desesperados por encontrar algún medio de derrotar al Guardián que espera en el Lago Negro, frente a las Muros de Moria.","Capítulo 9: Un arma de los días antiguos","Hundi está en Echad Dúnann, no muy lejos al oeste de Rathwald, en Eregion.\
\
Rathwald te ha enviado a hablar con su amigo Hundi, quien ayudó en la recuperación de una la caja con armas que podrían ser provechosas."}},
