[4805]={nameES="Epilogue: A Mending",objectivesES={"Caebar waits for you in the Tor-gardens outside Dâr Tabib.","Talk to Caebar in Dâr Tabib","Talk to Sigileth in Dâr Tabib","Retrieve Corudan's notes about the Fearwater from the satchel at the foot of his bed","Caebar thinks for a moment about what you have shown him.","Caebar is in Dâr Tabib.","Talk to Corudan in Dâr Tabib","Corudan lies in one of the beds of Dâr Tabib.","The Apothecary of Dâr Tabib is located in the Tor-gardens of Umbar Baharbêl.","Wait for Caebar to speak again","Epilogue: A Mending","Sigileth watches over her brother in Dâr Tabib.","Talk to Caebar in the Tor-gardens outside Dâr Tabib","Talk to Sigileth in Dâr Tabib and hear her account of their return to the city","Many of the beds of Dâr Tabib are occupied by the wounded","You retrieve a sheaf of Corudan's notes from the satchel","The recent upheavals scarred the city, but now it begins to heal, as do some of the companions who fought by your side.","Someone new has come to Dâr Tabib","Enter the Apothecary of Dâr Tabib in the Tor-gardens of Umbar Baharbêl","Sigileth is in Dâr Tabib.","Bring Corudan's notes to Caebar in Dâr Tabib","Caebar bids farewell to Corudan and Sigileth and departs Dâr Tabib","Caebar stands in the Tor-gardens outside Dâr Tabib.","Caebar emerges from his musings with a nod","Corudan's possessions can be found in the satchel at the foot of his bed.","And as a light breeze passes over the sea, thus ends 'The Song of Waves and Wind'"}},
[4806]={nameES="Epilogue: Amardam, the Ancient Evil",objectivesES={"Cánnakh se encuentra en Aughaire.\
\
Deberías hablar con Cánnakh.","Cánnakh has located the lost power, a Caerog buried in the Duvuinen Swamp. He asks for you to wake and defeat the slumbering evil before someone else finds it and Amardam regains its full strength.","Habla con Cánnakh","Defeat Amardam","Epilogue: Amardam, the Ancient Evil","Defeated Amardam","The rocks begin to move as the Caerog springs to life","Amardam can be found somewhere in the Duvuinen Swamp.\
\
You should awake and defeat Amardam."}},
[4807]={nameES="Epilogue: An Incomplete Key",objectivesES={"Wait for the metalworker to forge a key using the mould","The metalworker hands you the newly-forged key","Khîl Tale-spinner hurries toward you, and the metalworker falls silent","Metalworkers can be found on the lower level of Járnfast.","Khîl Tale-spinner has returned to the hidden chamber built by his thrice-great grandfather Vóin.","The newly-forged key should now be ready","The key clicks in the lock. Inside the box you find a small shard of glass, and nothing else","Is it possible that Khîl Tale-spinner might know something about the broken key given to you by Gothmog?","The metalworkers are by the forges on the lower level of Járnfast.","Khîl gives you the mould that matches the broken key","Unlock the tiny locked box in the hidden chamber","Khîl Tale-spinner is in the hidden chamber built by his thrice-great grandfather Vóin.","Talk to a metalworker by the forges on the lower level of Járnfast","Talk to Khîl Tale-spinner by the forges on the lower level of Járnfast","Gandalf may know what to make of the strange glass shard. Look for him at the Beorninghús","Bring the glass shard to Gandalf inside the Beorninghús","Gandalf intended to travel north with the casket containing the bones of Isildur, and should have arrived at the Beorninghús by now. You should bring him the glass shard you found within the tiny locked box from Khîl's home.","Find someone who knows about the broken key","Give the broken key to Khîl Tale-spinner in the hidden chamber","The metalworker is by the forges on the lower level of Járnfast. He should have finished forging the key by now.","You must find someone who knows what the broken key might once have unlocked. But who could hold that secret?","Epilogue: An Incomplete Key","Gothmog gave you a broken key as he died, but you do not know what it might have unlocked when whole. Unless your guess is wrong, it seems as if Gothmog himself did not know.","Khîl Tale-spinner is by the forges in Járnfast.","Talk to the metalworker by the forges in Járnfast","Talk to Khîl in the hidden chamber in his home","The metalworker needs some time to fashion a new key using the mould provided by Khîl Tale-spinner.","Give the mould to the metalworker by the forges in Járnfast","Khîl told you about a tiny locked box that he thought his mother used to store jewels, but perhaps it is far older than that...\
\
He has placed it on the table in the hidden chamber, and waits for you to try the newly-forged key in its lock.","Khîl Tale-spinner smiles a greeting at you as you approach"}},
[4808]={nameES="Epilogue: Closing the Book",objectivesES={"Epilogue: Closing the Book","Together, you and Gandalf have managed to reveal the last of the secrets hidden within the Black Book of Mordor, and the only remaining question concerns the matter of its final disposition.","Deliver the Black Book to Covadil in the Houses of Lore","Deliver the Black Book to Karazgar by the flat stone at the Old Ford","Gandalf gave you the choice of where to bring the Black Book and you have now performed that duty.","Deliver the Black Book to Khîl Tale-spinner in his home","Gandalf has presented you with a choice concerning the ultimate disposition of the Black Book of Mordor.","You stand at the Old Ford and resolve to wait for Karazgar to appear.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>"}},
[4809]={nameES="Epilogue: Endings and Beginnings",objectivesES={"Durin has come to Mótsog's Tomb to speak with the last of the Greymauls before the day is ended.","Durin is in Mótsog's Tomb, thinking about the words of the last Greymaul.","Durin's face is burdened with expectation as he waits for Mótsog's response","Durin is in Mótsog's Tomb, thinking about the road that brought him here... and the road that still lies ahead.","Talk to Durin in Mótsog's Tomb","Wait for Durin to arrive","And so concludes 'The Legacy of Durin and the Trials of the Dwarves'","Durin awaits Mótsog's reply, and does not speak.","The last of the Greymauls has left the world. Only his statue remains","Talk to Mótsog and hear his response","Durin wants to speak with Mótsog before the day is ended.","The entrance to the secret stair that leads to Mótsog's Tomb, deep below Gundabad, is in Zul-mazal.","Epilogue: Endings and Beginnings","Mótsog is gone, and only a statue remains.","Examine the statue of Mótsog","Return to Mótsog's Tomb at the bottom of the secret stair beneath Zul-mazal","Durin studies the statue where Mótsog once stood.","Durin hurries to Mótsog's Tomb to speak with the last of the Greymauls before the day comes to an end."}},
[4810]={nameES="Epilogue: Flight of the Golden Queen",objectivesES={}},
[4811]={nameES="Epilogue: Freed of the Burden",objectivesES={"The shade of Isildur fades from view","His vow fulfilled, the shade of Isildur at last knows peace","Talk to the shade of Isildur at the entrance to Rivendell","Talk to Gandalf by the waggon in Laerlad","Talk to Gandalf by the entrance to Rivendell and complete 'Instance: Freed of the Burden'","The shade of Tárandil fades from view","The shade of Tárandil has made his decision: he will seek out Bravantel and Héol, no matter the torment it will cause him.","Talk to the shade of Isildur by the waggon in Laerlad","Gandalf is by the waggon bearing the bones of Isildur northward, in Laerlad.","Talk to Gandalf by the waggon near the entrance to Rivendell","The waggon bearing the bones of Isildur has come a long way from Gondor, and so have you","The shade of Isildur is by the waggon bearing his bones northward, in Laerlad.","Gandalf is by the waggon bearing Isildur's bones to Rivendell, by the entrance to that secret valley.","The shade of Isildur has at last finished the journey he swore in life to undertake more than three thousand years ago.","The shade of Tárandil bows his head and fades from view","Epilogue: Freed of the Burden","Through the telling of his tale, the shade of Tárandil has achieved the clarity he had lost. It is time for another of the shades that has remained overlong in Middle-earth to find his own respite.","Gandalf is by the waggon bearing Isildur's bones to Rivendell, by the entrance to that secret valley. He has finished reading the secret writing in the Black Book of Mordor, and wishes to tell you the end of that tale.","After a brief rest, the waggon will return to Gondor","Meet up with Gandalf and the waggon bearing the bones of Isildur at the entrance to the valley of Rivendell","Gandalf suggested you catch up with the waggon bearing the bones of Isildur when it arrives at the entrance to the valley of Rivendell."}},
[4812]={nameES="Epilogue: His Father's Son",objectivesES={"Epilogue: His Father's Son","The shade of Isildur stares impassively at Tárandil, and says nothing.","The shade of Tárandil is by the waggon bearing the bones of Isildur northward.","Talk to the shade of Tárandil and complete 'Instance: His Father's Son'","Gandalf is by the waggon bearing the bones of Isildur northward.","The shade of Tárandil has manifested for a single purpose: he wishes to make his confession.","Talk to Gandalf by the waggon in Laerlad"}},
[4813]={nameES="Epilogue: Isildur's Last Journey",objectivesES={"Talk to the shade of Isildur beside the waggon in Laerlad","Talk to Gandalf by the waggon in Laerlad","Talk to Vágari the Wanderer","Vágari the Wanderer has come to this place, enveloped by a feeling of dread","Epilogue: Isildur's Last Journey","Gandalf is by the waggon bearing Isildur's bones through Laerlad.","The shade of Isildur feels the presence of his bones, and follows with interest their northward course along the river.","The waggon bearing Isildur's bones is in Laerlad, on the road beside the Gladden Fields.","Gandalf is by the waggon bearing Isildur's bones, near to the Gladden Fields.","Gandalf journeyed north ahead of the waggon bearing Isildur's bones, and he thinks it is time to check on its progress.","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> for the source of the dread by the waggon","Find the waggon carrying Isildur's bones on the road through Laerlad, beside the Gladden Fields","A sensation of dread surrounds the waggon bearing the bones of Isildur","Gandalf has directed you to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> for the source of the dread near the waggon bearing Isildur's bones.","Talk to Gandalf beside the waggon in Laerlad","Vágari the Wanderer has appeared by the waggon. But why has he chosen to appear now?"}},
[4814]={nameES="Epilogue: Restless Souls",objectivesES={"Treasures of the Second Age can be found in Western Gondor and the Paths of the Dead.\
\
You should seek out the five treasures of the Second Age.","The trinket was once a necklace of the king of the mountain","The amethyst represented the honour of Dunharrow","Drugât leaves you in hopes of one day to finally be at rest","Speak with Drugât","Find the Second Age Crown","The crown symbolized the oath we took for Isildur","Drugât is located in the caverns of Nimrond.\
\
You should return the Second Age treasures to Drugât.","Drugât wishes to reclaim that which should have been rightfully returned to him by Isildur.","Find the Second Age Amethyst","Epilogue: Restless Souls","Drugât wished to speak with you instead of fighting","Drugât has returned to the Vale and must be banished once and for all.","Drugât is located somewhere in the caverns of Nimrond.\
\
You should speak with Drugât.","Find the Second Age Ingot","Find and confront Drugât","Find the Second Age Rune","Find the Second Age Trinket","The rune told the history of Dunharrow","Drugât is located somewhere in the caverns of Nimrond.\
\
You should find and confront Drugât.","The ingot represented the strength of the Men of the Mountain","Return the Second Age treasures to Drugât"}},
[4815]={nameES="Epilogue: Sailing Into The Dawn",objectivesES={"DNT -- will not be seen","Search near Hata Kebir for Jajax and Daxamat","Jajax can be found along the coastline to the south of Aerthir.\
\
You have discovered Jajax and Daxamat resting from readying their ship, and should speak to them.","Search the shores of the Anduin south of Aerthir","Rumours abound of the strange Corsair, Jajax, who aided the Men of Linhir in crippling the Heirs of Castamir.","Aerthir can be found due south of Ost Anglebed along the shores of the Anduin.\
\
You have not found Jajax near Hata Kebir, but you should continue your search along the coast to the south of Aerthir.","Nimithil can be found in Ost Anglebed in north-central Lebennin.\
\
You found Jajax and Daxamat preparing to sail from Lebennin. You should tell Nimithil of your journey.","You discover Jajax and Daxamat preparing a boat!","Jajax can be found along the coastline to the south of Aerthir.\
\
You have shared wine with Jajax and should speak to him once more.","A bottle of wine can be found in the basket next to Jajax.\
\
Jajax has asked you to share a bottle of fine wine with him and Daxamat.","Epilogue: Sailing Into The Dawn","Talk to Jajax","Hata Kebir can be found far to the south-east of Ost Anglebed.\
\
Nimithil has asked you to seek out Jajax, if he still remains in Lebennin. You should begin your search near Hata Kebir.","Return to Nimithil in Ost Anglebed","You have found no sign of the two brothers, and should search further west along the shore","Share a drink with Jajax and Daxamat"}},
[4816]={nameES="Epilogue: The Disaster",objectivesES={"Talk to the shade of Tárandil by the waggon in Laerlad","The shade of Tárandil is by the waggon bearing the bones of Isildur northward.","The shade of Isildur stares impassively at Tárandil, and says nothing.","Talk to the shade of Tárandil and complete 'Instance: The Disaster'","Epilogue: The Disaster","The shade of Tárandil has manifested for a single purpose: he wishes to make his confession."}},
[4817]={nameES="Epilogue: The Ghad Imghêda",objectivesES={"Jínen was on her way to the Gate of Songs north of the city.","Talk to the leadership of Ghad Imghêda at Dâr Rapha","Talk to Jajax at Dâr Rapha","Rothog smiles at you, and his grin seems more ferocious than ever.","Talk to the leadership of the Ghad Imghêda at Dâr Rapha","Some familiar faces await you: the Ghad Imghêda of Umbar Baharbêl","Someone at the Northern Ship-yard around the corner to the east may have further information for you concerning the political situation in Umbar Baharbêl.","Your return to Umbar Baharbêl has revealed a change in the political situation of the city.","Talk to Jínen outside the Gate of Songs","Dâr Rapha is up the hill to the east of the Gate of Songs, outside the city.","Jajax has come to Dâr Rapha, outside the city.","Epilogue: The Ghad Imghêda","The leaders of the Ghad Imghêda are at Dâr Rapha.","Meet the Ghad Imghêda at Dâr Rapha, up the hill to the east","Find someone at the Northern Ship-yard who will tell you the situation in the city"}},
[4818]={nameES="Epilogue: The Wanderer's Confession",objectivesES={"Vágari has manifested for a single purpose: he wishes to make his confession.","The shade of Isildur stares impassively at Tárandil, and says nothing.","Epilogue: The Wanderer's Confession","The shade of Isildur stares impassively at Vágari, and says nothing.","Vágari the Wanderer is by the waggon bearing the bones of Isildur northward.","Talk to Vágari and complete 'Instance: The Wanderer's Confession'","Talk to Gandalf by the waggon in Laerlad","Gandalf is by the waggon bearing the bones of Isildur northward."}},
[4819]={nameES="Epilogue: The Waters of the Gilrain",objectivesES={"Epilogue: The Waters of the Gilrain","You have discovered Garvir - alive and resting on the banks of the Gilrain!","DNT -- will not be seen","Search the banks of the Gilrain for a man","Amid a brief peace in Linhir, Erchar has become fascinated by the stories you have shared of the Maiden of the Gilrain.","Erchar can be found in Linhir in eastern Dor-en-Ernil.\
\
You have learned that Garvir was saved by the Maiden of the Gilrain as he fell into the river. You should tell Erchar that his brother lives!","The man Roamingstar pulled from the Gilrain can be found along the nearby banks.\
\
Roamingstar rescued a man from the waters of the Gilrain and healed his wounds. You should examine the sleeping man.","Tell Erchar of Garvir's return","Talk to Roamingstar","Seek out Roamingstar in her glade","Garvir can be found in Linhir.\
\
Garvir has returned to Linhir, much to his brothers' amazement. You should speak to him, and welcome him home.","Talk to Garvir","Before you can finish telling Erchar, Garvir walks into Linhir, smiling widely","Roamingstar can be found in her glade in north-eastern Dor-en-Ernil.\
\
Erchar wishes to thank the Maiden of the Gilrain for watching over the people of Central Gondor.","Roamingstar can be found in her glade in north-eastern Dor-en-Ernil.\
\
You have discovered Garvir sleeping along the river-banks, much to your surprise. You should again speak to Roamingstar."}},
[4820]={nameES="Epílogo: El Bosque Salvaje de las Tierras de Bree",objectivesES={"Habla con Aran Verduno","Deberías volver a Puente de Caballetes o al Embarcadero de los Comerciantes","Vuelve a Embarcadero de los Comerciantes","Habla con Enid Picortiga","Vuelve a Puente de Caballetes","Ve al punto de encuentro entre Aran Verduno y Enid Picortiga","Los dos líderes están en plena conversación cuando llegas","Los líderes de la Liga del Hacha y de la Hermandad de los Leñadores pretenden colaborar para alcanzar sus objetivos en el Bosque Salvaje.","Enid Picortiga se encuentra en el punto de encuentro en el Bosque Salvaje.\
\
Deberías hablar con Enid Picortiga.","Encontrarás a Aran Verduno en el punto de encuentro del Bosque Salvaje.\
\
Deberías hablar con Aran Verduno.","Epílogo: El Bosque Salvaje de las Tierras de Bree","Aran Verdduno y Enid Picortiga tienen previsto reunirse en el centro del Bosque Salvaje.\
\
Debes dirigirte al punto de encuentro indicado."}},
[4821]={nameES="Epilogue: Trail of Rust",objectivesES={"Find Draigoch's bones","The Weeping Warrior's thirst for dragon bones is almost an obsession","Find Thorog's bones with Sigrun's aid","Karazgar the Weeping Warrior may have eluded your grasp, but retracing his path has taught you something of value: seeking to counteract his own decline, he turned to the dragon-venom that both strengthened and poisoned him for so long. He suffers in undeath, bound to the dragon-kind that he despises and upon which he now relies.","The dwarf Sigrun can aid you in the Misty Mountains, as can Fotri in Forochel. Draigoch's Lair can be found in Thrór's Coomb in Enedwaith.\
\
You should seek the bones of the dragons Bregmor, Draigoch, and Thorog.","Learned more about Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior.","Epilogue: Trail of Rust","The cavern has clearly been disturbed, and snow-covered rust trails across the mountain","Completado","Find Bregmor's bones with Fotri's aid","Fróthi suggests seeking out other dead dragons for clues to the riddle of the Weeping Warrior's motives."}},
[4822]={nameES="Epilogue: Vóin's Tale",objectivesES={"Talk to Gandalf inside the Beorninghús","Talk to Gandalf inside the Beorninghús and complete 'Instance: Vóin's Tale'","You have given Gandalf the glass shard you found locked in Khîl's home, and the Wizard believes it may prove crucial to revealing the secret writing in the Black Book of Mordor.","Gandalf is inside the Beorninghús.","Epilogue: Vóin's Tale","Gandalf is inside the Beorninghús, eager to decipher the secret writing in the Black Book of Mordor."}},
