[11649]={nameES="Thaurisgar: Purificación Nociva",objectivesES={"Regresa con Torvendor","Torvendor te ha pedido que purifiques Thaurisgar de sus infames rebuts.\
\
Thaurisgar, el Infame Boticario, se encuentra en Carn Dûm.","Torvendor es un montaraz del norte que ha venido como parte de una vanguardia para evitar que lo que se pudre en Carn Dûm escape al mundo exterior. Thaurisgar, el Infame Boticario, alberga algunas de las creaciones más infames y retorcidas.","Has eliminado tantas criaturas infames como pudiste dentro de Thaurisgar. Torvendor debe ser informado de inmediato.\
\
Torvendor se encuentra en Bail Avarc, fuera de Carn Dûm.","Thaurisgar: Purificación Nociva"}},
[11650]={nameES="Thaurisgar: Estudios de alquimia vil",objectivesES={"Thaurisgar: Estudios de alquimia vil","Baranoth te ha pedido que recojas las notas de investigación que permanecen intactas dentro de Thaurisgar.\
\
Thaurisgar, el Infame Boticario, se encuentra en Carn Dûm.","Estas notas de investigación deberían ser suficientes para que Baranoth las examine.\
\
Baranoth se encuentra en Bail Avarc, fuera de Carn Dûm.","Thaurisgar sirve como origen de algunos de los experimentos más retorcidos y las creaciones más malvadas de Aniochán el Atormentador. Debe ser estudiado antes de que se puedan implementar contramedidas.","Regresa con Baranoth"}},
[11651]={nameES="The Abandoned Camp",objectivesES={"Penda is disturbed by the loss of his companions at his Rohirrim-camp and is trying to discover what has happened.","You have collected sufficient evidence and should now return to Penda.","Penda is at the Rohirrim-camp along the road near the north base of the Cuthstan ridge.\
\
Penda believes that there may be clues around the Rohirrim-camp that could reveal what may have happened to cause his companions to leave so suddenly.","The Abandoned Camp","This small pool of dark blood seems fresh","This ale-barrel is nearly depleted and is surrounded  by half-empty cups","The chest is neatly packed full of someone's personal belongings","Search for more clues to the west of the camp","Penda has asked you to search for clues to the west of the Rohirrim-camp.","Penda is at the Rohirrim-camp along the road near the north base of the Cuthstan ridge.\
\
You have discovered a few clues while investigating outside of the Rohirrim-camp. You should return to Penda and report your findings to him.","Return to Penda to discuss your findings","A number of Rohirrim arrows litter the ground around the area","You have collected sufficient evidence and should inform Penda of your findings","The charred remains of an Orc suggests that a struggle recently took place here","The weapon-racks are mostly empty. It seems that many of the swords have been taken","Penda has asked you to look for more clues to the west","Return to Penda with the results of your search","Penda is at the Rohirrim-camp along the road near the north base of the Cuthstan ridge.\
\
You have discovered a few clues around the abandoned camp and should report your findings to Penda.","Search around the camp for clues regarding the missing Rohirrim"}},
[11652]={nameES="The Abominable Snow-beasts",objectivesES={"Brought cheer to the snow-beasts (3/3)","The Abominable Snow-beasts","Awakened from a deep sleep yet again, the beast has moved to a less noisy area. The beast still seems to have no intention of leaving Frostbluff. Perhaps a little more cheer will help.","The snow-beast has fallen back asleep. A bit more Yule cheer might drive him off.","The snow-beast has fallen asleep again. A bit more Yule cheer might drive him off.","The beast has moved to a less noisy area and is completely unmoved by your repeated attempts to drive him off. You should return to Guard Kember and explain the situation.","The snow-beast awakens and looks for a new place to rest","Brought cheer to the snow-beasts (1/3)","The beasts are no longer responding to your cheers. You should return to Guard Kember and ask him what to do next.","Talk to Guard Kember","Brought cheer to the snow-beasts (2/3)","Guard Kember has been tasked by Mayor Goodnough with driving off the nearby snow-beast family. He has noticed that they appear to despise merriment and recommends you bring a special variety of cheer to the beasts.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>","Bring some special Yule <rgb=#FF0000>cheer</rgb> to the snow-beasts (0/3)","Awakened from a deep sleep by your cheers, the snow-beast has moved to a less noisy area. The beast seems to have no intention of leaving Frostbluff. Perhaps a little more cheer will help.","The snow-beasts can be found to the east of Winter-home.\
\
Guard Kember wants you to bring some special Yule cheer to the snow-beasts of Frostbluff.","Bring some special Yule <rgb=#FF0000>cheer</rgb> to the snow-beasts (1/3)","Bring some special Yule <rgb=#FF0000>cheer</rgb> to the snow-beasts (2/3)","The snow-beasts appear completely uninterested in your merriment"}},
[11653]={nameES="The Abyss of Mordath (Tier 1)",objectivesES={"Cross the Abyss and pass into Thol Shíkug, the Screaming Deep","King Váskmun Greytooth and the Firehorns have descended into Glurnákh, The Pit of Greed. You must force King Greytooth to see reason or defeat him before he can lay claim to the Dwarf-ring, Manthríf.","The Order of the Eye has entered the Abyss of Mordath to seek vengeance upon King Váskmun Greytooth and lay claim to the lost artifacts of the Dark Lord. They have pursued the Firehorns into the depths of the Black Pits of Mordor.","The Abyss of Mordath has sunken into the deepest depths of the Black Pits of Mordor and now Sauron's greatest secrets are laid bare.","The Abyss of Mordath (Tier 1)","The Order of the Eye has laid claim to Thol Shíkug and descended into Murpraush, the Hall of Spoiling. They must be defeated if you are to continue your pursuit of King Greytooth and Firehorns.","As Sauron willed for King Greytooth and the Firehorns to pass unhindered deeper into the Mordath, Sagróg, the Bitter Warden, stands in your path. You must overcome him to continue your pursuit of King Greytooth and his folk.","Confront King Váskmun Greytooth and the Firehorns in Glurnákh, The Pit of Greed","Descend into the Black Pits of Mordor","Defeat the Order of the Eye in Murpraush, the Hall of Spoiling, and ascend the Black Stairs of Durshnúl","You have completed the Abyss of Mordath on Tier 1 and prevented the Dwarf-rings from being wielded to any evil end.","The Order of the Eye has crossed the Abyss dividing the Black Pits into a towering structure built into the foundations of Barad-dûr.","Completed: Abyss of Mordath (Tier 1)","Defeat Sagróg, the Bitter Warden, and enter the Ring-prisons in pursuit of the Firehorns"}},
[11654]={nameES="The Abyss of Mordath (Tier 2)",objectivesES={"Cross the Abyss and pass into Thol Shíkug, the Screaming Deep","You have completed the Abyss of Mordath on Tier 2 and prevented the Dwarf-rings from being wielded to any evil end.","King Váskmun Greytooth and the Firehorns have descended into Glurnákh, The Pit of Greed. You must force King Greytooth to see reason or defeat him before he can lay claim to the Dwarf-ring, Manthríf.","The Order of the Eye has entered the Abyss of Mordath to seek vengeance upon King Váskmun Greytooth and lay claim to the lost artifacts of the Dark Lord. They have pursued the Firehorns into the depths of the Black Pits of Mordor.","Completed: Abyss of Mordath (Tier 2)","As Sauron willed for King Greytooth and the Firehorns to pass unhindered deeper into the Mordath, Sagróg, the Bitter Warden, stands in your path. You must overcome him to continue your pursuit of King Greytooth and his folk.","The Order of the Eye has laid claim to Thol Shíkug and descended into Murpraush, the Hall of Spoiling. They must be defeated if you are to continue your pursuit of King Greytooth and Firehorns.","The Abyss of Mordath has sunken into the deepest depths of the Black Pits of Mordor and now Sauron's greatest secrets are laid bare.","Confront King Váskmun Greytooth and the Firehorns in Glurnákh, The Pit of Greed","Descend into the Black Pits of Mordor","Defeat the Order of the Eye in Murpraush, the Hall of Spoiling, and ascend the Black Stairs of Durshnúl","The Abyss of Mordath (Tier 2)","The Order of the Eye has crossed the Abyss dividing the Black Pits into a towering structure built into the foundations of Barad-dûr.","Defeat Sagróg, the Bitter Warden, and enter the Ring-prisons in pursuit of the Firehorns"}},
[11655]={nameES="La aldea maldita",objectivesES={"El aldeano condenado se encuentra en la aldea maldita de Audaghaim, en los Troncosombríos, al este de la Posada Embrujada.\
\
Deberías enfrentarte de nuevo a él, esta vez con pleno conocimiento de la verdad que trató de ocultar.","Enfréntate de nuevo al aldeano condenado","Habla con Prestadír en la Posada Embrujada","Prestadír ahora comprende que el aldeano condenado con el que hablaste anteriormente orquestó los asesinatos de todos aquellos que se resistieron al \\qprogreso\\q de la influencia del Nigromante. Desea que la negación del espectro se enfrente por fin a la verdad enterrada durante tanto tiempo.","La aldea maldita","Prestadír te espera en la Posada Embrujada en los Troncosombríos, al oeste de Audaghaim.\
\
Deberías hablar con él y decirle que el oscuro pasado de Audaghaim ha sido finalmente enfrentado."}},
[11656]={nameES="The Acres Aflame",objectivesES={"After failing the assault on Torsbury, Torferth sent you back to Stoke to inform Reeve Fríthild that he and his people would be late in coming.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: The bucket skill may only be used while on a war-steed.</rgb>","Fires can be found throughout the fields west of Stoke in the Broadacres.\
\
Reeve Fríthild has asked you to ride out and extinguish the fires that the Warg-riders started in the Broadacres.","The Acres Aflame"}},
[11657]={nameES="The Adoring Fan",objectivesES={"Hasna is too nervous to give Phêrida Iron-edge the vine circlet and has asked you to go instead.\
\
Phêrida can be found at the Dahâl Huliz.","<rgb=#FF0000>You've been spotted!</rgb>","A woman waits outside the Dahâl Huliz to see her favourite Hûlaz.","Before you can utter a single word, the Hûlaz politely holds up a hand to stop you.\
\
'This is from Hasna, is it not? I noticed she stopped coming to watch my fights, but she has always been there for me after. Even if she has been too nervous to approach me.' She chuckles. 'It was very sweet of you to help. Now, I do believe it is time for me to talk to her, so if you will excuse me....'","Hasna has asked you to pick leafy vines from trellises. However, you must avoid being spotted by gardeners more than a few times.\
\
The trellises can be found around the eastern side of the Tor-gardens pool.","Talk to Hasna at the Dahâl Huliz","The Adoring Fan","Habla con Phêrida Filohierro","You have gathered many leafy vines.\
\
You should bring them back to Hasna at the Dahâl Huliz."}},
[11658]={nameES="Las aventuras de Pisador",objectivesES={"Sigue el rastro de Pisador","Pisador ha huido al Bosque Salvaje occidental.\
\
Deberías buscar señales de la huida de Pisador.","Busca a Pisador","Las aventuras de Pisador","Minda se encuentra en la parte central del Bosque Salvaje.\
\
Deberías hablar con Minda Matosos.","Habla con Minda Matosos","Minda se encuentra en la parte occidental del Bosque Salvaje.\
\
Deberías hablar con Minda Matosos.","Tras escapar del malvado ladrón de carromatos, Pisador el poni ha huido, ¡pero puede que se esté metiendo en un peligro aún mayor!","En el Bosque Salvaje se pueden encontrar huellas de cascos.\
\
Deberías buscar más huellas de Pisador, el poni.","En el Bosque Salvaje se pueden encontrar cazadores de ponis.\
\
Minda Matosos te ha pedido que derrotes a los huargos que están cazando a Pisador, el poni.","Huellas de pezuñas, pero también huellas de patas muy grandes"}},
[11659]={nameES="The Adúrhid, the Kintai Elves",objectivesES={}},
[11660]={nameES="The Aftermath of Victory",objectivesES={"Talk to Nothmar","Talk to Cutha","Talk to  Aragorn","Aragorn can be found at his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.\
\
Help Aragorn survey the battlefield for the missing and presumed dead of Rohan.","Talk to Wídfara","Complete -- The Aftermath: Dervorin and Rossaran","Aragorn can be found at his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.\
\
You should return to Aragorn and tell him what you learned.","Talk to Duinhir","Complete -- The Aftermath: Forlong, Golasgil, and Hirluin","Ask Duinhir, Gléowine, Wídfara, Gamling, and Cutha about what they saw of the battle yesterday. They can all be found among the tents of Aragorn's Pavilion.","Talk to Gléowine","You should talk to Éomer and Nothmar, who can be found at Aragorn's Pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.","Talk to Golasgil","Habla con Aragorn","Aragorn has asked you to make a reckoning of those who fell in the Battle of the Pelennor Fields.","Habla con Éomer","Talk to Rossaran","Talk to Ingold","Complete -- The Aftermath: Duilin and Derufin","Talk to Dervorin","Aragorn can be found at his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.\
\
Help Aragorn survey the battlefield for the missing and presumed dead of Gondor.","You should talk to Aragorn, who can be found at his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.","Complete -- Book 7, Chapter 2: The Council of the Captains","You should speak with Rossaran, Dervorin, Golasgil, and Ingold, who can all be found in Aragorn's Pavilion, upon the after-battle Pelennor.","Complete -- The Aftermath: Elfmar, Harding, and Torferth","Talk to Gamling","Complete -- The Aftermath: The Valiant Rohirrim","The Aftermath of Victory","Complete -- The Aftermath: Ingold and Turgon"}},
[11661]={nameES="The Aftermath: Dervorin and Rossaran",objectivesES={"Habla con Aragorn","Find Dervorin","Find Rossaran","Aragorn can be found at his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.\
\
You should return to Aragorn now that Dervorin and Rossaran are found.","Aragorn has asked you to find Dervorin and Rossaran, both presumed to be missing in combat.","The Aftermath: Dervorin and Rossaran","Search for Dervorin and Rossaran on the after-battle Pelennor."}},
[11662]={nameES="The Aftermath: Duilin and Derufin",objectivesES={"Identify Duilin","You gently explain that Aragorn has asked Duinhir to identify his sons' bodies.\
\
'I cannot. I have seen so much death. To see theirs... You came to know them well in these last days, did you not? Will you go in my stead?'","You are certain this is the body of Derufin","Habla con Aragorn","You should speak with Duinhir, who can be found at Aragorn's pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.","Search among the slain for Duilin and Derufin's bodies.","Duinhir does not have the strength of mind to identify his sons","Identify Derufin","You are certain this is the body of Duilin","Talk to Duinhir","Aragorn can be found in his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.\
\
You should return to Aragorn now that you have identified Duilin and Derufin.","This is not one of Duinhir's sons","The Aftermath: Duilin and Derufin","Help identify the bodies of Duilin and Derufin among those recovered from the field."}},
[11663]={nameES="The Aftermath: Elfmar, Harding, and Torferth",objectivesES={"Habla con Aragorn","Torferth gave his life to Rohan and Gondor","Elfmar died valiantly","The Aftermath: Elfmar, Harding, and Torferth","You should talk to Aragorn, who can be found at his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.","Elfmar, Harding, Torferth were last seen somewhere on the Pelennor Fields. Look for them there, after the battle.","Find Torferth","Find Elfmar","Find Harding","Harding slew many before he fell in battle","Aragorn has asked you to find Elfmar, Harding, and Torferth, all presumed to be missing in combat."}},
[11664]={nameES="The Aftermath: Forlong, Golasgil, and Hirluin",objectivesES={"Habla con Aragorn","The Aftermath: Forlong, Golasgil, and Hirluin","Find Hirluin","Search for Forlong on the after-battle Pelennor.","Find Golasgil","You should talk to Aragorn, who stands by Forlong on the after-battle Pelennor.","Aragorn has asked you to find Forlong, Golasgil, and Hirluin, all presumed to be missing in combat.","You have found the spot where Hirluin lies slain.","Forlong lies dying on the after-battle Pelennor.\
\
Blow Forlong's horn to summon Thorongil.","Find Forlong","Aragorn arrives swiftly, a look of grave concern on his face, and stands by his old friend one last time","Search for Golasgil and Hirluin on the after-battle Pelennor.","Blow Forlong's horn"}},
[11665]={nameES="The Aftermath: Ingold and Turgon",objectivesES={"Find Turgon","Habla con Aragorn","Search for Ingold and Turgon on the after-battle Pelennor.","Find Ingold","Turgon died with honour, in combat","Aragorn can be found in his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.\
\
You should return to Aragorn now that you have found Ingold and Turgon.","Aragorn has asked you to find Ingold and Turgon, both presumed to be missing in combat.","The Aftermath: Ingold and Turgon"}},
[11666]={nameES="The Aftermath: The Valiant Rohirrim",objectivesES={"Herubrand was slain by Gothmog's Orcs","The Aftermath: The Valiant Rohirrim","Habla con Aragorn","Find Nothmar","Find Déorwine","Grimbold, Déorwine, Dúnhere, Guthláf, Herefara, and Herubrand died on the Pelennor. Nothmar is missing.\
\
Search for the valiant Rohirrim on the Pelennor Fields, after the battle.","Déorwine died protecting King Théoden","Dúnhere was felled by an arrow at Riders' Stand","Find Grimbold","Grimbold heroically attacked a fell-beast in his final moments","You should talk to Aragorn, who can be found at his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.","Aragorn has asked you to find the bodies of many Rohirrim who fell in combat, and to search for Nothmar, who was last seen making towards the city.","Find Dúnhere","Find Herubrand","Herefara was slain by Gothmog's Orcs","Find Guthláf","Find Herefara","Guthláf died protecting King Théoden"}},
[11667]={nameES="La Asociación de la Cerveza -- Un juego de hostigamiento de hobbits",objectivesES={"La Asociación de la Cerveza -- Un juego de hostigamiento de hobbits","A Ráthgeir, un enano bastante malicioso, se le puede encontrar fuera del Agujero Embrujado, escondido detrás de unas cajas.\
\
Deberías contarle a Ráthgeir todas las pequeñas travesuras que hiciste.","Cuéntale a Ráthgeir tus hilarantes correrías","Hay hobbits asustados por todo el Agujero Embrujado, y seguramente hay una manera de aterrorizarlos, porque es muy gracioso.\
\
Deberías hostigar y acosar a los hobbits.","Ráthgeir, miembro de la Asociación de la Cerveza, desea continuar el legado de su asociación en el Agujero Embrujado. Esta oportunidad de gastar bromas a los hobbits no puede dejarse escapar.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000> NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro de misiones cuando finalice el evento con el que está asociada. </rgb>"}},
[11668]={nameES="El Desafío de la Asociación Cervecera: Introducción",objectivesES={"Habla con Bjarni en el Póney Pisador","El Desafío de la Asociación Cervecera: Introducción","Bjarni se encuentra en la posada del Póney Pisador, en Bree.\
\
Deberías hablar con Bjarni si deseas unirte formalmente a la Asociación Cervecera.","Todo lo que la Liga de las Posadas puede hacer, la Asociación Cervecera quiere hacerlo mejor.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro de misiones cuando finalice el festival actual.</rgb>"}},
[11669]={nameES="El Desafío de la Asociación Cervecera: Entibo",objectivesES={"Bebe cervezas (5/6)","Bebiste una cerveza (3/6)","Bebiste una cerveza (5/6)","Bebe cervezas (0/6)","La Asociación Cervecera busca ganar reclutas en las Tierras de Bree para competir más que nunca con la Liga de las Posadas.\
