[12391]={nameES="The Hidden Vale",objectivesES={}},
[12392]={nameES="The Hidden Way",objectivesES={"Speak with Dagoras within Isengard","Quickbeam is at the river's edge, down in the Vale below his home.\
\
Quickbeam has asked you to meet him down by the river's edge, where he believes he has found a way to sneak you into Isengard.","Talk to Quickbeam by the Isen","The Hidden Way","You should sneak into Isengard through the tunnel Quickbeam has opened for you.","Quickbeam says that there is little more he can do until his kindred decide upon some course of action... but he believes that he has found a way for you to enter the fortress of Isengard undetected."}},
[12393]={nameES="The Hiddenhoard Revealed",objectivesES={"Prince Durin can be found at Zidir-nesad, the Steepset.\
\
You have triumphed over Hrímil Frost-heart at the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra. You should talk to Durin at Zidir-nesad.","From deep within the darkness of the passage ahead, a voice seems to beckon you...","Talk to Náin at Amgaruslun","The Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra can be found beyond the frozen falls of Amgaruslun in the Clovengap.\
\
According to Prince Durin, the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra can be found beyond Amgaruslun in the Clovegap. You should see if the dwarves of Náin's company have broken through the ice concealing the passage to the ancient Greymaul treasury.","The Hiddenhoard Revealed","Discover the passage to the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra","Meet up with Náin and his company at Amgaruslun in the Clovengap","It appears that Náin and his company have uncovered an old passage deeper into the Clovengap","Náin can be found at Amgaruslun in the north-western reaches of the Clovengap.\
\
The dwarves' hard work has borne fruit. You have discovered the passage to the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra. You should return to Náin.","Complete 'The Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra'","Prince Durin believes he has discovered where Hrímil Frost-heart has made her lair within Mount Gundabad: the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.","Talk to Durin at Zidir-nesad, the Steepset","<rgb=#00FF00>It is recommended, but not required, that you complete The Legacy of Durin and the Trials of the Dwarves before playing 'The Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra'.</rgb>\
\
'There are those who believe that Hrímil Frost-heart has abandoned Mount Gundabad. I say they are wrong! It is true she has fled, but only deeper into the Mountain-home—to Abnankâra!\
\
'Does that name sound unfamiliar to your ear? It should, my friend. It is known to none who still live, save for me, and that is only because I share the memories of the Durins who came before me!\
\
'Not long after the Greymaul Rebellion was ended and Motsóg came to dwell in solitude in the caverns deep beneath the Mountain-home, he confessed a secret to me—to the Durin I was then. Before that ruinous war between our peoples, he had set the Greymauls upon a great task: to delve a hidden treasury within the depths of Mount Gundabad. It was named Abnankâra, the Hiddenhoard, and it would have been the jewel of Motsóg's kingdom. Had the Greymauls succeeded in their plot to steal the wealth and mithril of Khazad-dûm, it is certain the spoils would have come to rest at Abnankâra.\
\
'Whether it was by some sense of duty or mere curiosity, I—when I was Durin the First—heeded Motsóg's words and found the hidden way to the gates of Abnankâra. I strode within its halls only once, and when I had seen all that I meant to, I sealed it behind me—leaving the few, ill-gotten riches of the Greymauls to be forgotten. And so it has been for many Ages of the world!\
\
'It lies still in the Clovengap, my friend, and in my heart, I am certain that that is where Hrímil Frost-heart has gone. I have sent my uncle, Náin, ahead with a small company to seek for the Hiddenhoard.\
\
'Will you aid him, my friend? Will you see our long struggle for the conquest of Mount Gundabad to its end?'","The Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra can be found in the Clovengap.\
\
Náin has asked you to muster your allies and aid Prince Durin in confronting Hrímil Frost-heart in the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.\
\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You must complete 'The Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra' on any difficulty Tier to advance this quest.</rgb>","Náin can be found at Amgaruslun in the north-western reaches of the Clovengap.\
\
After arriving at Amgaruslun, you have found Náin's company hard at work excavating what appears to be an old passageway deeper into Mount Gundabad. You should talk to Náin.","Náin and his company can be found at Amgaruslun in the north-western reaches of the Clovengap.\
\
Believing that an ancient Greymaul treasury known as the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra had long laid hidden in Mount Gundabad, Prince Durin has asked you to join Náin and his company at Amgaruslun in the Clovengap. You should meet up with Náin and his company at Amgaruslun."}},
[12394]={nameES="The Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra -- Tier 1",objectivesES={"Swayed by the power of Hrímil's voice, Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk and the Hobgoblins of Mount Gundabad guard the arming-chamber of Ibkêrmazal in the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.\
\
You must defeat Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk and the hobgoblins under the control of Hrímil Frost-heart and gain entry to Akrazulgibshîn, the treasury of the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.","Defeat Hrímil Frost-heart","The Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra -- Tier 1","Defeat the Heirs of Thyrstáth","Heirs to their fallen chieftain, Hrungrod, the ice-giants Armód, Kvethár, and Threkvegg guard the entrance to Abnankâra.\
\
You must defeat the Heirs of Thyrstáth and gain entry to the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.","Hrímil Frost-heart slumbers in her lair within Akrazulgibshîn, the long-forgotten treasury of the Greymauls in the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.\
\
You must defeat Hrímil Frost-heart, the Herald of Winter, and put an end to her rule of Mount Gundabad.","Defeat Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk","Beyond the falls of Amgaruslun in the Clovengap lies the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra. Once an ancient treasury wrought in secret by Mótsog and the Greymauls during their rebellion against the Longbeards in the Elder Days, it has become the lair of Hrímil Frost-heart, a dreaded cold-dragon of Morgoth. Within this frozen retreat, Hrímil tends her wounds and slumbers, dreaming of vengeance upon Prince Durin and the Dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ."}},
[12395]={nameES="The Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra -- Tier 2",objectivesES={"Swayed by the power of Hrímil's voice, Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk and the Hobgoblins of Mount Gundabad guard the arming-chamber of Ibkêrmazal in the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.\
\
You must defeat Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk and the hobgoblins under the control of Hrímil Frost-heart and gain entry to Akrazulgibshîn, the treasury of the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.","Defeat Hrímil Frost-heart","Defeat the Heirs of Thyrstáth","Heirs to their fallen chieftain, Hrungrod, the ice-giants Armód, Kvethár, and Threkvegg guard the entrance to Abnankâra.\
\
You must defeat the Heirs of Thyrstáth and gain entry to the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.","The Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra -- Tier 2","Hrímil Frost-heart slumbers in her lair within Akrazulgibshîn, the long-forgotten treasury of the Greymauls in the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.\
\
You must defeat Hrímil Frost-heart, the Herald of Winter, and put an end to her rule of Mount Gundabad.","Defeat Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk","Beyond the falls of Amgaruslun in the Clovengap lies the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra. Once an ancient treasury wrought in secret by Mótsog and the Greymauls during their rebellion against the Longbeards in the Elder Days, it has become the lair of Hrímil Frost-heart, a dreaded cold-dragon of Morgoth. Within this frozen retreat, Hrímil tends her wounds and slumbers, dreaming of vengeance upon Prince Durin and the Dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ."}},
